isakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Classic Malaysia And Singapore' package is an 8-day tour covering the vibrant destinations of Singapore and Kuala Lumpur. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Petronas Twin Towers, the historic Batu Caves, Gardens by the Bay, and Sentosa Island. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, thrilling experiences at Universal Studios, scenic cable car rides, and ample opportunities to explore bustling local night markets and shopping districts.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\nArrive at Kuala Lumpur – Enroute Putrajaya 15 mins Photo stop – (Private Basis)\nSelamat Datang! Welcome to Malaysia's capital city - Kuala Lumpur!\nUpon arrival at Kuala Lumpur, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.)  \nHighlights : 15 min photo-stop in Putrajaya: Pinkish Putra Mosque, Dataran Putra overlooking the Putrajaya Lake, Putra Bridge.\nCheck in Hotel.", 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Metro Bukit Bintang\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Royal KL\xa0(Value) /\xa0Berjaya Times Square\xa0(Premium) or Similar in\xa0Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\nHalf Day City Tour (Private Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Proceed for city tour.\n\xa0Experience the unique blend of modern, historic, secular, and religious sights found in Kuala Lumpur during this half-day sightseeing tour. Visit prominent sights such as the sky-high Petronas Towers (photo stop), the country's National Mosque, stunning buildings such as the King's Palace and various other places. These places will leave you awestruck. You can also get yourself some memorable gifts from the local shops, which will remind you of your good days in Kuala Lumpur.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Metro Bukit Bintang\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Royal KL\xa0(Value) /\xa0Berjaya Times Square\xa0(Premium) or Similar in\xa0Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nGenting Highlands Day Trip En-Route Batu Caves (15 Mins Photo-Stop Only) & 2 Ways Cable Car – (Private Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nPost breakfast, set out to explore Genting Highlands. It is an hour’s drive from Kuala Lumpur. With the landscape beautifully dotted with mountain peaks, Genting Highlands is also known as RWG (Resorts World Genting).\nIt is fashioned on Las Vegas- Asian style. The highlands include luxury hotels, casinos, and exciting shopping malls. It has a theme park in Pahang which is at a staggering height of 1800 meters on the peak of Gunung Ulu Kali. There is a lot more than the highlands offer.\nBATU CAVES: Batu Caves, one of Kuala Lumpur’s most frequented tourist attractions, is a limestone hill comprising three major caves and a number of smaller ones. Located approximately 11 kilometers to the north of Kuala Lumpur, this 100-year-old temple features idols and statues erected inside the main caves and around it. Incorporated with interior limestone formations said to be around 400 million years old, the temple is considered an important religious landmark by Hindus. Cathedral Cave – the largest and most popular cavern in Batu Caves – houses several Hindu shrines beneath its 100-metre-high arched ceiling. At the foot of Batu Hill are two other cave temples – the Art Gallery Cave and Museum Cave – which houses numerous Hindu statues and paintings.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Metro Bukit Bintang\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Royal KL\xa0(Value) /\xa0Berjaya Times Square\xa0(Premium) or Similar in\xa0Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart Kuala Lumpur – Arrive Singapore by Coach\nMorning after breakfast; you will be transferred to Singapore\nUpon arrival at the Singapore, transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.)', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Chancellor @ Albert Court or Ibis Style Albert\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Mercure Tyrwitt\xa0(Value) /\xa0One Farer\xa0(Premium) or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nVisit Universal Studios (SIC basis) (closed on Tuesday)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nLater, visit the Universal Studios\nStart your journey to Hollywood movie theme park - Universal Studios™ forms part of Resorts World™ Sentosa. Among the park's many rides and exciting attractions are Battlestar Galactica™, the world's tallest pair of dueling roller coasters and Far Far Away Castle™, the first castle from the world of Shrek where you can experience the amazing Shrek 4-D™ attraction. One of the biggest spectacles in live entertainment is based on the movie Waterworld™. The action comes gushing to life in a tidal wave of death-defying stunts, explosions, and thrilling action. Enjoy Jurassic Park Rapids Adventure™, Madagascar: A Crate Adventure™ and Revenge of the Mummy™, TRANSFORMERS The Ride and many more.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Chancellor @ Albert Court or Ibis Style Albert\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Mercure Tyrwitt\xa0(Value) /\xa0One Farer\xa0(Premium) or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nMarina Bay Sands Sky Park & Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome – Impression of Monet Expression + Cloud Forest) (SIC basis) + Visit Sentosa Island (One Way Cable Car, 4D Adventure Land Any 2, & Wings of Time) (SIC Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nVisit the Marina Bay Sands hotel to enjoy panoramic views of the city from MBS Sky Park. Take a walk from MBS to Gardens by the Bay. We then visit Gardens by the Bay – Flower Dome and Super Tree Observation Deck. Enter the flower Dome, the largest glass greenhouse in the world. It replicates a mild, dry climate and features plants found in the Mediterranean and other semi-arid tropical regions. Home to one of the world’s tallest indoor waterfalls and a lush mountain clad with plants from around the world, Cloud Forest rewards the curious and adventurous. Go on a fascinating journey of discovery and get up close with some of the world’s most exotic plant species as you stroll along its unique aerial walkways.\nSentosa is an island resort off Singapore’s southern coast, connected to the city by road, cable car, pedestrian boardwalk, and monorail.\nEnjoy the cable car ride and experience 4D adventure land any 2 options. Finish your day on Sentosa Island on a spectacular note with the award-winning Wings of Time show.\n\xa0\nNote: Wings of Time Fireworks Symphony shall be temporarily closed from 3 Nov - 16 Nov 2025.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Chancellor @ Albert Court or Ibis Style Albert\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Mercure Tyrwitt\xa0(Value) /\xa0One Farer\xa0(Premium) or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'Bird Paradise + Night Safari (SIC basis)\n Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nA peek into Paradise. Immerse yourself in the symphony of colors across 8 walk-through aviaries that will take you to different biomes and landscapes of the world. Bird Paradise is home to over 3,500 birds from over 400 avian species. Explore the Night Safari for an off-hour wildlife adventure to observe the Zoo’s nocturnal fauna', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Chancellor @ Albert Court or Ibis Style Albert\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Mercure Tyrwitt\xa0(Value) /\xa0One Farer\xa0(Premium) or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 8, 'description': 'Departure\nMorning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India\n\xa0\n* The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice\nPACKAGE ENVISAGED: Travel Validity: 01 July 2025 – 25 SEP 2026\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY \n\n\nHOTELS\n\n\nPACKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN USD\n\n\n\n\n