Name': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Singapore - Buy 1 Get 1 Free' package is a 5-day tour covering the vibrant city of Singapore. This special package features an incredible Buy One Get One Free offer where one adult companion travels completely free with a paying adult. Throughout the trip, participants will enjoy convenient seat-in-coach return airport transfers, a comprehensive Singapore city tour, and an exciting excursion to Sentosa Island, which includes a scenic one-way cable car ride and the mesmerizing Wings of Time show. Additionally, the package provides travel insurance for participants up to 60 years of age, ensuring a hassle-free and memorable tropical getaway.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive at Singapore\nWelcome to Singapore – also known as the Lion City (Singapura)!\nUpon arrival at the airport, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.).', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS Style Albert (Standard) /\xa0Furama Riverfront\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Singapore'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nHalf Day Singapore City tour\xa0 (SIC basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\n\xa0\nProceed for Half Day City Tour of Singapore. We drive past the Suntec city, Parliament House, Supreme Court, City Hall, China Town and Little India. Visit Singapore’s Iconic statue - one of the most famous depictions at Merlion Park.!\nRest day for leisure.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS Style Albert (Standard) /\xa0Furama Riverfront\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Singapore'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island (One Way Cable Car & Wings of Time) (SIC Basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nToday enjoy full day at the Sentosa Island. Sentosa is an island resort off Singapore’s southern coast, connected to the city by road, cable car, pedestrian boardwalk, and monorail.\nFinish your day on Sentosa Island on a spectacular note with the award-winning Wings of Time show.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS Style Albert (Standard) /\xa0Furama Riverfront\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Singapore'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Free\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\n\xa0\nDay is for Leisure.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS Style Albert (Standard) /\xa0Furama Riverfront\xa0(Value)\xa0or similar in\xa0Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDeparture\n\xa0\nMorning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India.\n\xa0\n* The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice*\n\xa0\nExtension Night:\nTravel Validity: From 01st Oct 2026 To 26th March 2027\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY \n\n\nHOTELS\n\n\nPAKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN SGD\n\n\n\n\nSINGLE\n\n\nTWIN / DOUBLE\n\n\nTRIPLE\n\n\nCHILD WITH BED\n\n\nCHILD NO BED\n\n\n\n\n03 star \n\n\nIBIS Style Singapore Albert or similar\n\n\nNA\n\n\n80\n\n\nNA\n\n\nNA\n\n\nNA\n\n\n\n\n04 star \n\n\nFurama Riverfront or similar\n\n\nNA\n\n\n100\n\n\nNA\n\n\nNA\n\n\nNA\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at hotel', '\nHotel Grand Copthorne Waterfront (Premium) or similar in Singapore\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\nHotel Grand Copthorne Waterfront (Premium) or similar in Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at hotel', '1': 'Overnight stay at hotel'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 78400.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at hotel']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 87400.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at hotel']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nReturn Airport Transfer (Airport - Hotel - Airport) - (SIC Basis)\xa0\n', 'As per itinerary', '\nReturn Airport Transfer (Airport - Hotel - Airport) - (SIC Basis)\n'], 'sightseeing': ['\nSingapore City Tour – (SIC Basis)\nSentosa Island (One Way Cable Car, & Wings of Time) – (SIC Basis)\xa0\n', 'Till Sep 2025\n\nNight Safari (SIC Basis)\nHalf Day City Tour (SIC basis), Visit Marina Bay Sands Sky Park & Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Cloud Forest) (SIC basis)\nVisit Universal Studios (SIC basis)\nVisit Sentosa Island (One Way Cable Car, Madame Tussauds 4 in 1 & Wings of Time) (SIC Basis)\n\n\xa0\nValid from Oct 2025 till Sep 2026:\n\nNight Safari (SIC Basis)\nHalf Day City Tour (SIC basis), Visit Marina Bay Sands Sky Park & Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Cloud Forest & Jurassic World) (SIC basis)\nVisit Sentosa Island (One Way Cable Car, 4D Adventure Land, & Wings of Time) (SIC Basis)\nVisit Universal Studios and Oceanarium – Non-Peak (SIC basis) (closed on Tuesday)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\n4 Nights’ Accommodation at the lowest room category with daily breakfast (except on day 1)\nReturn Airport Transfer (Airport - Hotel - Airport) - (SIC Basis)\xa0\nSingapore City Tour – (SIC Basis)\nSentosa Island (One Way Cable Car, & Wings of Time) - (SIC Basis)\nTravel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.)\n', 'exclusions': "\nTCS & GST\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable\xa0\nAll flights services\xa0\nVisa Services\nHigh & Peak Season Surcharge\nMeals not mentioned in the itinerary\nAny tips for guide & Driver\xa0\nAnything not mentioned in the inclusions\nAirport Taxes (Domestic & International)\nEnglish Speaking Guide\nPre & Post tour services & cost\xa0\nExpenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc)\nAll drink and beverages\xa0\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\nBlackout Dates: (Rates won’t be valid if the stay falls on or between the mentioned dates)\n\nFORMULA 1 (GRAND PRIX) – 24 SEP – 11 OCT 2026\nCHIRSTMAS & NEW YEAR - 15 DEC' 26 - 05 JAN 2027\nCHINESE NEW YEAR - 10 FEB'27 – 18FEB’27\nRAMADAN EID - 10 - 20 MAR'27\n\n\nMidnight surcharge\nAll transfers are made only on point-to-point basis only\xa0\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\n", 'termsAndConditions': 'TERMS AND CONDITIONS:\n\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014129/Singapore780.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014129/itinerary/SingaporeCity753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014129/itinerary/SingaporeMerlionpark2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014129/itinerary/SingaporeSentosa.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014129/itinerary/SingaporeFlyer.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014129/itinerary/Singapore7532.jpg']}, 'score': 11.498684, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014468', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014468', 'availableMonths': ['april_2027', 'november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Singapore - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 5, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 99709, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Singapore - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 5-day air-inclusive value tour covering the vibrant city of Singapore with the dedicated assistance of a tour manager throughout the journey. This comprehensive package includes visa and insurance services, comfortable stays in 4-star hotels on a bed-and-breakfast basis, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners. During the tour, participants will enjoy a guided city tour of Singapore, a visit to Sentosa Island featuring the 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds experience, an exploration of the stunning Gardens by the Bay with entrance to the Flower Dome and the Cloud Forest's Jurassic World Exhibition, and an exciting visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'images': ['Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'SentosaIsland.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'SingaporeFlyer.jpg', 'Singapore7532.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 99709, 'thumbnailImage': 'Singapore26787.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014468 is named 'Highlights Of Singapore - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 5 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Singapore, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay Welcome To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 99709.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n04 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n01 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. 500 ml water bottle per day Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs General Info Currency used: SINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: SINGAPORE : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or Necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSG550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Singapore - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 5-day air-inclusive value tour covering the vibrant city of Singapore with the dedicated assistance of a tour manager throughout the journey. This comprehensive package includes visa and insurance services, comfortable stays in 4-star hotels on a bed-and-breakfast basis, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners. During the tour, participants will enjoy a guided city tour of Singapore, a visit to Sentosa Island featuring the 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds experience, an exploration of the stunning Gardens by the Bay with entrance to the Flower Dome and the Cloud Forest's Jurassic World Exhibition, and an exciting visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive In Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\nWelcome To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed\xa0 For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods)\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park –\xa0 Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers \xa0(Optional)\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 99700.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n01 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non-Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Singapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings of Time Show\n', 'PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n500 ml water bottle per day\xa0\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': "\xa0\nNote:\xa0Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\nCurrency used:\xa0\xa0\n\nSINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar\xa0 (SGD)\n\nTime difference:\xa0\n\nSINGAPORE : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st\xa0December\xa02025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in\nThailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might\xa0give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds\xa0and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room.\xa0\n(Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs.\xa0 Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin\nroom is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for\nentire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or Necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour\xa0manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014468/Singapore26787.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014468/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014468/itinerary/SentosaIsland.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014468/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014468/itinerary/SingaporeFlyer.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014468/itinerary/Singapore7532.jpg']}, 'score': 11.029285, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014459', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014459', 'availableMonths': ['april_2027', 'november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Singapore Extravaganza With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 158669, 'packageSummary': "The 'Singapore Extravaganza With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore and the Genting Dream Cruise. This comprehensive itinerary features tour manager assistance, visa and insurance, four-star plus hotel accommodations, and specially curated Indian meals, including Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian options. Key activities in Singapore include a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with the Madame Tussauds four-in-one experience, and exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest, Jurassic World Exhibition, and Flower Dome. Additionally, travelers will enjoy visits to the Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium, along with special treats like tea, coffee, and ice cream at select sightseeing locations.", 'images': ['GardensBythebayNEW_753.jpg', 'Sentosa.jpg', 'SeaAquarium.jpg', 'GentingDreamcruise2.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise753.jpg', 'GentingDreamcruise2.jpg', 'Singapore.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 158669, 'thumbnailImage': 'Singapore26734.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Cruise', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014459 is named 'Singapore Extravaganza With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Singapore, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay Welcome To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Afternoon Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Note : Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs. All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card. Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Proceed To Take A Ride On The Singapore Flyer, One Of The World’s Largest Observation Wheels. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy The Rest Of The Day At Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise This Morning After Breakfast, Check-Out And Proceed To Cruise Terminal. Day Onboard Cruise With Lunch And Dinner - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 158669.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 01 Lunch Coupons)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs General Info: Currency used: Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct fight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - FFull shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSW55