ctivities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'On board Genting Dream Cruise'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'On board Genting Dream Cruise'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'On board Genting Dream Cruise'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 158700.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 01 Lunch Coupons)\n04 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'Singapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance to Wings of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\xa0\n\nGenting Dream Cruise:\n\nOnboard Genting Dream Cruise with full board meals, entertainment & activities.\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': "Note:\xa0Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\n\xa0\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info:\n\xa0\n\nCurrency used:\xa0Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD)\nTime difference: Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st\xa0December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\xa0\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\xa0\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining\xa0room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct fight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - FFull shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/Singapore26734.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/GardensBythebayNEW_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/Sentosa.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/SeaAquarium.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/GentingDreamcruise2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/GentingDreamcruise2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014459/itinerary/Singapore.jpg']}, 'score': 10.83901, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014469', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014469', 'availableMonths': ['april_2027', 'november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Singapore With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise Cruise - Sail on Genting Dream Cruise"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 139074, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Singapore With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day tour covering Singapore and a sailing experience on the Genting Dream Cruise. This air-inclusive value tour provides tour manager assistance, visa and insurance services, four-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian meals. During the trip, participants will enjoy a guided city tour of Singapore, a visit to Sentosa Island featuring the 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds, an exploration of Gardens by the Bay including the Flower Dome and the Cloud Forest's Jurassic World Exhibition, and a visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise, all complemented by a memorable cruise experience.", 'images': ['Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'SentosaIsland.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'Singaporecity23.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 139074, 'thumbnailImage': 'Singapore26756.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Cruise'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014469 is named 'Highlights Of Singapore With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Singapore, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay Welcome To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check-Out And Proceed To Cruise Terminal. Day Onboard Cruise With Lunch And Dinner - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 139074.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n, \n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n01 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager/ local representative. (subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. 500 ml of water per day Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th General Info CURRENCY USED : THAILAND : Thai Bhat (THB) TIME DIFFERENCE: THAILAND : 1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2023. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or Necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise Cruise - Sail on Genting Dream Cruise.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZSC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Singapore With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day tour covering Singapore and a sailing experience on the Genting Dream Cruise. This air-inclusive value tour provides tour manager assistance, visa and insurance services, four-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian meals. During the trip, participants will enjoy a guided city tour of Singapore, a visit to Sentosa Island featuring the 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds, an exploration of Gardens by the Bay including the Flower Dome and the Cloud Forest's Jurassic World Exhibition, and a visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise, all complemented by a memorable cruise experience.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\nWelcome To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed\xa0 For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition\xa0 & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At\nSingapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods)\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn\xa0or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park –\xa0 Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn\xa0or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers \xa0(Optional)\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn\xa0or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Check-Out And Proceed To Cruise Terminal.\nDay Onboard Cruise With Lunch And Dinner - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise\xa0(Inside Cabin)'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise\xa0(Inside Cabin)'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n', '\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 139100.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n01 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n', 'Singapore:\n\nGuided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens By The Bay\xa0 - Entrance To Cloud Forest With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car Ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings Of Time Show\n\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise:\n\nOnboard Genting Dream Cruise With Full Board Meals, Entertainment & Activities.\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager/ local representative.\n(subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n500 ml of water per day\xa0\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': "\xa0\nNote:\xa0Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAll travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\n\nCURRENCY USED :\xa0\xa0THAILAND : Thai Bhat (THB)\xa0\nTIME DIFFERENCE:\xa0THAILAND : 1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2023. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in\nThailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might\xa0give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds\xa0and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room.\xa0\n(Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs.\xa0 Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin\nroom is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for\nentire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or Necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour\xa0manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/Singapore26756.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/SentosaIsland.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014469/itinerary/Singaporecity23.jpg']}, 'score': 10.67132, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014454', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014454', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Dhamaka - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014454_0_20261007170441', 'price': 117335, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Dhamaka - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Kuala Lumpur and Singapore. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Petronas Twin Towers, the historic Batu Caves, the futuristic Gardens by the Bay, and the spectacular Marina Bay Sands. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic cable car rides, and exciting excursions to Sentosa Island and Universal Studios.", 'images': ['kuala_Lumpur.jpg', 'BatuCave.jpg', 'KualaLumpur.jpg', 'MerlionParkNew_753.jpg', 'GardensBythebayNEW_753.jpg', 'SeaAquarium.jpg', 'Singapore_New.jpeg'], 'minimumPrice': 117335, 'thumbnailImage': 'GardensByTheBay_srp.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Budget Friendly', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014454 is named 'Asian Dhamaka - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive Kuala Lumpur – Guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur Welcome to Malaysia. Upon arrival proceed to your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). In the afternoon, proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. NOTE : All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below. https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day excursion to Genting Highland - Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to the Sky way cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car. Visit Batu Caves, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at Leisure or Visit Sunway Lagoon (Optional) Today after breakfast rest of the day is at leisure or explore Kuala Lumpur on your own or join us on an optional excursion to visit Sunway Lagoon., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Drive to Singapore This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Notes: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs. Link : Prohibited and Controlled Goods All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card via an application called as SG Arrival. Link: ICA | SG Arrival Card It is highly advisable to carry an international activated mobile number & an international activated credit card., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour - Visit Gardens by the Bay - Half Day Sentosa Tour (Optional) This morning after buffet breakfast, Proceed for a guided city tour - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard Road, Photo stop at Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later we visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with the Jurassic World & Flower Dome. Rest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on Half Day Sentosa tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium (Optional) This morning after buffet breakfast, rest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on a visit to Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: FLY BACK Today after breakfast, check out from Hotel. Proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 117335.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n03 nights’ accommodation at Metro Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Novena or similar Singapore\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurants\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n\nWHAT’S MORE\n\xa0\n\n500 ml water bottle per day\n. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or local representative. (subject to minimum 20 customers). If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st November 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. VISA REQUIREMENTS: Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st November 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st November 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: General Info Currency used: Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) Currency used: Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Nov 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMS550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Dhamaka - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Kuala Lumpur and Singapore. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Petronas Twin Towers, the historic Batu Caves, the futuristic Gardens by the Bay, and the spectacular Marina Bay Sands. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic cable car rides, and exciting excursions to Sentosa Island and Universal Studios.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\nArrive Kuala Lumpur – Guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur\nWelcome to Malaysia. Upon arrival proceed to your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). In the afternoon, proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers.\nNOTE :\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.\nhttps://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Metro\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nDay excursion to Genting Highland - Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to the Sky way cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car. Visit Batu Caves', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Metro\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDay at Leisure or Visit Sunway Lagoon (Optional)\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast rest of the day is at leisure or explore Kuala Lumpur on your own or join us on an optional excursion to visit Sunway Lagoon.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Metro\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDrive to Singapore\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs).\nNotes:\xa0\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs. Link :\xa0 Prohibited and Controlled Goods \nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card via an application called as SG Arrival.\nLink: ICA | SG Arrival Card\nIt is highly advisable to carry an international activated mobile number & an international activated credit card.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS\xa0Novena\xa0or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour - Visit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Half Day Sentosa Tour (Optional)\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, Proceed for a guided city tour - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard Road, Photo stop at Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later we visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with the Jurassic World & Flower Dome.\nRest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on Half Day Sentosa tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS\xa0Novena\xa0or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium (Optional)\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, rest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on a visit to Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0IBIS\xa0Novena\xa0or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nFLY BACK\nToday after breakfast, check out from Hotel. Proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights’ accommodation at Metro Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Novena or similar Singapore\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n03 nights’ accommodation at Metro Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Novena or similar Singapore\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 117300.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights’ accommodation at Metro Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Novena or similar Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners a