d Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule. General Info: Currency used: Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) / Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST / Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Langkawi: Ride on Langkawi Cable Car I Visit Skybridge I See 3D Dome Cinema I Ride on Sky Rex I See 3D Art Museum Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Asia With Langkawi - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 9-day air-inclusive value tour covering Singapore, Langkawi, and Kuala Lumpur, complete with the assistance of a dedicated tour manager, visa and insurance services, four-star hotel accommodations on a bed-and-breakfast basis, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian meals. In Langkawi, travelers will experience the Langkawi Cable Car, the Skybridge, the 3D Dome Cinema, the Sky Rex ride, and the 3D Art Museum. The journey continues in Malaysia with a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and a day trip to Genting, while the Singapore leg features a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with the 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds experience, a trip to the Mandai Bird Paradise, and an exploration of Gardens by the Bay, including entrance to the Flower Dome and the Cloud Forest with its Jurassic World Exhibition.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\nArrive Into Langkawi\nWelcome to Langkawi, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the evening is at leisure to explore on your own.\n\xa0\nNOTE :\n\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. \nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card.\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/ main?registerMain\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Resort World\xa0or similar in Langkawi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour Of Langkawi\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed on a guided tour of Langkawi. Ride on the Langkawi Skycable car to 708 m above sea level to catch views of Langkawi town, the entire archipelago and Southern Thailand.On arrival Visit Skydome, Sky Bridge, Skyrex, 3D Art Langkawi, and more! Enjoy a fantastic view of Langkawi from the Sky Bridge.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Resort World\xa0or similar in Langkawi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\nFly to Kuala Lumpur Kuala Lumpur – Orientation Tour of Putrajaya - Guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur\n\xa0\nThis morning after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to the airport. Fly to Kuala Lumpur. Upon arrival proceed on an orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later check into your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). In the evening, proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day excursion to Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Sky way cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car. Visit Batu Caves', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nDay at Leisure or Visit Sunway Lagoon (Optional)\nToday after breakfast rest of the day is at leisure or explore Kuala Lumpur on your own or join us on an optional excursion to visit Sunway Lagoon.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDrive to Singapore - Guided City Tour - Visit Gardens by the Bay\xa0\n\xa0\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with the Jurassic World & Flower Dome followed by the Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card via an application called as SG Arrival.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn\xa0or similar Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park - Visit Sentosa Island by one way cable car\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island via a one-way cable car ride at Sentosa, Visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn\xa0or similar Singapore'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium (Optional) \n\xa0\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, rest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on a visit to S.E.A. Aquarium & Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn\xa0or similar Singapore'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly Black \nToday after breakfast, check out from Hotel. Proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n02 nights’ accommodation at Seri Pacific / Four points by Sheraton Chinatown / Mercure Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Copthorne Kings / Furama Riverfront / Aloft Hotel or Similar Singapore\n', '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n02 nights’ accommodation at Seri Pacific / Four points by Sheraton Chinatown / Mercure Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Copthorne Kings / Furama Riverfront / Aloft Hotel or Similar Singapore\n', '1': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 189100.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurants\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n', 'Breakfast Included', '\nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st June 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['LANGKAWI\n\nRide on Langkawi Cable Car\nVisit Skybridge\nSee 3D Dome Cinema\nRide on Sky Rex\xa0\nSee 3D Art Museum\xa0 \xa0\n\n\xa0\nKUALA LUMPUR\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit KL Tower Observatory\nVisit Chocolate Boutique\nGenting Highlands by 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\xa0\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\n\nMALACCA\n\nMalacca river cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\nSINGAPORE\xa0\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, 4D Marvel show & Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance to Wings of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\xa0\n', 'Langkawi:\xa0\n\nRide on Langkawi Cable Car\xa0\nVisit Skybridge\xa0\nSee 3D Dome Cinema\xa0\nRide on Sky Rex\xa0\nSee 3D Art Museum\n\n\xa0\nKuala Lumpur:\xa0\n\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Batu Caves\nGenting Highlands with 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park (Outdoor Park)\nVisit to Chocolate Boutique\n\n\xa0\nSingapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay – Entrance to Cloud Forest incl Jurassic World & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings of Time Show\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or local representative.\n(subject to minimum 20 customers). If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st\xa0December\xa0 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n500 ml water bottle per day\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\nMalaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival )\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\n\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop\ncoach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nWearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries.\nDownload Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash\n(THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info:\n\nCurrency used:\xa0Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) /\xa0Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD)\nTime difference:\xa0Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST /\xa0Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/MagicalAsiaWithLangkawi267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/Langkawi_Island_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/Langkawi-Cable-Car.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/kuala_Lumpur.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/7712_Genting_Highland_Cabe_Car_Malaysia753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/SunwayLagoonSingapore.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/Bird-Paradise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014472/itinerary/singapore3.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014466', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014466', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Asia -  April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 138331, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Asia - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day air-inclusive value tour covering the vibrant cities of Singapore and Kuala Lumpur. With the assistance of a dedicated tour manager throughout, this package includes visa, insurance, four-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, and specially curated Indian lunches and dinners. In Malaysia, travelers will experience a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and an exciting day trip to Genting. In Singapore, the itinerary features a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with the 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds experience, an exploration of Gardens by the Bay including the Flower Dome and the Cloud Forest with its Jurassic World Exhibition, and a visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'images': ['Putra_Pink_Mosque_753.jpg', 'Genting_Highland_7531.jpg', 'SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'SentosaIsland2.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'SingaporeCity753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 138331, 'thumbnailImage': 'MagicalAsia2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014466 is named 'Magical Asia -  April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Welcome To Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. Note : All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below. Https://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) - Batu Caves This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 138331.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n06 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. 500 ml water bottle per day Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Visa Requirements Malaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival ). Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Vis