le car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings of Time Show\n', 'PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n500 ml water bottle per day\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMalaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival )\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/MagicalAsia2671.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/Putra_Pink_Mosque_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/Genting_Highland_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/SentosaIsland2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014466/itinerary/SingaporeCity753.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014456', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014456', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Delights - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Johor Bahru', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 150661, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Delights - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore, Johor Bahru, and Kuala Lumpur. Accompanied by a dedicated tour manager, participants will enjoy four-star-plus hotel accommodations, visa and insurance assistance, and specially curated Indian meals. The itinerary features guided city tours of Kuala Lumpur and Singapore, a Malacca city tour, and an exciting day trip to Genting. Key highlights in Singapore include visits to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, Gardens by the Bay's Flower Dome and Cloud Forest with the Jurassic World Exhibition, Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium.", 'images': ['KualaLumpur1.jpg', 'BatuCaves.jpg', 'Putramosque753.jpg', '4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'Singapore_New.jpeg'], 'minimumPrice': 150661, 'thumbnailImage': 'Malaysia980.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['KidsFriendly', 'Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014456 is named 'Asian Delights - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory Welcome to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit the KL tower observatory. NOTE : Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card. All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below. https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Johor Bahru, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs. (https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods) All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 150661.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/ Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: General Info Currency Used : Malaysia : Malaysian Ringgit (Myr) Singapore : Singapore Dollar (Sgd) Time Difference: Malaysia & Singapore : 2 Hours And 30 Minutes Ahead Of Ist CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. Important Notes:Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Delights - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 7-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore, Johor Bahru, and Kuala Lumpur. Accompanied by a dedicated tour manager, participants will enjoy four-star-plus hotel accommodations, visa and insurance assistance, and specially curated Indian meals. The itinerary features guided city tours of Kuala Lumpur and Singapore, a Malacca city tour, and an exciting day trip to Genting. Key highlights in Singapore include visits to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, Gardens by the Bay's Flower Dome and Cloud Forest with the Jurassic World Exhibition, Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In\xa0 Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory\nWelcome to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening\xa0proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit \xa0the KL tower observatory. \nNOTE :\n\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card.\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.\n\nhttps://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain\xa0\n\n\n", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0 Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis morning\xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0 Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in\xa0Johar Bahru'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\xa0\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, \xa0check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed\xa0 for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition \xa0& Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At\nSingapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.\n(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio \nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/ Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/ Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 150700.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/ Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Kuala Lumpur:\n\nGuided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto Stop At Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Kl Tower Observatory\nVisit Chocolate Boutique\nGenting Highlands By 2 Ways Cable Car\nVisit Genting Sky World Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya\n\nMalacca:\n\nMalacca River Cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\nSingapore:\n\nGuided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens By The Bay\xa0 - Entrance To Cloud Forest With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car Ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance To Wings Of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': "General Info\nCurrency Used :\xa0\xa0\n\nMalaysia : Malaysian Ringgit (Myr)\xa0\nSingapore : Singapore Dollar\xa0 (Sgd)\xa0\n\nTime Difference:\xa0\n\nMalaysia & Singapore : 2 Hours And 30 Minutes Ahead Of Ist\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:Airline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/Malaysia980.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/KualaLumpur1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/BatuCaves.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014456/itinerary/Singapore_New.jpeg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014828', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014828', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Asia With Batam  (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Batam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Batam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Batam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["Luxury Stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa, Batam: Private Island: It occupies an entire tropical island, providing complete privacy and a secluded, crowd-free atmosphere. Dedicated Wellness Focus: The property features a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, and daily beachside yoga sessions. Kids' Club & Playground: A complimentary Westin Family Kids' Club offers children's yoga, nature walks, a dedicated pool, and safe playgrounds. Easy Singapore Access: Located on Nirup Island in Batam, can be reached by 2 ferries Singapore Harbour Bay – Batam – Nirup Island"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 163283, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Asia With Batam (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)' package is a 9-day tour covering Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and Batam. The itinerary features a luxury stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa on Batam, a private island resort that occupies an entire tropical island to provide complete privacy and a secluded, crowd-free atmosphere. Participants will enjoy a dedicated wellness focus with access to a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, and daily beachside yoga sessions, while families can take advantage of a complimentary Westin Family Kids' Club offering children's yoga, nature walks, a dedicated pool, and safe playgrounds. Additionally, travelers will benefit from easy Singapore access, as the resort is conveniently reached via two ferries from Singapore Harbour Bay to Batam and then to Nirup Island.", 'images': ['Putramosque753.jpg', '9955_Batu_Cave753.jpg', 'SunwayLagoon753.jpg', 'Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'BirdPark.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.avif', 'Batam7531.jpg', 'Batma753.jpg', 'Singapore business district iStock-564570852.avif'], 'minimumPrice': 163283, 'thumbnailImage': 'Batam2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['KidsFriendly', 'Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Luxury Escape', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014828 is named 'Magical Asia With Batam  (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive Kuala Lumpur – Orientation Tour of Putrajaya - Guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur Welcome to Malaysia. Upon arrival proceed on an orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later check into your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). In the evening, proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. NOTE : All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day excursion to Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Sky way cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car. Visit Batu Caves, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at Leisure or Visit Sunway Lagoon (Optional) Today after breakfast rest of the day is at leisure or explore Kuala Lumpur on your own or join us on an optional excursion to visit Sunway Lagoon., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive to Singapore - Guided City Tour - Visit Gardens by the Bay This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with the Jurassic World & Flower Dome followed by the Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods) All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card via an application called as SG Arrival. It is highly advisable to carry an international activated mobile number & an international activated credit card., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park - Visit Sentosa Island by one way cable car This morning after buffet breakfast, visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island via a one-way cable car ride at Sentosa, Visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, 4D Marvel show & Boat Ride Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium (Optional) This morning after buffet breakfast, rest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on a visit to S.E.A. Aquarium & Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Batam, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Ferry To Nirup Island, Batam (Indonesia) – Day At Leisure This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to Ferry Terminal for your ferry to Harbour Bay Batam, from there take a connecting ferry to Nirup Island. On arrival proceed to the hotel & check in. Rest of the day is at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Batam, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure. Spend rest of the day exploring activities at the resort on your own from the various optional tours available on attractive offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Batam, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ferry To Singapore - End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and take the ferry connecting to Harbour Bay Batam proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 163283.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights’ accommodation at Seri Pacific / Four points by Sheraton Chinatown / Mercure Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Copthorne Kings / Furama Riverfront / Aloft Hotel or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel Grand Lagoi Bintan or similar in Bintan\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurants\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or local representative. (subject to minimum 20 customers). If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st April 2026 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. 500 ml water bottle per day Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Malaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival ) Indonesian Visa on arrival (Indonesia Visa on arrival fees are to be paid by the guests at the time of immigration). Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. General Info CURRENCY USED : MALAYSIA : Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) SINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar (SGD) INDONESIA : Indonesian Rupiya (IDR) TIME DIFFERENCE: MALAYSIA / SINGAPORE / INDONESIA : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs Important Notes:Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: Luxury Stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa, Batam: Private Island: It occupies an entire tropical island, providing complete privacy and a secluded, crowd-free atmosphere. Dedicated Wellness Focus: The property features a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, and daily beachside yoga sessions. Kids' Club & Playground: A complimentary Westin Family Kids' Club offers children's yoga, nature walks, a dedicated pool, and safe playgrounds. Easy Singapore Access: Located on Nirup Island in Batam, can be reached by 2 ferries Singapore Harbour Bay – Batam – Nirup Island.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Asia With Batam (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)' package is a 9-day tour covering Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and Batam. The itinerary features a luxury stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa on Batam, a private island resort that occupies an entire tropical island to provide complete privacy and a secluded, crowd-free atmosphere. Participants will enjoy a dedicated wellness focus with access to a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, and daily beachside yoga sessions, while families can take advantage of a complimentary Westin Family Kids' Club offering children's yoga, nature walks, a dedicated pool, and safe playgrounds. Additionally, travelers will benefit from easy Singapore access, as the resort is conveniently reached via two ferries from Singapore Harbour Bay to Batam and then to Nirup Island.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive Kuala Lumpur – Orientation Tour of Putrajaya - Guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur\nWelcome to Malaysia. Upon arrival proceed on an orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later check into your hotel (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). In the evening, proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers.\n\xa0\nNOTE :\n\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain\n", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day excursion to Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Sky way cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car. Visit Batu Caves', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay at Leisure or Visit Sunway Lagoon (Optional)\nToday after breakfast rest of the day is at leisure or explore Kuala Lumpur on your own or join us on an optional excursion to visit Sunway Lagoon.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive to Singapore - Guided City Tour - Visit Gardens by the Bay\xa0\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with the Jurassic World & Flower Dome followed by the Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\nNotes: \n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At\xa0Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card via an application called as SG Arrival.\nIt is highly advisable to carry an international activated mobile number & an international activated credit card.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park - Visit Sentosa Island by one way cable car\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island via a one-way cable car ride at Sentosa, Visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, 4D Marvel show & Boat Ride Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium (Optional) \nThis morning after buffet breakfast, rest of the day is at leisure or explore Singapore on your own or join us on a visit to S.E.A. Aquarium & Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFerry To Nirup Island, Batam (Indonesia) – Day At Leisure\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to Ferry Terminal for your ferry to Harbour Bay Batam, from there take a connecting ferry to Nirup Island. On arrival proceed to the hotel & check in. Rest of the day is at leisure.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure. Spend rest of the day exploring activities at the resort on your own from the various optional tours available on attractive offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFerry To Singapore - End Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out and take the ferry connecting to Harbour Bay Batam\xa0 proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Seri Pacific / Four points by Sheraton Chinatown / Mercure Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Copthorne Kings / Furama Riverfront / Aloft Hotel or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel Grand Lagoi Bintan or similar in Bintan\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Seri Pacific / Four points by Sheraton Chinatown / Mercure Hotel or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Copthorne Kings / Furama Riverfront / Aloft Hotel or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel Grand Lagoi Bintan or similar in Bintan\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 163300.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurants\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', '\nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st June 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Kuala Lumpur:\xa0\n\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya\nGuided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto Stop At Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Batu Caves\nGenting Highlands With 2 Ways Cable Car\nVisit Genting Sky World Theme Park\xa0\nVisit To Chocolate Boutique\n\nSingapore\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens By The Bay – Entrance To Cloud Forest Incl Jurassic World & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car Ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, 4d Marvel Show & Boat Ride\xa0\nWings Of Time Show\n\n\xa0\nBatam – Indonesia\xa0\n\nExperience Some Relaxing Free Time And Explore Nirup Island In Batam\xa0\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'KUALA LUMPUR\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit KL Tower Observatory\nVisit Chocolate Boutique\nGenting Highlands by 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\n\n\xa0\nMALACCA\n\nMalacca river cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\n\xa0\nSINGAPORE\xa0\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, 4D Marvel show & Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance to Wings of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\xa0\n\n\xa0\nBINTAN – INDONESIA\xa0\n\nExperience some relaxing free time and explore the Bintan Islands\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or local representative.\n(subject to minimum 20 customers).\xa0\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st April 2026\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n500 ml water bottle per day\xa0\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\nMalaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival )\nIndonesian Visa on arrival\xa0\n\n(Indonesia Visa on arrival fees are to be paid by the guests at the time of immigration)\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': "Note:\xa0Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\nCURRENCY USED :\xa0\xa0\n\nMALAYSIA : Malaysian Ringgit (MYR)\xa0\nSINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar\xa0 (SGD)\xa0\nINDONESIA : Indonesian Rupiya (IDR)\n\nTIME DIFFERENCE:\xa0\n\nMALAYSIA / SINGAPORE / INDONESIA\xa0 : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:Airline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/Batam2671.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/9955_Batu_Cave753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/SunwayLagoon753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/BirdPark.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/Batam7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/Batma753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014828/itinerary/Singapore_business_district_iStock-564570852.avif']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014736', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014736', 'availableMonths': ['may_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Delights - Senior Citizen Special', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Johor Bahru', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 star plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johor Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Malaysia : Malacca city Tour | Genting Day Trip | Putrajaya Tour Singapore: Visit Gardens by the Bay | Visit Mandai Bird Paradise | Visit Singapore Oceanarium Two Professional Tour Managers travelling on this tour. Travel Insurance upto age of 70yrs"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 145102, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Delights - Senior Citizen Special' package is a 7-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and Johor Bahru. This specially curated itinerary features comfortable stays in four-star plus hotels, including a stay in Johor Bahru, and provides the dedicated assistance of two professional tour managers throughout the journey. Travelers will enjoy curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners, along with complimentary tea, coffee, and ice cream at select locations. Key activities include a Malacca city tour, a Genting day trip, and a Putrajaya tour in Malaysia, as well as visits to Singapore's iconic Gardens by the Bay, Mandai Bird Paradise, and the Singapore Oceanarium. The package also conveniently includes visa processing and travel insurance for participants up to 70 years of age.", 'images': ['KualaLumpur1.jpg', 'BatuCaves.jpg', 'Putramosque753.jpg', '4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'Singapore_New.jpeg'], 'minimumPrice': 145102, 'thumbnailImage': 'Malaysia980.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family', 'KidsFriendly'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014736 is named 'Asian Delights - Senior Citizen Special' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory Welcome to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit the KL tower observatory. NOTE : Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit carJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard d. All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.check-in time is 1500 hrs. https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion To Genting Highland - Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Upon arrival, free time to explore the world-famous entertainment capital. on own, one can visit the Indoor or Outdoor theme park or enjoy at Casino. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Johor Bahru, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs. (https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods) All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium, where you can explore a fascinating marine world and diverse aquatic exhibits., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 145102.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown or similar in Kuala Lumpur \n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of 2 professional & multilingual Tour Manager/ local representative. (subject to minimum 15 customers) A friendly and multilingual Tour Manager accompanies the tour when the group size is 15 or more passengers. For less than 15 passengers, the tour operates on Seat in Coach (SIC)/ Free independent Tour (FIT) basis with a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative providing remote support for daily coordination, briefings, reconfirmations, and assistance. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to departure. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st March 2026. Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 70 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st March 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: Compulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 5 per person per day The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st March 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leads to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink are not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips for guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. Meals other than what is mentioned in itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Wearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries. Download Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule. General Info: Currency used: Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) / Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST / Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 star plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johor Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Malaysia : Malacca city Tour | Genting Day Trip | Putrajaya Tour Singapore: Visit Gardens by the Bay | Visit Mandai Bird Paradise | Visit Singapore Oceanarium Two Professional Tour Managers travelling on this tour. Travel Insurance upto age of 70yrs.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZED990', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Delights - Senior Citizen Special' package is a 7-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and Johor Bahru. This specially curated itinerary features comfortable stays in four-star plus hotels, including a stay in Johor Bahru, and provides the dedicated assistance of two professional tour managers throughout the journey. Travelers will enjoy curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners, along with complimentary tea, coffee, and ice cream at select locations. Key activities include a Malacca city tour, a Genting day trip, and a Putrajaya tour in Malaysia, as well as visits to Singapore's iconic Gardens by the Bay, Mandai Bird Paradise, and the Singapore Oceanarium. The package also conveniently includes visa processing and travel insurance for participants up to 70 years of age.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In\xa0 Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory\nWelcome to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur along with photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit\xa0 the KL tower observatory.\n\xa0\nNOTE :\n\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit carJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard d.\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\n\nhttps://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain\xa0\n\n\n", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion To Genting Highland - Batu Caves\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Upon arrival, free time to explore the world-famous entertainment capital. on own, one can visit the Indoor or Outdoor theme park or enjoy at Casino. \xa0Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in\xa0Johar Bahru'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\xa0\xa0\nThis morning\xa0 after buffet breakfast, \xa0check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed\xa0 for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition\xa0 & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.\n(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium \nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium, where you can explore a fascinating marine world and diverse aquatic exhibits.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning\xa0 after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown or similar in Kuala Lumpur \n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown or similar in Kuala Lumpur \n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 145100.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown or similar in Kuala Lumpur \n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st March 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto Stop At Petronas Twin Tower\nGenting Highlands By 2 Ways Cable Car\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya\n\nMalacca\n\nMalacca River Cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\nSingapore\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens By The Bay\xa0 - Entrance To Cloud Forest With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car Ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance To Wings Of Time Show\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\xa0\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of 2 professional & multilingual Tour Manager/ local representative.\n(subject to minimum 15 customers)\nA friendly and multilingual Tour Manager accompanies the tour when the group size is 15 or more passengers. For less than 15 passengers, the tour operates on Seat in Coach (SIC)/ Free independent Tour (FIT) basis with a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative providing remote support for daily coordination, briefings, reconfirmations, and assistance. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to departure.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st\xa0 March 2026.\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 70 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st March 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nCompulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 5 per person per day\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st March 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leads to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink are not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips for guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc.\nMeals other than what is mentioned in itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\n\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop\ncoach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nWearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries.\nDownload Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash\n(THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info:\n\nCurrency used:\xa0Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) /\xa0Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD)\nTime difference:\xa0Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST /\xa0Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/Malaysia980.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/KualaLumpur1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/BatuCaves.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014736/itinerary/Singapore_New.jpeg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014829', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014829', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Delights With Batam (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Johor Bahru', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Batam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Batam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["Luxury Stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa, Batam: Private Island: It occupies an entire tropical island, providing complete privacy and a secluded, crowd-free atmosphere. Dedicated Wellness Focus: The property features a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, and daily beachside yoga sessions. Kids' Club & Playground: A complimentary Westin Family Kids' Club offers children's yoga, nature walks, a dedicated pool, and safe playgrounds. Easy Singapore Access: Located on Nirup Island in Batam, can be reached by 2 ferries Singapore Harbour Bay – Batam – Nirup Island Teh Tarik / Kopi / Kalapa Water at Batu Caves Teh Tarik / Coffee / Juice on the way to Singapore Ice Cream during Singapore City Tour Samosa & Masala Tea / Cold Drink in Sentosa 500 ml water bottle per day"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 193401, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Delights With Batam (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)' package is a 9-day tour covering Singapore, Batam, Kuala Lumpur, and Johor Bahru. The highlight of this itinerary is a luxury stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa, situated on a private island in Batam and accessible via a two-ferry journey from Singapore, which offers a secluded atmosphere, a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, beachside yoga, and a dedicated Westin Family Kids' Club. Throughout the journey, participants will enjoy guided experiences and delightful local treats, including Teh Tarik, Kopi, or Kalapa Water at Batu Caves, refreshing ice cream during the Singapore city tour, and samosas with masala tea or cold drinks in Sentosa, with daily bottled water provided for convenience.", 'images': ['KualaLumpur1.jpg', '7712_Genting_Highland_Cabe_Car_Malaysia753.jpg', 'Putramosque753.jpg', 'Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'Singapore7534.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'Batam7531.jpg', 'Batma753.jpg', 'SingaporeCityView753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 193401, 'thumbnailImage': 'SRP_KL.png', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family', 'KidsFriendly'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Luxury Escape', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014829 is named 'Asian Delights With Batam (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory Welcome To Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Along With Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. Visit The Kl Tower Observatory. Note : Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs. All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below. Https://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Johor Bahru, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya. Later Drive Towards Malacca. On Arrival Board The River Cruise And Visit The Maritime Museum. Later Drive Towards Johar Bahru And Check In To Your Hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs. (Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Proceed To Take A Ride On The Singapore Flyer, One Of The World’s Largest Observation Wheels. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, 4d Marvel Show & Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Vvisit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy The Rest Of The Day At Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Batam, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Ferry To Nirup Island, Batam (Indonesia) – Day At Leisure This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Ferry Terminal For Your Ferry To Harbour Bay Batam, From There Take A Connecting Ferry To Nirup Island. On Arrival Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Batam, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Activities At The Resort On Your Own From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ferry To Singapore - End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Take The Ferry Connecting To Harbour Bay Batam Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 193401.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st April 2026 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements : Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Malaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival ) Indonesian Visa on arrival (Indonesia Visa on arrival fees are to be paid by the guests at the time of immigration). Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Wearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries. Download Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule. General Info: Currency used: Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) / Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST / Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST. Highlights of the package: Luxury Stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa, Batam: Private Island: It occupies an entire tropical island, providing complete privacy and a secluded, crowd-free atmosphere. Dedicated Wellness Focus: The property features a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, and daily beachside yoga sessions. Kids' Club & Playground: A complimentary Westin Family Kids' Club offers children's yoga, nature walks, a dedicated pool, and safe playgrounds. Easy Singapore Access: Located on Nirup Island in Batam, can be reached by 2 ferries Singapore Harbour Bay – Batam – Nirup Island Teh Tarik / Kopi / Kalapa Water at Batu Caves Teh Tarik / Coffee / Juice on the way to Singapore Ice Cream during Singapore City Tour Samosa & Masala Tea / Cold Drink in Sentosa 500 ml water bottle per day.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZPI550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Delights With Batam (The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa)' package is a 9-day tour covering Singapore, Batam, Kuala Lumpur, and Johor Bahru. The highlight of this itinerary is a luxury stay at The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa, situated on a private island in Batam and accessible via a two-ferry journey from Singapore, which offers a secluded atmosphere, a signature Heavenly Spa, panoramic fitness studios, beachside yoga, and a dedicated Westin Family Kids' Club. Throughout the journey, participants will enjoy guided experiences and delightful local treats, including Teh Tarik, Kopi, or Kalapa Water at Batu Caves, refreshing ice cream during the Singapore city tour, and samosas with masala tea or cold drinks in Sentosa, with daily bottled water provided for convenience.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory\nWelcome To Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Along With Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. Visit \xa0The Kl Tower Observatory.\xa0\n\xa0\nNote :\n\nJoining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs.\xa0\nAll Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card\nAll Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below.\nHttps://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain\n", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya. Later Drive Towards Malacca. On Arrival Board The River Cruise And Visit The Maritime Museum. Later Drive Towards Johar Bahru And Check In To Your Hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, \xa0Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\xa0\n\xa0\nNotes:\n\nKindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.\n(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods)\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Proceed To Take A Ride On The Singapore Flyer, One Of The World’s Largest Observation Wheels. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, 4d Marvel Show & Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio \nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Vvisit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy The Rest Of The Day At Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFerry To Nirup Island, Batam (Indonesia) – Day At Leisure\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Ferry Terminal For Your Ferry To Harbour Bay Batam, From There Take A Connecting Ferry To Nirup Island. On Arrival Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Activities At The Resort On Your Own From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFerry To Singapore - End Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Take The Ferry Connecting To Harbour Bay Batam\xa0 Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 193400.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront or Similar Singapore\n02 nights’ accommodation at Hotel The Westin Nirup Island Resort & Spa or similar in Nirup Island, Batam\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['\nTransfer and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto Stop At Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Kl Tower Observatory\nVisit Chocolate Boutique\nGenting Highlands By 2 Ways Cable Car\nVisit Genting Sky World Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya\n\nMalacca\n\nMalacca River Cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\nSingapore\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens By The Bay - Entrance To Cloud Forest With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car Ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, 4d Marvel Show & Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance To Wings Of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\n\nBatam – Indonesia\xa0\n\nExperience Some Relaxing Free Time And Explore Nirup Island In Batam\xa0\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n<li>Airfare not included for joining direct passengers</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st April 2026\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements :\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\nMalaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival )\nIndonesian Visa on arrival\xa0\n\n(Indonesia Visa on arrival fees are to be paid by the guests at the time of immigration)\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\n\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop\ncoach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nWearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries.\nDownload Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash\n(THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info:\n\nCurrency used:\xa0Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) /\xa0Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD)\nTime difference:\xa0Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST /\xa0Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/SRP_KL.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/KualaLumpur1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/7712_Genting_Highland_Cabe_Car_Malaysia753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/Singapore7534.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/Batam7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/Batma753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014829/itinerary/SingaporeCityView753.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014457', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014457', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Delights With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Johor Bahru', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 200859, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Delights With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 10-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Kuala Lumpur, Singapore, Johor Bahru, and a Genting Dream Cruise. Guided by a professional tour manager, travelers will enjoy four-star-plus hotel accommodations, visa and insurance services, and specially curated Indian meals. The action-packed itinerary includes guided city tours of Kuala Lumpur and Singapore, a Malacca city tour, and a day trip to Genting. Key highlights in Singapore feature visits to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium, with delightful treats like tea, coffee, and ice cream provided during select sightseeing excursions.", 'images': ['KualaLumpur.jpg', 'BatuCaves.jpg', 'PutraMosquePutrajayaMalaysiashutterstock_565942705.jpg', '4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'SeaAquarium.jpg', 'ResortWorldCruise753.jpg', 'Genting_Dream_Cruise_753.jpg', 'Genting_Dream_Cruise2_753.jpg', 'Singaporesh.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 200859, 'thumbnailImage': 'Singapore2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['KidsFriendly', 'Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014457 is named 'Asian Delights With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory Welcome to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit the KL tower observatory. NOTE : Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card. All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below. https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Johor Bahru, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this afternoon proceed for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). NOTES: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs. (https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods) All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise This morning after breakfast, check-out and proceed to Cruise terminal. Day onboard cruise with lunch and Dinner - Explore onboard activities & entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day onboard cruise - Explore onboard activities & entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day onboard cruise - Explore onboard activities & entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 200859.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n06 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements: Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs General Info CURRENCY USED : MALAYSIA : Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) SINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar (SGD) TIME DIFFERENCE: MALAYSIA & SINGAPORE : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST Important Notes:Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZEC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Delights With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 10-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Kuala Lumpur, Singapore, Johor Bahru, and a Genting Dream Cruise. Guided by a professional tour manager, travelers will enjoy four-star-plus hotel accommodations, visa and insurance services, and specially curated Indian meals. The action-packed itinerary includes guided city tours of Kuala Lumpur and Singapore, a Malacca city tour, and a day trip to Genting. Key highlights in Singapore feature visits to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium, with delightful treats like tea, coffee, and ice cream provided during select sightseeing excursions.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In\xa0 Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory\nWelcome to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. \xa0Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit \xa0the KL tower observatory.\n\xa0\nNOTE :\n\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card.\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.\n\nhttps://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain\xa0\n\n\n", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum\nThis morning\xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, \xa0check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this afternoon proceed\xa0 for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition \xa0& Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNOTES:\xa0\n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At\nSingapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.\n(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio \nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nThis morning\xa0after breakfast, check-out and proceed to Cruise terminal.\nDay onboard cruise with lunch and Dinner - Explore onboard activities & entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay onboard cruise - Explore onboard activities & entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay onboard cruise - Explore onboard activities & entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'c