meals, entertainment & activities.\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements:\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': "\xa0Hotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\nCURRENCY USED :\xa0\xa0\n\nMALAYSIA : Malaysian Ringgit (MYR)\xa0\nSINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar\xa0 (SGD)\n\nTIME DIFFERENCE:\xa0\n\nMALAYSIA & SINGAPORE : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:Airline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/Singapore2671.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/KualaLumpur.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/BatuCaves.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/PutraMosquePutrajayaMalaysiashutterstock_565942705.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/SeaAquarium.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/ResortWorldCruise753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/Genting_Dream_Cruise_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/Genting_Dream_Cruise2_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014457/itinerary/Singaporesh.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014467', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014467', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Asia With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Genting Dream Cruise', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise Cruise - Sail on Genting Dream Cruise"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 166543, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Asia With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 10-day air-inclusive value tour covering Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and a sailing experience on the Genting Dream Cruise, all accompanied by a dedicated tour manager. This comprehensive package features four-star hotel accommodations with daily breakfast, visa and insurance coverage, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners. Key activities in Malaysia include a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and a day trip to Genting Highlands, while Singapore highlights feature a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with a 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds experience, entry to the Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest with the Jurassic World Exhibition and Flower Dome, and a visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise, all complemented by a scenic cruise on the Genting Dream.", 'images': ['Putra_Pink_Mosque_753.jpg', 'Genting_Highland_7531.jpg', 'SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'SentosaIsland.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'SingaporeCity753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 166543, 'thumbnailImage': 'MagicalAsiaWithCruise2678.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Trending Now', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014467 is named 'Magical Asia With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Welcome To Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. Note : All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below. Https://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) - Batu Caves This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check-Out And Proceed To Cruise Terminal. Day Onboard Cruise With Lunch And Dinner - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Genting Dream Cruise Day Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Genting Dream Cruise, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 166543.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n, \n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental /\xa0 Trigo\xa0 or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen/ Hilton Garden Inn\xa0 or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n06 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. 500 ml of water per day Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Visa Requirements: Malaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival ). Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise Cruise - Sail on Genting Dream Cruise.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDC550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Asia With Cruise - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 10-day air-inclusive value tour covering Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and a sailing experience on the Genting Dream Cruise, all accompanied by a dedicated tour manager. This comprehensive package features four-star hotel accommodations with daily breakfast, visa and insurance coverage, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners. Key activities in Malaysia include a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and a day trip to Genting Highlands, while Singapore highlights feature a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with a 5-in-1 Madame Tussauds experience, entry to the Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest with the Jurassic World Exhibition and Flower Dome, and a visit to the Mandai Bird Paradise, all complemented by a scenic cruise on the Genting Dream.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nWelcome To Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. \xa0\n\xa0\nNote :\nAll Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below.\nHttps://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) -\xa0 Batu Caves\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0 ', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional)\nThis Morning\xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\xa0\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, \xa0Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed\xa0 For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition\xa0 & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods)\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park –\xa0 Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers \xa0(Optional)\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nThis Morning\xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Check-Out And Proceed To Cruise Terminal.\nDay Onboard Cruise With Lunch And Dinner - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise\xa0'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise\xa0'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGenting Dream Cruise\nDay Onboard Cruise - Explore Onboard Activities & Entertainment.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard Genting Dream Cruise\xa0'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n', '\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental /\xa0 Trigo\xa0 or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen/ Hilton Garden Inn\xa0 or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n', '1': '\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental /\xa0 Trigo\xa0 or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen/ Hilton Garden Inn\xa0 or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 166500.0, 'hotels': ['\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental /\xa0 Trigo\xa0 or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen/ Hilton Garden Inn\xa0 or similar in Singapore\n03 Nights onboard Genting Dream Cruise (Inside Cabin)\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n06 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nFull board meal plan on Cruise\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Kuala\xa0Lumpur\n\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Batu Caves\nGenting Highlands with 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park (Outdoor Park)\nVisit to Chocolate Boutique\n\n\xa0\nSingapore\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings of Time Show\n', 'PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n500 ml of water per day\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements:\n\nMalaysia Visa Free entry ( Visa on arrival )\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/MagicalAsiaWithCruise2678.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/Putra_Pink_Mosque_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/Genting_Highland_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/SentosaIsland.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/GentingDreamCruise7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014467/itinerary/SingaporeCity753.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014463', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014463', 'availableMonths': ['january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Delights With Langkawi - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Langkawi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Langkawi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Johor Bahru', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Langkawi: Ride on Langkawi Cable Car I Visit Skybridge I See 3D Dome Cinema I Ride on Sky Rex I See 3D Art Museum Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 220743, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Delights With Langkawi - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 9-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore, Langkawi, Johor Bahru, Kuala Lumpur, and Malacca. Guided by a professional tour manager, participants will stay in four-star-plus hotels on a bed-and-breakfast basis and enjoy specially curated Indian meals alongside complimentary treats like tea, coffee, and ice cream. The itinerary features thrilling experiences in Langkawi, including the Langkawi Cable Car, Skybridge, 3D Dome Cinema, Sky Rex, and the 3D Art Museum. In Malaysia, guests will enjoy guided tours of Kuala Lumpur and Malacca, as well as a day trip to Genting. The Singapore leg of the journey offers a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and visits to Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium.", 'images': ['Langkawi_Island_753.jpg', 'Langkawi-Cable-Car.jpg', 'kuala_Lumpur.jpg', '7712_Genting_Highland_Cabe_Car_Malaysia753.jpg', 'Malaccarivercruise.jpeg', '4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'Bird-Paradise.jpg', 'UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'Singaporemerlionpark753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 220743, 'thumbnailImage': 'Langkawi4567.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'KidsFriendly', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014463 is named 'Asian Delights With Langkawi - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Langkawi, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive Into Langkawi Welcome to Langkawi, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the evening is at leisure to explore on your own. NOTE : Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card. All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Langkawi, Meals: Breakfast, and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour Of Langkawi This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed on a guided tour of Langkawi. Ride on the Langkawi Skycable car to 708 m above sea level to catch views of Langkawi town, the entire archipelago and Southern Thailand.On arrival Visit Skydome, Sky Bridge, Skyrex, 3D Art Langkawi, and more! Enjoy a fantastic view of Langkawi from the Sky Bridge., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly To Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory This morning after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to the airport. Fly to Kuala Lumpur. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit the KL tower observatory., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Johor Bahru, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on an Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs. (https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods) All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable CarThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 220743.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. General Info CURRENCY USED : MALAYSIA : Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) SINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar (SGD) TIME DIFFERENCE: MALAYSIA & SINGAPORE : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs Important Notes:Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, at certain sightseeing’s Langkawi: Ride on Langkawi Cable Car I Visit Skybridge I See 3D Dome Cinema I Ride on Sky Rex I See 3D Art Museum Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDL550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Delights With Langkawi - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 9-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Singapore, Langkawi, Johor Bahru, Kuala Lumpur, and Malacca. Guided by a professional tour manager, participants will stay in four-star-plus hotels on a bed-and-breakfast basis and enjoy specially curated Indian meals alongside complimentary treats like tea, coffee, and ice cream. The itinerary features thrilling experiences in Langkawi, including the Langkawi Cable Car, Skybridge, 3D Dome Cinema, Sky Rex, and the 3D Art Museum. In Malaysia, guests will enjoy guided tours of Kuala Lumpur and Malacca, as well as a day trip to Genting. The Singapore leg of the journey offers a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and visits to Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\nArrive Into Langkawi\nWelcome to Langkawi, Malaysia. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the evening is at leisure to explore on your own.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nNOTE :\n\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. \nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card.\nAll Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Resort World\xa0or similar in Langkawi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour Of Langkawi\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed on a guided tour of Langkawi. Ride on the Langkawi Skycable car \xa0to 708 m above sea level to catch views of Langkawi town, the entire archipelago and Southern Thailand.On arrival Visit Skydome, Sky Bridge, Skyrex, 3D Art Langkawi, and more! Enjoy a fantastic view of Langkawi from the Sky Bridge.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Resort World\xa0or similar in Langkawi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nFly To Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to the airport. Fly to Kuala Lumpur. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this\xa0evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit \xa0the KL tower observatory.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) & Batu Caves\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on an Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\xa0\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, \xa0check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed\xa0 for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.\n(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable CarThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio \nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 220700.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights’ accommodation at Resort World Langkawi or similar in Langkawi\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Furama Riverfront/Hotel Orchard Rendezvous\xa0or Similar in Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nTransfer and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'Langkawi:\n\nRide on Langkawi Cable Car\nVisit Skybridge\nSee 3D Dome Cinema\nRide on Sky Rex\xa0\nSee 3D Art Museum\xa0 \xa0\n\n\xa0\nKuala Lumpur:\n\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit KL Tower Observatory\nVisit Chocolate Boutique\nGenting Highlands by 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\xa0\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\n\nMalacca:\n\nMalacca river cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\nSingapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance to Wings of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n<li>Airfare not included for joining direct passengers</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': "Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\nCURRENCY USED :\xa0\xa0\n\nMALAYSIA : Malaysian Ringgit (MYR)\xa0\nSINGAPORE : Singapore Dollar (SGD)\n\nTIME DIFFERENCE:\xa0\n\nMALAYSIA & SINGAPORE : 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notes:Airline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E - cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/Langkawi4567.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/Langkawi_Island_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/Langkawi-Cable-Car.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/kuala_Lumpur.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/7712_Genting_Highland_Cabe_Car_Malaysia753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/Malaccarivercruise.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/Bird-Paradise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/UniversalStudiosSingapore.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014463/itinerary/Singaporemerlionpark753.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014455', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014455', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Asian Extravaganza - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Johor Bahru', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai MassageI Guided City Tour of Bangkok | Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise. Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium"], 'pdfName': 'PKG009482_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 189763, 'packageSummary': "The 'Asian Extravaganza - April 2026 To March 2027' package is an 11-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Pattaya, Singapore, Bangkok, Kuala Lumpur, and Johor Bahru. Guided by a professional tour manager, participants will enjoy stays in four-star-plus hotels, visa and insurance coverage, and specially curated Indian meals. The action-packed itinerary features a traditional Thai massage, a visit to Nong Nooch Village, a guided city tour of Bangkok, and a scenic dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River in Thailand. In Malaysia, travelers will embark on guided tours of Kuala Lumpur and Malacca, as well as a day trip to Genting. The Singapore leg of the journey offers a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and visits to Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium, with delightful treats like tea, coffee, ice cream, and coconut water provided at select sights.", 'images': ['AlcazarshowPattayaThailandshutterstock_45747421.jpg', 'coralisland2.jpg', 'Wat_TraimitNew.jpg', 'SafariWorldBangkok.jpg', 'kuala_Lumpur.jpg', 'BatuCaves1.jpg', 'Putramosque753.jpg', '4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'SeaAquarium.jpg', 'Singapore_New.jpeg'], 'minimumPrice': 189763, 'thumbnailImage': 'Singaporeskyline_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['KidsFriendly', 'Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Trending Now', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014455 is named 'Asian Extravaganza - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Pattaya, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show Welcome to Bangkok, Thailand. Upon arrival, proceed to Pattaya & Check into your hotel. Rest of the day is at leisure. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening enjoy the Alcazar Show. NOTE All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. All Guests have to fill up Thai Digital Arrival Card via the below link. https://tdac.immigration.go.th/arrival-card/#/home, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pattaya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes) This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed for an exciting tour of the Coral Island (subject to weather condition) by speedboat. Take a glass bottom boat ride. You will have free time to enjoy water-sports activities - Para sailing, Under water walk, banana boat ride, Jet Ski on your own.( Kindly note : Above mentioned watersport activities are not a part of our Tour Program. Incase you plan to undertake any of the above activities you need to book them directly at the counter.) Return to the hotel. Later proceed to Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy the Thai Cultural Show & the Elephant Show in Nong Nooch village. Later experience Traditional Thai message. Note: For activities at Coral island, it is important that guests are physically fit to travel in speed boats (As we need to Embark & Disembark from the speed boat on floating pontoons & Excursion to Coral Island does not have wheelchair accessibility)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping This morning after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to Bangkok. Visit the Gems Gallery. Upon arrival at Bangkok proceed on a guided city tour alongwith visits to Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) followed by free time for shopping., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Safari World & Marine Park – Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Safari World & Marine Park - famous for it Open Zoo, wildlife & various shows. Later this evening enjoy the Chao Phraya dinner cruise., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly To Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory This morning after breakfast check out & proceed to the airport. Fly to Kuala Lumpur. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit the KL tower observatory. NOTE : All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below. https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) - Batu Caves This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Johor Bahru, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods) All Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 189763.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights accommodation at A- One Hotel Bangkok / Grand Howard Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown /\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Wearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries. Download Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule. General Info: Currency used: Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) / Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD) Time difference: Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST / Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Premium Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4 Star Plus Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Stay at Johar Bahru Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Tea, Coffee, Ice Cream, Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai MassageI Guided City Tour of Bangkok | Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise. Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur |Malacca city Tour I Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 4 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise I Visit Singapore Flyer I Visit Universal Studios I Visit Singapore Oceanarium.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Asian Extravaganza - April 2026 To March 2027' package is an 11-day premium air-inclusive tour covering Pattaya, Singapore, Bangkok, Kuala Lumpur, and Johor Bahru. Guided by a professional tour manager, participants will enjoy stays in four-star-plus hotels, visa and insurance coverage, and specially curated Indian meals. The action-packed itinerary features a traditional Thai massage, a visit to Nong Nooch Village, a guided city tour of Bangkok, and a scenic dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River in Thailand. In Malaysia, travelers will embark on guided tours of Kuala Lumpur and Malacca, as well as a day trip to Genting. The Singapore leg of the journey offers a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and visits to Mandai Bird Paradise, the Singapore Flyer, Universal Studios, and the Singapore Oceanarium, with delightful treats like tea, coffee, ice cream, and coconut water provided at select sights.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show\nWelcome to Bangkok, Thailand. Upon arrival, proceed to Pattaya & Check into your hotel. Rest of the day is at leisure. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening enjoy the Alcazar Show.\n\xa0\nNOTE\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\nAll Guests have to fill up Thai Digital Arrival Card via the below link.\n\nhttps://tdac.immigration.go.th/arrival-card/#/home\xa0\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel M or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes)\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed for an exciting tour of the Coral Island (subject to weather condition) by speedboat. Take a glass bottom boat ride. You will have free time to enjoy water-sports activities - \xa0Para sailing, Under water walk, banana boat ride, Jet Ski on your own.( Kindly note : Above mentioned watersport activities are not a part of our Tour Program. Incase you plan to undertake any of the above activities you need to book them directly at the counter.) \xa0Return to the hotel. Later proceed to Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy the Thai Cultural Show & the Elephant Show in Nong Nooch village. Later experience Traditional Thai message.\nNote:\n\nFor activities at Coral island, it is important that guests are physically fit to travel in speed boats (As we need to Embark & Disembark from the speed boat on floating pontoons & Excursion to Coral Island does not have wheelchair accessibility).\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel M or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple\xa0 & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to Bangkok. Visit the Gems Gallery. Upon arrival at Bangkok proceed on a guided city tour alongwith visits to Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) followed by free time for shopping.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel A-One Bangkok / Grand Howard Hotel or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park – Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Safari World & Marine Park - famous for it Open Zoo, wildlife & various shows. Later this evening enjoy the Chao Phraya dinner cruise.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel A-One Bangkok / Grand Howard Hotel or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nFly To Kuala Lumpur - Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur - Visit Kl Tower Observatory\nThis morning\xa0after breakfast check out & proceed to the airport. Fly to Kuala Lumpur. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening\xa0proceed for a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur alongwith photo stops at Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & the Petronas Twin Towers. Visit the KL tower observatory.\nNOTE : All Guest have to fill up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card via the link given below.\nhttps://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main?registerMain\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown\xa0/\xa0 Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur\xa0or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) -\xa0 Batu Caves\nThis morning\xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, proceed to the Skyway cable car station for a ride up to Genting Highlands. Visit the Skyworld Theme Park. Later take a return cable car to the Skyway cable car station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Four points by Sheraton Chinatown /\xa0\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation Tour Of Putrajaya - Drive To Malacca - Malacca River Cruise - Visit Maritime Museum\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed on Orientation tour of Putrajaya. Later drive towards Malacca. On arrival board the river cruise and visit the maritime museum. Later drive towards Johar Bahru and check in to your hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in\xa0Johar Bahru'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, check out & drive to Singapore. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel & check in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Proceed for a guided city tour of Singapore - drive pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later this evening visit Gardens By the Bay - Visit the Cloud Forest Dome with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome followed by Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly take a note of prohibited items that are not to be carried in Singapore. At Singapore Immigration all bags will be scanned and checked before customs and immigration. No trolleys or Porters are available at this point & every guest needs to hand carry luggage through Singapore Customs.(https:// www.customs.gov.sg/individuals/going-throughcustoms/arrival/prohibited-and- controlled- goods)\nAll Guests have to fill up Singapore Landing card on SG Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Singapore Flyer - Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Mandai Bird Paradise, home to over 5,000 birds across 400 species, making it one of the largest bird parks in the world. Proceed to take a ride on the Singapore Flyer, one of the world’s largest observation wheels. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island by a one-way cable car ride. On arrival at Sentosa Island - visit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later this evening enjoy the spectacular Wings of Time show -a dazzling display of water, laser, and fire effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium - Visit Universal Studio \nThis morning\xa0after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Singapore Oceanarium & Universal Studios. Enjoy the rest of the day at Universal Studios.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights accommodation at A- One Hotel Bangkok / Grand Howard Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown /\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights accommodation at A- One Hotel Bangkok / Grand Howard Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown /\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'TH', 'countryName': 'Thailand', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Premium', 'price': 189800.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights accommodation at A- One Hotel Bangkok / Grand Howard Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n02 nights’ accommodation at Four points by Sheraton Chinatown /\xa0Royale Chulan Kuala Lumpur or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n01 night’ accommodation at Trinidad Suites Puteri or similar in Johar Bahru\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Furama Riverfront\xa0/ Orchard Rendezvous Hotel\xa0or Similar Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n08 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches (includes 02 Lunch Coupons)\n10 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st\xa0December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', 'Pattaya:\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBangkok:\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park\xa0\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n\n\xa0\nKuala\xa0Lumpur:\n\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit KL Tower Observatory\nVisit Chocolate Boutique\nGenting Highlands by 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\xa0\nVisit Batu Caves\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\n\n\xa0\nMalacca:\n\nMalacca river cruise\nVisit Maritime Museum\n\n\xa0\nSingapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Singapore Flyer\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nEntrance to Wings of Time Show\nVisit Universal Studios\nVisit Singapore Oceanarium\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st April 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items – E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-andprohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\n\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php?ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. ( Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time 1500 hrs; Standard check out time 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room’s requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop\ncoach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nWearing mask is mandatory in these foreign countries.\nDownload Morchana , MySejahtera App & Trace Together App in your mobile devices before your tour & register on both Applications.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing &inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men – Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash\n(THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info:\n\nCurrency used:\xa0Thailand: Thai Baht (THB) / Malaysia: Malaysian Ringgit (MYR) /\xa0Singapore: Singapore Dollar (SGD)\nTime difference:\xa0Thailand–1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST /\xa0Malaysia & Singapore - 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/Singaporeskyline_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/AlcazarshowPattayaThailandshutterstock_45747421.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/coralisland2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/Wat_TraimitNew.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/SafariWorldBangkok.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/kuala_Lumpur.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/BatuCaves1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/4596_Gardens_By_the_bay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/Sentosa_Island_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/SeaAquarium.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014455/itinerary/Singapore_New.jpeg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014465', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014465', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Juice and Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai MassageI Guided City Tour of Bangkok | Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise. Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 158667, 'packageSummary': "The 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027' is an 11-day package covering Kuala Lumpur, Singapore, Bangkok, and Pattaya. This air-inclusive value tour provides tour manager assistance, visa and insurance, 4-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, and curated Indian meals. Throughout the journey, travelers will enjoy key activities such as a guided city tour of Bangkok, a dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River, a traditional Thai massage, and a visit to Nong Nooch Village in Thailand. In Malaysia, the itinerary features a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and a day trip to Genting, while the Singapore leg includes a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, an exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and a visit to Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'images': ['Pattaya753.jpg', 'CoralISlandnew.jpg', 'WatPhoTemple753.jpg', 'SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'Putramosque753.jpg', 'BatuCave.jpg', 'SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'SentosaIsland2.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'Singapore7532.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 158667, 'thumbnailImage': 'GrandTourOFAsia267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014465 is named 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Pattaya, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show Welcome To Bangkok, Thailand. Upon Arrival, Proceed To Pattaya & Check Into Your Hotel. Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Enjoy The Alcazar Show. Note All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs. All Guests Have To Fill Up Thai Digital Arrival Card Via The Below Link.Https://Tdac.Immigration.Go.Th/Arrival-Card/#/Home, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pattaya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed For An Exciting Tour Of The Coral Island (Subject To Weather Condition) By Speedboat. Take A Glass Bottom Boat Ride. You Will Have Free Time To Enjoy Water-Sports Activities - Para Sailing, Under Water Walk, Banana Boat Ride, Jet Ski On Your Own.( Kindly Note : Above Mentioned Watersport Activities Are Not A Part Of Our Tour Program. Incase You Plan To Undertake Any Of The Above Activities You Need To Book Them Directly At The Counter.) Return To The Hotel. Later Proceed To Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy The Thai Cultural Show & The Elephant Show In Nong Nooch Village. Later Experience Traditional Thai Massage. Note: For Activities At Coral Island, It Is Important That Guests Are Physically Fit To Travel In Speed Boats (As We Need To Embark & Disembark From The Speed Boat On Floating Pontoons & Excursion To Coral Island Does Not Have Wheelchair Accessibility)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping This Morning After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To Bangkok. Visit The Gems Gallery. Upon Arrival At Bangkok Proceed On A Guided City Tour Alongwith Visits To Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) Followed By Free Time For Shopping., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch Coupon & Transfers( Optional) – Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure,Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Bangkok On Your Own Or Book An On-Tour Optional Excursion And Proceed To Visit Safari World & Marine Park - Famous For It Open Zoo, Wildlife & Various Shows. Later This Evening Enjoy The Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly To Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur This Morning After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To The Airport. Fly To Kuala Lumpur. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. Note: All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below. Https://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) - Batu Caves This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 158667.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Visa Requirements Thailand Visa on arrival* Malaysia Visa on arrival* It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Juice and Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai MassageI Guided City Tour of Bangkok | Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise. Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', '