 a visit to Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show\nWelcome To Bangkok, Thailand. Upon Arrival, Proceed To Pattaya & Check Into Your Hotel. Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Enjoy The Alcazar Show.\n\xa0\nNote\n\nAll Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card\nJoining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs.\xa0\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Thai Digital Arrival Card Via The Below Link.Https://Tdac.Immigration.Go.Th/Arrival-Card/#/Home\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel M Pattaya or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes)\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed For An Exciting Tour Of The Coral Island (Subject To Weather Condition) By Speedboat. Take A Glass Bottom Boat Ride. You Will Have Free Time To Enjoy Water-Sports Activities -\xa0 Para Sailing, Under Water Walk, Banana Boat Ride, Jet Ski On Your Own.( Kindly Note : Above Mentioned Watersport Activities Are Not A Part Of Our Tour Program. Incase You Plan To Undertake Any Of The Above Activities You Need To Book Them Directly At The Counter.)\xa0 Return To The Hotel. Later Proceed To Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy The Thai Cultural Show & The Elephant Show In Nong Nooch Village. Later Experience\xa0 Traditional Thai Massage.\nNote:\nFor Activities At Coral Island, It Is Important That Guests Are Physically Fit To Travel In Speed Boats (As We Need To Embark & Disembark From The Speed Boat On Floating Pontoons & Excursion To Coral Island Does Not Have Wheelchair Accessibility).', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast,\xa0Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel M Pattaya or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple\xa0 & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To Bangkok. Visit The Gems Gallery. Upon Arrival At Bangkok Proceed On A Guided City Tour Alongwith Visits To Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) Followed By Free Time For Shopping.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel A-One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch Coupon & Transfers( Optional) \xa0– Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure,Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Bangkok On Your Own Or Book An On-Tour Optional Excursion And Proceed To Visit Safari World & Marine Park - Famous For It Open Zoo, Wildlife & Various Shows. Later This Evening Enjoy The Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel A-One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nFly To Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To The Airport. Fly To Kuala Lumpur. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening\xa0Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers.\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below.\nHttps://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) -\xa0 Batu Caves\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0 ', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional)\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\xa0\xa0\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast,\xa0 Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed\xa0 For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition\xa0 & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\xa0\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At\nSingapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods)\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park –\xa0 Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers \xa0(Optional)\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back \nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'TH', 'countryName': 'Thailand', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 158700.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Pattaya:\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBangkok:\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n\n\xa0\nKuala\xa0Lumpur:\n\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Batu Caves\nGenting Highlands with 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\nVisit to Chocolate Boutique\n\n\xa0\nSingapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings of Time Show\n', 'PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nThailand Visa on arrival*\xa0\nMalaysia Visa on arrival*\xa0\xa0\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/GrandTourOFAsia267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Pattaya753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/CoralISlandnew.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/WatPhoTemple753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/BatuCave.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/SentosaIsland2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Singapore7532.jpg']}, 'score': 8.013525, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014554', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014554', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Disney Adventure Cruise - Singapore Sailings - 3 Nights', 'days': 4, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Disney Adventure', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Disney Adventure', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Disney Adventure', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Disney Adventure', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['3 Nights Cruise on Disney Adventure All Meals included on board the ship. International Shows onboard the ship. All Kids Activities Meet and greet with Disney Characters Experience fun filled adventure at Marvel Landing Enjoy live shows like Moana – Call of the Sea'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014554_0_20260507160308.pdf', 'price': 58786, 'packageSummary': "The 'Disney Adventure Cruise - Singapore Sailings - 3 Nights' package is a magical 4-day voyage aboard the Disney Adventure cruise ship, starting and ending in Singapore. Throughout this 3-night cruise, guests will enjoy all meals onboard, spectacular international shows, and a wide array of dedicated kids' activities. The itinerary is packed with unforgettable experiences, including exclusive meet-and-greets with beloved Disney characters, action-packed fun at Marvel Landing, and captivating live performances such as the 'Moana – Call of the Sea' stage show.", 'images': ['Disney_Adventure_Cruise_753.jpg', 'Let_Sail_Party_Disney_Adventure_753.jpg', 'Oceaners_Club_Marvel_Lab_753.jpg', 'OneBedroom_Oaceanview_Suite_DisneyAdventure_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 58786, 'thumbnailImage': 'Disney_Adventure_Cruise_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Cruise'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014554 is named 'Disney Adventure Cruise - Singapore Sailings - 3 Nights' and spans 4 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Disney Adventure, Meals: Dinner (One of the restaurants on the Cruise), Description: Boarding on the Cruise – Singapore – Boarding starts from 12 noon till 3:00pm. Ship sails 4:00pm The guests will be informed prior to the sailing what time they can board the cruise. The guests can enjoy the sail away. Sail away on a magical adventure as you explore 7 imaginatively themed areas across the ship—each bursting with immersive experiences that bring the tales from Disney, Marvel and Pixar to life on a grand scale. Some suggestive activities for today are Celebrating the Disney Princesses from Tangled, Cinderella, Frozen, The Princess and the Frog and more, this fantastical area offers lavishly themed dining, quaint cafes and lounges, imaginative salons and stunning shops. As the ship’s premier indoor entertainment hub, Town Square is also home to the iconic Walt Disney Theatre, where enchanting Broadway-style shows spring to life—and Spellbound, the shadowy lounge inspired by the Evil Queen from the Disney animated film Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Disney Adventure, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Snacks (One of the restaurants on the Cruise), Description: Day at Sea - Disney Imagination Garden, Photo Shoot with Disney Princesses After breakfast the guests can indulge in watching a broadways style musical and splash it at one of the Sparkling pool. Savour in upscale, restaurants, buffets, pool side snacks and room service. Find one-of-a-kind fun in unique venues designed for kids, teens, tweens and adults. Enjoy the Disney Imagination Garden – At the heart of the ship, amid a charming courtyard and majestic stage, lies a special gathering place brimming with the magic of 100 years of Disney storytelling. Because every story begins with a spark of imagination, your holiday at sea begins here, with a high-energy Let’s Set Sail dance party. Throughout your voyage, you can also catch captivating stage performances like Avengers Assemble!, spot favorite Disney Characters, and enjoy delicious Indian and Pacific cuisines at Gramma Tala’s Kitchen and Mowgli’s Eatery., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Disney Adventure, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (One of the restaurants on the Cruise), Description: Day at Sea Today’s suggestive activities: Marvel Landing, Toy Story Place Calling all Avengers! A fun-filled adventure zone on the high seas awaits you at Marvel Landing. Located on the ship’s upper deck, this mighty area is a celebration of all things Marvel, where new recruits and seasoned Superheroes alike can avenge their need for adventure with 3 brand-new, supercharged attractions—Groot Galaxy Spin, Pym Quantum Racers and Ironcycle Test Run, the first-ever roller coaster aboard a Disney Cruise Line ship. It is also the longest roller coaster at sea—spanning over 820 feet (250 meters)!Dive into aquatic family fun as the whimsical world of the Toy Story films spring to life in surprising and imaginative ways. This lively area, spanning the center of the upper decks, takes the joy of play to infinity and beyond, with the Sunnyside Family Pool, Woody and Jessie’s Wild Slides, the Flying Saucer Splash Zone, the Toy Story Splash Pad and several whirlpool spas. The family can also enjoy watching Disney films on 2 jumbo screens. And when it’s time to refuel, enjoy a quick bite from Pizza Planet or a soft-serve ice cream from Wheezy’s Freezies., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Disney Adventure, Meals: Breakfast on the ship, Description: Singapore - DisembarkationShip Docks in Singapore Cruise terminal at 7:00am. Guest can disembark post breakfast post 9 – 9:30am Important Note: The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Price Starting From:pricing in USD Travel Dates – 2026 Room category Price Applicable Per Person (1st & 2nd Adult) Price Applicable 3rd Adult after paying full price on 1st and 2nd pax Price Applicable 4th Adult after paying full price on 1st and 2nd pax March: 13, 23, 30 April: 06, 13, 20, 27 May: 4, 11, 18, 25 June: 1, 8, 15, 22, 29 July:6, 13, 20, 27 August:3, 10, 17, 24, 31 September: 7, 14, 21, 28 October:5, 12, 19, 26 November: 2, 9, 16, 23, 30 December: 7, 14, 21, 28 Inside Cabin USD 595 USD 391 USD 391 Ocean View USD 818 USD 465 USD 465 Balcony USD 970 USD 504 USD 504, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 58786.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n3 Nights in\xa0Ocean View (Value)\xa0on\xa0Disney Adventure\xa0Cruise\n, \n3 Nights in\xa0Balcony\xa0(Premium)\xa0on\xa0Disney Adventure\xa0Cruise\xa0\n, \n3 Nights in Inside Cabin (Standard)\xa0on\xa0Disney Adventure\xa0Cruise\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation Meals Unlimited Coffee, Tea & Soda Broadway-Quality Shows Character Experiences Movie Screenings Pools Waterslides, Splash Zones & Wading Pools Kids Clubs Disney's Oceaneer Club (3 to 10 years old) Disney's Oceaneer Lab (3 to 10 years old) Edge (11 to 14 years old) Vibe (14 to 17 years old) Adult-Exclusive Activities Nightclubs, Lounges & Live Music Adults-Only Pool & Whirlpool Spa Fitness Center. Exclusions: TCS Gratuities WiFi Bottled Water, Alcoholic Beverages, Specialty Coffees, Teas & Drinks Spa & Salon Ground Transfers Air Travel Pre and Post-Cruise Hotel Stays More Family Fun Royal Court Royal Tea, a tea party with Disney Characters for kids ages 3 to 12 Bibbidi Bobbidi Boutique and The Pirate’s League, offering magical makeovers for children Adult-Exclusive Dining Palo. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions: All prices are based on current ROE (Rate of Exchange) of the cruise liner. Please confirm with us at the date of booking of prevailing ROE. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. The rates are not valid on block out dates. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. Meals on land tour are not included. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. Thomas Cook (I) Ltd is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. Highlights of the package: 3 Nights Cruise on Disney Adventure All Meals included on board the ship. International Shows onboard the ship. All Kids Activities Meet and greet with Disney Characters Experience fun filled adventure at Marvel Landing Enjoy live shows like Moana – Call of the Sea.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Disney Adventure Cruise - Singapore Sailings - 3 Nights' package is a magical 4-day voyage aboard the Disney Adventure cruise ship, starting and ending in Singapore. Throughout this 3-night cruise, guests will enjoy all meals onboard, spectacular international shows, and a wide array of dedicated kids' activities. The itinerary is packed with unforgettable experiences, including exclusive meet-and-greets with beloved Disney characters, action-packed fun at Marvel Landing, and captivating live performances such as the 'Moana – Call of the Sea' stage show.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nBoarding on the Cruise – Singapore – Boarding starts from 12 noon till 3:00pm. Ship sails 4:00pm\nThe guests will be informed prior to the sailing what time they can board the cruise.\xa0 The guests can enjoy the sail away. Sail away on a magical adventure as you explore 7 imaginatively themed areas across the ship—each bursting with immersive experiences that bring the tales from Disney, Marvel and Pixar to life on a grand scale. Some suggestive activities for today are Celebrating the Disney Princesses from Tangled, Cinderella, Frozen, The Princess and the Frog and more, this fantastical area offers lavishly themed dining, quaint cafes and lounges, imaginative salons and stunning shops. As the ship’s premier indoor entertainment hub, Town Square is also home to the iconic Walt Disney Theatre, where enchanting Broadway-style shows spring to life—and Spellbound, the shadowy lounge inspired by the Evil Queen from the Disney animated film Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner (One of the restaurants on the Cruise)', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard the Disney Adventure\xa0Cruise (Over Night on the ship)\xa0'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay at Sea - Disney Imagination Garden, Photo Shoot with Disney Princesses\nAfter breakfast the guests can indulge in watching a broadways style musical and splash it at one of the\xa0 Sparkling pool. Savour in upscale, restaurants, buffets, pool side snacks and room service. Find one-of-a-kind\xa0 fun in unique venues designed for kids, teens, tweens and adults. Enjoy the Disney Imagination Garden –\xa0At the heart of the ship, amid a charming courtyard and majestic stage, lies a special gathering place\xa0brimming with the magic of 100 years of Disney storytelling. Because every story begins with a spark of imagination, your holiday at sea begins here, with a high-energy Let’s Set Sail dance party. Throughout your voyage, you can also catch captivating stage performances like Avengers Assemble!, spot favorite Disney Characters, and enjoy delicious Indian and Pacific cuisines at Gramma Tala’s Kitchen and Mowgli’s Eatery.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Snacks (One of the restaurants on the Cruise)', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard the Disney Adventure\xa0Cruise\xa0(Over Night on the ship)\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay at Sea \nToday’s suggestive activities: Marvel Landing, Toy Story Place\nCalling all Avengers! A fun-filled adventure zone on the high seas awaits you at Marvel Landing.\xa0\nLocated on the ship’s upper deck, this mighty area is a celebration of all things Marvel, where new\xa0recruits and seasoned Superheroes alike can avenge their need for adventure with 3 brand-new,\xa0supercharged attractions—Groot Galaxy Spin, Pym Quantum Racers and Ironcycle Test Run,\xa0the first-ever roller coaster aboard a Disney Cruise Line ship. It is also the longest roller coaster at sea—spanning over 820 feet (250 meters)!Dive into aquatic family fun as the whimsical world of the Toy Story films spring to life in surprising and imaginative ways. This lively area, spanning the center of the upper decks, takes the joy of play to infinity\xa0and beyond, with the Sunnyside Family Pool, Woody and Jessie’s Wild Slides, the Flying Saucer Splash Zone, the Toy Story Splash Pad and several whirlpool spas. The family can also enjoy watching Disney films on 2 jumbo screens. And when it’s time to refuel, enjoy a quick bite from Pizza Planet or a soft-serve\xa0ice cream from Wheezy’s Freezies.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner (One of the restaurants on the Cruise)', 'overnightStay': 'Onboard the\xa0Disney Adventure\xa0Cruise\xa0(Over Night on the ship)'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nSingapore - DisembarkationShip Docks in Singapore Cruise terminal at 7:00am. Guest can disembark post breakfast post 9 – 9:30am\n\xa0\nImportant Note: The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.\n