 your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs). A tropical paradise with classic beaches and one of the most attractive groups of islands in Southeast Asia, the Phi Phi Islands are renowned for their beauty, separating the large island of Phuket from the coasts of the Strait of Malacca. Rest of the day is at leisure. Overnight in Phi Phi Island, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Krabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Phi Phi Island - Krabi Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Later proceed to Krabi, Krabi, famous for its scenic view and breathtaking Beaches and Islands. Its coral reef vistas are also one of the world's most beautiful, which makes the city a great spot for coral diving. Rest of the day is at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Krabi, Meals: Breakfast and Lunch, Description: Four Island Tour with lunch by speedboat (SIC basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Enjoy exciting Island-hopping to the tropical hot spots in the Krabi Sea: Phra Nang Cave, Tub Island, Chicken Island and Poda Island. Swimming, snorkeling, sunbathing, exploring the islands are the main activities to enjoy. Expect a great day out, a rich variety of corals and fish, crystal clear water and white powdery beaches, lined with coconut palms., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Phuket, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Krabi – Phuket - Krabi to Phuket Transfer Enroute Phuket City Tour with Big Buddha (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Discover the best of paradise on a 5-hour coach tour of Phuket Island! Wind along Phuket’s southern shoreline, marvelling at white sands, lush tropical flora and the unique vibe of Patong, Karon, Kata and Rawai beaches. You’ll have plenty of photo opportunities from the seat of your comfortable coach or at each stop. Snap gorgeous shots from Karon Viewpoint and witness the sacred beauty of Wat Chalong temple. Phuket's Big Buddha is one of the most important and revered landmarks on the island. The huge image sits on top of the Nakkerd Hills between Chalong and Kata and, at 45 metres tall, can be seen from as far away as Phuket Town and Karon Beach. The lofty site offers the best 360-degree views of the island, with sweeping vistas of Phuket Town, Kata, Karon, Chalong Bay and more. Reachable via a winding, 6-km road leading from Phuket's main roads, it's a must-visit island destination. Great orientation of Phuket on this half-day sightseeing tour Amazing views of Phuket with plenty of photo opportunities. Rest of the day is at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Phuket, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Phuket - Hanuman World 10 Platforms (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Take to the air at Phuket's eco-adventure zipline park. “Hanuman” is one of the ancient forest gods in the Hindu/Buddhist epic Ramayana and you will have the chance to experience the deep forest as a god flying through the trees at Hanuman World! The professional team will start with registration and a safety briefing upon your arrival. You will be equipped with the latest Petzl® technical equipment and you will learn how to use all of your equipment to ensure you have a safe adventure in the treetops. Depending on the package chosen, your guide will take you above the forest floor to experience a variety of fun zip lines, rope swings, sky bridges and spiral staircases. Admire stunning views of Phuket, the Andaman Sea and even the distant Phi Phi Islands above! Walk, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Phuket, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Phuket – Fantasea Show (Standard Seat) with dinner Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Later in the evening experience Thailand's colorful traditions, Fantasy of a Kingdom is the first ever audiovisual extravaganza that includes: Thai culture has magical illusions, Four-dimensional theatrical effects, aerial ballet, indoor special effects, elephant acts and stunts create unforgettable theatrical masterpieces that captivate visitors from all over the 