nHotel rates are not valid during blackout period / surcharge dates / stop sales.\nBlackout date surcharges\nChristmas & New Year - 15 Dec 2026 – 10 Jan 2027\nFirework – 23 Nov 2026 – 30 Nov 2027\nChinese New year – 20 Jan 2027 – 08 Feb 2027\xa0\nSongkran – 05 Apr – 15 Apr 2027\nMidnight surcharge.\nMeals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary.\nTips for guide & driver.\nCity tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable).\nExpenditure of a personal nature (mini bar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.)\nCamera fee.\nPorterage facility\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable.\nVisa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable).\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary.\xa0\nCost of optional excursions.\nAnything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nAll travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nRates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling.\nHotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nHotel upgrade pricing does not guarantee rooms at the preferred / envisaged hotels.\nHotel upgrade rooms remain subject to availability at the time of booking.\nIf the selected upgrade hotel is unavailable, we will provide alternate options for a similar category.\nThe rates are not valid on blackout dates & Trade Fair periods.\xa0\nAny applicable surcharges will be communicated, and passengers will be required to pay them accordingly.\nSurcharges, if applicable, are additional to the total package price quoted at the time of booking.\nGuests are requested to confirm their onward\xa0 /connecting flights with the sales team before booking.\nAll rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing at the time of booking.\nWe reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\xa0\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\xa0\nInternational Check in time is\xa01400/1500 hours\xa0& Check out time is\xa01100/1200 hours respectively, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\nWherever transfers are included, they are provided without night surcharges.\nNo refunds (partial or full) will be provided for any unutilized services.\nAll sightseeing tours and excursions are operated by local service providers; timings and operating days are subject to change. Changes or Updates, if any, will be shared at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly subject to weather conditions, and local service providers reserve the right to cancel tours without prior notice.\nRates are subject to change without prior notice, including for clients travelling during weekends.\nAny promotional offer, if applicable, may be withdrawn at any time without prior notice.\nOnce bookings are confirmed, cancellation charges will apply as per policy and will be informed at that time.\nOrganization is not responsible for any price changes arising from factors beyond our control.\nA refundable security deposit is required at check-in as per international hotel policy, payable by credit card or cash; the amount varies by hotel and is returned at check-out. Guests should avoid using debit cards since the amount is charged instantly and may take 2–3 weeks to refund. Any additional hotel services (such as mini-bar, room service, etc.) may be deducted from this deposit, and Company is not responsible for such transactions, as these are directly between the hotel and the guest.\n\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015715/SRP_safariworld.png', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 8.260351, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014470', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014470', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights Of Thailand - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Juice and Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai Massage | Guided City Tour of Bangkok |Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise."], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 73026, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights Of Thailand - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 6-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Bangkok and Pattaya. This air-inclusive value tour provides travelers with the assistance of a dedicated tour manager, visa and insurance coverage, four-star hotel accommodations on a bed-and-breakfast basis, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners. Throughout the journey, participants will enjoy key activities including a visit to the beautiful Nong Nooch Village, a relaxing traditional Thai massage, a guided city tour of Bangkok, and a scenic dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River, with refreshing juice and coconut water provided at select sightseeing spots.", 'images': ['Pattaya753.jpg', 'CoralISlandnew.jpg', 'WatPhoTemple753.jpg', 'SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'Wat_Arun_753.jpeg', 'Bangkok1City.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 73026, 'thumbnailImage': 'HighlightsOfThailand267.jpg', 'packageTheme': [], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014470 is named 'Highlights Of Thailand - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Pattaya, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show Welcome to Thailand. Upon arrival, proceed to Pattaya & Check into your hotel. Rest of the day is at leisure. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening enjoy the Alcazar Show. NOTE Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card All Guests have to fill up Thai Digital Arrival Card via the below link.https://tdac.immigration.go.th/arrival-card/#/home, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pattaya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes) This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed for an exciting tour of the Coral Island (subject to weather condition) by speedboat. Take a glass bottom boat ride. You will have free time to enjoy water-sports activities - Para sailing, Under water walk, banana boat ride, Jet Ski on your own.( Kindly note : Above mentioned watersport activities are not a part of our Tour Program. Incase you plan to undertake any of the above activities you need to book them directly at the counter.) Return to the hotel. Later proceed to Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy the Thai Cultural Show & the Elephant Show in Nong Nooch village. Later experience Traditional Thai message Note: For activities at Coral island, it is important that guests are physically fit to travel in speed boats (As we need to Embark & Disembark from the speed boat on floating pontoons & Excursion to Coral Island does not have wheelchair accessibility )., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping This morning after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to Bangkok. Visit the Gems Gallery. Upon arrival at Bangkok proceed on a guided city tour along with visits to Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) followed by free time for shopping., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) – Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise This morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure, spend rest of the day exploring Bangkok on your own or book an on tour optional excursion and proceed to visit Safari World & Marine Park - famous for it Open Zoo, wildlife & various shows. Later this evening enjoy the Chao Phraya dinner cruise., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure. Spend rest of the day exploring Bangkok on your own OR “ Plan Your Day” from the various optional tours available on attractive offers, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This morning after buffet breakfast, check out and pproceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 73026.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n, \n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. WHAT’S MORE Coconut Water at Coral Island Juice during Bangkok City Tour 500 ml water bottle per day. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Visa Requirements Thailand Visa on arrival* It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs General Info Currency Used: THAILAND: Thai Bhat (THB) Time Difference: THAILAND: 1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. We advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc Prohibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in Thailand, Malaysia & Singapore Cigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc. Has restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import https://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports http://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences Hotels: Many hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size. For Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. As a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room. (Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking) Average standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter. Standard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs. Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In. All hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin room is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in. All selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary. Most hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for entire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. During certain dates stay may be split in two hotels Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or Necessary. Coaches: Most of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. One check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach. In most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. General Points: The tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you. Passengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost. When the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well. Tap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body. Health is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations. If a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country. For certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. Tipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc. Carry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour. Entire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements. Carry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear. Weather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers. International Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas. Tips & Optional can only be paid in Cash. Advisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia. Few rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Juice and Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai Massage | Guided City Tour of Bangkok |Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZTE550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights Of Thailand - April 2026 To March 2027' package is a 6-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Bangkok and Pattaya. This air-inclusive value tour provides travelers with the assistance of a dedicated tour manager, visa and insurance coverage, four-star hotel accommodations on a bed-and-breakfast basis, and specially curated Indian Jain, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian lunches and dinners. Throughout the journey, participants will enjoy key activities including a visit to the beautiful Nong Nooch Village, a relaxing traditional Thai massage, a guided city tour of Bangkok, and a scenic dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River, with refreshing juice and coconut water provided at select sightseeing spots.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show\nWelcome to Thailand. Upon arrival, proceed to Pattaya & Check into your hotel. Rest of the day is at leisure. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later this evening enjoy the Alcazar Show.\n\xa0\nNOTE\n\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nAll Guests have to fill up Thai Digital Arrival Card via the below link.https://tdac.immigration.go.th/arrival-card/#/home\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0M or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes)\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed for an exciting tour of the Coral Island (subject to weather condition) by speedboat. Take a glass bottom boat ride. You will have free time to enjoy water-sports activities -\xa0 Para sailing, Under water walk, banana boat ride, Jet Ski on your own.( Kindly note : Above mentioned watersport activities are not a part of our Tour Program. Incase you plan to undertake any of the above activities you need to book them directly at the counter.)\xa0 Return to the hotel. Later proceed to Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy the Thai Cultural Show & the Elephant Show in Nong Nooch village. Later experience\xa0 Traditional Thai message\xa0\nNote:\xa0For activities at Coral island, it is important that guests are physically fit to travel in speed boats (As we need to Embark & Disembark from the speed boat on floating pontoons & Excursion to Coral Island does not have wheelchair accessibility ).', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast,\xa0Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0M or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple\xa0 & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping\nThis morning after buffet breakfast check out & proceed to Bangkok. Visit the Gems Gallery. Upon arrival at Bangkok proceed on a guided city tour along with visits to Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) followed by free time for shopping.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel\xa0A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard\xa0or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) – Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure, spend rest of the day exploring Bangkok on your own or book an on tour optional excursion and proceed to visit Safari World & Marine Park - famous for it Open Zoo, wildlife & various shows. Later this evening enjoy the Chao Phraya dinner cruise.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard\xa0or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis morning \xa0after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure. Spend rest of the day exploring Bangkok on your own OR “ Plan Your Day” from the various optional tours available on attractive offers', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard\xa0or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back \nThis morning\xa0after buffet breakfast, check out and pproceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n', '\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\n', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'TH', 'countryName': 'Thailand', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 73000.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n', 'Pattaya\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBangkok\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\nWHAT’S MORE\n\nCoconut Water at Coral Island\nJuice during Bangkok City Tour\xa0\n500 ml water bottle per day\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nThailand Visa on arrival*\xa0\xa0\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'termsAndConditions': "\xa0\nNote:\xa0Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAll travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\n\xa0\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\n\xa0\n\nCurrency Used: THAILAND: Thai Bhat (THB)\xa0\nTime Difference: THAILAND: 1 hour and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st Dec 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket\nneeds to be bought by the passengers themselves\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\nWe advise to carry maximum of 1 big and 1 cabin bag per person, especially if internal flights on tour and Train Journey are involved during your tour. (Luggage allowance in Internal Flights 15kgs). Also, every bag is guest responsibility and porterage is not included at Hotels, Airport, Immigration halls, Train stations, Cruise terminals etc\nProhibited items - E- cigarettes, displaying Images of Buddha, Travelling by Land in\nThailand, Malaysia & Singapore\nCigarettes/ Liquor/ Toys or replica of Arms and explosive etc.\nHas restrictions to be carried. Please refer to below link for more information\n\nhttps://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and- prohibitedgoods-for-import\nhttps://www.export.gov/article?id=Malaysia-Prohibited-Restricted-Imports\nhttp://en.customs.go.th/content.php? ini_content=customs_offences&lang=en&left_me nu=menu_customs_offences\n\n\nHotels:\n\nMany hotels in Asia have only Twin beds. Double bed will mostly be Queen size and not King size.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don't have enough roll away beds, in that case they might\xa0give a double and a separate single room.\nAs a 3rd adult person in a triple room, most hotels use roll away beds or 2 queen size beds\xa0and the room size may be the SAME as a Twin/ double room.\xa0\n(Hence we also strongly suggest you to upgrade Triple into 2 separate rooms during booking)\nAverage standard room size in south East Asia is 15 - 18 square meter.\nStandard Check in time in Asia is 1500 hrs & Standard check out time in Asia is 1200hrs.\xa0 Early Check in & late Checkout is subjected to availability and at an extra Cost. Adjoining room's requests are subjected to availability during Check In.\nAll hotels rooms booked for group are Standard category. Getting a double room or a twin\nroom is subjected to availability of the same in Hotel during check in.\nAll selected hotels on above tour, serve breakfast which is a combination of continental & local dishes as per hotel standard. Indian meals will be provided during Lunches & Dinners as per itinerary.\nMost hotels have Centralized Air Conditioners which is set at a specific temperature for\nentire property. Restaurants & Sightseeing attractions are mostly naturally ventilated.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Asia such as Air Show, music festivals, sports championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nDuring certain dates stay may be split in two hotels\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or Necessary.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Asia is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygienic reasons it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour\xa0manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nOne check in bag and one hand bag per person only, due to limited boot space in the coach.\nIn most of cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Points:\n\nThe tour will be operated subject to a minimum of 25 full-paying passengers travelling together. In the event that the group size is less than 25 passengers you will be given on option of travelling on FIT basis, by paying an additional supplement on seat in coach basis with local representatives to assist you.\nPassengers can request for a direct flight from the hub city, by paying a supplement cost.\nWhen the tour has less than 25 adults and is operated on a seat-in-coach basis, there will be instances where the driver acts as a guide as well.\nTap water is portable in Singapore, approved by local govt body.\nHealth is of Paramount importance for all Tourists opting for this tour. It is important that every individual tourists to get their health examination done by Family physician before Travelling. Above tour includes walking at many sightseeing locations.\nIf a Traveller requires wheel chair, this has to be carried by individual from home city/ country.\nFor certain departures, we may re-route the itinerary. However, all sightseeing & inclusions will remain the same. On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\nTipping is not kept compulsory on your tour; although we appreciate your gesture of tipping to Guides, Drivers, Hotel staff etc.\nCarry passport, Travel document, Visa at all times during the tour.\nEntire Tour Program is designed & pre planned with various appointments and schedule, hence we strongly urge you to always be in time for smooth conduct of group tour. For those who repeatedly delay group departures, will be responsible to join the group by own transportation arrangements.\nCarry an umbrella and wear comfortable footwear during the tour. Advisable to carry a swim wear or nylon clothing & slippers/ Sandals for Beach locations & water theme parks if any. Casino dress code for men - Full shirt, Pant & covered footwear.\nWeather in South East Asia is warm and Humid throughout the year with unpredictable monsoon showers.\nInternational Debit/ Credit cards/ Currency cards are not accepted everywhere, but only at selected shops in Thailand/Malaysia/Singapore. Local currency in Cash (THB/MYR/SGD) accepted over counters at all locations. Money exchange is available at Airports and city center shopping areas.\nTips & Optional can only be paid in Cash.\nAdvisable to carry universal charging adaptors in South East Asia.\nFew rides inside Theme Park, Cable car ride, Wings of Time etc. are operated subject to weather conditions, & Maintenance schedule.\n", 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/HighlightsOfThailand267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/itinerary/Pattaya753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/itinerary/CoralISlandnew.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/itinerary/WatPhoTemple753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/itinerary/SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/itinerary/Wat_Arun_753.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014470/itinerary/Bangkok1City.jpg']}, 'score': 7.313436, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG010524', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG010524', 'availableMonths': ['june_2027', 'april_2027', 'july_2027', 'august_2027', 'november_2026', 'september_2027', 'may_2027', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Simply Thailand Fully Loaded - (3N Pattaya And 2N Bangkok)', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Hotel Specific freebies. Anya Nana Bangkok (Complimentary Welcome Drink + Fruit Platter) Mike Garden Pattaya (Complimentary Welcome Drink) Aiyara Grand Pattaya (Complimentary Welcome Drink)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG010524_0_20261002025937', 'price': 72412, 'packageSummary': "The 'Simply Thailand Fully Loaded - (3N Pattaya And 2N Bangkok)' package is a 6-day tour covering the exciting cities of Pattaya and Bangkok. Throughout this tropical getaway, travelers will enjoy exclusive hotel-specific freebies designed to enhance their stay. These special perks include a complimentary welcome drink and fruit platter at Anya Nana Bangkok, as well as complimentary welcome drinks at both Mike Garden Pattaya and Aiyara Grand Pattaya.", 'images': ['Pattaya1.jpg', 'coralisland1Thailand.jpg', 'NongNoochshutterstock_355776248.jpg', 'WatTraimit_753.jpg', 'SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'Bangkok1City.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 72412, 'thumbnailImage': 'Thailand26712.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Durga Puja Special', 'Couple Special', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG010524 is named 'Simply Thailand Fully Loaded - (3N Pattaya And 2N Bangkok)' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Pattaya, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive at Bangkok. Transfer to Pattaya. Visit Alcazar Show (PVT basis) Welcome to Thailand! Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.) In the evening we visit the Alcazar show. The Alcazar show is one of the most anticipated shows where professional performers are dancing in stunning costumes and millions of Thai Baht are used to apply colorful, complicated light effects and modern stage technology into creating the most extraordinary art product for all of its audiences., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pattaya, Meals: Breakfast and Lunch, Description: Visit Coral Island by joined speedboat with lunch (SIC basis) – Water sports not included and Art in Paradise (Ticket Only) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Discover Pattaya's rich underwater world, fly with a parachute, go on a sea walker dive, and more on a secluded beach. This Coral Island activity combines 5 fun water things to do in Pattaya, and you are sure to find something you've always wanted to try. Select from snorkeling, sea walker diving, parasailing, jet-skiing, and banana boating! Experience Art in Paradise Pattaya is another great place for tourists to visit in Pattaya City because it is, in the present, the first and only one illusion art museum - the museum presenting Anamorphosis. Additionally, visitors can enjoy the museum interactively by taking photos of your posture with 3d illusion painting or even touching the painting. Besides, its location is really great since it is in the city, Near North Pattaya Big C Supercenter. Not surprisingly, the museum is popular for visitors in different ages, especially kids., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pattaya, Meals: Breakfast and Lunch, Description: Pattaya – Nong Nooch Village with Show (Thai Cultural and Elephants) & Lunch (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Morning free to explore or shopping. Later proceed to the fascinating tourist destination renowned for its wide-ranging orchid species, a palm garden, various flowering and decorative plants from all corners of the world. The highlight of our program and every body's favorite is the elephant show. You'll see these gentle giants, the symbols of Siam, perform various tricks such as riding bikes, playing football and they'll even invite you to a tug of war. In our well-kept, beautifully landscape gardens, you can quietly stroll among flower beds, enjoying the profuse colors and fragrance of millions of flowers, as well as the well-trained chimpanzees and elephants in the natural surroundings., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Pattaya – Bangkok enroute City Tour of Bangkok (Golden Buddha & Marble Buddha with Gems Gallery) (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Visit Thailand’s famous attractions today as you drive past the city. Visit Bangkok City & Temples (Golden Buddha Temple & Marble Temple)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast and Lunch, Description: Visit Safari World & Marine Park with lunch (SIC basis) (closed on Monday) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Visit one of Thailand's top open zoos, the Safari World in Bangkok. The Park is divided into the Safari Park and Marine Park, each of which is home to a distinct collection of species. Visit the Safari Park to get up close and personal with animals like tigers and giraffes. Be enthralled by the Marine Park's beautiful aquatic wildlife. Don't forget to attend the various performances the park hosts for guests. So, come along with your loved ones and enjoy your day., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Travel Validity: 01 Apr 2026 - 26 Oct 2027 PATTAYA EXTENSION NIGHT CATEGORY HOTELS PER PERSON IN USD TWIN / DOUBLE Standard Golden Sea Pattaya/ Mike Garden Pattaya or similar 50 Value Aiyara Grand Hotel Pattaya or similar 56 BANGKOK EXTENSION NIGHT CATEGORY HOTELS PER PERSON IN USD TWIN / DOUBLE Standard Anya Nana Bangkok or Seasons Siam Bangkok or similar 56 Value Citrus Sukhumvit 11 Bangkok or similar 75 Travel Validity: 01 NOV 2026 - 26 MAR 2027 PATTAYA EXTENSION NIGHT CATEGORY HOTELS PER PERSON IN USD TWIN / DOUBLE Standard Golden Sea Pattaya/ Mike Garden Pattaya or similar 53 Value Aiyara Grand Hotel Pattaya or similar 59 BANGKOK EXTENSION NIGHT CATEGORY HOTELS PER PERSON IN USD TWIN / DOUBLE Standard Anya Nana Bangkok or Seasons Siam Bangkok or similar 59 Value Citrus Sukhumvit 11 Bangkok or similar 79 All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 72412.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Dusit\xa0(Premium) or similar in Pattaya\n2 Nights Hotel\xa0Grand Mercure Atrium\xa0(Premium) or similar in Bangkok\n, \n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Golden Sea Pattaya or Mike Garden Resort or Similar in Pattaya\n2 Nights Hotel\xa0Anya Nana Bangkok or Seasons Siam Bangkok\xa0or Similar in Bangkok\n, \n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Aiyara Grand Hotel Pattaya or Similar in Pattaya\n2 Nights Hotel\xa0Citrus Sukhumvit 11 Bangkok or Similar in Bangkok\n. Meals include: \nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\nLunch as per itinerary\n. Inclusions: 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Pattaya 02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Bangkok Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Return airport transfers on Private Basis Alcazar Show Standard Seat on Private Basis Art in Paradise (Ticket Only) Coral Island tour with Indian lunch by speedboat on Sharing Basis Noong Nooch Village Entry + Show (Thai Cultural & Elephants) + Lunch – Private Basis Pattaya to Bangkok transfers on Private Basis Enroute Bangkok City & Temple Tour with Golden Buddha & Marble Buddha & Gems Gallery on Private Basis Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST. The rates are valid for a minimum of 02 adults travelling together. All flight services. Pre and post tour services & costs. Hotel rates not valid during blackout period / surcharge dates / stop sales. Blackout date surcharges – Songkran – 10th Apr 2027 – 15th Apr 2027 Pattaya Fireworks Festival, Loy Krathong Festival, Yi Peng Lantern Festival (Chiang Mai) – 27 Nov – 28 Nov 2026. Tomorrow Land – 11 Dec – 15 Dec 2026 Christmas & New Year - 15 Dec 2026 - 10 Jan 2027 Chinese New Year – 05th Feb – 07th Feb 2027 Meals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary. Tips for guide & driver. City tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable). Expenditure of a personal nature (mini bar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.) Camera fee. Porterage facility Departure PCR test, if applicable. Visa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable). Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of optional excursions. Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list.. Product Terms and Conditions: All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th Terms and Conditions: The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling. SURCHARGE of USD 20 per person for Pick Up & Drop At DMK Airport. The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: Hotel Specific freebies. Anya Nana Bangkok (Complimentary Welcome Drink + Fruit Platter) Mike Garden Pattaya (Complimentary Welcome Drink) Aiyara Grand Pattaya (Complimentary Welcome Drink).", 'departureCities': [{'cityName