a Fireworks Festival, Loy Krathong Festival, Yi Peng Lantern Festival (Chiang Mai) - 20 Nov - 28 Nov 2026.\nChristmas & New Year - 14 Dec 2026 - 05 Jan 2027\nChinese New Year - (ON REQUEST) - 01 Feb - 22 Feb 2027\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nAll travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nRates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling.\nHotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nHotel upgrade pricing does not guarantee rooms at the preferred / envisaged hotels.\nHotel upgrade rooms remain subject to availability at the time of booking.\nIf the selected upgrade hotel is unavailable, we will provide alternate options for a similar category.\nThe rates are not valid on blackout dates & Trade Fair periods.\xa0\nAny applicable surcharges will be communicated, and passengers will be required to pay them accordingly.\nSurcharges, if applicable, are additional to the total package price quoted at the time of booking.\nGuests are requested to confirm their onward\xa0 /connecting flights with the sales team before booking.\nAll rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing at the time of booking.\nWe reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\xa0\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\xa0\nInternational Check in time is\xa01400/1500 hours\xa0& Check out time is\xa01100/1200 hours respectively, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\nWherever transfers are included, they are provided without night surcharges.\nNo refunds (partial or full) will be provided for any unutilized services.\nAll sightseeing tours and excursions are operated by local service providers; timings and operating days are subject to change. Changes or Updates, if any, will be shared at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly subject to weather conditions, and local service providers reserve the right to cancel tours without prior notice.\nRates are subject to change without prior notice, including for clients travelling during weekends.\nAny promotional offer, if applicable, may be withdrawn at any time without prior notice.\nOnce bookings are confirmed, cancellation charges will apply as per policy and will be informed at that time.\nOrganization is not responsible for any price changes arising from factors beyond our control.\nA refundable security deposit is required at check-in as per international hotel policy, payable by credit card or cash; the amount varies by hotel and is returned at check-out. Guests should avoid using debit cards since the amount is charged instantly and may take 2–3 weeks to refund. Any additional hotel services (such as mini-bar, room service, etc.) may be deducted from this deposit, and Company is not responsible for such transactions, as these are directly between the hotel and the guest.\n\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014887/Pattaya26790.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014887/itinerary/Pattaya1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014887/itinerary/coralisland1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014887/itinerary/Pattaya-City.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014887/itinerary/5268_Safari_World_Bangkok753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014887/itinerary/Thailand_bangkok.jpg']}, 'score': 3.5732946, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG010862', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG010862', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'UNIQUE CHIANG MAI CHIANG RAI', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Chiang Mai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chiang Mai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chiang Mai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chiang Mai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chiang Rai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chiang Rai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Chiang Rai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG010862_0_20261008200148.pdf', 'price': 81293, 'packageSummary': "The 'UNIQUE CHIANG MAI CHIANG RAI' package is a 7-day tour covering the culturally rich northern Thai cities of Chiang Mai and Chiang Rai. The itinerary includes visits to the iconic Wat Phra That Doi Suthep, the stunning Wat Rong Khun (White Temple), the historic Golden Triangle, and vibrant local night markets. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, ethical elephant sanctuary interactions, scenic boat rides along the Mekong River, and immersive cultural experiences in traditional hill tribe villages.", 'images': ['chaingmaitinerary.jpg', 'chiangmaicityitinerary.jpg', 'DoiSuthepMonkTraiandDoiSutheptempleitinerary.jpg', 'elephantsanctuarychiangmai.jpg', 'WatRongSuaTenBlueTempleChiangRAI.jpg', 'BaanDamChaingRAI.jpg', 'chiangrAICITYthAILAND.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 81293, 'thumbnailImage': 'chiaingmaiSRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Couple Special', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG010862 is named 'UNIQUE CHIANG MAI CHIANG RAI' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Chiang Mai, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive at Chiang Mai. Welcome to Thailand! Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx 1400 hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Chiang Mai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: City Tour of Chiang Mai (PVT basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Proceed to city tour with visit to the most interesting temples: Wat Chiang Man, The oldest temple in Chiang Mai Town. The temple is famous for its Lanna style chedi supported by rows of elephant shaped buttresses. Continue to Wat Chedi Luang, Wat Montean, Wat Lok Molee and Wat Suan Dok. Later in the afternoon, we visit Chiang Mai Night Market., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Chiang Mai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Visit Doi Suthep Monk Trail and Doi Suthep Temple (PVT basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Today we proceed to a private half day Doi Suthep Monk Trail is a 6.3 kilometer heavily trafficked out and back trail located near Chiang Mai city that features a waterfall and is rated as moderate. The trail is primarily used for hiking and walking. Start hiking trip at Chiang Mai Zoo area. The first section takes you to a small temple (called Wat Pha Lat), take no more than 1 hour. We are serenaded by weird exotic sounds of the forest -birds, insects, grinding bamboos, streams. Wat Pa Lad is the small temple less famous, but has many interesting architecture and sculptures such as the Buddha's statue and pagoda. and is constructed in Burmese architecture style and over 600 years old. The second section is Doi Suthep Temple, the most famous landmark in Chiang Mai. At the top of the temple, you can view the pagoda, believed to enshrine the holy relics of the Lord Buddha, shining with real gold. A viewing platform also offers panoramic view of Chiang Mai City. Overnight stay at Chiang Mai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Chiang Mai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Elephant Jungle Sanctuary Tour (SIC basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. In the afternoon, proceed to Elephant Jungle Sanctuary Tour. Pick up from hotel and drive approximately 1.5 hours South of Chiang Mai through rolling hills, forest, and local agriculture area. Arrive at the Elephant Jungle Sanctuary. Learn about the elephants and change into traditional Karen clothing. Meet the elephants. Feed, interact and play with the elephants in a natural environment as you learn about their behavior and history. Take photos with the elephants. Have a mud spa with the elephants. Walk with the elephants to a river and bathe them. Say goodbye to the elephants and drive back to Chiang Mai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Chiang Rai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Chiang Mai – Chiang Rai. Visit Wat Rong Sua Ten (Blue Temple) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Depart from Chiang Mai and drive to Chiang Rai on private basis and on the way short stop at Mae Kajan Hot Spring and Wat Rong Khun, the temple is well known for its decorations with white tone decorated reflected mirrors. Afternoon visit Wat Rong Sua Ten (Blue Temple) which is in Rong Suea Ten in the district of Rimkok. The interior of the wihan is very beautiful. The entrance is guarded by two spectacular dragon statues. Then, visit the local market and evening explore Walking Street of Chiang Rai (open on Saturday & Sunday only) Overnight stay at Chiang Rai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Chiang Rai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Visit Baan Dam and Golden Triangle Area (PVT basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. After breakfast, private visit Baan Dam (Black House) which is the unique creation of national artist, Thawan Duchanee. Part art studio, part museum, part home. Baan Dam is an eclectic mix of traditional northern Thai buildings interspersed with some outlandish modern designs. Continue to Choui Fong Tea Plantation to enjoy stunning tea plantation views and the best matcha desserts! After lunch visit to the Golden Triangle area on the bank of the Mekong River where Myanmar, Laos and Thailand border meet. Board a long-tail boat to visit the river bank scenery along Mekhong River. Visit Opium Museum and Wat Pra Thad Jom Kitti by climbing up 383 steps to the top of the hill. Afterwards, visit Long Neck Karen. Overnight stay at Chiang Rai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Chiang Rai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure to Chiang Rai International Airport Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. * The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th PACKAGE ENVISAGED RATES IN USD PER PERSON Travel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 2027 CATEGORY 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-9 PAX 10 PAX INF STANDARD 730 592 730 553 0 VALUE 914 783 914 743 0 PREMIUM 1053 914 1053 882 0 Extention Night Cost: Travel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 2027 CATEGORY SR OTHERS DBL TRPL 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-9 PAX 10 PAX CWB CNB INF STANDARD 288 258 258 183 148 183 138 194 168 0 VALUE 378 304 304 229 196 229 186 228 198 0 PREMIUM 449 340 340 263 229 263 220 255 221 0, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 81293.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\xa0\nHOTELS\n\n\n03 star\xa0\nDuangtawan Chiang Mai (Superior) or similar in Chiang Mai\n\n\nWiang Inn Chiang Rai (Superior) or similar in Chiang Rai\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\xa0\nHOTELS\n\n\n05 star\xa0\nMelia Chiang Mai (Melia room) or similar in Chiang Mai\n\n\nThe Riverie by Katathani (Deluxe Ga