cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'UNIQUE CHIANG MAI CHIANG RAI' package is a 7-day tour covering the culturally rich northern Thai cities of Chiang Mai and Chiang Rai. The itinerary includes visits to the iconic Wat Phra That Doi Suthep, the stunning Wat Rong Khun (White Temple), the historic Golden Triangle, and vibrant local night markets. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, ethical elephant sanctuary interactions, scenic boat rides along the Mekong River, and immersive cultural experiences in traditional hill tribe villages.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive\xa0at\xa0Chiang\xa0Mai.\nWelcome\xa0to\xa0Thailand!\n\xa0\nUpon\xa0arrival\xa0at\xa0the\xa0airport,\xa0pick\xa0up\xa0from\xa0airport\xa0and\xa0transfer\xa0to\xa0your\xa0hotel.\xa0Check\xa0in\xa0at\xa0hotel\xa0(standard\xa0time\xa0approx\xa01400\xa0hrs).\xa0\n\xa0\nRest\xa0of\xa0the\xa0day\xa0is\xa0at\xa0leisure.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Duangtawan Hotel\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Bodhi Serene Chiang Mai\xa0(Value) /\xa0Melia Chiang Mai\xa0(Premium) or similar in Chiang Mai'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nCity\xa0Tour\xa0of\xa0Chiang\xa0Mai\xa0(PVT\xa0basis)\nEnjoy\xa0Breakfast\xa0in\xa0Hotel.\nProceed\xa0to\xa0city\xa0tour\xa0with\xa0visit\xa0to\xa0the\xa0most\xa0interesting\xa0temples:\xa0Wat\xa0Chiang\xa0Man,\xa0The\xa0oldest\xa0temple\xa0in\xa0Chiang\xa0Mai\xa0Town.\xa0The\xa0temple\xa0is\xa0famous\xa0for\xa0its\xa0Lanna style\xa0chedi\xa0supported\xa0by\xa0rows\xa0of\xa0elephant\xa0shaped\xa0buttresses.\xa0Continue\xa0to\xa0Wat\xa0Chedi\xa0Luang,\xa0Wat\xa0Montean,\xa0Wat\xa0Lok\xa0Molee\xa0and\xa0Wat\xa0Suan\xa0Dok.\xa0Later\xa0in\xa0the\xa0afternoon,\xa0we\xa0visit\xa0Chiang\xa0Mai\xa0Night\xa0Market.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Duangtawan Hotel\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Bodhi Serene Chiang Mai\xa0(Value) /\xa0Melia Chiang Mai\xa0(Premium) or similar in Chiang Mai'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0Visit Doi Suthep Monk Trail and Doi Suthep Temple (PVT basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nToday we proceed to a private half day Doi Suthep Monk Trail is a 6.3 kilometer heavily trafficked out and back trail located near Chiang Mai city that features a waterfall and is rated as moderate. The trail is primarily used for hiking and walking. Start hiking trip at Chiang Mai Zoo area. The first section takes you to a small temple (called Wat Pha Lat), take no more than 1 hour. We are serenaded by weird exotic sounds of the forest -birds, insects, grinding bamboos, streams. Wat Pa Lad is the small temple less famous, but has many interesting architecture and sculptures such as the Buddha's statue and pagoda. and is constructed in Burmese architecture style and over 600 years old.\nThe second section is Doi Suthep Temple, the most famous landmark in Chiang Mai. At the top of the temple, you can view the pagoda, believed to enshrine the holy relics of the Lord Buddha, shining with real gold. A viewing platform also offers panoramic view of Chiang Mai City.\nOvernight stay at Chiang Mai.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Duangtawan Hotel\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Bodhi Serene Chiang Mai\xa0(Value) /\xa0Melia Chiang Mai\xa0(Premium) or similar in Chiang Mai'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nElephant Jungle Sanctuary Tour (SIC basis)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nIn the afternoon, proceed to Elephant Jungle Sanctuary Tour. Pick up from hotel and drive approximately 1.5 hours South of Chiang Mai through rolling hills, forest, and local agriculture area. Arrive at the Elephant Jungle Sanctuary.\xa0 Learn about the elephants and change into traditional Karen clothing. Meet the elephants. Feed, interact and play with the elephants in a natural environment as you learn about their behavior and history. Take photos with the elephants. Have a mud spa with the elephants. Walk with the elephants to a river and bathe them. Say goodbye to the elephants and drive back to Chiang Mai.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Duangtawan Hotel\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Bodhi Serene Chiang Mai\xa0(Value) /\xa0Melia Chiang Mai\xa0(Premium) or similar in Chiang Mai'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nChiang Mai – Chiang Rai. Visit Wat Rong Sua Ten (Blue Temple)\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nDepart from Chiang Mai and drive to Chiang Rai on private basis and on the way short stop at Mae Kajan Hot Spring and Wat Rong Khun, the temple is well known for its decorations with white tone decorated reflected mirrors.\nAfternoon visit Wat Rong Sua Ten (Blue Temple) which is in Rong Suea Ten in the district of Rimkok. The interior of the wihan is very beautiful. The entrance is guarded by two spectacular dragon statues. Then, visit the local market and evening explore Walking Street of Chiang Rai (open on Saturday & Sunday only)\nOvernight stay at Chiang Rai.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Wiang\xa0Inn\xa0Hotel (Standard) /\xa0Mora Boutique (Value) /\xa0The\xa0Riverie\xa0by\xa0Katathani (Premium) or Similar in Chiang Rai'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Baan Dam and Golden Triangle Area (PVT basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, private visit Baan Dam (Black House) which is the unique creation of national artist, Thawan Duchanee. Part art studio, part museum, part home. Baan Dam is an eclectic mix of traditional northern Thai buildings interspersed with some outlandish modern designs. Continue to Choui Fong Tea Plantation to enjoy stunning tea plantation views and the best matcha desserts!\n\xa0\nAfter lunch visit to the Golden Triangle area on the bank of the Mekong River where Myanmar, Laos and Thailand border meet. Board a long-tail boat to visit the river bank scenery along Mekhong River. Visit Opium Museum and Wat Pra Thad Jom Kitti by climbing up 383 steps to the top of the hill. Afterwards, visit Long Neck Karen.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Chiang Rai.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Wiang\xa0Inn\xa0Hotel (Standard) /\xa0Phowadol\xa0Resort\xa0and\xa0Spa (Value) /\xa0The\xa0Riverie\xa0by\xa0Katathani (Premium) or Similar in Chiang Rai\xa0(June - Sep 2024)\nWiang\xa0Inn\xa0Hotel (Standard) /\xa0Mora Boutique (Value) /\xa0The\xa0Riverie\xa0by\xa0Katathani (Premium) or Similar in Chiang Rai\xa0(Oct\xa0- Mar 2025)'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDeparture\xa0to\xa0Chiang\xa0Rai\xa0International\xa0Airport\n\xa0\nMorning\xa0after\xa0breakfast;\xa0you\xa0will\xa0be\xa0transferred\xa0to\xa0the\xa0airport\xa0for\xa0your\xa0flight\xa0back\xa0home\xa0to\xa0India.\xa0\n\xa0\n* The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.\nAll travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\n\xa0\nPACKAGE ENVISAGED\xa0\nRATES IN USD PER PERSON\nTravel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 2027\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n\n\n4-5 PAX\n\n\n6-7 PAX\n\n\n8-9 PAX\n\n\n10 PAX\n\n\nINF\n\n\n\n\nSTANDARD\n\n\n730\n\n\n592\n\n\n730\n\n\n553\n\n\n0\n\n\n\n\nVALUE\n\n\n914\n\n\n783\n\n\n914\n\n\n743\n\n\n0\n\n\n\n\nPREMIUM\n\n\n1053\n\n\n914\n\n\n1053\n\n\n882\n\n\n0\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nExtention Night Cost:\nTravel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 2027\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n\n\nSR OTHERS\n\n\nDBL\n\n\nTRPL\n\n\n4-5 PAX\n\n\n6-7 PAX\n\n\n8-9 PAX\n\n\n10 PAX\n\n\nCWB\n\n\nCNB\n\n\nINF\n\n\n\n\nSTANDARD\n\n\n288\n\n\n258\n\n\n258\n\n\n183\n\n\