on Section)\n\nYi Peng Lantern Festival (24-26 NOV'26, tentative)\nLoy Krathong Festival (25 NOV'26)\nPattaya International Fireworks Festival - 27-29 Nov 26\nChristmas & New Year - 15 Dec 26 - 08 Jan 27\xa0\nChinese New Year - 05 Feb 27 - 12 Feb 27\nSongkran - 10 Apr 27 - 17 Apr 27\nUbon Ratchathani Candle Festival (17-22 JUL'27)\n", 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nAll travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\n\xa0\nTERMS AND CONDITIONS:\n\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/chiaingmaiSRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/chaingmaitinerary.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/chiangmaicityitinerary.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/DoiSuthepMonkTraiandDoiSutheptempleitinerary.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/elephantsanctuarychiangmai.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/WatRongSuaTenBlueTempleChiangRAI.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/BaanDamChaingRAI.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG010862/itinerary/chiangrAICITYthAILAND.jpg']}, 'score': 3.5732946, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014465', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014465', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027', 'days': 11, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pattaya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuala Lumpur', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Singapore', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Juice and Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai MassageI Guided City Tour of Bangkok | Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise. Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise"], 'pdfName': 'PKG002219_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 158667, 'packageSummary': "The 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027' is an 11-day package covering Kuala Lumpur, Singapore, Bangkok, and Pattaya. This air-inclusive value tour provides tour manager assistance, visa and insurance, 4-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, and curated Indian meals. Throughout the journey, travelers will enjoy key activities such as a guided city tour of Bangkok, a dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River, a traditional Thai massage, and a visit to Nong Nooch Village in Thailand. In Malaysia, the itinerary features a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and a day trip to Genting, while the Singapore leg includes a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, an exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and a visit to Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'images': ['Pattaya753.jpg', 'CoralISlandnew.jpg', 'WatPhoTemple753.jpg', 'SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'Putramosque753.jpg', 'BatuCave.jpg', 'SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'SentosaIsland2.jpg', 'UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'Singapore7532.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 158667, 'thumbnailImage': 'GrandTourOFAsia267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014465 is named 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027' and spans 11 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Pattaya, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show Welcome To Bangkok, Thailand. Upon Arrival, Proceed To Pattaya & Check Into Your Hotel. Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Enjoy The Alcazar Show. Note All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs. All Guests Have To Fill Up Thai Digital Arrival Card Via The Below Link.Https://Tdac.Immigration.Go.Th/Arrival-Card/#/Home, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pattaya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed For An Exciting Tour Of The Coral Island (Subject To Weather Condition) By Speedboat. Take A Glass Bottom Boat Ride. You Will Have Free Time To Enjoy Water-Sports Activities - Para Sailing, Under Water Walk, Banana Boat Ride, Jet Ski On Your Own.( Kindly Note : Above Mentioned Watersport Activities Are Not A Part Of Our Tour Program. Incase You Plan To Undertake Any Of The Above Activities You Need To Book Them Directly At The Counter.) Return To The Hotel. Later Proceed To Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy The Thai Cultural Show & The Elephant Show In Nong Nooch Village. Later Experience Traditional Thai Massage. Note: For Activities At Coral Island, It Is Important That Guests Are Physically Fit To Travel In Speed Boats (As We Need To Embark & Disembark From The Speed Boat On Floating Pontoons & Excursion To Coral Island Does Not Have Wheelchair Accessibility)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping This Morning After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To Bangkok. Visit The Gems Gallery. Upon Arrival At Bangkok Proceed On A Guided City Tour Alongwith Visits To Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) Followed By Free Time For Shopping., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch Coupon & Transfers( Optional) – Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure,Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Bangkok On Your Own Or Book An On-Tour Optional Excursion And Proceed To Visit Safari World & Marine Park - Famous For It Open Zoo, Wildlife & Various Shows. Later This Evening Enjoy The Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly To Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur This Morning After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To The Airport. Fly To Kuala Lumpur. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers. Note: All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below. Https://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) - Batu Caves This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Kuala Lumpur, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Drive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Visit Gardens By The Bay This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting). Notes: Kindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At Singapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods) All Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mandai Bird Park – Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Singapore, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. CHILD POLICY Infant Child No Bed Child With Bed 0 - 1.99 yrs 2 - 6.99 yrs 7 - 11.99 yrs, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 158667.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), \nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Services of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative. (Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers) If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary. Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. Single - entry Singapore visa. It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Exclusions: The cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. City Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. The tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000. Govt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same. Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. Any expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us. Tips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable) Meals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary Visa Requirements Thailand Visa on arrival* Malaysia Visa on arrival* It is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa) Passport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure. Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa & Insurance 4* Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners Whats More Like - Juice and Coconut Water at certain sightseeing’s Thailand: Visit Nong Nooch Village I Enjoy Traditional Thai MassageI Guided City Tour of Bangkok | Dinner on Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise. Malaysia : Guided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur | Putrajaya Tour | Genting Day Trip Singapore: Guided City Tour of Singapore | Visit Sentosa Island with 5 in 1 Madame Tussauds |Visit Gardens by the Bay - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome I Visit Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Tiruchirappali', 'cityCode': 'TRZ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAJ550', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Grand Bargain Tour of Asia - April 2026 To March 2027' is an 11-day package covering Kuala Lumpur, Singapore, Bangkok, and Pattaya. This air-inclusive value tour provides tour manager assistance, visa and insurance, 4-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, and curated Indian meals. Throughout the journey, travelers will enjoy key activities such as a guided city tour of Bangkok, a dinner cruise on the Chao Phraya River, a traditional Thai massage, and a visit to Nong Nooch Village in Thailand. In Malaysia, the itinerary features a guided city tour of Kuala Lumpur, a Putrajaya tour, and a day trip to Genting, while the Singapore leg includes a guided city tour, a visit to Sentosa Island with Madame Tussauds, an exploration of Gardens by the Bay's Cloud Forest and Flower Dome, and a visit to Mandai Bird Paradise.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive In Bangkok - Proceed To Pattaya – See Alcazar Show\nWelcome To Bangkok, Thailand. Upon Arrival, Proceed To Pattaya & Check Into Your Hotel. Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening Enjoy The Alcazar Show.\n\xa0\nNote\n\nAll Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card\nJoining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs.\xa0\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Thai Digital Arrival Card Via The Below Link.Https://Tdac.Immigration.Go.Th/Arrival-Card/#/Home\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel M Pattaya or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Coral Island By Speedboat - Glass Boat Ride - Visit Nong Nooch Village – Experience A Traditional Thai Massage ( 60 Minutes)\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed For An Exciting Tour Of The Coral Island (Subject To Weather Condition) By Speedboat. Take A Glass Bottom Boat Ride. You Will Have Free Time To Enjoy Water-Sports Activities -\xa0 Para Sailing, Under Water Walk, Banana Boat Ride, Jet Ski On Your Own.( Kindly Note : Above Mentioned Watersport Activities Are Not A Part Of Our Tour Program. Incase You Plan To Undertake Any Of The Above Activities You Need To Book Them Directly At The Counter.)\xa0 Return To The Hotel. Later Proceed To Nong Nooch Village. Enjoy The Thai Cultural Show & The Elephant Show In Nong Nooch Village. Later Experience\xa0 Traditional Thai Massage.\nNote:\nFor Activities At Coral Island, It Is Important That Guests Are Physically Fit To Travel In Speed Boats (As We Need To Embark & Disembark From The Speed Boat On Floating Pontoons & Excursion To Coral Island Does Not Have Wheelchair Accessibility).', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast,\xa0Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel M Pattaya or similar in Pattaya'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Bangkok- Visit Gems Gallery - Guided City Tour Of Bangkok - Visit Wat Traimit Temple\xa0 & Wat Pho Temple – Free Time For Shopping\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To Bangkok. Visit The Gems Gallery. Upon Arrival At Bangkok Proceed On A Guided City Tour Alongwith Visits To Wat Traimit (Golden Buddha Temple) & Wat Pho (Reclining Buddha Temple) Followed By Free Time For Shopping.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel A-One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch Coupon & Transfers( Optional) \xa0– Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure,Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Bangkok On Your Own Or Book An On-Tour Optional Excursion And Proceed To Visit Safari World & Marine Park - Famous For It Open Zoo, Wildlife & Various Shows. Later This Evening Enjoy The Chao Phraya Dinner Cruise.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel A-One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nFly To Kuala Lumpur - Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya- Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast Check Out & Proceed To The Airport. Fly To Kuala Lumpur. Upon Arrival, Proceed On Orientation Tour Of Putrajaya Followed By Check In To The Hotel. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later This Evening\xa0Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Kuala Lumpur Alongwith Photo Stops At Istana Negara (New King's Palace) , National Monument, Merdeka Square (Independence Square) & The Petronas Twin Towers.\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0All Guest Have To Fill Up Malaysian Digital Arrival Card Via The Link Given Below.\nHttps://Imigresen-Online.Imi.Gov.My/Mdac/Main?Registermain\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Chocolate Boutique - Day Excursion To Genting Highland -Visit Skyworld Theme Park (Outdoor Park) -\xa0 Batu Caves\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Chocolate Boutique. Later, Proceed To The Skyway Cable Car Station For A Ride Up To Genting Highlands. Visit The Skyworld Theme Park. Later Take A Return Cable Car To The Skyway Cable Car Station. Visit Batu Caves.\xa0 ', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Sunway Lagoon With Lunch Coupon & Transfers (Optional)\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Kuala Lumpur On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDrive To Singapore - Guided City Tour Of Singapore\xa0 - Visit Gardens By The Bay\xa0\xa0\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast,\xa0 Check Out & Drive To Singapore. Upon Arrival, Proceed To The Hotel & Check In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Proceed\xa0 For A Guided City Tour Of Singapore - Drive Pass Suntek City, Business District, China Town, Orchard, Buddha Tooth Relic Temple & Merlion Park. Later This Evening Visit Gardens By The Bay - Visit The Cloud Forest Dome With Jurassic World Exhibition\xa0 & Flower Dome Followed By Light & Sound Show (Weather Permitting).\xa0\n\xa0\nNotes:\xa0\n\nKindly Take A Note Of Prohibited Items That Are Not To Be Carried In Singapore. At\nSingapore Immigration All Bags Will Be Scanned And Checked Before Customs And Immigration. No Trolleys Or Porters Are Available At This Point & Every Guest Needs To Hand Carry Luggage Through Singapore Customs.(Https:// Www.Customs.Gov.Sg/Individuals/Going-Throughcustoms/Arrival/Prohibited-And- Controlled- Goods)\nAll Guests Have To Fill Up Singapore Landing Card On Sg Arrival App.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Mandai Bird Park –\xa0 Visit Sentosa Island By One Way Cable Car\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Mandai Bird Paradise, Home To Over 5,000 Birds Across 400 Species, Making It One Of The Largest Bird Parks In The World. Later, Proceed To Sentosa Island By A One-Way Cable Car Ride. On Arrival At Sentosa Island - Visit Madame Tussauds With Bollywood Avenue, Spirit Of Singapore, Images Of Singapore, Boat Ride. Later This Evening Enjoy The Spectacular Wings Of Time Show -A Dazzling Display Of Water, Laser, And Fire Effects.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure Or Visit Universal Studio & Singapore Oceanarium With Lunch Coupon & Transfers \xa0(Optional)\nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Singapore On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back \nThis Morning \xa0After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\nCHILD POLICY\n\n\n\n\nInfant\n\n\nChild No Bed\n\n\nChild With Bed\n\n\n\n\n0 - 1.99 yrs\n\n\n2 - 6.99 yrs\n\n\n7 - 11.99 yrs\n\n\n\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': '\n02 nights accommodation at M Hotel / Heeton Concept Hotel by Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Montien Riverside / Away Bangkok Riverside Kene Hotel / Cross Vibe Bangkok Hotel or similar in Bangkok\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'SG', 'countryName': 'Singapore', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'TH', 'countryName': 'Thailand', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'MY', 'countryName': 'Malaysia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 158700.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 Nights accommodation at M Hotel Pattaya or similar in Pattaya\n02 nights\xa0 accommodation at A- One Bangkok / Grand Howard or similar in Bangkok\xa0\n03 nights’ accommodation at Grand Continental / Trigo or similar in Kuala Lumpur\xa0\n03 Nights’ accommodation at Ibis Bencoolen / Hilton Garden Inn or similar in Singapore\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n05 Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', '\nDaily buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Pattaya:\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBangkok:\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n\n\xa0\nKuala\xa0Lumpur:\n\nOrientation Tour of Putrajaya\nGuided City Tour of Kuala Lumpur\nPhoto stop at Petronas Twin Tower\nVisit Batu Caves\nGenting Highlands with 2 ways cable car\nVisit Genting Sky world Theme Park ( Outdoor Park)\nVisit to Chocolate Boutique\n\n\xa0\nSingapore:\n\nGuided city tour of Singapore\xa0\nVisit Gardens by the Bay\xa0 - Entrance to Cloud Forest with Jurassic World Exhibition & Flower Dome\nVisit Mandai Bird Paradise\xa0\nVisit Sentosa Island by One way Cable car ride\nVisit Madame Tussauds with Bollywood Avenue, Spirit of Singapore, Images of Singapore, Boat Ride\xa0\nWings of Time Show\n', 'PATTAYA\n\nEntrance to Alcazar Show\nVisit Coral Island with Speed boat & Glass bottom boat ride\nVisit Nong Nooch Village - See Elephant & Thai Cultural Show\xa0\nTraditional Thai Massage ( 60 minutes)\n\n\xa0\nBANGKOK\n\nGuided city tour of Bangkok\xa0 - Visit to Wat Pho Temple & Wat Traimit Temple\nVisit Safari World & Marine Park (Optional)\nChao Phraya Dinner Cruise\nFree time for shopping\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVisa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nServices of a professional & multilingual Tour Manager or Local representative.\n(Tour Manager subject to minimum 20 customers)\nIf the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nSingle - entry Singapore visa.\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of deviation, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCity Tax or Tourism tax (If applicable)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges, porterage and passport charges.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 10,000.\nGovt Taxes & Service taxes as applicable.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st December\xa02025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. The company will not be held responsible for the same.\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nAny expenses of personal nature such as laundry, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menus provided by us.\nTips to guides, hotel waiters, drivers etc. (If applicable)\nMeals other than what is mentioned in the itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers other than those included in your itinerary\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements\n\nThailand Visa on arrival*\xa0\nMalaysia Visa on arrival*\xa0\xa0\nIt is compulsory to hold a hard copy of Visa Paper (In case of E visa)\nPassport should be valid for 6 months from the date of departure\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/GrandTourOFAsia267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Pattaya753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/CoralISlandnew.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/WatPhoTemple753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/SafariWorldBangkok_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Putramosque753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/BatuCave.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/SunwayLagoonMalaysia.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Gardensbythebay753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/SentosaIsland2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/UniversalStudio753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014465/itinerary/Singapore7532.jpg']}, 'score': 3.5732946, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG010858', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG010858', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'UNIQUE BANGKOK KANCHANABURI', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kanchanaburi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kanchanaburi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG010858_0_20261008195516.pdf', 'price': 70030, 'packageSummary': "The 'UNIQUE BANGKOK KANCHANABURI' package is a 6-day tour covering the bustling metropolis of Bangkok and the scenic, historic province of Kanchanaburi. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Grand Palace, Wat Pho, the historic Bridge over the River Kwai, and the Allied War Cemetery. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing, a scenic train ride along the infamous Death Railway, a boat ride through local floating markets, and a chance to explore the stunning multi-tiered waterfalls of Erawan National Park.", 'images': ['Mahanakhon_SkyWalk.png', 'floatingmrketthailand.jpeg', 'kanchanburiiiitinerary.jpg', 'naturalimagekanchanabureitinerary.jpg', 'Thailand2.jpg', 'Thailand_bangkok.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 70030, 'thumbnailImage': 'Thailand9.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Couple Special'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG010858 is named 'UNIQUE BANGKOK KANCHANABURI' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Bangkok, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive at Bangkok. Visit Mahanakhon Sky Walk (incl.soft drink only) (SIC basis) Welcome to Thailand! Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx 1400 hrs). Today we visit Mahanakhon Skywalk, Thailand’s highest observation deck at 314 meters offers 360 degree panoramic views from an indoor and outdoor viewing area, and is a must-see attraction to add to your Bangkok bucket list., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Visit Damnoen Saduak Floating Market (SIC basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Damnoen Saduak is one of the most popular floating markets around Bangkok. It has a lot of amazing things to look forward to, from shopping to dining and strolling around., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kanchanaburi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bangkok – Kanchanaburi (PVT basis). Kanchanaburi City Tour (SIC basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Today we check out and transfer to Kanchanaburi. Start your tour with a visit to war cemeteries, JEATH War Museum, and last but not least, the Bridge over the River Kwai - the prominent places that always remind you of the WWII history and Kao Poon Cave & Temple., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kanchanaburi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Adventure and Nature Explore Tour (SIC basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Pick up from hotel to join Adventure and Nature Explore in Kanchanaburi. Depart the hotel for Erawan Waterfall National Park. Upon arrival, start to trek along its nature trail to the splendid waterfalls inside. Then enjoy relaxing and swimming in the emerald-coloured pools. After Lunch, continue a journey to enjoy elephant riding and rafting. Enjoy the train excursion from Wang Poh to Tha Kilaen stations along the Death Railway. We then head back to the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Kanchanaburi – Bangkok (PVT basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Today we check out and transfer to Bangkok. Rest of the day is at leisure to explore on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th PACKAGE ENVISAGED Travel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 2027 CATEGORY 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-9 PAX 10 PAX INF STANDARD 671 638 671 651 0 VALUE 724 691 724 697 0 PREMIUM 842 816 842 822 0 EXTENSION NIGHT Travel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 2027 CATEGORY 4-5 PAX 6-7 PAX 8-9 PAX 10 PAX INF STANDARD 168 160 168 163 0 VALUE 181 173 181 174 0 PREMIUM 211 204 211 206 0, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 70030.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n3N\xa0Accomodation\xa0in\xa0Ramada by Wyndham D’Ma (Superior Room) or similar in Bangkok\n2N Accomodation\xa0in River Kwai Village (Cliff Wing room) or similar in Kanchanaburi\n, \n3N\xa0Accomodation\xa0in\xa0The Berkeley Pratunam (Luxury room) or similar in Bangkok\n2N Accomodation\xa0in Home Phu-Toey (Deluxe room) or similar in Kanchanaburi\n, \n3N\xa0Accomodation\xa0in\xa0The Ecotel Bangkok (Superior) or similar in Bangkok\n2N Accomodation\xa0in\xa0Pung-Waan Resort Kwai Noi (Standard) or similar in Kanchanaburi\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Bangkok 02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Kanchanaburi Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Airport / hotel / airport transfers on PVT basis Visit Mahanakhon Sky Walk (SIC Basis) Visit Damnoen Saduak Floating Market (SIC basis) Kanchanaburi City Tour (SIC basis) Adventure and Nature Explore Tour (SIC basis) Travel Insurance - Valid for 7 days up to the age of 60 years. Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa charges Departure PCR test, if applicable The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times All flights services Meals not mentioned in the itinerary Any tips (Around USD 05.00 per person / per day) - for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge SURCHARGE of USD 15 per person for Pick Up & Drop At DMK Airport. GENERAL BLACKOUTS Ubon Ratchathani Candle Festival (5-11 JUL'25), Pattaya Marathon (19-21 JUL'25) Asahna Bucha Day - 10 Jul'25 Loy Krathong Festival (5 NOV'25), Yi Peng Lantern Festival (4-6 NOV'25, tentative). CHRISTMAS & NEW YEAR 15 DEC'25 - 05 JAN'26 Chinese New Year 2026 (ON REQUEST) Tue, 10 Feb, 2026 – Tue, 3 Mar, 2026 SONGKRAN 05 APR - 19 APR'26. Product Terms and Conditions: All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration: https://tdac.immigration.go.th TERMS AND CONDITIONS: The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for eac