 list.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'All travelers entering Thailand (by air, land, or sea) will be required to complete the Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) process online before arriving. Register within 3 days before your arrival. Please click on the link given here for Thailand Digital Arrival Card (TDAC) registration:\xa0https://tdac.immigration.go.th\nCHILD POLICY\n\nInfant: 0-1.99 yrs\nChild No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs\nChild With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs\n\n\xa0\nA person aged 12 years and below is considered a child, while anyone above 12 years is classified as an adult.\n\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nThe package price is valid until 27 March 2027.\nRates are valid for a minimum of 02 adults travelling together.\nHotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nHotel upgrade pricing does not guarantee rooms at the preferred / envisaged hotels.\nHotel upgrade rooms remain subject to availability at the time of booking.\nIf the selected upgrade hotel is unavailable, we will provide alternate options for a similar category.\nThe rates are not valid on blackout dates & Trade Fair periods.\xa0\nAny applicable surcharges will be communicated, and passengers will be required to pay them accordingly.\nSurcharges, if applicable, are additional to the total package price quoted at the time of booking.\nGuests are requested to confirm their onward/connecting flights with the sales team before booking.\nAll rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing at the time of booking.\nWe reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\xa0\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\xa0\nInternational Check in time is 1400/1500 hours & Check out time is 1100/1200 hours respectively, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\nWherever transfers are included, they are provided without night surcharges.\nNo refunds (partial or full) will be provided for any unutilized services.\nAll sightseeing tours and excursions are operated by local service providers; timings and operating days are subject to change. Changes or Updates, if any, will be shared at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly subject to weather conditions, and local service providers reserve the right to cancel tours without prior notice.\nRates are subject to change without prior notice, including for clients travelling during weekends.\nAny promotional offer, if applicable, may be withdrawn at any time without prior notice.\nOnce bookings are confirmed, cancellation charges will apply as per policy and will be informed at that time.\nOrganization is not responsible for any price changes arising from factors beyond our control.\nA refundable security deposit is required at check in as per international hotel policy, payable by credit card or cash; the amount varies by hotel and is returned at check out. Guests should avoid using debit cards since the amount is charged instantly and may take 2–3 weeks to refund. Any additional hotel services (such as mini bar, room service, etc.) may be deducted from this deposit, and Company is not responsible for such transactions, as these are directly between the hotel and the guest.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG009665/Phuket_SRP.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG009665/itinerary/85745_paradise_beach_Phuket_Thailand753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG009665/itinerary/8097_Long_Tail_Boat_Phuket_Thailand753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG009665/itinerary/753_Chalong_temple_Phuket.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG009665/itinerary/43654_Karon_View_Point_Phuket_Thailand_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG009665/itinerary/161992_Promthep_Cape_View_Phuket_Thailand_753.jpg']}, 'score': 3.5732946, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012805', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012805', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'CLASSIC HUA HIN BANGKOK', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Hua Hin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Hua Hin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Hua Hin', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bangkok', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012805_0_20261008194354.pdf', 'price': 80206, 'packageSummary': "The 'CLASSIC HUA HIN BANGKOK' package is a 6-day tour covering the vibrant metropolis of Bangkok and the serene coastal resort town of Hua Hin. Throughout this exciting journey, travelers will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, visit historic temples, and explore bustling local night markets. The itinerary also offers ample time to relax on the beautiful beaches of Hua Hin, indulge in authentic Thai cuisine, and experience the unique blend of modern city life and coastal tranquility.", 'images': ['Hua Hin_C.jfif', 'Remarkable-thailand-winter_C.jpg', 'Hua-Hin-High-Light_VineYard_C.jpg', 'Chaophray.jpg', 'GoldenBuddhatheTempleThailand.jpg', 'Thailand_bangkok.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 80206, 'thumbnailImage': 'HuaHin2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG012805 is named 'CLASSIC HUA HIN BANGKOK' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Hua Hin, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive at Bangkok. Transfer to Hua Hin. Enroute visit Swiss Sheep Farm and Vana Nava Water Jungle Park (PVT Basis) Welcome to Thailand! Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.) Enroute we visit the Swiss Sheep Farm. Take a detour from Hua Hin’s traditional sightseeing spots and head to one of its most original attractions — Swiss Sheep Farm. Take a stroll through a real countryside farm inspired by the picturesque farmlands of Switzerland and explore charming European architecture. Later we visit Vana Nava Water Jungle Park. Vana Nava Water Park Hua Hin is one of Thailand's finest water parks! More than just amazing sets with pipes, waterfalls, and fountains, it also offers thrilling rides, slides, and world-class facilities. Overnight in Hua Hin, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Hua Hin, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Visit Damnoen Saduak Floating Market (Motor Boat include) (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. The Damnoen Saduak floating markets provide tourists with an intimate view of daily life at sea in Thailand. Join your guide as they navigate through the backwaters of Bangkok's canals in a motorboat, stopping by local merchants to see what they have to offer - from fresh fruits and vegetables, to mementos and artisanal confectioneries made in classic canoes. This unique adventure is ideal for those eager to step away from the bustling urban areas and immerse themselves in a taste of the local culture and essence. Overnight stay at Hua Hin., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Hua Hin, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Visit Hua Hin High Light + Vine Yard (SIC Basis) Evening Hua Hin Night Market (SIC Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Take in breathtaking views of the sea from Monkey Mountain (Khao Takiab); walk through Rajabhakti Park, known for its massive statues of Thai Kings; and check out the Buddhist temple of Wat Huay Mongkol. Conclude the day with a guided tour of the Hua Hin Hills Vineyard, renowned for its selection of 'new latitude wines'. Later we visit Hua Hin Night Market, which combines contemporary art, inventions, handmade work, home decorations, clothes, second-hand appliances and SME products with creative ideas to show and sell for visitors. Overnight stay at Hua Hin., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Hua Hin – Bangkok. Evening Chaophraya Dinner Cruise Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Transfer form Hua Hin to Bangkok, Check-in at the Hotel. Later, Today we Indulge in luxury with 5-star cruises on the Chaophraya River offered by The Chaophraya Cruise in Bangkok. Experience the beauty of Thai exquisite architecture and immerse yourself in the rich cultural and historical heritage of Thailand, all while cruising elegantly along the river. Marvel at iconic landmarks such as the Temple of Dawn (Wat Arun), the Grand Palace, the Suspension Rama VIII Bridge, Asiatique, and the stunning waterfront hotels. Enjoy a delectable Thai and International buffet, top-notch beverages, cocktails, and live music featuring a saxophone for an unforgettable cruising experience. Overnight stay at Bangkok, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Visit Bangkok City Tour (Golden Buddha + Marble Buddha) (SIC Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Visit Thailand’s famous attractions today as you drive past the city. Visit Bangkok City & Temples (Golden Buddha Temple & Marble Temple). Overnight stay at Bangkok., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bangkok, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. * The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. PACKAGE ENVISAGED Travel Validity – 01 Oct 2026 – 25 MAR 