2026-10-13 03:58:04,756 - voice_bot.livekit - INFO - Search packages by name response: [{'id': 'PKG013464', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013464', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Mesmerizing Kashmir', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Sonamarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Meal Daily Breakfast 05 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013464_0_20260722110900.pdf', 'price': 25860, 'packageSummary': "The 'Mesmerizing Kashmir' package is a 7-day tour covering Srinagar, Pahalgam, Sonamarg, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features memorable experiences such as a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake, a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, and an exciting Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg. Travelers will also enjoy visits to the beautiful Shalimar Bagh, Nishat Bagh, and ABC Valley, with all entry tickets included. Throughout the journey, participants will benefit from daily breakfast, five complimentary dining experiences, private chauffeur-driven transfers and sightseeing, and travel insurance for those under 69 years of age.", 'images': ['5110653473_0bcbca9659_k.jpg', '53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'Aruvalley.jpg', '20036255981_8352f56000_b.jpg', 'Dal_Lake.jpg', '20353066101_3492de1ddd_o.jpg', '7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 25860, 'thumbnailImage': '20036255981_8352f56000_b.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013464 is named \'Mesmerizing Kashmir\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Na, Description: Arrive in Srinagar Welcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver. Transfer from Airport to Hotel and check-in at the hotel. You can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit. Visit Shalimar Bagh Visit Nishant Bagh Enjoy shikara ride in Dal lake. (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Overnight Srinagar at the Houseboat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Pahalgam After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for ABC Valley Tour. Betaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab") Enjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam Note: Day excursion to Betaab, and Chandanwari is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Sonamarg, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Pahalgam to Sonmarg (166 Kms / approx 05 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Sonmarg - Golden Meadow. Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Sonmarg, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Sonmarg to Srinagar (80 Kms / approx 02 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Srinagar - Evening is free for shopping. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Srinagar – Excursion to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", Arrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) Later proceed to Srinagar. En-route visit Handloom Emporium. Arrive into Srinagar and Check In Houseboat. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Srinagar - Fly Back Home Departure from Srinagar: Today after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!! Special Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 25860.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n05 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n. Inclusions: Assistance on Arrival. Meal:- Daily Breakfast 05 Complimentary Dinner 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Kashmiri lunch on the lake. (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle All transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills ) All currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Exclusions: Any Air or Rail fare. Any other meal not mentioned in price includes. Any other destination not mentioned in itinerary. Any monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges. Any expenses of personal nature. GST @ Current Rate SUPPLEMENT STANDARD VALUE PREMIUM Upgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle] 11025 11025 11025. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] BASICS Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. HOTELS Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same. OTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills Guests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card) Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Food in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy. Being Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited. Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle. Do Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do not Drink or Smoke in Public Places; Do check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption. Do not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult. Take Proper permits are required to take video or film; Do not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation Leave Places Better than you found it! Most leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes. Jai Hind!. Highlights of the package: Meal Daily Breakfast 05 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs).', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Mesmerizing Kashmir' package is a 7-day tour covering Srinagar, Pahalgam, Sonamarg, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features memorable experiences such as a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake, a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, and an exciting Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg. Travelers will also enjoy visits to the beautiful Shalimar Bagh, Nishat Bagh, and ABC Valley, with all entry tickets included. Throughout the journey, participants will benefit from daily breakfast, five complimentary dining experiences, private chauffeur-driven transfers and sightseeing, and travel insurance for those under 69 years of age.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive in Srinagar\n\xa0\nWelcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver.\n\xa0\nTransfer from Airport to Hotel and check-in at the hotel. You can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit.\nVisit Shalimar Bagh\nVisit Nishant Bagh\nEnjoy shikara ride in Dal lake.\n\xa0\n(Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\nOvernight Srinagar at the Houseboat.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nNa', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - Royale Comfort/Himalayn Hill/River View or similar in Pahalgam\nValue - Hotel The Kudrat / Hotel Walnut Creek or similar in Pahalgam\nPremium - Hotel ITC Fortune or similar in Pahalgam\n\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for ABC Valley Tour.\n\xa0\nBetaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab")\n\xa0\nEnjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam\n\xa0\nNote: Day excursion to Betaab, and Chandanwari is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - Royale Comfort/Himalayn Hill/River View or similar in Pahalgam\nValue - Hotel The Kudrat / Hotel Walnut Creek or similar in Pahalgam\nPremium - Hotel ITC Fortune or similar in Pahalgam\n\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam to Sonmarg (166 Kms / approx 05 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for\xa0 Sonmarg - Golden Meadow.\xa0Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. \n\xa0\nSonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). \n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Sonmarg', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - Glacier Heights/ Hotel Divine Inn or smilar in Sonmarg\nValue - Hotel Village walk or smilar in Sonmarg\nPremium - HOTEL Four Points By Sheraton, Sonmarg or smilar in Sonmarg\n\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nSonmarg to Srinagar (80 Kms / approx 02 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Srinagar - Evening is free for shopping. \n\xa0\nDinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar. ', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nSrinagar – Excursion to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", \n\xa0\nArrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of\xa0 Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) \n\xa0\nLater proceed to Srinagar. En-route visit Handloom Emporium. Arrive into Srinagar and Check In Houseboat. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\xa0\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar - Fly Back Home\n\xa0\nDeparture from Srinagar:\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!!\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking. ', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 25900.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 34100.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 50000.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n05 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Assistance on Arrival.\nMeal:-\n\nDaily Breakfast \n05 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Kashmiri lunch on the lake. (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n\nExperience Or Activity\n\nShikara ride on Dal Lake\n01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire\nGondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)\n\nEntrance Or Entry tickets\n\nEntry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh\nEntry Ticket for Nishant Bagh\nEntry Ticket for ABC Valley\n\nNote: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\n\nPrivate Chauffeur Driven Vehicle\nAll transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills )\nAll currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate\n\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\xa0SUPPLEMENT\nSTANDARD\nVALUE\nPREMIUM\n\n\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n11025\n11025\n11025\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\n\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/20036255981_8352f56000_b.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/5110653473_0bcbca9659_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/Aruvalley.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/20036255981_8352f56000_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/Dal_Lake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/20353066101_3492de1ddd_o.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013464/itinerary/7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg']}, 'score': 5.670021, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013460', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013460', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Full Of Kashmir', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gulmarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Meal Daily Breakfast 05 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013460_0_20260720145846.pdf', 'price': 29680, 'packageSummary': "The 'Full Of Kashmir' package is a 7-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. Throughout this journey, travelers will enjoy daily breakfast, five complimentary dining experiences, and seamless transfers and sightseeing in a private chauffeur-driven vehicle. The itinerary is packed with memorable highlights, including a traditional Shikara ride on Dal Lake with a special photography session in Kashmiri attire, and a scenic Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg. Additionally, the package includes entry tickets to the stunning Shalimar Bagh, Nishat Bagh, and ABC Valley, ensuring a comprehensive and hassle-free exploration of the region's most beautiful sights.", 'images': ['5110653473_0bcbca9659_k.jpg', '53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'Aruvalley.jpg', '25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', 'Dal_Lake.jpg', '51377664923_70aae44865_h.jpg', '7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 29680, 'thumbnailImage': '3262037185_bc0bfb81af_k.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013460 is named \'Full Of Kashmir\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Na, Description: Arrive in Srinagar Welcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver. Transfer from the airport to the hotel and check in. You can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit. Visit Shalimar Bagh Visit Nishant Bagh Enjoy shikara ride in Dal lake. (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Overnight Srinagar at the Houseboat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Pahalgam After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for ABC Valley Tour. Betaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab") Enjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam Note: Day excursion to Betaab, and Chandanwari is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Gulmarg, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", Arrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg. Note: - In case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg. In Gulmarg - The vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Gulmarg to Srinagar (50 Kms / approx 02 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Srinagar - Evening is free for shopping. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Excursion to Sonmarg (83 Kms / approx 02 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Sonmarg - Golden Meadow. Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). Return back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Srinagar - Fly Back Home Departure from Srinagar: Today after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!! Special Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 29680.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n05 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n. Inclusions: Assistance on Arrival. Meal:- Daily Breakfast 05 Complimentary Dinner 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle All transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills ) All currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Exclusions: Any Air or Rail fare. Any other meal not mentioned in price includes. Any other destination not mentioned in itinerary. Any monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges. Any expenses of personal nature. GST @ Current Rate SUPPLEMENT STANDARD VALUE PREMIUM Upgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle] 11025 11025 11025. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. BASICS Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. HOTELS Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same. OTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills Guests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card) Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Food in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy. Being Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited. Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle. Do Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do not Drink or Smoke in Public Places; Do check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption. Do not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult. Take Proper permits are required to take video or film; Do not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation Leave Places Better than you found it! Most leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes. Jai Hind!. Highlights of the package: Meal Daily Breakfast 05 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle.', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Full Of Kashmir' package is a 7-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. Throughout this journey, travelers will enjoy daily breakfast, five complimentary dining experiences, and seamless transfers and sightseeing in a private chauffeur-driven vehicle. The itinerary is packed with memorable highlights, including a traditional Shikara ride on Dal Lake with a special photography session in Kashmiri attire, and a scenic Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg. Additionally, the package includes entry tickets to the stunning Shalimar Bagh, Nishat Bagh, and ABC Valley, ensuring a comprehensive and hassle-free exploration of the region's most beautiful sights.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive in Srinagar\n\xa0\nWelcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver.\n\xa0\nTransfer from the airport to the hotel and check in. You can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit.\n\xa0\nVisit Shalimar Bagh\nVisit Nishant Bagh\nEnjoy shikara ride in Dal lake.\n\xa0\n(Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\nOvernight Srinagar at the Houseboat.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nNa', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nStandard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nStandard - Royale Comfort/Himalayn Hill/River View or similar in Pahalgam\nValue - Hotel The Kudrat / Hotel Walnut Creek or similar in Pahalgam\nPremium - Hotel ITC Fortune or similar in Pahalgam\n\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for ABC Valley Tour.\n\xa0\xa0\nBetaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab")\n\xa0\xa0\nEnjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam\n\xa0\nNote: Day excursion to Betaab, and Chandanwari is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nStandard - Royale Comfort/Himalayn Hill/River View or similar in Pahalgam\nValue - Hotel The Kudrat / Hotel Walnut Creek or similar in Pahalgam\nPremium - Hotel ITC Fortune or similar in Pahalgam\n\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", \n\xa0\nArrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of\xa0 Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) \n\xa0\nDinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg. \n\xa0\nNote: -\nIn case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg.\nIn Gulmarg - The vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis.\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nStandard - Hotel Zahgeer or similar in Gulmarg\nValue -Hotel Pine Spring / Hotel Rosewood or similar in Gulmarg\nPremium - Hotel Hilltop / Hotel The Vintage or similar in Gulmarg'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nGulmarg to Srinagar (50 Kms / approx 02 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Srinagar - Evening is free for shopping. \n\xa0\nDinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar. ', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nStandard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion to Sonmarg (83 Kms / approx 02 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Sonmarg - Golden Meadow.\xa0Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. \n\xa0\nSonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). \n\xa0\nReturn back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nStandard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar - Fly Back Home\n\xa0\nDeparture from Srinagar:\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!!\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking. ', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 29700.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 31000.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 44800.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n05 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Assistance on Arrival.\nMeal:-\n\nDaily Breakfast \n05 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n\nExperience Or Activity\n\nShikara ride on Dal Lake\n01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire\nGondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)\n\nEntrance Or Entry tickets\n\nEntry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh\nEntry Ticket for Nishant Bagh\nEntry Ticket for ABC Valley\n\nNote: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\n\nPrivate Chauffeur Driven Vehicle\nAll transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills )\nAll currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate\n\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\xa0SUPPLEMENT\nSTANDARD\nVALUE\nPREMIUM\n\n\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n11025\n11025\n11025\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/3262037185_bc0bfb81af_k.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/5110653473_0bcbca9659_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/Aruvalley.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/Dal_Lake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/51377664923_70aae44865_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013460/itinerary/7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg']}, 'score': 5.0943527, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013456', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013456', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Best Of Kashmir', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gulmarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Meal Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013456_0_20261008114149.pdf', 'price': 28120, 'packageSummary': "The 'Best Of Kashmir' package is a 6-day tour covering Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake complete with a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, a thrilling Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg, and visits to the beautiful Shalimar Bagh and Nishat Bagh gardens. Participants will enjoy daily breakfast, four complimentary dining experiences, and seamless transfers and sightseeing in a private chauffeur-driven vehicle, with travel insurance included for travelers under 69 years of age.", 'images': ['52752121832_5d39a1535f_h.jpg', '49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', '53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'AdobeStock_811215833.avif', 'AdobeStock_236611875.avif', '7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 28120, 'thumbnailImage': '8515523204_db73b32068_k.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013456 is named \'Best Of Kashmir\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Na, Description: Arrive in Srinagar Welcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver. Transfer from Airport to Houseboat And check-in at the houseboat, you can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for Visit . Visit Shalimar Bagh Visit Nishant Bagh Enjoy shikara ride in Dal lake. (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Overnight Srinagar at the Houseboat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath. Overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Pahalgam (Day Trip - ABC Valley Tour) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for ABC Valley Tour. Aru valley (Scenic meadows ,Natural environment and scenery) Betaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab") Chandanwari (Starting point for the Amarnath Yatra and a popular hiking spot) Enjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own. overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam Note: Day excursion to Betaab, and Chandanwari is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Gulmarg, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", Arrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg. Note: - In case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg. Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but subject to availability. Clients can also check and pre book on www.jammukashmircablecar.com . However, pls. be noted, Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling. In Gulmarg - The vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Gulmarg to Srinagar (60 Kms / 02 hrs). After Breakfast, proceed for Transfer to Srinagar. Overnight stay at hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Gulmarg to Srinagar - Fly Back Home Departure from Srinagar: Today after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!! Special Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 28120.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n. Inclusions: Assistance on Arrival. Meal:- Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dinner 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Entry Ticket for ABC Valley (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle All transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills ) All currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Exclusions: Any Air or Rail fare. Any other meal not mentioned in price includes. Any other destination not mentioned in itinerary. Any monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges. Any expenses of personal nature. GST @ Current Rate SUPPLEMENT STANDARD VALUE PREMIUM Upgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle] 9450 9450 9450. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. BASICS Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. HOTELS Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same. OTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills Guests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card) Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Food in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy. Being Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited. Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle. Do Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do not Drink or Smoke in Public Places; Do check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption. Do not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult. Take Proper permits are required to take video or film; Do not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation Leave Places Better than you found it! Most leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes. Jai Hind!. Highlights of the package: Meal Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs).', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Best Of Kashmir' package is a 6-day tour covering Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake complete with a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, a thrilling Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg, and visits to the beautiful Shalimar Bagh and Nishat Bagh gardens. Participants will enjoy daily breakfast, four complimentary dining experiences, and seamless transfers and sightseeing in a private chauffeur-driven vehicle, with travel insurance included for travelers under 69 years of age.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive in Srinagar\n\xa0\nWelcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfer from Airport to Houseboat And check-in at the houseboat, you can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for Visit .\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Shalimar Bagh\n\xa0\nVisit Nishant Bagh\n\xa0\nEnjoy shikara ride in Dal lake.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\n(Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\nOvernight Srinagar at the Houseboat.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nNa', 'overnightStay': 'Royal Batoo Hotel (Standard)/ The Kabo (Value) / Hotel Four Points By Sheraton (Premium) Or Similar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'White Water Resort\xa0 (Standard)/\xa0 Hotel Walnut Creek (Value) / Eden Resort & Spa (Premium)\xa0or Similar\n\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': 'Pahalgam (Day Trip - ABC Valley Tour)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for ABC Valley Tour.\nAru valley (Scenic meadows ,Natural environment and scenery)\nBetaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab")\nChandanwari (Starting point for the Amarnath Yatra and a popular hiking spot)\nEnjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own.\n\xa0\novernight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam\n\xa0\nNote: Day excursion to Betaab, and Chandanwari is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'White Water Resort\xa0 (Standard)/\xa0 Hotel Walnut Creek (Value) / Eden Resort & Spa (Premium) or Similar\n\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': 'Srinagar to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers",\n\xa0\nArrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of\xa0 Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis)\n\xa0\nDinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.\n\xa0\nNote: -\nIn case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg.\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but subject to availability. Clients can also check and pre book on www.jammukashmircablecar.com . However, pls. be noted, Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling.\nIn Gulmarg - The vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Zahgeer (Standard)/ Hotel Rosewood (Value) / Hotel Hilltop (Premium) or Similar'}, {'day': 5, 'description': 'Gulmarg to Srinagar (60 Kms / 02 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Breakfast, proceed for Transfer to Srinagar.\nOvernight stay at hotel.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Royal Batoo Hotel (Standard)/ The Kabo (Value) / Hotel Four Points By Sheraton (Premium) Or Similar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nGulmarg to Srinagar - Fly Back Home\n\xa0\nDeparture from Srinagar:\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!!\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your\xa0\xa0reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 28100.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 34200.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 48300.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Assistance on Arrival.\nMeal:-\n\nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n\nExperience Or Activity\n\nShikara ride on Dal Lake\n01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire\nGondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)\n\nEntrance Or Entry tickets\n\nEntry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh\nEntry Ticket for Nishant Bagh\nEntry Ticket for ABC Valley\n\n(Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\nPrivate Chauffeur Driven Vehicle\n\nAll transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills )\nAll currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\xa0SUPPLEMENT\nSTANDARD\nVALUE\nPREMIUM\n\n\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n9450\n9450\n9450\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/8515523204_db73b32068_k.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/itinerary/52752121832_5d39a1535f_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/itinerary/53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/itinerary/AdobeStock_811215833.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/itinerary/AdobeStock_236611875.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013456/itinerary/7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg']}, 'score': 5.0943527, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013455', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013455', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Kashmir With Pahalgam Special', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Meal Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dine 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013455_0_20260720132722.pdf', 'price': 22480, 'packageSummary': "The 'Kashmir With Pahalgam Special' package is a 6-day tour covering the beautiful destinations of Pahalgam and Srinagar. The itinerary features a variety of memorable activities, including a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake with a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, a thrilling Phase-1 Gondola ride at Gulmarg, and visits to the historic Shalimar Bagh and Nishat Bagh gardens. Guests will enjoy curated culinary experiences such as daily breakfast, four complimentary dinners, a traditional Kashmiri dinner, a riverside lunch, and a unique Hi-Tea on the lake with Kashmiri Kahwa and vegetable pakoras. The package also includes all transfers and sightseeing in a private chauffeur-driven vehicle, along with travel insurance for participants under 69 years of age.", 'images': ['17493011608_034a812663_b.jpg', '25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', '20036255981_8352f56000_b.jpg', '53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'Aruvalley.jpg', '7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 22480, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_1062426595.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013455 is named \'Kashmir With Pahalgam Special\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Na, Description: Arrive in Srinagar Welcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver. Transfer from Airport to Houseboat And check-in at the houseboat, you can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for Visit . Visit Shalimar Bagh Visit Nishant Bagh Enjoy shikara ride in Dal lake. (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Overnight Srinagar at the Houseboat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar – Excursion to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", Arrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) Later proceed to Srinagar. En-route visit Handloom Emporium. Arrive into Srinagar and Check In Houseboat. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar Note: - In case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Day Excursion to Sonmarg (83 Kms / approx 02 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Sonmarg - Golden Meadow. Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). Return back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Pahalgam After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Betaab Valley Tour. Betaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab") Enjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam Note: Day excursion to Betaab is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Pahalgam to Srinagar - Fly Back Home Departure from Srinagar: Today after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!! Special Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 22480.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\xa0\n. Inclusions: Assistance on Arrival. Meal:- Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dinner 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle All transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills ) All currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Exclusions: Any Air or Rail fare. Any other meal not mentioned in price includes. Any other destination not mentioned in itinerary. Any monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges. Any expenses of personal nature. GST @ Current Rate SUPPLEMENT STANDARD VALUE PREMIUM Upgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle] 7875 7875 7875. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. BASICS Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. HOTELS Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same. OTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills Guests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card) Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Food in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy. Being Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited. Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle. Do Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do not Drink or Smoke in Public Places; Do check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and