titude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). \n\xa0\nReturn back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam (90 Kms / approx 03 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath.\n\xa0\nEnjoy Betaab valley - on direct payment basis & subject to Operation)\n\xa0\nDinner & Overnight stay at hotel.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - Royale Comfort/Himalayn Hill/River View or similar in Pahalgam\nValue - Hotel The Kudrat / Hotel Walnut Creek or similar in Pahalgam\nPremium - Hotel ITC Fortune or similar in Pahalgam'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam to Srinagar - Fly Back Home\n\xa0\nDeparture from Srinagar:\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!!\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking. ', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nN/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 21200.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 28200.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 40800.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n03 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Assistance on Arrival.\nMeal:-\n\nDaily Breakfast \n03 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n\nExperience Or Activity\n\nShikara ride on Dal Lake\n01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire\n\nEntrance Or Entry tickets\n\nEntry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh\nEntry Ticket for Nishant Bagh\n\nNote: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\n\nPrivate Chauffeur Driven Vehicle\nAll transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills )\nAll currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\xa0SUPPLEMENT\nSTANDARD\nVALUE\nPREMIUM\n\n\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n7875\n7875\n7875\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/7162146702_b896312393_h.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/Dal_Lake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/7162484002_4696c449e0_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/Sunset_3.jpg']}, 'score': 4.234508, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015596', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015596', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Kashmir with Vaishno Devi Group Tour', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Katra', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Katra', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Sonamarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Katra', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['A 10-Days of Kashmir Fully Loaded Group Tour with Vaishno Devi, all meals, evening tea/coffee & snacks, sightseeing with entrances, Tour Manager, Insurance under 69 yrs., sightseeing with all entrances. Vaishno Devi Helicopter: Return tickets included from Katra to Sanjichhat. Gulmarg Gondola: Phase 1 cable car tickets to Kongdori Valley. Pahalgam Valleys: 4x4 local union transport for Aru, Betaab, and Chandanwari Dal Lake Shikara: 1-hour traditional wooden boat cruise. Mughal Gardens: Entry tickets included for Shalimar and Nishat Bagh Heritage Sites: Entry passes for Awantipura Ruins and Martand Sun Temple. Kashmir Willow: Guided stop at a local cricket bat factory. Sites covered - Sacred Mountain trails of Katra to the rushing rivers of Pahalgam, the dramatic alpine glaciers of Sonamarg, the snow-dusted ski slopes of Gulmarg, and the serene, historic houseboats of Srinagar.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG015596_0_20260922114246.pdf', 'price': 67800, 'packageSummary': "The 'Kashmir with Vaishno Devi Group Tour' is a comprehensive 10-day itinerary covering Katra, Srinagar, Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. This fully loaded package includes all meals, evening snacks, sightseeing with entrances, a dedicated Tour Manager, and travel insurance. Key highlights of the journey include return helicopter tickets from Katra to Sanjichhat for the Vaishno Devi pilgrimage, a Phase 1 Gulmarg Gondola cable car ride to Kongdori Valley, and a 4x4 local transport excursion to the scenic Aru, Betaab, and Chandanwari valleys in Pahalgam. Participants will also enjoy a 1-hour traditional Shikara boat cruise on Dal Lake, entry to the Shalimar and Nishat Bagh Mughal Gardens, visits to the historic Awantipura Ruins and Martand Sun Temple, and a guided stop at a local Kashmir Willow cricket bat factory, all while experiencing the sacred mountain trails, rushing rivers, alpine glaciers, and serene houseboats of this beautiful region.", 'images': [], 'minimumPrice': 67800, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_362192710.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Domestic Diwali Special', 'Summer GIT', 'Family', 'Winter GIT'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015596 is named 'Kashmir with Vaishno Devi Group Tour' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Katra, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Katra, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pahalgam, Meals: N/A, Description: nA, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Pahalgam, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Pahalgam, Meals: N/A, Description: N/S, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Pahalgam, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Sonamarg, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Srinagar, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Srinagar, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Katra, Meals: N/A, Description: N/A, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 67800.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 06; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\n\xa0. Inclusions: Accommodation on twin sharing basis in hotels mentioned or similar. Meal (09 Breakfast 08 Vegetarian Lunches & 09 Dinner) Vaishno Devi Darshan by Helicopter including RFID Card Assistance and Shighra Darshan at Bhawan; Entrance to Mughal Gardens- Shalimar Bagh & Nishat Bagh Experience Shikara ride on Dal Lake. Experience Gulmarg Gondola ride (Phase - 1) in Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Half Day excursion to Aru Valley, Betaab Valley, Chandanwari in Pahalgam Services of a Professional Tour Manager [Subject to Min. 15 Pax Travelling] Travel Insurance (for age below 69yrs) Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Additional / personal use of vehicle. Any personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral water, alcoholic & non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc. Any extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary. Camera fees Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions. GST will be applicable as per prevailing rates. Product Terms and Conditions: The tour price printed is dynamic & is purely on first come first serve basis. The person booking tour early is likely to get the lowest price as communicated / offered by the Company, subject to availability of seats It is mandatory to carry photo ID card (except Pan Card) while you are on tour. Valid ID for Kashmir: Driving License/ Voter ID/Passport/Aadhar Card The vehicle used for transfers is not at disposal. This is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon circumstances. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfers timings. At Sonmarg, Gulmarg & Pahalgam the vehicles are allowed only up to the common parking lot. Thereafter one has to walk or hire ponies/ local vehicles for local conveyance on direct payment basis. Tour-program is subject to change depending upon circumstances Please note that only post paid mobile number works in Kashmir. Highlights of the package: A 10-Days of Kashmir Fully Loaded Group Tour with Vaishno Devi, all meals, evening tea/coffee & snacks, sightseeing with entrances, Tour Manager, Insurance under 69 yrs., sightseeing with all entrances. Vaishno Devi Helicopter: Return tickets included from Katra to Sanjichhat. Gulmarg Gondola: Phase 1 cable car tickets to Kongdori Valley. Pahalgam Valleys: 4x4 local union transport for Aru, Betaab, and Chandanwari Dal Lake Shikara: 1-hour traditional wooden boat cruise. Mughal Gardens: Entry tickets included for Shalimar and Nishat Bagh Heritage Sites: Entry passes for Awantipura Ruins and Martand Sun Temple. Kashmir Willow: Guided stop at a local cricket bat factory. Sites covered - Sacred Mountain trails of Katra to the rushing rivers of Pahalgam, the dramatic alpine glaciers of Sonamarg, the snow-dusted ski slopes of Gulmarg, and the serene, historic houseboats of Srinagar..", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'JNKVGT', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Kashmir with Vaishno Devi Group Tour' is a comprehensive 10-day itinerary covering Katra, Srinagar, Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. This fully loaded package includes all meals, evening snacks, sightseeing with entrances, a dedicated Tour Manager, and travel insurance. Key highlights of the journey include return helicopter tickets from Katra to Sanjichhat for the Vaishno Devi pilgrimage, a Phase 1 Gulmarg Gondola cable car ride to Kongdori Valley, and a 4x4 local transport excursion to the scenic Aru, Betaab, and Chandanwari valleys in Pahalgam. Participants will also enjoy a 1-hour traditional Shikara boat cruise on Dal Lake, entry to the Shalimar and Nishat Bagh Mughal Gardens, visits to the historic Awantipura Ruins and Martand Sun Temple, and a guided stop at a local Kashmir Willow cricket bat factory, all while experiencing the sacred mountain trails, rushing rivers, alpine glaciers, and serene houseboats of this beautiful region.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 2, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 3, 'description': 'nA', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 4, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 5, 'description': 'N/S', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 6, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 8, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 9, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}, {'day': 10, 'description': 'N/A', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 67800.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 06; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\n\xa0'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nVehicles as per group size on Sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; Vehicle Type Cannot be confirmed at the time of Booking)\nVehicle is not at disposal – means it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\nSeats Allotment in the Vehicle is on first come first serve basis at the venue, irrespective of the booking dates.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary', 'Srinagar\n\nShikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake\n\nNishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens)\nPari Mahal (Palace of Fairies)\n\nPahalgam\n\nPampore\nAvantipur Ruins\nBetaab Valley\nChandanwari\nMartand Sun Temple\nKashmiri Cricket Bat Factory\xa0\n\nGulmarg\n\nGondola\nHandloom Emporium\xa0\n\n\xa0'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 25 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '', 'inclusions': '\nAccommodation on twin sharing basis in hotels mentioned or similar.\nMeal (09 Breakfast 08 Vegetarian Lunches & 09 Dinner)\nVaishno Devi Darshan by Helicopter including RFID Card Assistance and Shighra Darshan at Bhawan;\nEntrance to Mughal Gardens- Shalimar Bagh & Nishat Bagh\nExperience Shikara ride on Dal Lake.\nExperience Gulmarg Gondola ride (Phase - 1) in Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)\nHalf Day excursion to Aru Valley, Betaab Valley, Chandanwari in Pahalgam\nServices of a Professional Tour Manager [Subject to Min. 15 Pax Travelling]\nTravel Insurance (for age below 69yrs)\n\n\xa0\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAdditional / personal use of vehicle.\nAny personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral water, alcoholic & non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc.\nAny extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary.\nCamera fees\nAny incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions.\nGST will be applicable as per prevailing rates\n\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': '\nThe tour price printed is dynamic & is purely on first come first serve basis. The person booking tour early is likely to get the lowest price as communicated / offered by the Company, subject to availability of seats\nIt is mandatory to carry photo ID card (except Pan Card) while you are on tour. Valid ID for Kashmir: Driving License/ Voter ID/Passport/Aadhar Card\nThe vehicle used for transfers is not at disposal.\nThis is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon circumstances. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfers timings.\nAt Sonmarg, Gulmarg & Pahalgam the vehicles are allowed only up to the common parking lot. Thereafter one has to walk or hire ponies/ local vehicles for local conveyance on direct payment basis.\nTour-program is subject to change depending upon circumstances\nPlease note that only post paid mobile number works in Kashmir\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015596/AdobeStock_362192710.jpeg', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 3.9049602, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013451', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013451', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Kashmir Special With Gulmarg And Sonmarg Stay', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gulmarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Sonmarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Meal Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013451_0_20260924114803.pdf', 'price': 25890, 'packageSummary': "The 'Kashmir Special With Gulmarg And Sonmarg Stay' package is a 6-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Sonmarg, Srinagar, and Gulmarg. This curated itinerary offers travelers a range of memorable experiences, including a traditional Shikara ride on Dal Lake, a unique photography session in Kashmiri attire, and a breathtaking Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg. Guests will enjoy daily breakfast, four complimentary dining experiences or activities, and entry tickets to the historic Shalimar Bagh and Nishat Bagh. The package also ensures a hassle-free journey with all transfers and sightseeing conducted in a private chauffeur-driven vehicle, alongside included travel insurance for participants under the age of 69.", 'images': ['Dal_Lake.jpg', '25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', '49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'KheerBhawaniTemple.jpg', '7162484002_4696c449e0_h.jpg', '7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 25890, 'thumbnailImage': '53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013451 is named \'Kashmir Special With Gulmarg And Sonmarg Stay\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Na, Description: Arrive in Srinagar Welcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver. Transfer from the airport to the hotel and check in. You can relax for a while after arrival. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit. Visit Shalimar Bagh Visit Nishant Bagh Enjoy shikara ride in Dal lake. (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Overnight Srinagar at the Houseboat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Gulmarg, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", Arrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg. Note: - In case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Sonmarg, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Gulmarg to Sonmarg (125 Kms / approx 04 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Sonmarg - Golden Meadow. Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Sonmarg., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Sonmarg to Srinagar (125 Kms / approx 04 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Srinagar - En-route - Visit Kheer Bhawani Temple.. Evening is free for shopping. Dinner & overnight stay will be at hotel in Srinagar., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast And Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam: (Day Trip) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath. Enjoy Betaab valley - on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) Return back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Srinagar - Fly Back Home Departure from Srinagar: Today after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!! Special Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 25890.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n. Inclusions: Assistance on Arrival. Meal:- Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dinner 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle All transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills ) All currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Exclusions: Any Air or Rail fare. Any other meal not mentioned in price includes. Any other destination not mentioned in itinerary. Any monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges. Any expenses of personal nature. GST @ Current Rate UPPLEMENT STANDARD VALUE PREMIUM Upgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle] 9450 9450 9450. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. BASICS Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. HOTELS Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same. OTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills Guests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card) Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Food in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy. Being Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited. Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle. Do Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do not Drink or Smoke in Public Places; Do check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption. Do not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult. Take Proper permits are required to take video or film; Do not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation Leave Places Better than you found it! Most leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes. Jai Hind!. Highlights of the package: Meal Daily Breakfast 04 Complimentary Dine Experience Or Activity Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh All transfers and sightseeing Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle Travel Insurance Travel Insurance Included (for age below 69yrs).', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai