t availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - Hotel Zahgeer or similar in Gulmarg\nValue -Hotel Pine Spring / Hotel Rosewood or similar in Gulmarg\nPremium - Hotel Hilltop / Hotel The Vintage or similar in Gulmarg'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nGulmarg to Sonmarg (125 Kms / approx 04 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Sonmarg - Golden Meadow.\xa0Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. \n\xa0\nSonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). \n\xa0\nDinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Sonmarg. ', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - Glacier Heights/ Hotel Divine Inn or similar in Sonmarg\nValue - Hotel Village walk or similar in Sonmarg\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Sonmarg'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nSonmarg to Srinagar (125 Kms / approx 04 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for Srinagar - En-route - Visit Kheer Bhawani Temple..\nEvening is free for shopping. \n\xa0\nDinner & overnight stay will be at hotel in Srinagar.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam: (Day Trip)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath.\n\xa0\nEnjoy Betaab valley - on direct payment basis & subject to Operation)\n\xa0\n\xa0\nReturn back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast And Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar - Fly Back Home\n\xa0\nDeparture from Srinagar:\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!!\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your\xa0\xa0reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 25900.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 36300.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 49100.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast\xa0\n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': 'Assistance on Arrival.\nMeal:-\n\nDaily Breakfast \n04 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Lunch At River Side\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n\nExperience Or Activity\n\nShikara ride on Dal Lake\n01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire\nThe Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg\xa0 (Tickets are subject to availability)\n\nEntrance Or Entry tickets\n\nEntry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh\nEntry Ticket for Nishant Bagh\n\nNote: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\n\nPrivate Chauffeur Driven Vehicle\nAll transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills )\nAll currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate\n\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\n\n\n\nUPPLEMENT\nSTANDARD\nVALUE\nPREMIUM\n\n\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n9450\n9450\n9450\n\n\n\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/53073277540_2a766a4a52_b.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/itinerary/Dal_Lake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/itinerary/25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/itinerary/KheerBhawaniTemple.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/itinerary/7162484002_4696c449e0_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013451/itinerary/7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg']}, 'score': 3.6230025, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG011953', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG011953', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Kashmir - Special 4 (Srinagar - Gulmarg - Pahalgam - Sonmarg ) ', 'days': 5, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Meal Experience 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Inculded Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Inculded Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Transfers: Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle. Note: During the The Badamwari Spring season, we will visit the Badamwari Park, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG011953_0_20260922114608.pdf', 'price': 19840, 'packageSummary': "The 'Kashmir - Special 4 (Srinagar - Gulmarg - Pahalgam - Sonmarg)' package is a 5-day tour based in Srinagar that offers a rich blend of scenic beauty and cultural experiences. Throughout the journey, travelers will enjoy private chauffeur-driven transfers to explore key highlights, including a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake complete with a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, and a Gondola ride (Phase 1) in Gulmarg, subject to ticket availability. The itinerary features entry tickets to the beautiful Shalimar Bagh and Nishat Bagh, with seasonal visits to the Tulip Garden or Badamwari Park when in bloom. Guests will also indulge in curated culinary experiences, such as a lakeside Hi-Tea with Kashmiri Kahwa and vegetable pakoras, a riverside lunch on the first day depending on flight arrival times, and a traditional Kashmiri dinner.", 'images': ['AdobeStock_85975647.jpeg', 'Gulmarg2.jpg', '49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'Aruvalley.jpg', '7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 19840, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_296897404.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG011953 is named \'Kashmir - Special 4 (Srinagar - Gulmarg - Pahalgam - Sonmarg ) \' and spans 5 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: NA, Description: Arrive in Srinagar Welcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver. Transfer from Airport to Hotel and check-in at the hotel. You can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit. Later in the evening, proceed for Visit . Visit Shalimar Bagh Visit Nishant Bagh Enjoy shikara ride in Dal lake. (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Overnight Srinagar at the Houseboat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Srinagar – Excursion to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers", Arrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1: KHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis) Later proceed to Srinagar. En-route visit Handloom Emporium. Arrive into Srinagar and Check In Houseboat. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar. Note: - In case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg. Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but subject to availability. Clients can also check and pre book on www.jammukashmircablecar.com . However, pls. be noted, Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling. In Gulmarg - The vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Excursion to Sonmarg (83 Kms / approx 02 hrs). After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Sonmarg - Golden Meadow. Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment). Return back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam: (Day Trip) After Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath. Enjoy Betaab valley - on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) Return back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly Back Home - Departure from Srinagar: Today after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!! Special Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 19840.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast\n03 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Kashmiri lunch on the lake.\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n. Inclusions: Assistance on Arrival. Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary) Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle All transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills ) All currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Any Air or Rail fare. Any other meal not mentioned in price includes. Any other destination not mentioned in itinerary. Any monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges. Any expenses of personal nature. GST @ Current Rate Upgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle] Standard Value Premium 7875 7875 7875. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] BASICS Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. HOTELS Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same. OTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills Guests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card) Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Food in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy. Being Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited. Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle. Do Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do not Drink or Smoke in Public Places; Do check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption. Do not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult. Take Proper permits are required to take video or film; Do not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation Leave Places Better than you found it! Most leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes. Jai Hind!. Highlights of the package: Meal Experience 01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora) 01 Lunch At River Side (Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1) 01 Kashmiri Dinner Experience Or Activity Inculded Shikara ride on Dal Lake 01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire Gondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability) Entrance Or Entry tickets Inculded Entry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh Entry Ticket for Nishant Bagh (Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.) Transfers: Private Chauffeur Driven Vehicle. Note: During the The Badamwari Spring season, we will visit the Badamwari Park, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary..', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Kashmir - Special 4 (Srinagar - Gulmarg - Pahalgam - Sonmarg)' package is a 5-day tour based in Srinagar that offers a rich blend of scenic beauty and cultural experiences. Throughout the journey, travelers will enjoy private chauffeur-driven transfers to explore key highlights, including a scenic Shikara ride on Dal Lake complete with a photography session in traditional Kashmiri attire, and a Gondola ride (Phase 1) in Gulmarg, subject to ticket availability. The itinerary features entry tickets to the beautiful Shalimar Bagh and Nishat Bagh, with seasonal visits to the Tulip Garden or Badamwari Park when in bloom. Guests will also indulge in curated culinary experiences, such as a lakeside Hi-Tea with Kashmiri Kahwa and vegetable pakoras, a riverside lunch on the first day depending on flight arrival times, and a traditional Kashmiri dinner.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive in Srinagar\n\xa0\nWelcome onboard a wonderful tour to one of the most happening destinations - Kashmir! On arrival at the Srinagar Airport, you will be welcomed & received by our representative/driver.\n\xa0\nTransfer from Airport to Hotel and check-in at the hotel. You can relax for a while. Later in the evening, proceed for a visit.\n\xa0\nLater in the evening, proceed for Visit .\n\nVisit Shalimar Bagh\nVisit Nishant Bagh\nEnjoy shikara ride in Dal lake.\n\n\xa0\n(Note: During the Tulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary.)\n\xa0\nOvernight Srinagar at the Houseboat.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nNA', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar – Excursion to Gulmarg (90 kms / 3 ½ hours one way)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Gulmarg - "Meadow of Flowers",\n\xa0\nArrive Gulmarg Enjoy Asia\'s Highest Cable Car Project Gulmarg Gondola - The Gondola offers all tourists, scenic views of Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley as you head towards Phase 1:\nKHILANMARG. You may enjoy an Sledge ride or Snow Mobile ride on the snow covered slopes (on direct payment basis)\n\xa0\nLater proceed to Srinagar. En-route visit Handloom Emporium. Arrive into Srinagar and Check In Houseboat. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\n\xa0\nNote: -\n\xa0\nIn case of heavy snow fall and Gulmarg is not operational, we will take clients to Yusmarg. Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but subject to availability. Clients can also check and pre book on www.jammukashmircablecar.com . However, pls. be noted, Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling. In Gulmarg - The vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis.\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDay Excursion to Sonmarg (83 Kms / approx 02 hrs).\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Sonmarg - Golden Meadow. Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains.\n\xa0\nSonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier (on direct payment basis & subject to Operation) or Sledge Riding on snow (on direct payment).\n\xa0\nReturn back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam: (Day Trip)\n\xa0\nAfter Buffet Breakfast, proceed for day excursion to Pahalgam - Pahalgam is famous for its scenic beauty and is the jewel of the picturesque Liddar valley in the high Himalayas. It provides an ideal setting for hiking, trekking, and fishing. It is also the starting point of the annual pilgrimage to the holy cave of Amarnath.\n\xa0\nEnjoy\xa0 Betaab valley\xa0 - on direct payment basis & subject to Operation)\n\xa0\nReturn back to Srinagar by evening. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Standard - The Olive Hotel/ Hotel Sapphire or similar in Srinagar\nValue - Hotel Dewan BY Royal Naqash / Hotel Ramada or similar in Srinagar\nPremium - Hotel Four Points By Sheraton, Srinagar /\xa0 Hotel Orchard Retreat & Spa or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nFly Back Home -\xa0Departure from Srinagar:\n\xa0\nToday after breakfast, transfer to Srinagar airport to board the return flight with Happy Memories!!!\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Hotels in any Seasonal hill Station / weekend destination in Srinagar) follow dynamic pricing method – the price may vary from month to month, day to day, depending on the festivals, functions, events, long weekends, occasions and market demand. The above mentioned rates are for your reference – however, the same may change at the time of booking. Request you to re-check the availability and the prevailing rates at the time of actual booking.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nN/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 19800.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 27700.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 40100.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Breakfast\n03 Complimentary Dinner\n01 Hi Tea On the lake (Kashmiri Kahwa With vegetables Pakora)\n01 Kashmiri lunch on the lake.\xa0(Subject to flight arrival time on Day 1)\n01 Kashmiri Dinner\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Included as per itinerary', 'inclusions': '\nAssistance on Arrival.\nShikara ride on Dal Lake\n01 Photography during Shikara Ride with Kashmiri Attire\nGondola ride (Phase - 1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)\nEntry Ticket for Shalimar Bagh\nEntry Ticket for Nishant Bagh\nTulip season, we will visit the Tulip Garden, as an additional sightseeing in our itinerary)\nPrivate Chauffeur Driven Vehicle\nAll transfers and sightseeing by AC Vehicle. (Please note that AC will be switched off during hills )\nAll currently applicable hotel taxes except GST @ Current Rate\n\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n\n\n\nStandard\nValue\xa0\nPremium\n\n\n7875\n7875\n7875\n\n\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\n\n\xa0\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011953/AdobeStock_296897404.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011953/itinerary/AdobeStock_85975647.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011953/itinerary/Gulmarg2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011953/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011953/itinerary/Aruvalley.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011953/itinerary/7845531024_d0b41e9634_k.jpg']}, 'score': 3.6230025, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014983', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014983', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gulmarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Stay in Houseboat on Dal Lake Enjoy Shikara ride on Dal Lake till Char Chinar The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014983_0_20260826144349', 'price': 45700, 'packageSummary': "The 'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special' package is a 7-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features unique experiences such as staying in a traditional houseboat on Dal Lake and enjoying a relaxing Shikara ride to Char Chinar. Additionally, participants will have the opportunity to experience the famous Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg, with tickets subject to availability, making for an unforgettable holiday in the valley.", 'images': ['Dallake.jpg', 'AdobeStock_296897404.jpeg', 'AdobeStock_1062426595.jpeg', '7162146702_b896312393_h.jpg', 'gondola.jpg', '49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'kashmir8.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 45700, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_362192710.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Winter GIT', 'Domestic Winter GIT', 'Durga Puja Domestic'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Durga Puja Special', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG014983 is named \'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival in Srinagar Welcome to Srinagar and transfer to the houseboat. Check in to the houseboat and freshen up. Enjoy a romantic Shikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake (Kashmir\'s iconic jewel, a serene houseboat haven) Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the houseboat Note: Room heating facilities in houseboats are available depending on weather conditions., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam (90 Km / ~03 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the houseboat and check out. Srinagar sightseeing Shankaracharya Temple (Dedicated to Lord Shiva) Nishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens) Pari Mahal (Palace of Fairies) Drive to Pahalgam (A picturesque valley surrounded by snow-capped mountains, offering stunning natural beauty and adventure opportunities) En route visit Pampore for saffron demonstration and shopping Avantipur Ruins (ancient temple complex) Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Check in at the hotel and relax. Dinner and overnight stay in Pahalgam at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Pahalgam Morning breakfast at the hotel. Full Day city tour, visiting the below attractions Betaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab") Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Enjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam Note: Day excursion to Betaab is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Gulmarg, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Pahalgam to Gulmarg (140Km / ~ 04 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the hotel and check out. Drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of flowers) En route visit, Martand Sun Temple (ancient ruins) Kashmiri Cricket Bat Factory (Witness the craftsmanship of world-renowned cricket bats made from Kashmir willow) Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Check in at the hotel and relax. Dinner and overnight stay in Gulmarg at the hotel. Note : In case of heavy rainfall/ Gulmarg is not operational due to any sort of Weather conditions, we will take clients to Doodhpathri. Gulmarg Gondola Ticket up to Phase 1 is part of the package and subject to availability as per the booking dates. Please be noted, that Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling. In Gulmarg - The Tour Vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg hotel. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Gulmarg to Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 02 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the hotel and check out. Experience the Gulmarg Gondola (Asia\'s highest cable car project) Enjoy panoramic views of the Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley. Experience sledge riding on snow – on direct payment basis Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Enroute visit Handloom Emporium on the way back to Srinagar. Drive to Srinagar Check in to the hotel and relax Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Srinagar – Sonmarg – Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 2 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the hotel. Drive to Sonmarg (Golden meadow) Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier- on direct payment basis Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Optional: Sledge or snowmobile ride – on direct payment basis Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Morning breakfast at the hotel and check out. Proceed to the airport for your onward journey, taking with you cherished memories of your Kashmir experience. Note: As this is a group tour, the airport transfer departs from the Srinagar hotel at 10:00 AM., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 45700.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 06; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\n\xa0. Inclusions: Hotels: Twin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar Meals: Breakfasts: 06; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 06 Breakfast & Dinners will be Buffet Lunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed Extra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day Additional Inclusions: Round-trip economy class airfare Water: 500 ml water per person per day Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Airfare not included for joining direct passengers Additional / personal use of vehicle. Any personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral water, alcoholic & non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc. Any extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary. Camera fees Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions. GST will be applicable as per prevailing rates. Product Terms and Conditions: The tour price printed is dynamic & is purely on first come first serve basis. The person booking tour early is likely to get the lowest price as communicated / offered by the Company, subject to availability of seats It is mandatory to carry photo ID card (except Pan Card) while you are on tour. Valid ID for Kashmir: Driving License/ Voter ID/Passport/Aadhar Card The vehicle used for transfers is not at disposal. This is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon circumstances. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfers timings. At Sonmarg, Gulmarg & Pahalgam the vehicles are allowed only up to the common parking lot. Thereafter one has to walk or hire ponies/ local vehicles for local conveyance on direct payment basis. Tour-program is subject to change depending upon circumstances Please note that only post paid mobile number works in Kashmir. Highlights of the package: Stay in Houseboat on Dal Lake Enjoy Shikara ride on Dal Lake till Char Chinar The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability).', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'JKDPEK', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special' package is a 7-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features unique experiences such as staying in a traditional houseboat on Dal Lake and enjoying a relaxing Shikara ride to Char Chinar. Additionally, participants will have the opportunity to experience the famous Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg, with tickets subject to availability, making for an unforgettable holiday in the valley.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\nArrival in Srinagar\n\xa0\nWelcome to Srinagar and transfer to the houseboat.\n\xa0\nCheck in to the houseboat and freshen up.\n\xa0\nEnjoy a romantic Shikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake (Kashmir's iconic jewel, a serene houseboat haven)\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the houseboat\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0Room heating facilities in houseboats are available depending on weather conditions.", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - Khyber Houseboats or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam (90 Km / ~03 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the houseboat and check out.\n\xa0\nSrinagar sightseeing\n\nShankaracharya Temple (Dedicated to Lord Shiva)\nNishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens)\nPari Mahal (Palace of Fairies)\n\n\xa0\nDrive to Pahalgam (A picturesque valley surrounded by snow-capped mountains, offering stunning natural beauty and adventure opportunities)\n\xa0\nEn route visit\n\nPampore for saffron demonstration and shopping\nAvantipur Ruins (ancient temple complex)\n\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nCheck in at the hotel and relax.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Pahalgam at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - White Water Resorts or similar in Pahalgam\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel.\n\xa0\nFull Day city tour, visiting the below attractions\n\nBetaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab")\n\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nEnjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0Day excursion to Betaab is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - White Water Resorts or similar in Pahalgam\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam to Gulmarg (140Km / ~ 04 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel and check out.\n\xa0\nDrive to Gulmarg (Meadow of flowers)\n\xa0\nEn route visit,\n\nMartand Sun Temple (ancient ruins)\nKashmiri Cricket Bat Factory (Witness the craftsmanship of world-renowned cricket bats made from Kashmir willow)\n\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nCheck in at the hotel and relax.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Gulmarg at the hotel.\n\xa0\nNote :\n\nIn case of heavy rainfall/ Gulmarg is not operational due to any sort of Weather conditions, we\xa0 will take clients to Doodhpathri.\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket up to Phase 1 is part of the package and subject to availability as per the booking dates. Please be noted, that Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling.\nIn Gulmarg - The Tour Vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg hotel. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel -\xa0Royal Park or Similar in\xa0Gulmarg\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nGulmarg to Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 02 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel and check out.\n\xa0\nExperience the Gulmarg Gondola (Asia's highest cable car project)\n\xa0\nEnjoy panoramic views of the Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley.\n\xa0\nExperience sledge riding on snow – on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nEnroute visit\n\xa0\n\nHandloom Emporium on the way back to Srinagar.\n\n\xa0\nDrive to Srinagar\n\xa0\nCheck in to the hotel and relax\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel.\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Paisley Palace or similar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar – Sonmarg – Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 2 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel.\n\xa0\nDrive to Sonmarg (Golden meadow)\n\xa0\nEnjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier- on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nOptional: Sledge or snowmobile ride – on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Paisley Palace or similar'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel and check out.\n\xa0\nProceed to the airport for your onward journey, taking with you cherished memories of your Kashmir experience.\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0As this is a group tour, the airport transfer departs from the Srinagar hotel at 10:00 AM.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 45700.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 06; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\n\xa0'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nVehicles as per group size on Sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; Vehicle Type Cannot be confirmed at the time of Booking)\nVehicle is not at disposal – means it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\nSeats Allotment in the Vehicle is on first come first serve basis at the venue, irrespective of the booking dates.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Srinagar\n\nShikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake\n\nNishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens)\nPari Mahal (Palace of Fairies)\n\nPahalgam\n\nPampore\nAvantipur Ruins\nBetaab Valley\nChandanwari\nMartand Sun Temple\nKashmiri Cricket Bat Factory\xa0\n\nGulmarg\n\nGondola\nHandloom Emporium\xa0\n\n\xa0', 'As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 25 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '', 'inclusions': 'Hotels:\n\nTwin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\nAdditional Inclusions:\n\nRound-trip economy class airfare\nWater: 500 ml water per person per day\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAirfare not included for joining direct passengers\nAdditional / personal use of vehicle.\nAny personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral water, alcoholic & non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc.\nAny extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary.\nCamera fees\nAny incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions.\nGST will be applicable as per prevailing rates\n\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': '\nThe tour price printed is dynamic & is purely on first come first serve basis. The person booking tour early is likely to get the lowest price as communicated / offered by the Company, subject to availability of seats\nIt is mandatory to carry photo ID card (except Pan Card) while you are on tour. Valid ID for Kashmir: Driving License/ Voter ID/Passport/Aadhar Card\nThe vehicle used for transfers is not at disposal.\nThis is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon circumstances. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfers timings.\nAt Sonmarg, Gulmarg & Pahalgam the vehicles are allowed only up to the common parking lot. Thereafter one has to walk or hire ponies/ local vehicles for local conveyance on direct payment basis.\nTour-program is subject to change depending upon circumstances\nPlease note that only post paid mobile number works in Kashmir\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/AdobeStock_362192710.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/Dallake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/AdobeStock_296897404.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/AdobeStock_1062426595.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/7162146702_b896312393_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/gondola.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/kashmir8.jpg']}, 'score': 3.3790202, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG011603', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG011603', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Anant Kashi Ayodhya Yatra', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prayagraj', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prayagraj', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['VIP Darshan - Kashi Vishwanath temple Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot; Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi (Subject to availability) Extras: Escorted Darshan in Varanasi, and Ayodhya; Experience Manager** Stay in Deluxe 3* Hotels in Varanasi, Ayodhya, Prayagraj (Chitrakot Excursion) All meals and evening tea/coffee with snacks All major temple and monuments All Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi - Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal Experience Dev Deepawali Celebration for the Departure Dated 04th Nov 2025. Dev Deepawali marks the descent of gods to Earth. Varanasi glows with millions of diyas along the Ganges.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG011603_0_20260901183209', 'price': 44490, 'packageSummary': "The 'Anant Kashi Ayodhya Yatra' is a 6-day spiritual tour covering the holy cities of Prayagraj, Varanasi, Ayodhya, and Chitrakoot. This comprehensive package offers travelers VIP Darshan at the Kashi Vishwanath temple, guided Teerth Darshan of sacred sites, and a scenic boat ride on the River Ganges. Participants will enjoy escorted visits to major landmarks such as the Dashashwamedh Ghat, Sarnath, the holy Sangam dip, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, and Hanuman Garhi, alongside a day excursion to Chitrakoot's Ram Ghat and Kamad Giri. With deluxe 3-star hotel accommodations, all meals, and an Experience Manager included, guests on the November 4, 2025 departure will also have the unique opportunity to witness the spectacular Dev Deepawali celebration, where Varanasi glows with millions of diyas.", 'images': ['8403831008_080f39d1ef_b.jpg', '48011063662_e70a005e73_h.jpg', '47519436781_5d96ebe956_h.jpg', '49408764761_079785d448_k.jpg', 'KanakBhawan.jpg', '49211464657_f049880725_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 44490, 'thumbnailImage': '40637097564_10b682199c_k.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Winter GIT', 'Family', 'Spiritual', 'Domestic Winter GIT'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG011603 is named \'Anant Kashi Ayodhya Yatra\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Varanasi, Meals: Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi Arrival at Varanasi airport. Pls. schdedule a flight before 1330 hrs Meet and greet and at 1330 hrs we get transferred to Hotel. Checkin and freshen up. After lunch at 1600 Hrs we get transfer to Ganges for Boating and Evening Ganga Aarti on famous Dashashwamedh Ghat. Dashashwamedh Ghat is the main ghat in Varanasi on the Ganga River. It is located close to Vishwanath Temple and is probably the most spectacular ghat. Two Hindu legends are associated with it: According to one, Lord Brahma created it to welcome Lord Shiva. According to another legend, Lord Brahma sacrificed ten horses during Dasa-Ashwamedha yajna performed here. Overnight in Varanasi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Varanasi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi Early morning Temple darshan (Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir, Kala Bhairov Mandir) followed with Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir & Benaras Hindu University (BHU). After breakfast move for Sarnath (Sarnath is the place where Gautam Buddha after attain enlightenment delivers his first sermon to 5 followers). Sightseeing of Sarnath including Sarnath Museum (Our National Emblem excavated from Sarnath is on Display built by Samrat Ashoka), Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple. Evening is free. Overnight in Varanasi. Note: Boats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME. VIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Prayagraj, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi - Prayagraj (145 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way) After early breakfast check out and transfer to PRAYAGRAJ. (The city\'s original name – Prayag, or "place of offerings" – comes from its position at the Sangam (confluence) of the Ganga, Yamuna and Sarasvati rivers. It is the second-oldest city in India, and plays a central role in Hindu scriptures. Allahabad was originally called Kaushambi (now a separate district) by the Kuru rulers of Hastinapur, who developed it as their capital. Since then, Allahabad has been a political, cultural and administrative centre of the Doab region. Mughal emperor Akbar renamed it Ilahabad, which the British changed to Allahabad. In 1833 it became the seat of the Ceded and Conquered Provinces region before its capital was moved to Agra in 1835. Allahabad became the capital of the North-Western Provinces in 1858, and was the capital of India for a day. The city was the capital of the United Provinces from 1902 to 1920 and remained at the forefront of national importance during the struggle for Indian independence.) Places of interest HOLY DIP IN SANGAM, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree (Akshayavat ("the indestructible banyan tree") is a sacred fig tree mentioned in the Hindu mythology. According to a legend, once the sage Markandeya asked Lord Narayana to show him a specimen of the divine power. Narayana flooded the entire world for a moment, during which only the Akshayavat could be seen above the water level.) & Anand Bhawan (Birthplace of first Prime Minister of Independent India Pt. Jawaharlal Nehru) Experience the exclusivity of Magh Mela as you explore the sacred Sangam, witness vibrant rituals, and immerse yourself in the spiritual essence of this grand gathering., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Prayagraj, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Prayagraj - Chitrakoot - Prayagraj (120 Km 3-4 Hrs. One Way) After breakfast day trip to Chitrakoot (Chitrakoot, "the hills of many wonders" is indeed a gift of nature and the gods. Located in the Banda district of modern Uttar Pradesh(U.P), on the banks of river Paisuni(Mandikini), Chitrakoot is a tranquil retreat on the northern spur of the Vindhyas. Just 6 km south of Karvi and 72 km south east of Banda district on the road to Allahabad, Chitrakoot Dham is one of the most ancient holy pilgrim places of India. Legends have it that it was the abode of Lord Rama, his wife Sita and brother Lakshman for eleven years of their fourteen years of exile. This is also the place,where they came in contact with sage Atri and sati Anasuya.This abode of the gods is credited to have seen the incarnations of Brahma,Vishnu and Mahesh. Chitrakoot ,sacred with the touch of Lord\'s feet,was where Goswami Tulsidas, the creator of the epic "Shri Ramcharitmanas" spent many years of his life. Dotted with innumerable temples and shrines, nature\'s splendor here is wrapped in peace and tranquility, permeated only by singing birds and gushing streams.). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Prayagraj. Places of Interest:- Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Prayagraj - Ayodhaya (180 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way) After breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Ayodhaya (Ayodhya, also known as Saketa, is an ancient city of India, believed to be the birthplace of Rama and setting of the epic Ramayana. It is adjacent to Faizabad city in the central region of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh. Ayodhya used to be the capital of the ancient Kosala Kingdom. Owing to the belief as the birthplace of Rama, Ayodhya (Awadh) has been regarded as one of the seven most important pilgrimage sites (Saptapuri) for Hindus. It is believed that the birth spot of Rama). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Ayodhaya. Places of Interest:- Ram Janam Bhoomi; Kanak Bhawan; Hanuman Garhi; Raj Darbar; Karsevak Sthal., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ayodhaya - Varanasi Drop Via Chpaiya (250 Km. 5-6 Hrs. One Way) After early breakfast, checkout from hotel in Ayodhya to move for Varanasi airport for onward/return journey. Pls. Note: Flight should be after 7 PM onwards from Varanasi Airport, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 44490.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Hotels: Twin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar Meals: All meals option are pure veg/non-veg/Jain food In Ayodhya pure veg meals are available Breakfasts: 05; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 05 Breakfast & Dinners will be Buffet Lunches will be packed or en-route in a restaurant/hotel Extra toppings: Daily evening snacks with tea/coffee/coconut water/fresh drink/ice cream Special Experiences, Sightseeing and Activities: Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by HAND Boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits) All Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi - Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal Adiitional Inclusions: Transfers: Transfers and sightseeing by air-conditioned vehicles (Subject to Min. 20 Pax) Guides: Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot Water: 2-liter water bottle per person per day Entrance fees: All entrance fees included in the itinerary VIP Darshan: Kashi Vishwanath temple Minimum Operating Strength for the Group is 10 Pax Tour Manager : Local Tour Escort from 15 Pax Onwards. Professional Tour Manager From 25 Pax Onwards. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Extra add-on (If possible): Language Pandit For Rituals (Varanasi, Prayagraj) Special Puja like Mangala Aarti, Pind Dan Puja Excursion to Bodh Gaya Make You Own Regional Group Vehicle Details: Type: Vehicles as per group size on a sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; vehicle type cannot be confirmed at the time of booking) Usage: Vehicle is not at disposal; it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary. Seat Allotment: Seats in the vehicle are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis at the venue, regardless of booking dates Note: Boats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME. VIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month.. Exclusions: Any airfare/rail fare Remittance charge/Bank charge for transfer of money. Tips and gratuities Any Jungle/National Park Safari. Mobile/ camera/video tickets/monument entry Christmas & New Year Gala Dinner cost Meals other than mentioned. Any VIP Darshan/Dakshina/Prashad/Garland fees Any personal nature expenses. GST Extra Any guide/escort Personal expenditure like soft drinks, mineral water, phone calls, tips, porter age etc. Anything not specifically mentioned in the “Package tour price includes” box. Any expenses of personal nature. High season surcharge, applicable during New Year, Puja, special dates. High Season / Special events supplements will be applicable at the time of booking only. Any optional tour. Direct Darshan Ticket Portal Link - https://www.shrikashivishwanath.org/ https://online.srjbtkshetra.org/#/login. Product Terms and Conditions: Basics Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of the Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. An Upgrade to a Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on the current tariff & are subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. Hotels Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges. Please remember that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expense arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress/Roll over Extra mattress on the floor provided where a proper extra bed isn’t available. In case the guests cannot climb higher floors, we request you to update us at the time of booking, so that we may take the appropriate action and try for rooms on the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hilly areas, scarcity of water & electricity may happen. To overcome the water crisis, certain hotels have a fixed schedule for supplying hot & cold water. We strongly regret the inconvenience and look forward to your cooperation. On hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in case any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy - Tea/coffee maker/mini fridge/enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, loofah, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, the menu will be on a fixed plan/buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks/liquor, Soups or Deserts. For an order on A-la-Carte basis, guests are requested to make a direct payment for additional items. TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicles used are an Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per the itinerary for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in the Vehicle will be switched off during a hilly drive. Please consult the driver/local representative for the next day’s sightseeing schedule/Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/Bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as the vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monuments will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Parks are Closed Around Mid Jun-Mid Nov. INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by the Company are in capacity of an agent only. The Company will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us in situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of a discontinued itinerary due to these reasons, no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.. Highlights of the package: VIP Darshan - Kashi Vishwanath temple Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot; Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi (Subject to availability) Extras: Escorted Darshan in Varanasi, and Ayodhya; Experience Manager** Stay in Deluxe 3* Hotels in Varanasi, Ayodhya, Prayagraj (Chitrakot Excursion) All meals and evening tea/coffee with snacks All major temple and monuments All Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi - Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal Experience Dev Deepawali Celebration for the Departure Dated 04th Nov 2025. Dev Deepawali marks the descent of gods to Earth. Varanasi glows with millions of diyas along the Ganges..', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'UPAKAY', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Anant Kashi Ayodhya Yatra' is a 6-day spiritual tour covering the holy cities of Prayagraj, Varanasi, Ayodhya, and Chitrakoot. This comprehensive package offers travelers VIP Darshan at the Kashi Vishwanath temple, guided Teerth Darshan of sacred sites, and a scenic boat ride on the River Ganges. Participants will enjoy escorted visits to major landmarks such as the Dashashwamedh Ghat, Sarnath, the holy Sangam dip, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, and Hanuman Garhi, alongside a day excursion to Chitrakoot's Ram Ghat and Kamad Giri. With deluxe 3-star hotel accommodations, all meals, and an Experience Manager included, guests on the November 4, 2025 departure will also have the unique opportunity to witness the spectacular Dev Deepawali celebration, where Varanasi glows with millions of diyas.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival at Varanasi airport. Pls. schdedule a flight before 1330 hrs\xa0\n\xa0\nMeet and greet and at 1330 hrs we get transferred to Hotel. Checkin and freshen up.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter lunch at 1600 Hrs we get transfer to Ganges for Boating and Evening Ganga Aarti on famous Dashashwamedh Ghat. Dashashwamedh Ghat is the main ghat in Varanasi on the Ganga River. It is located close to Vishwanath Temple and is probably the most spectacular ghat. Two Hindu legends are associated with it: According to one, Lord Brahma created it to welcome Lord Shiva. According to another legend, Lord Brahma sacrificed ten horses during Dasa-Ashwamedha yajna performed here.\xa0\n\xa0\nOvernight in Varanasi.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Pinnacle/Buddha Lineage or similar in Varanasi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi\xa0\n\xa0\nEarly morning Temple darshan (Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir, Kala Bhairov Mandir) followed with Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir & Benaras Hindu University (BHU). After breakfast move for Sarnath (Sarnath is the place where Gautam Buddha after attain enlightenment delivers his first sermon to 5 followers).\n\xa0\nSightseeing of Sarnath including Sarnath Museum (Our National Emblem excavated from Sarnath is on Display built by Samrat Ashoka), Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple. Evening is free.\n\xa0\nOvernight in Varanasi.\n\xa0\nNote:\n\nBoats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME.\nVIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Pinnacle/Buddha Lineage or similar in Varanasi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi - Prayagraj\xa0 (145 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter early brea