ift of nature and the gods. Located in the Banda district of modern Uttar Pradesh(U.P), on the banks of river Paisuni(Mandikini), Chitrakoot is a tranquil retreat on the northern spur of the Vindhyas. Just 6 km south of Karvi and 72 km south east of Banda district on the road to Allahabad, Chitrakoot Dham is one of the most ancient holy pilgrim places of India. Legends have it that it was the abode of Lord Rama, his wife Sita and brother Lakshman for eleven years of their fourteen years of exile. This is also the place,where they came in contact with sage Atri and sati Anasuya.This abode of the gods is credited to have seen the incarnations of Brahma,Vishnu and Mahesh. Chitrakoot ,sacred with the touch of Lord\'s feet,was where Goswami Tulsidas, the creator of the epic "Shri Ramcharitmanas" spent many years of his life. Dotted with innumerable temples and shrines, nature\'s splendor here is wrapped in peace and tranquility, permeated only by singing birds and gushing streams.). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Prayagraj.\n\xa0\nPlaces of Interest:- Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Placid/Rama Continental or similar in Prayagraj'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nPrayagraj - Ayodhaya (180 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Ayodhaya (Ayodhya, also known as Saketa, is an ancient city of India, believed to be the birthplace of Rama and setting of the epic Ramayana. It is adjacent to Faizabad city in the central region of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh. Ayodhya used to be the capital of the ancient Kosala Kingdom. Owing to the belief as the birthplace of Rama, Ayodhya (Awadh) has been regarded as one of the seven most important pilgrimage sites (Saptapuri) for Hindus. It is believed that the birth spot of Rama). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Ayodhaya.\n\xa0\nPlaces of Interest:- Ram Janam Bhoomi; Kanak Bhawan; Hanuman Garhi; Raj Darbar; Karsevak Sthal.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Krinoscco or similar in\xa0Ayodhaya\xa0'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nAyodhaya - Varanasi Drop Via Chpaiya (250 Km. 5-6 Hrs. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter early breakfast, checkout from hotel in Ayodhya to move for Varanasi airport for onward/return journey.\xa0\n\xa0\nPls. Note: Flight should be after 7 PM onwards from Varanasi Airport', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 44500.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nUsual vehicles used are an Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per the itinerary for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\xa0\nA/c in the Vehicle will be switched off during a hilly drive.\nPlease consult the driver/local representative for the next day’s sightseeing schedule/Transfers timings.\xa0\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/Bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as the vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonuments will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Parks are Closed Around Mid Jun-Mid Nov.\xa0\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Varanasi\n\nDashashwamedh Ghat\nKashi Vishwanath\nAnnapurna Mandir\nKala Bhairov Mandir\nSankat Mochan Mandir\nDurga Mandir\nTulsi Manas Mandir\nBenaras Hindu University\nSarnath\nAncient ruins\nMahabodhi society Temple\n\nPrayagraj\n\nHoly Dip In Sangam\nBada Hanuman Mandir\nAkshayvat Tree\nChitrakoot\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 25 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Hotels:\n\nTwin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nAll meals option are pure veg/non-veg/Jain food\nIn Ayodhya pure veg meals are available\nBreakfasts: 05; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 05\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be packed or en-route in a restaurant/hotel\nExtra toppings: Daily evening snacks with tea/coffee/coconut water/fresh drink/ice cream\n\nSpecial Experiences, Sightseeing and Activities:\n\nBoating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by HAND Boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits)\nAll Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi -\xa0 Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal\n\n\nAdiitional Inclusions:\n\nTransfers: Transfers and sightseeing by air-conditioned vehicles (Subject to Min. 20 Pax)\nGuides: Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot\nWater: 2-liter water bottle per person per day\nEntrance fees: All entrance fees included in the itinerary\xa0\nVIP Darshan:\xa0 \xa0Kashi Vishwanath temple\nMinimum Operating Strength for the Group is 10 Pax\nTour Manager : Local Tour Escort from 15 Pax Onwards. Professional Tour Manager From 25 Pax Onwards.\xa0\n\nInsurance\xa0\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n\nExtra add-on (If possible):\n\nLanguage Pandit For Rituals (Varanasi, Prayagraj)\nSpecial Puja like Mangala Aarti, Pind Dan Puja\nExcursion to Bodh Gaya\nMake You Own Regional Group\n\nVehicle Details:\n\nType: Vehicles as per group size on a sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; vehicle type cannot be confirmed at the time of booking)\nUsage: Vehicle is not at disposal; it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\nSeat Allotment: Seats in the vehicle are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis at the venue, regardless of booking dates\n\nNote:\n\nBoats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME.\nVIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny airfare/rail fare\nRemittance charge/Bank charge for transfer of money.\nTips and gratuities\nAny Jungle/National Park Safari.\nMobile/ camera/video tickets/monument entry\nChristmas & New Year Gala Dinner cost\nMeals other than mentioned.\nAny VIP Darshan/Dakshina/Prashad/Garland fees\nAny personal nature expenses.\nGST Extra\nAny guide/escort\nPersonal expenditure like soft drinks, mineral water, phone calls, tips, porter age etc.\nAnything not specifically mentioned in the “Package tour price includes” box.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nHigh season surcharge, applicable during New Year, Puja, special dates.\nHigh Season / Special events supplements will be applicable at the time of booking only.\nAny optional tour.\n\n\xa0\nDirect Darshan Ticket Portal Link -\xa0\nhttps://www.shrikashivishwanath.org/\nhttps://online.srjbtkshetra.org/#/login\xa0\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': 'Basics\n\xa0\n\nPrice is subject to change\xa0\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of the Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. An Upgrade to a Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\xa0\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on the current tariff & are subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\n\xa0\nHotels\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges.\xa0\nPlease remember that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expense arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress/Roll over Extra mattress on the floor provided where a proper extra bed isn’t available.\xa0\nIn case the guests cannot climb higher floors, we request you to update us at the time of booking, so that we may take the appropriate action and try for rooms on the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hilly areas, scarcity of water & electricity may happen. To overcome the water crisis, certain hotels have a fixed schedule for supplying hot & cold water. We strongly regret the inconvenience and look forward to your cooperation.\nOn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it.\xa0\nThere will not be any refund in case any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy - Tea/coffee maker/mini fridge/enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, loofah, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, the menu will be on a fixed plan/buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks/liquor, Soups or Deserts. For an order on A-la-Carte basis, guests are requested to make a direct payment for additional items.\n\n\xa0\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicles used are an Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per the itinerary for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\xa0\nA/c in the Vehicle will be switched off during a hilly drive.\nPlease consult the driver/local representative for the next day’s sightseeing schedule/Transfers timings.\xa0\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/Bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as the vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonuments will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Parks are Closed Around Mid Jun-Mid Nov.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\xa0\nAll arrangements made by the Company are in capacity of an agent only. The Company will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us in situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of a discontinued itinerary due to these reasons, no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/40637097564_10b682199c_k.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/itinerary/8403831008_080f39d1ef_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/itinerary/48011063662_e70a005e73_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/itinerary/47519436781_5d96ebe956_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/itinerary/49408764761_079785d448_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/itinerary/KanakBhawan.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011603/itinerary/49211464657_f049880725_k.jpg']}, 'score': 2.774882, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013746', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013746', 'availableMonths': ['june_2027', 'april_2027', 'november_2026', 'may_2027', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Kashi To Kathmandu Bhakti Yatra', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bhairahawa', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kathmandu', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kathmandu', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pokhara', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pokhara', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["10 Days Fully Loaded Pilgrimage Across Sacred Sites of India and Nepal With All Meals, Evening Tea/Coffee; Snacks; Guided Darshan; Internal Flights Three Flights Fares between 3 Sectors : Bhairahawa – Kathmandu; Kathmandu – Pokhara; Pokhara – Bhairahawa Pandit Ji Assisted Darshan at Kashi Vishwanath Ji. Guided Darshan at Ayodhya Aarti At Pehwa Lake Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by hand boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits) The journey offers spiritual enlightenment, cultural immersion, and visits to revered religious landmarks across India and Nepal, including Varanasi's Ganges, Lumbini's Buddha birthplace, Kathmandu's Hindu and Buddhist temples, Pokhara's serene lakeside, and Ayodhya, the birthplace of Shri Ram. Covers Important Temples of Vishwanath, Pashupatinath Temple and more."], 'pdfName': 'PKG013746_0_20260916122949.pdf', 'price': 76900, 'packageSummary': "The 'Kashi To Kathmandu Bhakti Yatra' package is a 10-day fully loaded pilgrimage tour covering Varanasi, Ayodhya, Bhairahawa, Pokhara, and Kathmandu across India and Nepal. This spiritual journey includes all meals, evening refreshments, and three internal flights connecting Bhairahawa, Kathmandu, and Pokhara to ensure a seamless travel experience. Key highlights of the itinerary include a Pandit Ji assisted darshan at Kashi Vishwanath Ji, guided darshan in Ayodhya, a scenic hand-boat ride on the River Ganges in Varanasi, and an evening aarti at Phewa Lake. Participants will enjoy spiritual enlightenment and cultural immersion as they visit revered landmarks such as the Pashupatinath Temple, the birthplace of Buddha in Lumbini, and the birthplace of Shri Ram in Ayodhya.", 'images': ['day1.jpg', 'day2.jpg', 'day3.jpg', 'day4.jpg', 'day5.jpg', 'Day6.jpg', 'day7.jpg', 'day8.jpg', 'day9.jpg', 'day10.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 76900, 'thumbnailImage': 'srpnepal.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Domestic Diwali Special', 'Family', 'Domestic Winter GIT', 'Spiritual'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013746 is named \'Kashi To Kathmandu Bhakti Yatra\' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Varanasi, Meals: Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi Arrival Welcome to Varanasi. Varanasi is also known as Banaras or Kashi, a city on the banks of the Ganges. Transfer to Hotel. In evening, get ready to experience one of the most memorable moments of your life, as you will be taken to River Ganges. Enjoy Ganges Aarti. Get a glimpse of the spiritualism at the Ganges Ghats (river front) and Overnight stay at Varanasi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Varanasi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi Local Sightseeing Today morning after breakfast, you will be taken for a boat ride on the Ganges. It is a mystical and spiritual experience as you watch people offering water to the Sun God and devotees taking holy dip in the Ganges. We will visit all the famous Ghats of Varanasi by the boat. Visit the below : Kashi Vishwanath temple: It is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas, sacred shrines believed to be places where Shiva manifested as a pillar of light. The temple is situated on the western bank of the holy Ganges River. VIP Darshan with Pandit Ji at Kashi Vishwanath Ji. Annapurna Temple: one of the most famous Hindu temples (Mandir) in the holy city of Varanasi. This temple has great religious importance in Hinduism. The Bharat Mata temple: Instead of traditional statues of gods and goddesses, this temple has a huge map of Akhand Bharat carved in marble Sankat Mochan (Hanuman temple): he Sankat Mochan Hanuman Temple is a Hindu temple in Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh, India dedicated to the Hindu deity Hanuman, in his form as "Sankat Mochan," Manas Mandir: The Tulsi Manas Mandir is a prominent temple in Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh, known for its association with the saint and poet Goswami Tulsidas Back to hotel breakfast. In the evening enjoy shopping of Banarasi saris and overnight stay., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bhairahawa, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Drive to Bhairahawa Breakfast at hotel. Drive to Bhairahawa, an approximately 296 km away and a 7-to-8-hour drive. Check In to hotel, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kathmandu, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Lumbini Sightseeing & Fly to Kathmandu Breakfast at hotel Check out & visit Lumbini Lumbini (Birthplace of Gautama Buddha) Major attractions in Lumbini are: Maya Devi Temple: a significant Hindu and Buddhist site, with two temples bearing the name: one in Haridwar, India, dedicated to the goddess Maya, and another in Lumbini, Nepal, marking the birthplace of Buddha. World Peace Pagoda: The large World Peace Pagoda at the northern end of Lumbini is designed to be a symbol to unite humanity in a desire for peace. Lumbini Museum: Tucked away at the northern end of the compound, this museum is devoted to the life of the Buddha, with a nice collection of artifacts and photos from Buddhist sites around the world Royal Thai Buddhist Monastery: The Royal Thai Monastery in Lumbini, Nepal, is one of the magnificent monasteries that echo the significant historical and spiritual value of the region. Myanmar Golden Temple: Myanmar Golden Temple in Lumbini is the oldest structure of the city. Built in Burmese style of architecture, the temple is dedicated to Lord Buddha Then transfer to Airport to fly Kathmandu and transfer to hotel Check in to hotel rest of the day leisure, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kathmandu, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Kathmandu Local Sightseeing Breakfast at hotel Afterward, visit the following sites: Pashupatinath Temple: A sacred Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Shiva. Witness the rituals and ceremonies along the Baghmati River Guheshwori Shakti peeth: A Significant religious site for Goddess Durga Bouddanath Stupa: One of the Largest Stupa in the world and UNESCO World Heritage Site. Walk around the stupa, spin prayer wheels Swyambunath Stupa (Monkey Temple): A UNESCO World Heritage site located on a hilltop offering a panoramic view of Kathmandu Valley and explore the stupa\'s intricate architecture Kathmandu Durbar Square: Also known as Hanuman Dhoka, is a UNESCO World Heritage site Key attractions include Hanuman Dhoka Place, Kumari Ghar (home of the living goddess, Kumari), Taleju Temple, Shiva - Parvati Temple, Various Temples and Palaces: The square is filled with numerous temples, palaces and other architectural wonders, each with its own unique history and significance. Return to the hotel Leisure time explore local markets, Cafe, Casinos, club, etc. at your own, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Pokhara, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Fly to Pokhara Breakfast at hotel Drive to domestic Airport to fly Pokhara Pick up from Pokhara Airport then transfer to hotel Check in to your hotel Relax and explore Lakeside (Pokhara\'s tourist hub) on your own Evening (Optional) Attend Aarti at Phewa Lake: A spiritual and cultural event with chanting of Mantras, the ringing of bells and the soft glow of oil Lamps. It\'s a serene and mesmerizing experience that showcases the spiritual and cultural richness of Nepal., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Pokhara, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Pokhara Local Sightseeing Breakfast at hotel Sightseeing in Pokhara: Bindhyabasini Temple: A Hindu temple dedicated to Goddess Durga Shanti Stupa (World Peace Pagoda): A Buddhist stupa offering panoramic views of the city and mountains Pumdikot: Visit the tallest Shiva statue in Nepal surrounded by a white stupa and enjoys the serene surroundings Davis fall: A mesmerizing waterfall that disappears underground Gupteswor Mahadev Cave: A sacred cave dedicated to Lord Shiva, located opposite Davis Fall Phewa Lake: The Second Largest Lake in Nepal, with the famous Tal Barahi Temple. Back to the hotel or relax by the Lakeside and soak in the peaceful ambiance, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Fly to Bhairahawa & Drive to Ayodhya Drive to domestic Airport to fly Bhairahawa Arrive in Bhairahawa and begin your drive to Ayodhya, approximately 194 km away and 5/6-hour drive Arrive in Ayodhya and check in to your hotel Spend the evening at leisure or explore markets, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Ayodhya Sightseeing After breakfast, we will visit the most Holy place of Hindus & Birth place of Lord Rama, Kanak Bhawan: It is one of the most famous temples of Ayodhya. It is believed that this palace was gifted by Kaikeyi, immediately after the marriage of Rama with Sita and hence, it is their personal Hanuman Garhi: a significant Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman, revered for his devotion to Lord Rama Dasharath Darbar: refers to the court or kingdom of King Dasharatha, a central figure in the Hindu epic Ramayana, who ruled over Ayodhya& various temples, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure (Ayodhya) Breakfast at hotel Depart to your own destinations, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 76900.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\nHotel\xa0\nStandard\n\n\nVaranasi 2N\nHotel Alokah Kash\n\n\nBhairahawa 1N\nHotel Asian Buddha\n\n\nKathmandu 2N\xa0\nHotel Marshyangdi\n\n\nPokhara 2N\xa0\nHotel Lake star\n\n\nAyodhya 2N\xa0\nHotel Trayamb Inn by Asapin Hotel\n\n\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, All Meals - 9 Breakfast, 9 Lunches, 9 Dinner (buffet/thali/fixed). Inclusions: Accommodation in above mentioned hotel or similar in the base category room All Meals - 9 Breakfast, 9 Lunches, 9 Dinner (buffet/thali/fixed) Welcome Drink Evening Tea and Snacks 2 water bottle per person per day Accompanying Tour Escort (Subject to Min. 25 Pax) All major temple and monuments as per the itinerary only. Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by hand boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits) Three Flights Fares between 3 Sectors : Bhairahawa – Kathmandu; Kathmandu – Pokhara; Pokhara – Bhairahawa Pandit Ji Assisted Darshan at Kashi Vishwanath Ji. Guided Darshan at Ayodhya Attend Aarti at Phewa Lake All transfer & sightseeing as per the tour plan only Transfers and Sighsteeing in Sharing AC Vehicle And only as per the itinerary. Insurance (For the claim of insurance, customer must possess a valid Indian passport) Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Current GST Anything Not Mentioned in the Inclusions Rickshaw Ride Boat Ride on Phewa Lake Monument entrance fees during sightseeing Any additional services not mentioned in the itinerary Currency Advice: For your convenience during the trip, it is recommended to carry Indian Rupees (INR) in denominations of INR 100 or US Dollars (USD). These currencies are widely accepted and will help you manage your expensed more effectively while exploring Nepal Guide Supplement Cost @ INR 3,000 /- per day on spot basis (below 13 pax) & @ INR 4,500 /- per day on spot basis (above 14 pax) Tour Leader for above 25+ cost @ INR 10,500 /- for flight ticket. Product Terms and Conditions: Nepal Travel Guidelines Details of valid identity proof for travel to Kathmandu (Nepal) For Indian Nationals: 1. Age Group (0-3yrs): Valid Original Birth certificate on which DOB mentioned with parents’ name 2. Age Group (below 18yrs) : travelling with parent (or) guardian, will be allowed with School Id Card (original) or Letter Head from School with Photo and Principal’s Stamp & Signature or a valid passport (with the expiry date of six months at least from the date of return) if travelling alone 3. Age Group (18 and above) : Only valid Voter ID or Passport is valid to travel to Nepal 4. The Emergency Certificate and Identity Certificate issued by the Embassy of India, Kathmandu will be valid for single journey for travelling back to India. Also Note:- 1. Aadhaar (UID) card / PAN card / Driving License are not an acceptable travel document for travel to Nepal. 2. Certificate of Registration issued by the Embassy of India, Kathmandu, Nepal to Indian nationals is not an acceptable travel document for travelling between India & Nepal Tour price is subject to change as per the occupancy on the tour. Early birds get the best deal! Itinerary is subject to change on ground keeping the arrival time / on ground feasibility. Few of the sightseeing are closed during the week which we shall try to cover next day. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Room up-gradation payable at the hotel directly Please be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. In hills, most of the hotels are located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it Passengers with children need to carry Birth Certificate along with School ID card (ID proof should be valid for 6 months from the travel Date) The old Indian Currency of INR 500 and 1000 are no more a legal tender currency in Nepal. The New Indian 500 as well as the 2000 denominations are also not valid. The Indian 100 or below notes are valid All Indian nationals visiting Nepal does not require visa to enter Nepal. However, they MUST produce any of the following documents. Valid Indian Passport (Validity Should be more than 06 Months at the end of the Tour) Election/Voter ID card Children below the age of 17 year without the above mentioned travel documents, the following are required: a) Original Birth Certificate in English. (School going child should provide school ID in addition with Birth Certificate) NOTE: All documents must be original and photocopy of it will not be considered a valid document during travel. Package and rates offered are not valid OCI, NRIs and PIO Passport Holders and Foreigner nationals Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to acute shortage of water supply on the hills, there is restricted water supply by the hotels in the rooms. Please co-operate with hotels on this front. Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the vehicle reporting may get delayed. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.. Highlights of the package: 10 Days Fully Loaded Pilgrimage Across Sacred Sites of India and Nepal With All Meals, Evening Tea/Coffee; Snacks; Guided Darshan; Internal Flights Three Flights Fares between 3 Sectors : Bhairahawa – Kathmandu; Kathmandu – Pokhara; Pokhara – Bhairahawa Pandit Ji Assisted Darshan at Kashi Vishwanath Ji. Guided Darshan at Ayodhya Aarti At Pehwa Lake Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by hand boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits) The journey offers spiritual enlightenment, cultural immersion, and visits to revered religious landmarks across India and Nepal, including Varanasi\'s Ganges, Lumbini\'s Buddha birthplace, Kathmandu\'s Hindu and Buddhist temples, Pokhara\'s serene lakeside, and Ayodhya, the birthplace of Shri Ram. Covers Important Temples of Vishwanath, Pashupatinath Temple and more..', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'KTKDNP', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Kashi To Kathmandu Bhakti Yatra' package is a 10-day fully loaded pilgrimage tour covering Varanasi, Ayodhya, Bhairahawa, Pokhara, and Kathmandu across India and Nepal. This spiritual journey includes all meals, evening refreshments, and three internal flights connecting Bhairahawa, Kathmandu, and Pokhara to ensure a seamless travel experience. Key highlights of the itinerary include a Pandit Ji assisted darshan at Kashi Vishwanath Ji, guided darshan in Ayodhya, a scenic hand-boat ride on the River Ganges in Varanasi, and an evening aarti at Phewa Lake. Participants will enjoy spiritual enlightenment and cultural immersion as they visit revered landmarks such as the Pashupatinath Temple, the birthplace of Buddha in Lumbini, and the birthplace of Shri Ram in Ayodhya.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi Arrival\n\xa0\nWelcome to Varanasi. Varanasi is also known as Banaras or Kashi, a city on the banks of the Ganges. Transfer to Hotel. In evening, get ready to experience one of the most memorable moments of your life, as you will be taken to River Ganges. Enjoy Ganges Aarti.\nGet a glimpse of the spiritualism at the Ganges Ghats (river front) and Overnight stay at Varanasi.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nLunch & Dinner\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Alokah Kashi or similar in Varanasi'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi Local Sightseeing\n\xa0\nToday morning after breakfast, you will be taken for a boat ride on the Ganges. It is a mystical and spiritual experience as you watch people offering water to the Sun God and devotees taking holy dip in the Ganges.\nWe will visit all the famous Ghats of Varanasi by the boat. Visit the below :\nKashi Vishwanath temple:\xa0It is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas, sacred shrines believed to be places where Shiva manifested as a pillar of light. The temple is situated on the western bank of the holy Ganges River. VIP Darshan with Pandit Ji at Kashi Vishwanath Ji.\nAnnapurna Temple:\xa0one of the most famous Hindu temples (Mandir) in the holy city of Varanasi. This temple has great religious importance in Hinduism.\nThe Bharat Mata temple:\xa0Instead of traditional statues of gods and goddesses, this temple has a huge map of Akhand Bharat carved in marble\nSankat Mochan (Hanuman temple):\xa0he Sankat Mochan Hanuman Temple is a Hindu temple in Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh, India dedicated to the Hindu deity Hanuman, in his form as "Sankat Mochan,"\nManas Mandir:\xa0The Tulsi Manas Mandir is a prominent temple in Varanasi, Uttar Pradesh, known for its association with the saint and poet Goswami Tulsidas\nBack to hotel breakfast.\nIn the evening enjoy shopping of Banarasi saris and overnight stay.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Alokah Kashi or similar in Varanasi'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nDrive to Bhairahawa\xa0\n\xa0\nBreakfast at hotel.\nDrive to Bhairahawa, an approximately 296 km away and a 7-to-8-hour drive.\nCheck In to hotel', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Asian Buddha Similar or similar in Bhairahawa'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nLumbini Sightseeing & Fly to Kathmandu\n\xa0\nBreakfast at hotel\nCheck out & visit Lumbini\nLumbini (Birthplace of Gautama Buddha)\nMajor attractions in Lumbini are:\nMaya Devi Temple:\xa0a significant Hindu and Buddhist site, with two temples bearing the name: one in Haridwar, India, dedicated to the goddess Maya, and another in Lumbini, Nepal, marking the birthplace of Buddha.\nWorld Peace Pagoda:\xa0The large World Peace Pagoda at the northern end of Lumbini is designed to be a symbol to unite humanity in a desire for peace.\nLumbini Museum:\xa0Tucked away at the northern end of the compound, this museum is devoted to the life of the Buddha, with a nice collection of artifacts and photos from Buddhist sites around the world\nRoyal Thai Buddhist Monastery:\xa0The Royal Thai Monastery in Lumbini, Nepal, is one of the magnificent monasteries that echo the significant historical and spiritual value of the region.\nMyanmar Golden Temple:\xa0Myanmar Golden Temple in Lumbini is the oldest structure of the city. Built in Burmese style of architecture, the temple is dedicated to Lord Buddha\nThen transfer to Airport to fly Kathmandu and transfer to hotel\nCheck in to hotel rest of the day leisure', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Marshyangdi/ Simal/ Skye inn or similar in Kathmandu'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nKathmandu Local Sightseeing\n\xa0\nBreakfast at hotel\nAfterward, visit the following sites:\nPashupatinath Temple:\xa0A sacred Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Shiva. Witness the rituals and ceremonies along the Baghmati River\nGuheshwori Shakti peeth:\xa0A Significant religious site for Goddess Durga\nBouddanath Stupa:\xa0One of the Largest Stupa in the world and UNESCO World Heritage Site. Walk around the stupa, spin prayer wheels\nSwyambunath Stupa (Monkey Temple):\xa0 A UNESCO World Heritage site located on a hilltop offering a panoramic view of Kathmandu Valley and explore the stupa's intricate architecture\nKathmandu Durbar Square:\xa0Also known as Hanuman Dhoka, is a UNESCO World Heritage site\nKey attractions include\nHanuman Dhoka Place, Kumari Ghar (home of the living goddess, Kumari), Taleju Temple, Shiva - Parvati Temple, Various Temples and Palaces: The square is filled with numerous temples, palaces and other architectural wonders, each with its own unique history and significance.\xa0\xa0\nReturn to the hotel\nLeisure time explore local markets, Cafe, Casinos, club, etc. at your own", 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Marshyangdi/ Simal/ Skye inn or similar in Kathmandu'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nFly to Pokhara\n\xa0\nBreakfast at hotel\nDrive to domestic Airport to fly Pokhara\nPick up from Pokhara Airport then transfer to hotel\nCheck in to your hotel\nRelax and explore Lakeside (Pokhara's tourist hub) on your own\nEvening (Optional)\nAttend Aarti at Phewa Lake: A spiritual and cultural event with chanting of Mantras, the ringing of bells and the soft glow of oil Lamps. It's a serene and mesmerizing experience that showcases the spiritual and cultural richness of Nepal.", 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Lake star/White pear or similar in Pokhara'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nPokhara Local Sightseeing\xa0\n\xa0\nBreakfast at hotel\nSightseeing in Pokhara:\nBindhyabasini Temple:\xa0A Hindu temple dedicated to Goddess Durga\nShanti Stupa (World Peace Pagoda):\xa0A Buddhist stupa offering panoramic views of the city and mountains\nPumdikot:\xa0Visit the tallest Shiva statue in Nepal surrounded by a white stupa and enjoys the serene surroundings\nDavis fall:\xa0A mesmerizing waterfall that disappears underground\nGupteswor Mahadev Cave:\xa0A sacred cave dedicated to Lord Shiva, located opposite Davis Fall\nPhewa Lake:\xa0The Second Largest Lake in Nepal, with the famous Tal Barahi Temple.\nBack to the hotel or relax by the Lakeside and soak in the peaceful ambiance', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Lake star/White pearl or similar in Pokhara'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nFly to Bhairahawa & Drive to Ayodhya\n\xa0\nDrive to domestic Airport to fly Bhairahawa\nArrive in Bhairahawa and begin your drive to Ayodhya, approximately 194 km away and 5/6-hour drive\nArrive in Ayodhya and check in to your hotel\nSpend the evening at leisure or explore markets\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Trayamb Inn by Asapin Hotel or similar in\xa0Ayodhya'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nAyodhya Sightseeing\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, we will visit the most Holy place of Hindus & Birth place of Lord Rama,\nKanak Bhawan:\xa0It is one of the most famous temples of Ayodhya. It is believed that this palace was gifted by Kaikeyi, immediately after the marriage of Rama with Sita and hence, it is their personal\nHanuman Garhi:\xa0a significant Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman, revered for his devotion to Lord Rama\nDasharath Darbar:\xa0refers to the court or kingdom of King Dasharatha, a central figure in the Hindu epic Ramayana, who ruled over Ayodhya& various temples', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel Trayamb Inn by Asapin Hotel or similar in\xa0Ayodhya'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nDeparture (Ayodhya)\xa0\n\xa0\nBreakfast at hotel\nDepart to your own destinations', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nNA\xa0'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\nHotel\xa0\nStandard\n\n\nVaranasi 2N\nHotel Alokah Kash\n\n\nBhairahawa 1N\nHotel Asian Buddha\n\n\nKathmandu 2N\xa0\nHotel Marshyangdi\n\n\nPokhara 2N\xa0\nHotel Lake star\n\n\nAyodhya 2N\xa0\nHotel Trayamb Inn by Asapin Hotel\n\n\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': '\n\n\nHotel\xa0\nStandard\n\n\nVaranasi 2N\nHotel Alokah Kash\n\n\nBhairahawa 1N\nHotel Asian Buddha\n\n\nKathmandu 2N\xa0\nHotel Marshyangdi\n\n\nPokhara 2N\xa0\nHotel Lake star\n\n\nAyodhya 2N\xa0\nHotel Trayamb Inn by Asapin Hotel\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'NP', 'countryName': 'Nepal', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 76900.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\nHotel\xa0\nStandard\n\n\nVaranasi 2N\nHotel Alokah Kash\n\n\nBhairahawa 1N\nHotel Asian Buddha\n\n\nKathmandu 2N\xa0\nHotel Marshyangdi\n\n\nPokhara 2N\xa0\nHotel Lake star\n\n\nAyodhya 2N\xa0\nHotel Trayamb Inn by Asapin Hotel\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', 'All Meals - 9 Breakfast, 9 Lunches, 9 Dinner (buffet/thali/fixed)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['All transfers & sightseeing by AC vehicles\n\nVehicles as per group size on Sharing basis\nVehicle is not at disposal – means it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\nSeats Allotment in the Vehicle is on first come first serve basis at the venue, irrespective of the booking dates.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Varanasi\n\n\xa0Kashi Vishwanath temple\nAnnapurna Temple\nThe Bharat Mata temple\nSankat Mochan (Hanuman temple)\nManas Mandir\n\nLumbini\n\nMaya Devi Temple\nWorld Peace Pagoda\nLumbini Museum\nRoyal Thai Buddhist Monastery\nMyanmar Golden Temple\n\nKathmandu\n\nPashupatinath Temple\nGuheshwori Shakti peeth\nBouddanath Stup\nSwyambunath Stupa (Monkey Temple)\nKathmandu Durbar Square\n\nPokhara\n\nBindhyabasini Temple\nShanti Stupa (World Peace Pagoda)\nPumdikot\nDavis fall\nGupteswor Mahadev Cave\nPhewa Lake\n\nAyodhya\n\nKanak Bhawan\nHanuman Garh\nDasharath Darbar\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\nAccommodation in above mentioned hotel or similar in the base category room\nAll Meals - 9 Breakfast, 9 Lunches, 9 Dinner (buffet/thali/fixed)\nWelcome Drink\nEvening Tea and Snacks\n2 water bottle per person per day\nAccompanying Tour Escort (Subject to Min. 25 Pax)\nAll major temple and monuments as per the itinerary only.\nBoating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by hand boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits)\nThree Flights Fares between 3 Sectors : Bhairahawa – Kathmandu; Kathmandu – Pokhara; Pokhara – Bhairahawa\nPandit Ji Assisted Darshan\xa0at Kashi Vishwanath Ji.\nGuided Darshan at Ayodhya\nAttend Aarti at Phewa Lake\nAll transfer & sightseeing as per the tour plan only\nTransfers and Sighsteeing in Sharing AC Vehicle And only as per the itinerary.\n\n\xa0\nInsurance (For the claim of insurance, customer must possess a valid Indian passport)\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n', 'exclusions': '\nCurrent GST\xa0\nAnything Not Mentioned in the Inclusions\nRickshaw Ride\nBoat Ride on Phewa Lake\nMonument entrance fees during sightseeing\nAny additional services not mentioned in the itinerary\xa0\nCurrency Advice: For your convenience during the trip, it is recommended to carry Indian Rupees (INR) in denominations of INR 100 or US Dollars (USD). These currencies are widely accepted and will help you manage your expensed more effectively while exploring Nepal\nGuide Supplement Cost @ INR 3,000 /- per day on spot basis (below 13 pax) & @ INR 4,500 /- per day on spot basis (above 14 pax)\nTour Leader for above 25+ cost @ INR 10,500 /- for flight ticket\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nNepal Travel Guidelines\nDetails of valid identity proof for travel to Kathmandu (Nepal)\nFor Indian Nationals:\n1. Age Group (0-3yrs): Valid Original Birth certificate on which DOB mentioned with parents’ name\n2. Age Group (below 18yrs) : travelling with parent (or) guardian, will be allowed with School Id Card (original) or Letter Head from School with Photo and Principal’s Stamp & Signature or a valid passport (with the expiry date of six months at least from the date of return) if travelling alone\n3. Age Group (18 and above) : Only valid Voter ID or Passport is valid to travel to Nepal\n4. The Emergency Certificate and Identity Certificate issued by the Embassy of India, Kathmandu will be valid for single journey for travelling back to India.\nAlso Note:-\n1. Aadhaar (UID) card / PAN card / Driving License are not an acceptable travel document for travel to Nepal.\n\xa0\n2. Certificate of Registration issued by the Embassy of India, Kathmandu, Nepal to Indian nationals is not an acceptable travel document for travelling between India & Nepal\n\xa0\n\nTour price is subject to change as per the occupancy on the tour. Early birds get the best deal!\nItinerary is subject to change on ground keeping the arrival time / on ground feasibility. Few of the sightseeing are closed during the week which we shall try to cover next day.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nRoom up-gradation payable at the hotel directly\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nIn hills, most of the hotels are located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it\nPassengers with children need to carry Birth Certificate along with School ID card (ID proof should be valid for 6 months from the travel Date)\nThe old Indian Currency of INR 500 and 1000 are no more a legal tender currency in Nepal. The New Indian 500 as well as the 2000 denominations are also not valid. The Indian 100 or below notes are valid\nAll Indian nationals visiting Nepal does not require visa to enter Nepal. However, they MUST produce any of the following documents.\n\n\nValid Indian Passport (Validity Should be more than 06 Months at the end of the Tour)\nElection/Voter ID card\nChildren below the age of 17 year without the above mentioned travel documents, the following are required:\na) Original Birth Certificate in English. (School going child should provide school ID in addition with Birth Certificate)\n\n\nNOTE: All documents must be original and photocopy of it will not be considered a valid document during travel. Package and rates offered are not valid OCI, NRIs and PIO Passport Holders and Foreigner nationals\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to acute shortage of water supply on the hills, there is restricted water supply by the hotels in the rooms. Please co-operate with hotels on this front.\nExtra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the vehicle reporting may get delayed. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/srpnepal.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day3.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day4.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day5.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/Day6.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day7.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day8.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day9.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013746/itinerary/day10.jpg']}, 'score': 2.5407047, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015018', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015018', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Anant Kashi Ayodhya  Bhakti Yatra Durga Puja Special', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prayagraj', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prayagraj', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['VIP Darshan - Kashi Vishwanath temple Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot; Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi (Subject to availability) Extras: Escorted Darshan in Varanasi, and Ayodhya; Experience Manager** Stay in Deluxe 3* Hotels in Varanasi, Ayodhya, Prayagraj (Chitrakot Excursion) All meals and evening tea/coffee with snacks All major temple and monuments All Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi - Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal Experience Dev Deepawali Celebration for the Departure Dated 04th Nov 2025. Dev Deepawali marks the descent of gods to Earth. Varanasi glows with millions of diyas along the Ganges.'], 'pdfName': 'PKG015018_0_20260915085754', 'price': 40990, 'packageSummary': "The 'Anant Kashi Ayodhya Bhakti Yatra Durga Puja Special' is a 6-day spiritual tour covering Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, and Chitrakoot. This comprehensive itinerary features VIP Darshan at the Kashi Vishwanath temple, guided Teerth Darshans of holy sites, a day tour of Chitrakoot, and a scenic boat ride on the River Ganges. Participants will enjoy escorted temple visits, deluxe three-star hotel stays, and all meals while exploring major landmarks such as Dashashwamedh Ghat, Sarnath, the holy Sangam for a ritual dip, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, and Hanuman Garhi. Additionally, guests on the November 4, 2025 departure will experience the magical Dev Deepawali celebration, witnessing Varanasi glow with millions of earthen lamps along the sacred river.", 'images': ['8403831008_080f39d1ef_b.jpg', '48011063662_e70a005e73_h.jpg', '47519436781_5d96ebe956_h.jpg', '49408764761_079785d448_k.jpg', 'KanakBhawan.jpg', '49211464657_f049880725_k.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 40990, 'thumbnailImage': '40637097564_10b682199c_k.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Domestic Winter GIT', 'Winter GIT', 'Durga Puja Domestic', 'Family', 'Spiritual'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Durga Puja Special', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG015018 is named \'Anant Kashi Ayodhya  Bhakti Yatra Durga Puja Special\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Varanasi, Meals: Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi Arrival at Varanasi airport. Pls. schdedule a flight before 1330 hrs Meet and greet and at 1330 hrs we get transferred to Hotel. Checkin and freshen up. After lunch at 1600 Hrs we get transfer to Ganges for Boating and Evening Ganga Aarti on famous Dashashwamedh Ghat. Dashashwamedh Ghat is the main ghat in Varanasi on the Ganga River. It is located close to Vishwanath Temple and is probably the most spectacular ghat. Two Hindu legends are associated with it: According to one, Lord Brahma created it to welcome Lord Shiva. According to another legend, Lord Brahma sacrificed ten horses during Dasa-Ashwamedha yajna performed here. Overnight in Varanasi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Varanasi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi Early morning Temple darshan (Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir, Kala Bhairov Mandir) followed with Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir & Benaras Hindu University (BHU). After breakfast move for Sarnath (Sarnath is the place where Gautam Buddha after attain enlightenment delivers his first sermon to 5 followers). Sightseeing of Sarnath including Sarnath Museum (Our National Emblem excavated from Sarnath is on Display built by Samrat Ashoka), Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple. Evening is free. Overnight in Varanasi. Note: Boats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME. VIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Prayagraj, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Varanasi - Prayagraj (145 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way) After early breakfast check out and transfer to PRAYAGRAJ. (The city\'s original name – Prayag, or "place of offerings" – comes from its position at the Sangam (confluence) of the Ganga, Yamuna and Sarasvati rivers. It is the second-oldest city in India, and plays a central role in Hindu scriptures. Allahabad was originally called Kaushambi (now a separate district) by the Kuru rulers of Hastinapur, who developed it as their capital. Since then, Allahabad has been a political, cultural and administrative centre of the Doab region. Mughal emperor Akbar renamed it Ilahabad, which the British changed to Allahabad. In 1833 it became the seat of the Ceded and Conquered Provinces region before its capital was moved to Agra in 1835. Allahabad became the capital of the North-Western Provinces in 1858, and was the capital of India for a day. The city was the capital of the United Provinces from 1902 to 1920 and remained at the forefront of national importance during the struggle for Indian independence.) Places of interest HOLY DIP IN SANGAM, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree (Akshayavat ("the indestructible banyan tree") is a sacred fig tree mentioned in the Hindu mythology. According to a legend, once the sage Markandeya asked Lord Narayana to show him a specimen of the divine power. Narayana flooded the entire world for a moment, during which only the Akshayavat could be seen above the water level.) & Anand Bhawan (Birthplace of first Prime Minister of Independent India Pt. Jawaharlal Nehru) Experience the exclusivity of Magh Mela as you explore the sacred Sangam, witness vibrant rituals, and immerse yourself in the spiritual essence of this grand gathering., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Prayagraj, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Prayagraj - Chitrakoot - Prayagraj (120 Km 3-4 Hrs. One Way) After breakfast day trip to Chitrakoot (Chitrakoot, "the hills of many wonders" is indeed a gift of nature and the gods. Located in the Banda district of modern Uttar Pradesh(U.P), on the banks of river Paisuni(Mandikini), Chitrakoot is a tranquil retreat on the northern spur of the Vindhyas. Just 6 km south of Karvi and 72 km south east of Banda district on the road to Allahabad, Chitrakoot Dham is one of the most ancient holy pilgrim places of India. Legends have it that it was the abode of Lord Rama, his wife Sita and brother Lakshman for eleven years of their fourteen years of exile. This is also the place,where they came in contact with sage Atri and sati Anasuya.This abode of the gods is credited to have seen the incarnations of Brahma,Vishnu and Mahesh. Chitrakoot ,sacred with the touch of Lord\'s feet,was where Goswami Tulsidas, the creator of the epic "Shri Ramcharitmanas" spent many years of his life. Dotted with innumerable temples and shrines, nature\'s splendor here is wrapped in peace and tranquility, permeated only by singing birds and gushing streams.). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Prayagraj. Places of Interest:- Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Prayagraj - Ayodhaya (180 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way) After breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Ayodhaya (Ayodhya, also known as Saketa, is an ancient city of India, believed to be the birthplace of Rama and setting of the epic Ramayana. It is adjacent to Faizabad city in the central region of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh. Ayodhya used to be the capital of the ancient Kosala Kingdom. Owing to the belief as the birthplace of Rama, Ayodhya (Awadh) has been regarded as one of the seven most important pilgrimage sites (Saptapuri) for Hindus. It is believed that the birth spot of Rama). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Ayodhaya. Places of Interest:- Ram Janam Bhoomi; Kanak Bhawan; Hanuman Garhi; Raj Darbar; Karsevak Sthal., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ayodhaya - Varanasi Drop Via Chpaiya (250 Km. 5-6 Hrs. One Way) After early breakfast, checkout from hotel in Ayodhya to move for Varanasi airport for onward/return journey. Pls. Note: Flight should be after 7 PM onwards from Varanasi Airport, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 40990.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Hotels: Twin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar Meals: All meals option are pure veg/non-veg/Jain food In Ayodhya pure veg meals are available Breakfasts: 05; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 05 Breakfast & Dinners will be Buffet Lunches will be packed or en-route in a restaurant/hotel Extra toppings: Daily evening snacks with tea/coffee/coconut water/fresh drink/ice cream Special Experiences, Sightseeing and Activities: Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by HAND Boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits) All Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi - Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal Adiitional Inclusions: Transfers: Transfers and sightseeing by air-conditioned vehicles (Subject to Min. 20 Pax) Guides: Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot Water: 2-liter water bottle per person per day Entrance fees: All entrance fees included in the itinerary VIP Darshan: Kashi Vishwanath temple Minimum Operating Strength for the Group is 10 Pax Tour Manager : Local Tour Escort from 15 Pax Onwards. Professional Tour Manager From 25 Pax Onwards. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Extra add-on (If possible): Language Pandit For Rituals (Varanasi, Prayagraj) Special Puja like Mangala Aarti, Pind Dan Puja Excursion to Bodh Gaya Make You Own Regional Group Vehicle Details: Type: Vehicles as per group size on a sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; vehicle type cannot be confirmed at the time of booking) Usage: Vehicle is not at disposal; it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary. Seat Allotment: Seats in the vehicle are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis at the venue, regardless of booking dates Note: Boats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME. VIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month.. Exclusions: Any airfare/rail fare Remittance charge/Bank charge for transfer of money. Tips and gratuities Any Jungle/National Park Safari. Mobile/ camera/video tickets/monument entry Christmas & New Year Gala Dinner cost Meals other than mentioned. Any VIP Darshan/Dakshina/Prashad/Garland fees Any personal nature expenses. GST Extra Any guide/escort Personal expenditure like soft drinks, mineral water, phone calls, tips, porter age etc. Anything not specifically mentioned in the “Package tour price includes” box. Any expenses of personal nature. High season surcharge, applicable during New Year, Puja, special dates. High Season / Special events supplements will be applicable at the time of booking only. Any optional tour. Direct Darshan Ticket Portal Link - https://www.shrikashivishwanath.org/ https://online.srjbtkshetra.org/#/login. Product Terms and Conditions: Basics Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of the Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. An Upgrade to a Higher Category is available at an extra cost. All domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on the current tariff & are subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra. Hotels Many regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent. Packages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted. Quote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges. Please remember that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expense arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress/Roll over Extra mattress on the floor provided where a proper extra bed isn’t available. In case the guests cannot climb higher floors, we request you to update us at the time of booking, so that we may take the appropriate action and try for rooms on the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out. In hilly areas, scarcity of water & electricity may happen. To overcome the water crisis, certain hotels have a fixed schedule for supplying hot & cold water. We strongly regret the inconvenience and look forward to your cooperation. On hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in case any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip. The Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy - Tea/coffee maker/mini fridge/enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, loofah, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc. For meal plans, the menu will be on a fixed plan/buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks/liquor, Soups or Deserts. For an order on A-la-Carte basis, guests are requested to make a direct payment for additional items. TRANSPORTATION Usual vehicles used are an Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax Transfers as per the itinerary for the mentioned Sightseeing only. A/c in the Vehicle will be switched off during a hilly drive. Please consult the driver/local representative for the next day’s sightseeing schedule/Transfers timings. Due to unforeseen situations (force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/Bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as the vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP. Monuments will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Parks are Closed Around Mid Jun-Mid Nov. INCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS All arrangements made by the Company are in capacity of an agent only. The Company will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us in situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of a discontinued itinerary due to these reasons, no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.. Highlights of the package: VIP Darshan - Kashi Vishwanath temple Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot; Boating on River Ganges in Varanasi (Subject to availability) Extras: Escorted Darshan in Varanasi, and Ayodhya; Experience Manager** Stay in Deluxe 3* Hotels in Varanasi, Ayodhya, Prayagraj (Chitrakot Excursion) All meals and evening tea/coffee with snacks All major temple and monuments All Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi - Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal Experience Dev Deepawali Celebration for the Departure Dated 04th Nov 2025. Dev Deepawali marks the descent of gods to Earth. Varanasi glows with millions of diyas along the Ganges..', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'UPAKDP', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Anant Kashi Ayodhya Bhakti Yatra Durga Puja Special' is a 6-day spiritual tour covering Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, and Chitrakoot. This comprehensive itinerary features VIP Darshan at the Kashi Vishwanath temple, guided Teerth Darshans of holy sites, a day tour of Chitrakoot, and a scenic boat ride on the River Ganges. Participants will enjoy escorted temple visits, deluxe three-star hotel stays, and all meals while exploring major landmarks such as Dashashwamedh Ghat, Sarnath, the holy Sangam for a ritual dip, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, and Hanuman Garhi. Additionally, guests on the November 4, 2025 departure will experience the magical Dev Deepawali celebration, witnessing Varanasi glow with millions of earthen lamps along the sacred river.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival at Varanasi airport. Pls. schdedule a flight before 1330 hrs\xa0\n\xa0\nMeet and greet and at 1330 hrs we get transferred to Hotel. Checkin and freshen up.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter lunch at 1600 Hrs we get transfer to Ganges for Boating and Evening Ganga Aarti on famous Dashashwamedh Ghat. Dashashwamedh Ghat is the main ghat in Varanasi on the Ganga River. It is located close to Vishwanath Temple and is probably the most spectacular ghat. Two Hindu legends are associated with it: According to one, Lord Brahma created it to welcome Lord Shiva. According to another legend, Lord Brahma sacrificed ten horses during Dasa-Ashwamedha yajna performed here.\xa0\n\xa0\nOvernight in Varanasi.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDesc