capital of the United Provinces from 1902 to 1920 and remained at the forefront of national importance during the struggle for Indian independence.)\nPlaces of interest HOLY DIP IN SANGAM, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree (Akshayavat ("the indestructible banyan tree") is a sacred fig tree mentioned in the Hindu mythology. According to a legend, once the sage Markandeya asked Lord Narayana to show him a specimen of the divine power. Narayana flooded the entire world for a moment, during which only the Akshayavat could be seen above the water level.) & Anand Bhawan (Birthplace of first Prime Minister of Independent India Pt. Jawaharlal Nehru)\n\xa0\n\nExperience the exclusivity of Magh Mela as you explore the sacred Sangam, witness vibrant rituals, and immerse yourself in the spiritual essence of this grand gathering.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Placid/Rama Continental or similar in Prayagraj'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nPrayagraj - Chitrakoot - Prayagraj (120 Km 3-4 Hrs. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast day trip to Chitrakoot (Chitrakoot, "the hills of many wonders" is indeed a gift of nature and the gods. Located in the Banda district of modern Uttar Pradesh(U.P), on the banks of river Paisuni(Mandikini), Chitrakoot is a tranquil retreat on the northern spur of the Vindhyas. Just 6 km south of Karvi and 72 km south east of Banda district on the road to Allahabad, Chitrakoot Dham is one of the most ancient holy pilgrim places of India. Legends have it that it was the abode of Lord Rama, his wife Sita and brother Lakshman for eleven years of their fourteen years of exile. This is also the place,where they came in contact with sage Atri and sati Anasuya.This abode of the gods is credited to have seen the incarnations of Brahma,Vishnu and Mahesh. Chitrakoot ,sacred with the touch of Lord\'s feet,was where Goswami Tulsidas, the creator of the epic "Shri Ramcharitmanas" spent many years of his life. Dotted with innumerable temples and shrines, nature\'s splendor here is wrapped in peace and tranquility, permeated only by singing birds and gushing streams.). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Prayagraj.\n\xa0\nPlaces of Interest:- Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Placid/Rama Continental or similar in Prayagraj'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nPrayagraj - Ayodhaya (180 Km. 3-4 Hrs. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Ayodhaya (Ayodhya, also known as Saketa, is an ancient city of India, believed to be the birthplace of Rama and setting of the epic Ramayana. It is adjacent to Faizabad city in the central region of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh. Ayodhya used to be the capital of the ancient Kosala Kingdom. Owing to the belief as the birthplace of Rama, Ayodhya (Awadh) has been regarded as one of the seven most important pilgrimage sites (Saptapuri) for Hindus. It is believed that the birth spot of Rama). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Ayodhaya.\n\xa0\nPlaces of Interest:- Ram Janam Bhoomi; Kanak Bhawan; Hanuman Garhi; Raj Darbar; Karsevak Sthal.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Krinoscco or similar in\xa0Ayodhaya\xa0'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nAyodhaya - Varanasi Drop Via Chpaiya (250 Km. 5-6 Hrs. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter early breakfast, checkout from hotel in Ayodhya to move for Varanasi airport for onward/return journey.\xa0\n\xa0\nPls. Note: Flight should be after 7 PM onwards from Varanasi Airport', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 41000.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nUsual vehicles used are an Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per the itinerary for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\xa0\nA/c in the Vehicle will be switched off during a hilly drive.\nPlease consult the driver/local representative for the next day’s sightseeing schedule/Transfers timings.\xa0\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/Bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as the vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonuments will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Parks are Closed Around Mid Jun-Mid Nov.\xa0\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Varanasi\n\nDashashwamedh Ghat\nKashi Vishwanath\nAnnapurna Mandir\nKala Bhairov Mandir\nSankat Mochan Mandir\nDurga Mandir\nTulsi Manas Mandir\nBenaras Hindu University\nSarnath\nAncient ruins\nMahabodhi society Temple\n\nPrayagraj\n\nHoly Dip In Sangam\nBada Hanuman Mandir\nAkshayvat Tree\nChitrakoot\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 25 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Hotels:\n\nTwin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nAll meals option are pure veg/non-veg/Jain food\nIn Ayodhya pure veg meals are available\nBreakfasts: 05; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 05\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be packed or en-route in a restaurant/hotel\nExtra toppings: Daily evening snacks with tea/coffee/coconut water/fresh drink/ice cream\n\nSpecial Experiences, Sightseeing and Activities:\n\nBoating on River Ganges in Varanasi once during the stay by HAND Boat (If weather/water level/water flow permits)\nAll Must See Sightseeing with Entrances: Varanasi -\xa0 Dashashwamedh Ghat, Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir,Kala Bhairov Mandir, Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir, Benaras Hindu University, Sarnath, Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple, Anand Bhawan, Holy Dip In Sangam, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree, Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund, Ram Janam Bhoomi, Kanak Bhawan, Hanuman Garhi, Raj Darbar, Karsevak Sthal\n\n\nAdiitional Inclusions:\n\nTransfers: Transfers and sightseeing by air-conditioned vehicles (Subject to Min. 20 Pax)\nGuides: Guided Teerth Darshan of the Holy Sites of Varanasi, Prayagraj, Ayodhya, Day tour of Chitrakoot\nWater: 2-liter water bottle per person per day\nEntrance fees: All entrance fees included in the itinerary\xa0\nVIP Darshan:\xa0 \xa0Kashi Vishwanath temple\nMinimum Operating Strength for the Group is 10 Pax\nTour Manager : Local Tour Escort from 15 Pax Onwards. Professional Tour Manager From 25 Pax Onwards.\xa0\n\nInsurance\xa0\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n\nExtra add-on (If possible):\n\nLanguage Pandit For Rituals (Varanasi, Prayagraj)\nSpecial Puja like Mangala Aarti, Pind Dan Puja\nExcursion to Bodh Gaya\nMake You Own Regional Group\n\nVehicle Details:\n\nType: Vehicles as per group size on a sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; vehicle type cannot be confirmed at the time of booking)\nUsage: Vehicle is not at disposal; it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\nSeat Allotment: Seats in the vehicle are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis at the venue, regardless of booking dates\n\nNote:\n\nBoats in any locations are not covered DURING MONSOON & FLOOD TIME.\nVIP TICKET FOR KASHI VISHWANATH MANDIR IS NOT APPLICABLE FROM 10th July 2025 – 10th Aug 2025 due to Shravan month.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny airfare/rail fare\nRemittance charge/Bank charge for transfer of money.\nTips and gratuities\nAny Jungle/National Park Safari.\nMobile/ camera/video tickets/monument entry\nChristmas & New Year Gala Dinner cost\nMeals other than mentioned.\nAny VIP Darshan/Dakshina/Prashad/Garland fees\nAny personal nature expenses.\nGST Extra\nAny guide/escort\nPersonal expenditure like soft drinks, mineral water, phone calls, tips, porter age etc.\nAnything not specifically mentioned in the “Package tour price includes” box.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nHigh season surcharge, applicable during New Year, Puja, special dates.\nHigh Season / Special events supplements will be applicable at the time of booking only.\nAny optional tour.\n\n\xa0\nDirect Darshan Ticket Portal Link -\xa0\nhttps://www.shrikashivishwanath.org/\nhttps://online.srjbtkshetra.org/#/login\xa0\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': 'Basics\n\xa0\n\nPrice is subject to change\xa0\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of the Hotel Room/Airlines Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. An Upgrade to a Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\xa0\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on the current tariff & are subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\n\xa0\nHotels\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges.\xa0\nPlease remember that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expense arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress/Roll over Extra mattress on the floor provided where a proper extra bed isn’t available.\xa0\nIn case the guests cannot climb higher floors, we request you to update us at the time of booking, so that we may take the appropriate action and try for rooms on the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hilly areas, scarcity of water & electricity may happen. To overcome the water crisis, certain hotels have a fixed schedule for supplying hot & cold water. We strongly regret the inconvenience and look forward to your cooperation.\nOn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it.\xa0\nThere will not be any refund in case any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy - Tea/coffee maker/mini fridge/enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, loofah, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, the menu will be on a fixed plan/buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks/liquor, Soups or Deserts. For an order on A-la-Carte basis, guests are requested to make a direct payment for additional items.\n\n\xa0\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicles used are an Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo Traveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per the itinerary for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\xa0\nA/c in the Vehicle will be switched off during a hilly drive.\nPlease consult the driver/local representative for the next day’s sightseeing schedule/Transfers timings.\xa0\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/Bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as the vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonuments will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays. National Parks are Closed Around Mid Jun-Mid Nov.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\xa0\nAll arrangements made by the Company are in capacity of an agent only. The Company will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/traffic jams/traffic halts/diversions/bandh/curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us in situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of a discontinued itinerary due to these reasons, no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/40637097564_10b682199c_k.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/itinerary/8403831008_080f39d1ef_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/itinerary/48011063662_e70a005e73_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/itinerary/47519436781_5d96ebe956_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/itinerary/49408764761_079785d448_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/itinerary/KanakBhawan.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015018/itinerary/49211464657_f049880725_k.jpg']}, 'score': 2.0274122, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}]
