ipants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'East European Explorer' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Budapest, Vienna, and Prague. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Hungarian Parliament Building, the majestic Schönbrunn Palace, Prague Castle, and the famous Charles Bridge. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, a scenic cruise along the Danube River, and ample opportunities to immerse themselves in the rich history, stunning architecture, and vibrant local culture of these imperial capitals.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Prague\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only.\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel St. George (Standard) / Carlton (Value) or similar in Prague'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nPrague City Tour\n\xa0\nPrague City Tour: Prague Castle! St. Vitus Cathedral! Charles Bridge! Visit the most significant Czech monument - an ancient symbol of the Czech State with a tradition of more than 1000 years. Learn about its history and the most important monarchs who ruled the Czech Lands from the heights of the Prague Castle. See St. Vitus Cathedral, Old Royal Palace, St. George’s Basilica, and much more. Enjoy panoramic views over Prague - all this with a knowledgeable guide! (Duration of the tour: 3 hrs)\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel St. George (Standard) / Carlton (Value) or similar in Prague'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPrague To Vienna Via Train (Approx 4 Hrs)\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station to board the train to Vienna!\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Vienna train station, you will make your way to the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed)\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Art Vienna (Standard) / Zeitgeist (Value) or similar in Vienna'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nVienna City Tour\n\xa0\nVienna City Tour: Take a tour of the main sights within the city centre and visit the magnificently decorated rooms of Schonbrunn Palace. This city tour will introduce you to the the most important sights of the Austrian capital. As we drive around the famous 'Ringstrasse', Vienna's main boulevard, we pass by the State Opera, the Museums of Fine Art and Natural History, the Parliament building, the Burgtheater (National Theatre), the City Hall and the University. The highlight of this programme is the visit to Schonbrunn Palace where we take a tour of some of the most magnificently decorated rooms. (Duration of the Tour: 3 hours)\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Art Vienna (Standard) / Zeitgeist (Value) or similar in Vienna'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVienna To Budapest Via Train (Approx 3 Hrs)\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nMake your way to the train station to board the train to Budapest!\xa0\nUpon your arrival at Budapest train station, you will make your way to the hotel.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nPlease note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed\nCheck in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Benczur (Standard) / Royal Park Boutique (Value) or similar in Budapest'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nBudapest City Tour\n\xa0\nBudapest City Tour: On this tour you will be passing by the Parliament building before crossing the Danube on the Margaret Bridge and drive to the Royal Castle on the Buda side of the city. Here you will have some free time to yourself to visit the Fishermen's Bastion which offers stunning views over the city and the Mathias Church. Your tour will continue to the Gillert Hill before crossing the Elisabeth Bridge from where you will drive towards the Heroes' Square. Passing by the Opera and St Stephen's Basilica you reach the Hotel Intercontinental where your tour ends. [Duration of this tour: Approx. 3 hrs.]\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Benczur (Standard) / Royal Park Boutique (Value) or similar in Budapest'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'Depart Budapest\n\xa0\nTransfers: From Budapest hotel to the Airport in private transfer.\xa0\n\xa0\nSpecial Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight.\n\xa0\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\nSt. George Hotel / Hotel Prague Central Plaza / Galileo Hotel / Ibis Praha (Wenceslas Square) / Ibis Praha (Mala Strana) or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nArt Hotel Vienna / Ibis Wien Hauptbahnhof / Ibis Wien Mariahilf Hotel/ Admiral or similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nBenczur / City Hotel Ring / Hotel Charles / Hotel Orion Varkert or similar\n\n\n\n', '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\n\xa0Hotel Carlton / Louis Leger / Royal Court Hotel / Best Western City Hotel Moran / Clarion Prague City / NH Prague City or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nHotel Zeitgeist Vienna, Mercure Wien Westbahnhof, Mercure Wien City or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nRoyal Park Boutique Hotel /\xa0 Corvin Center Suites / City Inn or similar\n\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\n\xa0Hotel Carlton / Louis Leger / Royal Court Hotel / Best Western City Hotel Moran / Clarion Prague City / NH Prague City or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nHotel Zeitgeist Vienna, Mercure Wien Westbahnhof, Mercure Wien City or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nRoyal Park Boutique Hotel /\xa0 Corvin Center Suites / City Inn or similar\n\n\n\n', '0': '\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\nSt. George Hotel / Hotel Prague Central Plaza / Galileo Hotel / Ibis Praha (Wenceslas Square) / Ibis Praha (Mala Strana) or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nArt Hotel Vienna / Ibis Wien Hauptbahnhof / Ibis Wien Mariahilf Hotel/ Admiral or similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nBenczur / City Hotel Ring / Hotel Charles / Hotel Orion Varkert or similar\n\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'HU', 'countryName': 'Hungary', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CZ', 'countryName': 'Czech Republic', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 114700.0, 'hotels': ['\xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\nSt. George Hotel / Hotel Prague Central Plaza / Galileo Hotel / Ibis Praha (Wenceslas Square) / Ibis Praha (Mala Strana) or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nArt Hotel Vienna / Ibis Wien Hauptbahnhof / Ibis Wien Mariahilf Hotel/ Admiral or similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nBenczur / City Hotel Ring / Hotel Charles / Hotel Orion Varkert or similar\n\n\n\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 133500.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\n\xa0Hotel Carlton / Louis Leger / Royal Court Hotel / Best Western City Hotel Moran / Clarion Prague City / NH Prague City or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nHotel Zeitgeist Vienna, Mercure Wien Westbahnhof, Mercure Wien City or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nRoyal Park Boutique Hotel /\xa0 Corvin Center Suites / City Inn or similar\n\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['Transportation:\xa0[Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Prague Airport to Prague Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Budapest Hotel to Budapest Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Pass:\xa0[Seat Reservation would be additional]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Prague to Vienna\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Vienna to Budapest\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrague - City Tour including Prague Castle\nVienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace\nBudapest City Tour\n\n\xa0'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation:\n\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Prague based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Vienna based on the hotel category selected or similar\n2 Nights’ accommodation in Budapest based on the hotel category selected or similar\n\n\xa0\nMeals:\n\nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n\n\xa0\nTransportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis]\n\nArrival Airport Transfer from Prague Airport to Prague Hotel\nDeparture Airport transfer from Budapest Hotel to Budapest Airport\n\n\xa0\nTrain Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional]\n\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Prague to Vienna\n2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Vienna to Budapest\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point)\n\nPrague - City Tour including Prague Castle\nVienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace\nBudapest City Tour\n\n\xa0\nInsurance:\n\nOverseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only)\n', 'exclusions': '\nInternational air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges.\nLunch & Dinner (if not mentioned)\nDrinks during meals\nTCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount.\nLaundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature.\nMandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price.\nCity taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel.\nCost of foreign exchange for personal use.\nCost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual\nAny items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Note:\n\nThe above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together.\nThe above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events\nMaximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room.\nMidnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs.\nWIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\n(Supplement charges may apply for such services)\nStandard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs.\nMost hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned.\nAt this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability\nTCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost.\n\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nTravel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026\nBlack out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\nMaximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room.\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses\nSurcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking.\nTo proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour.\nShould the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/Budapest_3.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/Viena_20.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/SchonbrunnPalace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/Budapest_Hungary.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/DanubeCruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014516/itinerary/Budapest.jpg']}, 'score': 3.593409, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015039', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015039', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'European Express (Winter)', 'days': 13, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Paris', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Eindhoven', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Rhineland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Central Switzerland', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Innsbruck', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Padova', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Arezzo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Arezzo', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pisa', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG011816_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 376585, 'packageSummary': "The 'European Express (Winter)' package is a 13-day tour covering Arezzo, Eindhoven, Pisa, Rhineland, Central Switzerland, Padova, Paris, and Innsbruck. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Leaning Tower of Pisa, the Eiffel Tower in Paris, and the breathtaking, snow-dusted alpine landscapes of Central Switzerland and Innsbruck. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic winter drives through the historic Rhineland, and ample opportunities to explore the rich cultural heritage and festive charm of these diverse European destinations.", 'images': ['arcdetriumphateveningfrance76115509.jpg', 'EiffelTower1.jpg', 'Grand_place_753.jpg', 'Kukenhof_Tulip_Garden1_753.jpg', 'CologneCathedral.jpg', 'RhineFallsSchaffhausen753.jpg', 'JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'Titles753.jpg', 'Sworowski_753.jpg', 'Venice_Gandola_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Florence_Dome_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Colleseum_Rome_Adobe_753.jpg', 'Pisa_Adobe_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 376585, 'thumbnailImage': 'OldTownInnsbruckAustria267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015039 is named 'European Express (Winter)' and spans 13 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Paris, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Paris On arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Paris, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Versailles Palace - Guided city tour of Paris - Seine River Cruise –Eiffel Tower Level 3 – Illumination tour of Paris Today, proceed for a Guided Tour of Versailles Palace with private apartments, Opera Hall, the Chapel & Hall of Mirrors. Next, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris: See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides and Champs Elysees. Later we take a Scenic Cruise on River Seine. Next, we visit the Eiffel Tower 3rd level. In the evening enjoy “Illumination Tour of Paris” and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up. Note: Visiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 - 5 hours in the queue. Due to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation Tour of Brussels – Visit Beer Museum – Photo stop at Atomium Today we check out and drive towards Brussels. On arrival, enjoy an Orientation Tour of Brussels: See the Grand Place with some free time near Manneken Pis. Next, we visit the Beer Museum with beer tasting. Later, we take a photo stop at Atomium., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Eindhoven, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Till 17th March: Madurodam – Cheese Farm and Wooden Shoe Making – Amsterdam canal cruise Today, we proceed to Keukenhof – the largest spring garden in the world. Next, we get to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, enjoy a cruise on the canals of Amsterdam in a glass–topped boat. OR From 18th March: Keukenhof – Cheese Farm and Wooden Shoe Making – Amsterdam canal cruise Today, we proceed to Madurodam: Holland in Miniature. Next, we get to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, enjoy a cruise on the canals of Amsterdam in a glass– topped boat., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Rhineland, Meals: Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner, Description: Photo stop at Cologne Cathedral – Rhine River cruise Today, we drive to Cologne and take a photo stop at the Cologne Cathedral, which is the largest Gothic church in northern Europe and features immense twin towers that stand 515 feet (157 metres) tall. Later, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the River Rhine., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Central Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Black Forest – Cuckoo Clock Demonstration – View Rhine Falls Today, we drive in the heart of the Black Forest region, known for its dense, evergreen forests and picturesque villages. Here, we also get to see how the famous Cuckoo Clocks are made. Next, we drive to Schaffhausen in Switzerland to see the Rhine falls., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Central Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Excursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken Today, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Central Switzerland, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Mt. Titlis – Orientation tour of Lucerne – Lake Lucerne Cruise Today, we visit Mt Titlis. Our cable car ride includes the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair – to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Lucerne: See the Lion Monument and Kapellbrucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Later we take a scenic cruise on Lake Lucerne. Note: On the days, Mt Titlis is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to alternate mountain excursion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Innsbruck, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Orientation tour of Vaduz – Swarovski Crystal Worlds – Orientation tour of Innsbruck Today, we drive to Innsbruck. En route, visit Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Here, we enjoy an orientation tour of Vaduz. Here you get some free time to shop at the Huber watch store. Next, we visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds in Wattens. Later, proceed for an orientation tour of Innsbruck: See the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Padova, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Private boat to St. Mark’s Square – Orientation tour of Venice Today, we drive to Italy and proceed to the pier to take a private boat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark’s square to see the Basilica, Doge’s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 11 - Arezzo, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided walking tour of Florence Today, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the Duomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise and Piazza Della Signoria., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 12 - Arezzo, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day trip to Rome: Guided tour of Rome and Vatican City Today we go on a day trip to Rome and Vatican City. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vatican City: the smallest country in the world (shorts or sleeveless vests not allowed), where we visit the famous St. Peter’s Basilica and St. Peter’s Square. Next, we continue for a guided city tour of Rome: See Circus Maximus and photo-stop at Colosseum & Arc of Constantine., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 13 - Pisa, Meals: Breakfast, Description: See Leaning Tower of Pisa – Fly back home with pleasant memories! Today, we proceed to Pisa to see the world-famous leaning tower of Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: Due to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of Rome instead of Milan. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 376585.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n02 nights at Holiday Inn Express / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn or similar in Eindhoven, Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn Express / Best Western Morfeldon / Achat / Sunday hotel or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n03 nights at Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Wald / Lizumerhof / Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria.\n01 night at Four points / Unaway / SHG or similar in Padova / Occhiobello / Bologna, Italy.\n02 nights at Fortuna / Grand Fonti / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n, \n02 nights at Hotel\xa0Ibis / B&b /\xa0Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\xa0\n02 nights at NH /\xa0Best Western\xa0or similar in Belgium / Netherlands\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt or similar in Germany\n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n01 night at Hotel Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria\n01 night at Hotel Blue Dream or similar in Padova / Ferrara, Italy\xa0\n01 night at Hotel BB Pomezia or similar in Rome, Italy\xa0\n01 night at Hotel Park or similar in Arezzo, Italy\n. Meals include: \nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Coffee, Hot Eggs & Cut Fruits)\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian lunches\n01 Local Lunch\n12 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\xa0In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches., \nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Coffee, Hot Eggs & Cut Fruits)\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian lunches\n12 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026 Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing, and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 13 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 39 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers. Important Notes : Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st September, 2023. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels Due to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, the hotel in Paris may be at the outskirts of the city and may attracted extra surcharge. (1st July – 31st September) Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing: On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. Due to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, city tours may not take place for several groups in case of road closures for rehearsals / events that would be taking place from 11th July, 2024 to 23rd September, 2024. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZVE763', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'European Express (Winter)' package is a 13-day tour covering Arezzo, Eindhoven, Pisa, Rhineland, Central Switzerland, Padova, Paris, and Innsbruck. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the Leaning Tower of Pisa, the Eiffel Tower in Paris, and the breathtaking, snow-dusted alpine landscapes of Central Switzerland and Innsbruck. Participants will enjoy guided city sightseeing tours, scenic winter drives through the historic Rhineland, and ample opportunities to explore the rich cultural heritage and festive charm of these diverse European destinations.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Paris\nOn arrival, our Tour Manager / Local Representative will meet and welcome you outside the Airport. Later, we proceed to the hotel and check in.\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\nWe may have to proceed directly for dinner or Packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Express / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided tour of Versailles Palace - Guided city tour of Paris -\xa0Seine River Cruise\xa0\xa0\xa0–Eiffel Tower Level 3 – Illumination tour of Paris\nToday, proceed for a Guided Tour of Versailles Palace with private apartments, Opera Hall, the Chapel & Hall of Mirrors. Next, we proceed for a guided city tour of Paris:\xa0 See the Alexander Bridge, Arc de Triomphe, Concorde Square, Opera House, Invalides and Champs Elysees. Later we take a Scenic Cruise on River Seine. Next, we visit the Eiffel Tower 3rd level. In the evening enjoy “Illumination Tour of Paris” and see Paris by night, with some of the city’s famous monuments / sights lit up.\nNote:\xa0\n\nVisiting Eiffel Tower 3rd Level is subject to availability due to weather conditions / temporary operational closures. In case of such, the group shall visit the Eiffel Tower up till 2nd Level.\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel Tower, it may take up to 4 - 5 hours in the queue.\nDue to revised Eiffel Tower regulations, guests may be required to queue at the ticket counter to collect their tickets. The Tour Manager will assist and guide guests throughout the process.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Express / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area),\xa0France'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation Tour of Brussels – Visit Beer Museum – Photo stop at Atomium\xa0\nToday we check out and drive towards Brussels. On arrival, enjoy an Orientation Tour of Brussels: See the Grand Place with some free time near Manneken Pis. Next, we visit the Beer Museum with beer tasting. Later, we take a photo stop at Atomium.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0NH / Best Western\xa0or similar in Eindhoven,\xa0Netherlands'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nTill 17th March:\xa0 Madurodam\xa0– Cheese Farm and Wooden Shoe Making – Amsterdam canal cruise\nToday, we proceed to Keukenhof – the largest spring garden in the world. Next, we get to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, enjoy a cruise on the canals of Amsterdam in a glass–topped boat.\xa0\n\xa0\nOR\n\xa0\nFrom 18th March:\xa0 Keukenhof – Cheese Farm and Wooden Shoe Making – Amsterdam canal cruise\nToday, we proceed to Madurodam: Holland in Miniature. Next, we get to experience Wooden shoe making and Cheese Farms. Later, enjoy a cruise on the canals of Amsterdam in a glass– topped boat.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0NH / Best Western\xa0or similar in\xa0Eindhoven,\xa0Netherlands'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nPhoto stop at Cologne Cathedral – Rhine River cruise\xa0\nToday, we drive to Cologne and take a photo stop at the Cologne Cathedral, which is the largest Gothic church in northern Europe and features immense twin towers that stand 515 feet (157 metres) tall. Later, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the River Rhine.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Packed Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Holiday Inn Express / Best Western Morfeldon / Achat or similar in Rhineland, Germany.'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Black Forest – Cuckoo Clock Demonstration – View Rhine Falls\nToday, we drive in the heart of the Black Forest region, known for its dense, evergreen forests and picturesque villages. Here, we also get to see how the famous Cuckoo Clocks are made. Next, we drive to Schaffhausen in Switzerland to see the Rhine falls.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in Central Switzerland'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken\nToday, we proceed for an excursion to Jungfraujoch - The Top of Europe. We board the cable car followed by a cogwheel train up to a height of 3,454 meters to Europe’s highest railway station. Visit the Ice Palace and the Sphinx observatory deck to view the longest glacier in the Alps. Later, we visit Interlaken.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in\xa0Central Switzerland'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Mt. Titlis – Orientation tour of Lucerne – Lake Lucerne Cruise\nToday, we visit Mt Titlis. Our cable car ride includes the world’s first rotating cable car, the Rotair – to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 meters. Do visit the “Cliff Walk” a suspension bridge along the cliff of Mt. Titlis. Next, we proceed for an orientation tour of Lucerne: See the Lion Monument and Kapellbrucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Later we take a scenic cruise on Lake Lucerne.\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0On the days, Mt Titlis is closed due to maintenance or weather conditions, we shall take the group to alternate mountain excursion.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in\xa0Central Switzerland'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\nOrientation tour of Vaduz – Swarovski Crystal Worlds – Orientation tour of Innsbruck\nToday, we drive to Innsbruck. En route, visit Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein. Here, we enjoy an orientation tour of Vaduz. Here you get some free time to shop at the Huber watch store.\xa0Next, we visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds in Wattens. Later, proceed for an orientation tour of Innsbruck: See the Golden Roof and the Maria Theresien Strasse.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Wald / Lizumerhof / Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\nPrivate boat to St. Mark’s Square – Orientation tour of Venice\nToday, we drive to Italy and proceed to the pier to take a private boat to Venice. On arrival, we visit St. Mark’s square to see the Basilica, Doge’s Palace, Campanile and Bridge of Sighs.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Four points / Unaway / SHG or similar in Padova / \xa0Occhiobello / Bologna, Italy'}, {'day': 11, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided walking tour of Florence\nToday, we proceed to Florence for a guided walking tour: see the Duomo, the Campanile, the Baptistery with its Gates of Paradise and Piazza Della Signoria.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Fortuna / Grand Fonti / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy'}, {'day': 12, 'description': '\xa0\nDay trip to Rome: Guided tour of Rome and Vatican City\nToday we go on a day trip to Rome and Vatican City. On arrival, we proceed for a guided city tour of Vatican City: the smallest country in the world (shorts or sleeveless vests not allowed), where we visit the famous St. Peter’s Basilica and St. Peter’s Square. Next, we continue for a guided city tour of Rome: See Circus Maximus and photo-stop at Colosseum & Arc of Constantine.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Fortuna / Grand Fonti / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo,\xa0Italy'}, {'day': 13, 'description': '\xa0\nSee Leaning Tower of Pisa – Fly back home with pleasant memories!\xa0\nToday, we proceed to Pisa to see the world-famous leaning tower of Pisa. Later, we drive to Milan airport for your flight back home. Kindly spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your Europe tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nDue to flight connectivity, few groups may depart out of Rome instead of Milan. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Holiday Inn Express / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn or similar in Eindhoven, Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn Express / Best Western Morfeldon / Achat / Sunday hotel or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n03 nights at Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Wald / Lizumerhof / Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria.\n01 night at Four points / Unaway / SHG or similar in Padova / Occhiobello / Bologna, Italy.\n02 nights at Fortuna / Grand Fonti / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n', '\n02 nights at Hotel\xa0Ibis / B&b /\xa0Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\xa0\n02 nights at NH /\xa0Best Western\xa0or similar in Belgium / Netherlands\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt or similar in Germany\n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n01 night at Hotel Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria\n01 night at Hotel Blue Dream or similar in Padova / Ferrara, Italy\xa0\n01 night at Hotel BB Pomezia or similar in Rome, Italy\xa0\n01 night at Hotel Park or similar in Arezzo, Italy\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n02 nights at Holiday Inn Express / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn or similar in Eindhoven, Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn Express / Best Western Morfeldon / Achat / Sunday hotel or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n03 nights at Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Wald / Lizumerhof / Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria.\n01 night at Four points / Unaway / SHG or similar in Padova / Occhiobello / Bologna, Italy.\n02 nights at Fortuna / Grand Fonti / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n', '0': '\n02 nights at Hotel\xa0Ibis / B&b /\xa0Moxy CDG or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France\xa0\n02 nights at NH /\xa0Best Western\xa0or similar in Belgium / Netherlands\n01 night at Hotel NH Frankfurt or similar in Germany\n03 nights at Hotel Ibis Zurich /BB Oftringen / HI Express Neuenkirch or similar in Switzerland\n01 night at Hotel Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria\n01 night at Hotel Blue Dream or similar in Padova / Ferrara, Italy\xa0\n01 night at Hotel BB Pomezia or similar in Rome, Italy\xa0\n01 night at Hotel Park or similar in Arezzo, Italy\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'IT', 'countryName': 'Italy', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'NL', 'countryName': 'Netherlands', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'LCH', 'countryName': 'Liechtenstein', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'DE', 'countryName': 'Germany', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'VA', 'countryName': 'Vatican City', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'BE', 'countryName': 'Belgium', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 376600.0, 'hotels': ['\n02 nights at Holiday Inn Express / City Residence or similar in Paris (CDG Area), France.\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel NH / Holiday Inn or similar in Eindhoven, Netherlands.\n01 night at Holiday Inn Express / Best Western Morfeldon / Achat / Sunday hotel or similar in Rhineland, Germany.\n03 nights at Terrace / Central / HI Express Neuenkirch / Prizeotel or similar in Central Switzerland.\n01 night at Wald / Lizumerhof / Alpenkoning or similar in Seefeld / Innsbruck, Austria.\n01 night at Four points / Unaway / SHG or similar in Padova / Occhiobello / Bologna, Italy.\n02 nights at Fortuna / Grand Fonti / Planet or similar in Chianciano Terme/ Arezzo, Italy.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Coffee, Hot Eggs & Cut Fruits)\n10 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian lunches\n01 Local Lunch\n12 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\xa0In certain places, there is a possibility of providing cash out to the passengers instead of packed lunches.', '\nDaily Continental Buffet Breakfast (Breakfast includes Bread, Butter, Jam, Cereals, Fruit Juice, Milk, Coffee, Hot Eggs & Cut Fruits)\n07 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian lunches\n12 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non–Vegetarian dinners\n\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['PARIS :\n\nGuided tour of Versailles Palace\nGuided city tour of Paris\nVisit 3rd level of Eiffel Tower\xa0\nSeine River cruise\nIllumination tour of Paris\n\nBELGIUM :\n\nOrientation Tour of Brussels\nPhoto stop at Atomium.\nVisit Beer Museum\n\nNETHERLANDS :\n\nVisit Keukenhof (Till 10th May)\nVisit Madurodam (From 11th May)\nCheese Farm and Wooden Shoe making\nAmsterdam Canal Cruise\n\nGERMANY :\n\nSee the Cologne Cathedral\nEnjoy River Rhine Cruise\nVisit Black Forest\nCuckoo clock demonstration\xa0\n\nSWITZERLAND :\n\nView\xa0the Rhine\xa0Falls\xa0\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch with lunch and Interlaken\nVisit Mt. Titlis\nOrientation Tour of Lucerne.\nLake Lucerne Cruise\n\nLIECHTENSTEIN :\n\nOrientation tour of Vaduz\n\nAUSTRIA :\n\nVisit the Swarovski Crystal\xa0Worlds\nOrientation tour of Innsbruck\n\n\xa0\nITALY :\nVENICE\n\nVisit St. Mark’s Square on a Private Boat\nOrientation tour of Venice\n\nFLORENCE\n\nGuided Walking Tour of Florence\n\nROME\n\nGuided City Tour of Rome\n\nVATICAN CITY\n\nVisit the St. Peter’s Basilica & Square\n\n\xa0\nPISA\n\nVisit the Field of Miracles – See the Leaning Tower of Pisa\n', 'PARIS :\n\nGuided City Tour\nGuided Tour of Versailles Palace\nVisit 2nd level of Eiffel Tower\n\nBELGIUM :\n\nOrientation Tour of Brussels\xa0\nPhoto stop at Atomium\n\nNETHERLANDS :\n\nVisit Keukenhof (Till 12th May)\nVisit Madurodam (From 13th May)\nVisit a Cheese Farm and a Wooden Shoe Workshop\xa0\xa0\nVisit Dam Square\n\nGERMANY :\n\nVisit the Cologne Cathedral\nEnjoy River Rhine Cruise\nVisit Black Forest\n\nSWITZERLAND :\n\nPhoto stop at Rhine Falls\xa0\nVisit Mt. Titlis\nOrientation Tour of Lucerne\n\nAUSTRIA :\n\nVisit the Swarovski Crystal Museum and Shop\nOrientation tour of Innsbruck\n\nITALY :\nVENICE\n\nVisit St. Mark’s Square on a Private Boat\nOrientation tour of Venice\n\nFLORENCE\n\nGuided Walking Tour\n\nROME\n\nGuided City Tour\n\nVATICAN CITY\n\nVisit St. Peter’s Basilica & Square\n\n\xa0\nPISA\n\nVisit the Field of Miracles – See the Leaning Tower of Pisa\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing, and consulate fees.\xa0 \xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 13 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 39 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nNote: Optional will be operated subject to minimum strength of 20 passengers.\nImportant Notes :\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st September, 2023.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights to note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\nHotels:\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels\nDue to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, the hotel in Paris may be at the outskirts of the city and may attracted extra surcharge. (1st July – 31st September)\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay, shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\n\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\nOn certain days a packed lunch will be provided.\n\n\xa0\nSightseeing:\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they chose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nDue to 2024 Summer Olympics held in Paris, city tours may not take place for several groups in case of road closures for rehearsals / events that would be taking place from 11th July, 2024 to 23rd September, 2024.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/OldTownInnsbruckAustria267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/arcdetriumphateveningfrance76115509.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/EiffelTower1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Grand_place_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Kukenhof_Tulip_Garden1_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/CologneCathedral.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/RhineFallsSchaffhausen753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/JungfraujochSummer753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Titles753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Sworowski_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Venice_Gandola_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Florence_Dome_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Colleseum_Rome_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015039/itinerary/Pisa_Adobe_753.jpg']}, 'score': 3.593409, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015094', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015094', 'availableMonths': ['march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'European Dhamaka (Winter)', 'days': 7, 'cities': [], 'highlights': ['France Guided City Tour of Paris Visit 2nd level of Eiffel Tower Visit Fragonard Perfume Museum Seine River Cruise and Illumination Tour of Paris (OPTIONAL) Switzerland Visit Mt Titlis Orientation tour of Lucerne Chance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch & Interlaken (OPTIONAL) Austria Orientation tour of Innsbruck Visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds'], 'pdfName': 'PKG015094_0_20260908214504', 'price': 210456, 'packageSummary': "The 'European Dhamaka (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering scenic destinations across France, Switzerland, and Austria. The itinerary includes a guided city tour of Paris featuring a visit to the second level of the Eiffel Tower, a stop at the Fragonard Perfume Museum, and an optional Seine River Cruise and Illumination Tour. In Switzerland, participants will enjoy a visit to Mt. Titlis and an orientation tour of Lucerne, with an optional excursion to Jungfraujoch for lunch and a visit to Interlaken. The journey concludes in Austria with an orientation tour of Innsbruck and a visit to the dazzling Swarovski Crystal Worlds.", 'images': [], 'minimumPrice': 210456, 'thumbnailImage': 'Prague_260.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015094 is named 'European Dhamaka (Winter)' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nThe price is 210456.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n. Meals include: \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk and coffee)\n06 Basic Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches/dinner, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: Airline And Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Joining Direct Clients: Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they choose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. No refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: France Guided City Tour of Paris Visit 2nd level of Eiffel Tower Visit Fragonard Perfume Museum Seine River Cruise and Illumination Tour of Paris (OPTIONAL) Switzerland Visit Mt Titlis Orientation tour of Lucerne Chance to visit Jungfraujoch with lunch & Interlaken (OPTIONAL) Austria Orientation tour of Innsbruck Visit the Swarovski Crystal Worlds.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE159', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'European Dhamaka (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering scenic destinations across France, Switzerland, and Austria. The itinerary includes a guided city tour of Paris featuring a visit to the second level of the Eiffel Tower, a stop at the Fragonard Perfume Museum, and an optional Seine River Cruise and Illumination Tour. In Switzerland, participants will enjoy a visit to Mt. Titlis and an orientation tour of Lucerne, with an optional excursion to Jungfraujoch for lunch and a visit to Interlaken. The journey concludes in Austria with an orientation tour of Innsbruck and a visit to the dazzling Swarovski Crystal Worlds.", 'itinerary': []}, 'hotels': ['\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CH', 'countryName': 'Switzerland', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'FR', 'countryName': 'France', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 210500.0, 'hotels': ['\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk and coffee)\n06 Basic Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches/dinner, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\n'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\nThis cost includes documentation, processing, and consulate fees.\xa0\xa0 \n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['AUSTRIA\nVienna \n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nHUNGARY\nBudapest \n\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour\nDanube River Cruise\xa0\nSee the Basilica Esztergom\xa0\nVisit Szentendre\n\n\xa0\nSLOVAKIA\nBratislava\xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\xa0\n\xa0\n\nOrientation city tour\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCZECH REPUBLIC\nPrague\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\n\nCesky Krumlov\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\n\n\xa0'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare&nbsp;as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\nAirline And Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJoining Direct Clients:\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\xa0\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they choose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\xa0\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n\n\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015094/Prague_260.jpg', 'constructed_images': []}, 'score': 3.593409, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015063', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015063', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'december_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'East European Dhamaka  (Winter)', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bratislava', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015063_0_20260909000334', 'price': 190479, 'packageSummary': "The 'East European Dhamaka (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering Prague, Vienna, Budapest, and Bratislava. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Prague Castle, the majestic Schönbrunn Palace in Vienna, and the charming old town of Bratislava. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, scenic walks through festive winter markets, and a memorable sightseeing cruise along the Danube River in Budapest.", 'images': ['Vienna9.jpg', 'PearlofDanube_C.jpg', 'PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'Slovakia_753.jpg', 'Czech-Republic-Cesky-Krumlov.jpg', 'Prague1.jpg', 'Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 190479, 'thumbnailImage': 'Prague_260.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015063 is named 'East European Dhamaka  (Winter)' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Vienna, Meals: Dinner, Description: Welcome to Vienna! The Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet you outside the airport. Proceed for dinner and then to the hotel and check in. Note: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration. Oveernight in Vienna, Austria, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour of Vienna - Danube River cruise Today, we proceed for a Guided city tour of Vienna: See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, St. Stephen’s Church and many more interesting monuments of this beautiful city. Next, we drive to Budapest. Upon arrival, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the Danube river. Overnight in Budapest, Hungary, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Budapest – See the Basilica Esztergom – Visit Szentendre Today proceed for a Guided tour of Budapest: See the equestrian statue of St. Stephen and experience the domination of the seven turrets at Fisherman’s Bastion, visit the Heroes Square and see more interesting sights. Next we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bratislava, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Onto Bratislava – Orientation tour of Bratislava Today we drive towards Bratislava. Enroute, we take a stop at Pandorf and we have some free time for shopping at McArthur Glen Desinger Outlets (Subject to time permitting). Upon arrival in Bratislava, we proceed for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Prague Today we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. Later, we drive to Prague - the city of hundred spires, built at the meandering Vltava River., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Guided city tour of Prague Today, we proceed for a Guided city tour of Prague: visit a panoramic point on the Prague castle gallery. Next, we visit the Old Town square and take a photo stop at the Astronomical Clock - the oldest Functional Astronomical clock in the world. Next, we take a walk over the most visited Charles Bridge. In the evening, we have some free time in the city., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Fly back home with pleasant memories! Proceed to the airport for your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime. Note: Due to flight connectivity, a few groups may depart out of Vienna instead of Prague. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 190479.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n. Meals include: \nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk and coffee)\n06 Basic Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches/dinner, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. All local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026. Cost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary. All transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach. Services of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers). Visa Requirements Multiple entry Schengen visa. This cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Tipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026) Government Taxes as applicable are extra. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. No porterage included. Any expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary. Private airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: IMPORTANT NOTES: Airline And Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Passengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense. Joining Direct Clients: Main Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price. Arrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price. The Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel. Hotels: All hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts. The hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts. Most hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult. Hotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions. Functioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority. During heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures. Most hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms. Due to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. In Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels. Any damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. In certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast. Coaches: Most of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean. Due to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted on the coach. One check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach. In major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Due to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot. Meals: Meals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible. On certain days, a packed lunch will be provided. Sightseeing On certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. The Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed. The lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they choose not to climb the stairs. Due to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue. No refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour. Arrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings. Security alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same. There are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour. All optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted). Optional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy. GST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India. In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBE156', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'East European Dhamaka (Winter)' package is a 7-day tour covering Prague, Vienna, Budapest, and Bratislava. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the historic Prague Castle, the majestic Schönbrunn Palace in Vienna, and the charming old town of Bratislava. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, scenic walks through festive winter markets, and a memorable sightseeing cruise along the Danube River in Budapest.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nWelcome to Vienna!\nThe Tour Manager / Station Manager will meet you outside the airport. Proceed for dinner and then to the hotel and check in.\xa0\nNote: Joining direct passenger / NRI can check in on your own at the hotel. The standard check in time is 1500 hrs. We may have to proceed directly for dinner or packed dinner will be provided in case of late arrivals of flight or long queue at the immigration.\nOveernight in Vienna, Austria\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel B&B / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided City Tour of Vienna - Danube River cruise\nToday, we proceed for a Guided city tour of Vienna:\xa0 See the magnificent Opera House, Rathaus, St. Stephen’s Church and many more interesting monuments of this beautiful city. Next, we drive to Budapest. Upon arrival, we enjoy a scenic cruise on the Danube river.\nOvernight in Budapest, Hungary', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Budapest – See the Basilica Esztergom – Visit Szentendre\nToday proceed for a Guided tour of Budapest: See the equestrian statue of St. Stephen and experience the domination of the seven turrets at Fisherman’s Bastion, visit the Heroes Square and see more interesting sights. Next we proceed to Esztergom and we see the Basilica Esztergom: the largest church in Hungary. Later, we visit Szentendre, a Hungarian town on the Danube River best known for its baroque architecture and churches, colourful houses and narrow lanes.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest,\xa0Hungary'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nOnto Bratislava – Orientation tour of Bratislava\nToday we drive towards Bratislava. Enroute, we take a stop at Pandorf and we have some free time for shopping at McArthur Glen Desinger Outlets (Subject to time permitting). Upon arrival in Bratislava, we proceed for an Orientation tour of the city: See the Bratislava castle and the old town.\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided tour of Cesky Krumlov – Onto Prague\nToday we drive to Cesky Krumlov. On arrival, enjoy a Guided tour: See the Cesky Krumlov Castle. Surrounded by landscaped gardens, the mighty castle stands on a rock promontory sculpted by the Vltava River. Later, we drive to Prague - the city of hundred spires, built at the meandering Vltava River.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nGuided city tour of Prague\nToday, we proceed for a Guided city tour of Prague: visit a panoramic point on the Prague castle gallery. Next, we visit the Old Town square and take a photo stop at the Astronomical Clock - the oldest Functional Astronomical clock in the world. Next, we take a walk over the most visited Charles Bridge. In the evening, we have some free time in the city.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Ibis Praha or similar in Prague,\xa0Czech Republic'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nFly back home with pleasant memories!\nProceed to the airport for your flight back home. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your European tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.\xa0\nNote:\xa0\n\nDue to flight connectivity, a few groups may depart out of Vienna instead of Prague. Kindly check with your sales staff for your exact flight details.\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches and it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Your Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'HU', 'countryName': 'Hungary', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'AT', 'countryName': 'Austria', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'SK', 'countryName': 'Slovakia', 'continentName': 'Europe'}, {'continentId': 5, 'countryCode': 'CZ', 'countryName': 'Czech Republic', 'continentName': 'Europe'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 190500.0, 'hotels': ['\n1 night at Senator/ B&B Hotel / Ibis Wien or similar in Vienna, Austria.\xa0\n2 nights at Hotel Amadeus / Ibis / B&B Hotel or similar in Budapest, Hungary.\n1 night at Vienna house/ Ibis / Hotel Bratislava or similar in Bratislava, Slovakia.\n2 nights at Hotel Duo/ Ibis Praha or similar in Prague, Czech Republic.\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily continental breakfast (Breakfast includes bread, butter, jam, cereals, fruit juice, milk and coffee)\n06 Basic Indian Jain / vegetarian / non vegetarian dinners.\nNote: Packed lunches/dinner, if applicable, will be Jain / vegetarian.\n'], 'visa': ['\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\nThis cost includes documentation, processing, and consulate fees.\xa0\xa0 \n'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['AUSTRIA\nVienna \n\nGuided City Tour\n\n\xa0\nHUNGARY\nBudapest \n\xa0\n\nGuided City Tour\nDanube River Cruise\xa0\nSee the Basilica Esztergom\xa0\nVisit Szentendre\n\n\xa0\nSLOVAKIA\nBratislava\xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0 \xa0\xa0\n\xa0\n\nOrientation city tour\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCZECH REPUBLIC\nPrague\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\n\nCesky Krumlov\n\nGuided City Tour\xa0\n\n\xa0'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare&nbsp;as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\xa0\nAll local taxes and services as of 1st July, 2026.\nCost of Visa and Medical Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\xa0\nSightseeing and accommodation as per the above mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and extensive excursions with entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air conditioned coach.\nServices of a professional, friendly and multilingual Tour Manager or a local Representative. (Subject to minimum 15 customers).\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nMultiple entry Schengen visa.\xa0\nThis cost includes documentation, processing and consulate fees.\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e., before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\xa0\nTipping is expected from anyone providing your service e.g., Coach Driver, Local Guides, Hotel & Restaurant staff etc. It is mandatory to tip a nominal amount of EUR 3 per person/per day. For the entire duration of this tour, which is 07 Days, the total Tips amount is EUR 21 per person to be paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 250,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as on 1st July, 2026)\nGovernment Taxes as applicable are extra.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nNo porterage included.\nAny expenses of a personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, wines, mineral water, food and drink not in the regular menu provided by us, minibar, telephone calls, etc.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in your itinerary.\nPrivate airport transfers, Cost of Suggested / Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nIMPORTANT NOTES:\nAirline And Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st July 2026.\nAny further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights note that the entire ticket gets no show and new return ticket needs to be bought by the passengers themselves.\xa0\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\xa0\nPassengers joining this tour must travel to / from the hub city at their own expense.\n\n\xa0\nJoining Direct Clients:\n\nMain Sector air tickets to reach the first overnight city and last departure city is not included in the Joining Direct package price.\nArrival and Departure Transfers are not included in the package price.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager shall meet the clients directly at the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nHotels:\xa0\n\nAll hotels will be either around the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nThe hotel room size in Europe would be up to 16 – 18 sq. mts.\nMost hotels in Europe have only Twin beds. The double bed will be Queen size and not King size.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels use rollaway beds and room size may be the same as the double room.\xa0\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\xa0\nA person 11.99 years and below is considered a child and 12 years and above, an adult.\xa0\xa0\nHotel rooms may not be air conditioned / air cooled nor will fans be provided. Air conditioning / cooling in hotels are set as per European weather conditions.\xa0\nFunctioning of Air cooling / Air conditioning in hotels is subject to official declaration of summer by the local authority.\xa0\nDuring heat wave in Europe air conditioning of the hotels and coaches may cease to function as they are not built for such high temperatures.\xa0\nMost hotels in Europe do not provide tea kettles in the rooms.\xa0\nDue to international events and trade fairs all throughout Europe such as the Air Show, music festivals, ice skating championships etc., you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nIn Switzerland the stay may be split in two hotels.\nAny damage caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during your stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\xa0\nIn certain cities hotels have not started the buffet breakfasts yet and if the same does not change by the time the tours begin, we will either provide breakfast or the groups will be taken to an Indian / local restaurant for breakfast.\xa0\n\n\xa0\nCoaches:\n\nMost of your journey in Europe is by coach and hence you are requested to keep the coach clean.\xa0\nDue to hygienic reasons, it is not permitted to use toilets on the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\xa0\nEating & drinking is not permitted on the coach.\xa0\nOne check-in bag and one handbag per person only, due to limited boot space on the coach.\xa0\nIn major European cities, there are parking restrictions for coaches, and it may not be possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches are non-wheelchair compliant. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\xa0\nDue to private coaches being forbidden inside most of the European cities, as per EU norms to preserve them and to avoid getting them polluted and overcrowded, most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and on foot.\xa0\n\nMeals:\n\nMeals are pre–set and a–la carte is not possible.\xa0\nOn certain days, a packed lunch will be provided.\n\nSightseeing\xa0\n\nOn certain departures, we may sometimes amend / reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\xa0\nGenerally, you will have to walk to sightseeing places, amusement parks and the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\xa0\nThe Eiffel Tower on certain Days due to strong wind conditions or being overcrowded or for security reasons may be closed.\xa0\nThe lifts at the Eiffel tower are currently closed due to safety. Hence the visit to the tower is only allowed by climbing the staircase. In case there is no change in the same on tour customers will be refunded the amount for the same if they choose not to climb the stairs.\xa0\nDue to stringent security checks at the Eiffel tower, it may take up to 4-5 hours in the queue.\nNo refund will be provided in case the group is unable to visit Eiffel Tower 3rd Level due to weather conditions / operational closures.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\xa0\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate members.\xa0\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during your initial part of the tour.\xa0\nArrival and Departure flights should be booked according to the group flight timings. In case there is any sightseeing involved on the first or last day of the itinerary to avoid missing any of the services. Please check with your sales officer for the group flight timings.\nSecurity alerts and random closures might affect the itinerary.\xa0\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\xa0\nDisabled clients should carry their own wheelchair and should be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client.\xa0\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers. Insurance policies must be carried while on tour.\xa0\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\xa0\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delays or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\xa0\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we will sometimes amend the itinerary. However, all the services will remain the same.\xa0\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e., meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour.\xa0\nAll optional activities will have to be booked and paid to the Tour Manager on Day 01 of the tour. Payments to be made by cash in EURO only. (Credit or Debit cards not accepted).\nOptional tours are booked & paid on 100% non-refundable & non cancellation policy.\nGST will be applicable for all optional activities pre-paid in India.\xa0 \xa0\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\xa0\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purposes only.\xa0\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in EURO out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange.\xa0\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\xa0\n\n\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/Prague_260.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Vienna9.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/PearlofDanube_C.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Slovakia_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Czech-Republic-Cesky-Krumlov.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Prague1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015063/itinerary/Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg']}, 'score': 3.2622025, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014892', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014892', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)   ', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prague', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Vienna', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Budapest', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014892_0_20260609125554.pdf', 'price': 114252, 'packageSummary': "The 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)' package is a 7-day tour covering the historic and picturesque cities of Prague, Budapest, and Vienna. Throughout this captivating journey, participants will immerse themselves in the rich cultural heritage of Eastern Europe, enjoying guided city tours of majestic palaces, scenic walks through medieval old towns, and breathtaking views along the Danube River. This specially curated holiday offers a perfect blend of sightseeing, local experiences, and festive celebrations, making it an unforgettable holiday experience.", 'images': ['Praguethroughtheeyesofbirds.jpg', 'PragueCastle_114396274.jpg', 'Viena_20.jpeg', 'SchonbrunnPalace.jpg', 'Budapest_Hungary.jpg', 'DanubeCruise.jpg', 'Budapest.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 114252, 'thumbnailImage': 'Budapest_3.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Durga Puja Special', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Budget Friendly', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014892 is named 'East European Explorer (Durga Puja - Navratri Special)   ' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Prague, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Prague Transfers: Upon your arrival you will meet the representative and then be transferred to the hotel in a private vehicle. Special Note: Check in is subject to standard operating norms of 15:00 hrs. or at the discretion of the hotel management. Private transfers will have a minimum of 60 mins waiting and will operate to selected hotels only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Prague, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague City Tour Prague City Tour: Prague Castle! St. Vitus Cathedral! Charles Bridge! Visit the most significant Czech monument - an ancient symbol of the Czech State with a tradition of more than 1000 years. Learn about its history and the most important monarchs who ruled the Czech Lands from the heights of the Prague Castle. See St. Vitus Cathedral, Old Royal Palace, St. George’s Basilica, and much more. Enjoy panoramic views over Prague - all this with a knowledgeable guide! (Duration of the tour: 3 hrs), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prague To Vienna Via Train (Approx 4 Hrs) Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train to Vienna! Upon your arrival at Vienna train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed) Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Vienna, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna City Tour Vienna City Tour: Take a tour of the main sights within the city centre and visit the magnificently decorated rooms of Schonbrunn Palace. This city tour will introduce you to the the most important sights of the Austrian capital. As we drive around the famous 'Ringstrasse', Vienna's main boulevard, we pass by the State Opera, the Museums of Fine Art and Natural History, the Parliament building, the Burgtheater (National Theatre), the City Hall and the University. The highlight of this programme is the visit to Schonbrunn Palace where we take a tour of some of the most magnificently decorated rooms. (Duration of the Tour: 3 hours), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Vienna To Budapest Via Train (Approx 3 Hrs) Transfers: Make your way to the train station to board the train to Budapest! Upon your arrival at Budapest train station, you will make your way to the hotel. Special Note: Please note cost of the ticket is included, however the same is subject to vary until ticketed Check in will be as per the standard timings of 15:00 hrs or as per hotel discretion., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Budapest City Tour Budapest City Tour: On this tour you will be passing by the Parliament building before crossing the Danube on the Margaret Bridge and drive to the Royal Castle on the Buda side of the city. Here you will have some free time to yourself to visit the Fishermen's Bastion which offers stunning views over the city and the Mathias Church. Your tour will continue to the Gillert Hill before crossing the Elisabeth Bridge from where you will drive towards the Heroes' Square. Passing by the Opera and St Stephen's Basilica you reach the Hotel Intercontinental where your tour ends. [Duration of this tour: Approx. 3 hrs.], GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Budapest, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Budapest Transfers: From Budapest hotel to the Airport in private transfer. Special Notes: You will reach airport 3 - 4 hours prior to your departure flight. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 114252.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nStandard category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\nSt. George Hotel / Hotel Prague Central Plaza / Galileo Hotel / Ibis Praha (Wenceslas Square) / Ibis Praha (Mala Strana) or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nArt Hotel Vienna / Ibis Wien Hauptbahnhof / Ibis Wien Mariahilf Hotel/ Admiral or similar\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nBenczur / City Hotel Ring / Hotel Charles / Hotel Orion Varkert or similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nHotels Envisaged Or Similar\n\n\n\n\nCities\n\n\nValue category\n\n\n\n\nPrague\n\n\n\xa0Hotel Carlton / Louis Leger / Royal Court Hotel / Best Western City Hotel Moran / Clarion Prague City / NH Prague City or similar\n\n\n\n\nVienna\n\n\nHotel Zeitgeist Vienna, Mercure Wien Westbahnhof, Mercure Wien City or similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nBudapest\n\n\nRoyal Park Boutique Hotel /\xa0 Corvin Center Suites / City Inn or similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast Except Day 1\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights’ accommodation in Prague based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Vienna based on the hotel category selected or similar 2 Nights’ accommodation in Budapest based on the hotel category selected or similar Meals: Daily Breakfast *(Except Day 1) Transportation: [Includes Privates services on Point to Point Basis] Arrival Airport Transfer from Prague Airport to Prague Hotel Departure Airport transfer from Budapest Hotel to Budapest Airport Train Pass: [Seat Reservation would be additional] 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Prague to Vienna 2nd Class Train Ticket cost from Vienna to Budapest Sightseeing: (For SIC Package tours will operate on seat in coach basis and from a designated point) Prague - City Tour including Prague Castle Vienna City Tour with Schonbrunn Palace Budapest City Tour Insurance: Overseas Travel Insurance (up to 60 yrs age group only). Exclusions: International air ticket, Domestic ticket if any, Airport taxes & Visa charges. Lunch & Dinner (if not mentioned) Drinks during meals TCS and GST is not included in the above cost and will be charged on final amount. Laundry, telephone, optional excursions and other items of a personal nature. Mandatory tipping to Guide/ driver of USD 10 per person per day is not included in the price. City taxes / Resort Fees – To be paid at the hotel. Cost of foreign exchange for personal use. Cost of PCR Test is not included & any medical examination will be treated as actual Any items or services not specified in the itinerary ‘INCLUSIONS’ head.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Note: The above price is based on minimum 2 Passengers travelling together. The above price is not valid for travel during Trade Fairs & Events Maximum 3 persons (adult / child) are allowed per room. Midnight surcharges apply for transfers between 2200 hrs. – 0700 hrs. WIFI, Tea / Coffee making facility etc. in the rooms cannot be guaranteed. (Supplement charges may apply for such services) Standard check-in time into the hotel is 1500 Hrs. Most hotels in Europe are not air-conditioned. At this point of time no services are confirmed and the same is subject to availability TCS & GST as applicable on the above tour cost. Terms and Conditions: Travel Validity: 1 April 2026 – 30 September 2026 Black out period will attract surcharges and above rates could differ. The rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times. Maximum 3 persons (2 adult + 1 child or 3 adults) are allowed per room. The rates are not valid on block out dates which covers sporting events, trade fairs, conventions, and major congresses Surcharges wherever applicable would be advised at the time of booking. To proceed with the booking, you need to pay Non-Refundable Booking deposit depending on the package which will be adjusted towards the cost of the tour. Should the period of travel, or the number of participants, or the type of accommodation, or the type of transport or the duration of the trip, change the quote will be adjusted accordingly. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. We are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package. International Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends. Offer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients. The organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode':