ption': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\n03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Kuta/ Seminyak\n02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Ubud.\nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\nReturn airport transfers on Pvt basis\nFull Day Benoa Watersport (01 Banana Boat + Jet Ski + Parasailing) Followed By Sunset Tanah Lot Temple Tour On Pvt Basis\nFull Day Kintamani Hot Spring Followed by Ubud Market on Pvt Basis\xa0\xa0\nTravel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.)\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nTCS & GST.\nThe rates are valid for a minimum of 02 adult travelling.\nAll flight services.\nPre and post tour services & costs.\nHotel rates are not valid during blackout period / surcharge dates / stop sales.\nBlackout date surcharges\nChristmas & New Year 15 Dec 2026 to 06 Jan 2027\nNyepi day 03 Mar to 08 Mar 2027\nNyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 08 Mar 2027. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 08 Mar to 06.00 am 09 Mar 2027.\nMidnight surcharge.\nMeals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary.\nTips for guide & driver.\nCity tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable).\nExpenditure of a personal nature (mini bar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.)\nCamera fee.\nPorterage facility\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable.\nVisa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable).\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary.\xa0\nCost of optional excursions.\nAnything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Package Terms and Conditions:\n\nThe package price is valid until as mentioned above.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nDuring Peak Season: Minimum 2 Nights Stay is required\nNo Check Out period on 31 December 2025 and 01 January 2026\nNyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 19 March 2026. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 19 March 2026 to 06.00 am 20 March 2026\nCompulsory New Year Dinner will be Applicable according to the Resort\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/BaliWaterSport267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Seminyak753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/TanahLotTemple75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Bali_Scenic_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Ubud.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Bali_Sunset_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/bali_shutterstock_224711452.jpg']}, 'score': 11.286367, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012571', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012571', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026'], 'packageName': 'Albelu Bali', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["Diwali Special Dates : Nov - 08, 09 2N Free Upgrade to One Bedroom Pool Villa in Seminyak Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg Dinners Enjoy Balinese Massage 1hr Experience Bali Swing Gala Dinner 1 Snack box pp What's More Like - Complimentary Welcome Gift on arrival, Complimentary 2 Bottles of 500 ml Mineral Water per person per day, Beach Lunch Bali Sightseeings: Visit Kintamani & Ubud Village Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset Enjoy Water Sports at Benoa Beach - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet ski (parasailing subject to weather conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple and enjoy Kecak Dance Visit Tegenungan Waterfall Enjoy Balinese Spa for 1 Hr Visit Full Day Nusa Penida Tour Free time for shopping"], 'pdfName': 'PKG011302_0_20230519164442.pdf', 'price': 132864, 'packageSummary': "The 'Albelu Bali' package is a 7-day tour covering Bali and Kuta, featuring special Diwali departure dates and a two-night free upgrade to a one-bedroom pool villa in Seminyak. Staying in four-star hotels on a bed-and-breakfast basis, travelers will enjoy curated Indian Jain and vegetarian dinners, a gala dinner, a beach lunch, and a relaxing one-hour Balinese massage. The action-packed itinerary includes visits to Kintamani, Ubud Village, the Tegenungan Waterfall, the Uluwatu Temple for a traditional Kecak Dance performance, and the Tanah Lot Floating Temple at sunset, alongside a full-day tour of Nusa Penida. Additionally, guests can experience the Bali Swing, enjoy thrilling water sports like banana boating, parasailing, and jet skiing at Benoa Beach, and take advantage of free time for shopping, all while receiving complimentary perks such as travel insurance, a welcome gift, and daily mineral water.", 'images': ['840623_Bali753.jpg', 'Kintamani.jpg', 'Bali_Swing.jpg', 'WaterSports_Bali.jpg', 'TegenunganWaterfall753.jpg', 'NusaPenida_753.jpg', 'Bali_Freeday.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 132864, 'thumbnailImage': 'Tegenungan_Waterfall_SRP.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG012571 is named \'Albelu Bali\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuta, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival – Check in Welcome to Bali, Indonesia, one of the most famous destinations in the world for holidays and packages. Upon arrival at Denpasar airport, you will be met by our representative/ Tour Manager who will assist you for your transfer to the hotel. On arrival in Bali, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. NOTE: All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Celuk & Mas Village - Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour Today after breakfast, proceed to Celuk Silver Smith Village - famous for its silver & gold handicrafts. Later visit Mas Wooden Carved Art Village village is one of the art villages in Bali which is famous with high quality wooden statues followed by visit to Kintamani Village– explore some of the most desirable and beautiful areas located in the northeast of Bali including incredible views of the Mount Batur volcano and the lakes. Later proceed for the Ubud Village Tour - one of the most famous villages of Bali, located amongst rice paddies and steep ravines in the central foot hills of the Gianyar regency. Later visit Bali Coffee Plantation and enjoy coffee tasting., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Experience Bali Swing – Tanah Lot Sunset Tour Post breakfast, proceed for an exciting swing, the most famous Bali Swing, it offers you and experiences and amazing views. The swings are handcrafted wonders, woven from wood and rope, offer a unique and exhilarating perspective on the island\'s beauty. Soaring through verdant jungles, emerald rice terraces, Bali\'s swings are a must-do for anyone seeking an unforgettable adrenaline rush and a touch of paradise. Later arrive at Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset - one of the most popular sites in Indonesia. An ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves; a not to be missed icons., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance After breakfast, proceed the beach at Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski. (*Parasailing subjected to weather conditions) Later proceed for Ulluwatu Temple Tour; located at 70-meter-high cliff the main site on Uluwatu Tours is visiting this temple. There are hundreds of monkeys roaming along the path outside the temple. When the sun goes down, we will witness the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Tegenungan Waterfall – Enjoy Balinese Spa 1Hr - Shopping Tour Post breakfast checkout and proceed to Tegenungan Waterfall also known as Blangsinga Waterfall, is one of the most famous and biggest waterfalls in the island of Bali. With a height of 15 meters, makes Tegenungan Waterfall as the highest waterfall around the Ubud area. Later proceed for a relaxing spa session. Enjoy the spa presenting a natural relaxation and treatment assortment for health and beauty. (60 Minutes Traditional Balinese Massage). Enjoy free time for Shopping. Later check in to your Villa for an exclusive stay., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Gala Dinner, Description: Full Day Nusa Penida Tour Today after breakfast proceed to Join Day Tour of Nusa Penida, where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point, the natural pool of Angel\'s Billabong. Kelingking beach - often referred to as Kelingking Secret Point, is one of Nusa Penida\'s most breathtaking landmarks. With its iconic T-rex shaped cliff, the beach offers stunning panoramic views of turquoise waters crashing against dramatic limestone formations. Angel billabong - is a stunning natural pool located on the western coast of Nusa Penida. This picturesque spot features crystal-clear turquoise waters that are surrounded by dramatic rocky cliffs, creating a serene oasis that feels almost otherworldly. Broken beach - This stunning cove features a dramatic archway in the rocky cliffs, creating a picturesque "broken" effect that opens up to the sparkling turquoise ocean below. The surrounding cliffs are adorned with lush greenery, adding to the enchanting atmosphere. Crystal Bay - a serene cove on the western coast of Nusa Penida, Bali, renowned for its crystal-clear turquoise waters, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Transfer to Airport – Flight back home This morning after breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. * The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Final Itinerary will be handed over on the day of arrival. CHILD POLICY: Infant: 0-1.99 yrs Child No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs Child With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 132864.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n04 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0 **Free upgrade to Grand Kesambi Villa Seminyak or similar\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily American breakfast. (Except Day 1)\xa0\n04 Vegetarian Lunches at Indian restaurant\n01 Local Lunch\xa0\n05 Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\n01 Gala Dinner\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be vegetarian\n(B - Breakfast | L - Lunch | LC - Lunch coupon | PL – Packed Lunch | D – Dinner)\n, Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary Ex Ahmedabad Accommodations at the hotels specified above or similar. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary Return Airport transfers from all airports. All transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If groups size is less than 15 customers then the tour will operate without Tour Manager on Seat in Coach and FIT Basis.. Exclusions: GST and TCS as applicable Indonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Tourist Tax entering Bali (Approx USD 10) to be paid by guest before arrival to Bali. The cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost. City Tax or Tourism Tax Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. Meals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary. Drinks during meals / sightseeing tours are not included The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 15 January 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Tips / Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions. If you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Hotels This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant. Coaches Coaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. Meals All Meals are pre–set. Sightseeing Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc. General On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour. Security alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. TCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Diwali Special Dates : Nov - 08, 09 2N Free Upgrade to One Bedroom Pool Villa in Seminyak Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg Dinners Enjoy Balinese Massage 1hr Experience Bali Swing Gala Dinner 1 Snack box pp What\'s More Like - Complimentary Welcome Gift on arrival, Complimentary 2 Bottles of 500 ml Mineral Water per person per day, Beach Lunch Bali Sightseeings: Visit Kintamani & Ubud Village Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset Enjoy Water Sports at Benoa Beach - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet ski (parasailing subject to weather conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple and enjoy Kecak Dance Visit Tegenungan Waterfall Enjoy Balinese Spa for 1 Hr Visit Full Day Nusa Penida Tour Free time for shopping.', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZCB200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZCB200', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Albelu Bali' package is a 7-day tour covering Bali and Kuta, featuring special Diwali departure dates and a two-night free upgrade to a one-bedroom pool villa in Seminyak. Staying in four-star hotels on a bed-and-breakfast basis, travelers will enjoy curated Indian Jain and vegetarian dinners, a gala dinner, a beach lunch, and a relaxing one-hour Balinese massage. The action-packed itinerary includes visits to Kintamani, Ubud Village, the Tegenungan Waterfall, the Uluwatu Temple for a traditional Kecak Dance performance, and the Tanah Lot Floating Temple at sunset, alongside a full-day tour of Nusa Penida. Additionally, guests can experience the Bali Swing, enjoy thrilling water sports like banana boating, parasailing, and jet skiing at Benoa Beach, and take advantage of free time for shopping, all while receiving complimentary perks such as travel insurance, a welcome gift, and daily mineral water.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrival – Check in\nWelcome to Bali, Indonesia, one of the most famous destinations in the world for holidays and packages. Upon arrival at Denpasar airport, you will be met by our representative/ Tour Manager who will assist you for your transfer to the hotel.\xa0\nOn arrival in Bali, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure.\n\xa0\nNOTE:\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar in Bali'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Celuk & Mas Village - Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour\nToday after breakfast, proceed to Celuk Silver Smith Village - famous for its silver & gold handicrafts. Later visit Mas Wooden Carved Art Village village is one of the art villages in Bali which is famous with high quality wooden statues followed by visit to Kintamani Village– explore some of the most desirable and beautiful areas located in the northeast of Bali including incredible views of the Mount Batur volcano and the lakes. Later proceed for the Ubud Village Tour - one of the most famous villages of Bali, located amongst rice paddies and steep ravines in the central foot hills of the Gianyar regency.\xa0\nLater visit Bali Coffee Plantation and enjoy coffee tasting.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar in Bali'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\nExperience Bali Swing – Tanah Lot Sunset Tour\nPost breakfast, proceed for an exciting swing, the most famous Bali Swing, it offers you and experiences and amazing views. The swings are handcrafted wonders, woven from wood and rope, offer a unique and exhilarating perspective on the island's beauty. Soaring through verdant jungles, emerald rice terraces, Bali's swings are a must-do for anyone seeking an unforgettable adrenaline rush and a touch of paradise.\nLater arrive at Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset - one of the most popular sites in Indonesia. An ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves; a not to be missed icons.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar in Bali'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nWater Sports at Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\nAfter breakfast, proceed the beach at Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski.\n(*Parasailing subjected to weather conditions)\nLater proceed for Ulluwatu Temple Tour; located at 70-meter-high cliff the main site on Uluwatu Tours is visiting this temple. There are hundreds of monkeys roaming along the path outside the temple. When the sun goes down, we will witness the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar in Bali'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nTegenungan Waterfall – Enjoy Balinese Spa 1Hr - Shopping Tour\nPost breakfast checkout and proceed to Tegenungan Waterfall also known as Blangsinga Waterfall, is one of the most famous and biggest waterfalls in the island of Bali. With a height of 15 meters, makes Tegenungan Waterfall as the highest waterfall around the Ubud area.\xa0\nLater proceed for a relaxing spa session. Enjoy the spa presenting a natural relaxation and treatment assortment for health and beauty. (60 Minutes Traditional Balinese Massage). Enjoy free time for Shopping. Later check in to your Villa for an exclusive stay.\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar in Bali **Free upgrade to Grand Kesambi Villa Seminyak or similar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nFull Day Nusa Penida Tour\nToday after breakfast proceed to Join Day Tour of Nusa Penida, where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point, the natural pool of Angel\'s Billabong.\xa0\nKelingking beach - often referred to as Kelingking Secret Point, is one of Nusa Penida\'s most breathtaking landmarks. With its iconic T-rex shaped cliff, the beach offers stunning panoramic views of turquoise waters crashing against dramatic limestone formations.\nAngel billabong - is a stunning natural pool located on the western coast of Nusa Penida. This picturesque spot features crystal-clear turquoise waters that are surrounded by dramatic rocky cliffs, creating a serene oasis that feels almost otherworldly.\nBroken beach - This stunning cove features a dramatic archway in the rocky cliffs, creating a picturesque "broken" effect that opens up to the sparkling turquoise ocean below. The surrounding cliffs are adorned with lush greenery, adding to the enchanting atmosphere.\nCrystal Bay - a serene cove on the western coast of Nusa Penida, Bali, renowned for its crystal-clear turquoise waters', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Gala Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar in Bali\xa0**Free upgrade to Grand Kesambi Villa Seminyak or similar'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nTransfer to Airport – Flight back home\nThis morning after breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with your Tour Manager. Your valued suggestions will be most appreciated.\n* The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Final Itinerary will be handed over on the day of arrival.\n\xa0\nCHILD POLICY:\nInfant: 0-1.99 yrs\nChild No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs\nChild With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs\n\xa0\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n04 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0 **Free upgrade to Grand Kesambi Villa Seminyak or similar\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n04 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0 **Free upgrade to Grand Kesambi Villa Seminyak or similar\n', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 132900.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0\xa0\n02 nights at Hotel Bintang Resort Kuta or similar\xa0 **Free upgrade to Grand Kesambi Villa Seminyak or similar\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily American breakfast. (Except Day 1)\xa0\n04 Vegetarian Lunches at Indian restaurant\n01 Local Lunch\xa0\n05 Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\n01 Gala Dinner\nNote: Packed lunches, if applicable, will be vegetarian\n(B - Breakfast | L - Lunch | LC - Lunch coupon | PL – Packed Lunch | D – Dinner)\n', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nTransfers and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['\nVisit Kintamani & Ubud Village\xa0\nExperience Bali Swing\xa0\nVisit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset\nEnjoy Water Sports at Benoa Beach - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet ski (parasailing subject to weather conditions)\xa0\nVisit Uluwatu Temple and enjoy Kecak Dance\nVisit Tegenungan Waterfall\nEnjoy Balinese Spa for 1 Hr\nVisit Full Day Nusa Penida Tour\nFree time for shopping\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary', '\nFull Day Barong Dance & Kintamani Ubud Village Tour with Mt Batur view\nRoyal Taman Ayun, Alas Kedaton & Tanah Lot Sunset Tour\nHalf day Water Sports Benoa - including 1 x round of Banana boat, Parasailing / flying fish and Jet ski (parasailing subject to weather)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary Ex Ahmedabad</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><br />TENTATIVE FLIGHT DETAILS :</strong></p>\n<table class="MsoNormalTable" style="height: 163px; width: 480px;" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">\n<tbody>\n<tr style="mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; height: 19.0pt;">\n<td style="width: 465px;" colspan="5" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Flight Details for 7 May, 28 May, 3 Sep, 8 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 19pt; text-align: center;">\n<td style="width: 200.99px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">DATE</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 66.0104px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Flight</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 66px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Sector</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 79px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Departure</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 53px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Arrival</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 17.45pt; text-align: center;">\n<td style="width: 200.99px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><strong><span lang="EN-IN">07/28 May, 3 Sep, 8 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 66.0104px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><spa