ing="0" cellpadding="0">\n<tbody>\n<tr style="height: 35px;">\n<td style="width: 468px; height: 35px;" colspan="5" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Flight Details for 9 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 35px; text-align: center;">\n<td style="width: 209px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">DATE</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.8958px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Flight</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.1042px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Sector</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 79px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Departure</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 51px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p align="center"><strong><span lang="EN-IN">Arrival</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 35px; text-align: center;">\n<td style="width: 209px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><strong><span lang="EN-IN">08 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.8958px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">MH 107</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.1042px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">AMD-KUL</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 79px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">22:45</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 51px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">6:45</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 35px; text-align: center;">\n<td style="width: 209px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><strong><span lang="EN-IN">09 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.8958px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">MH&nbsp;851</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.1042px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">KUL-DPS</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 79px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">12:20</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 51px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">15:25</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 35.1979px; text-align: center;">\n<td style="width: 209px; height: 35.1979px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><strong><span lang="EN-IN">15 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.8958px; height: 35.1979px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">MH&nbsp;714</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 64.1042px; height: 35.1979px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">DPS-KUL</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 79px; height: 35.1979px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">13:10</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 51px; height: 35.1979px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">16:05</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 35px;">\n<td style="text-align: center; width: 209px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><strong><span lang="EN-IN">15 Nov</span></strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style="text-align: center; width: 64.8958px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">MH&nbsp;106</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="text-align: center; width: 64.1042px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">KUL-AMD</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="text-align: center; width: 79px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p><span lang="EN-IN">18:45</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style="width: 51px; height: 35px;" nowrap="nowrap">\n<p style="text-align: center;"><span lang="EN-IN">21:40</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Note : Above Flight details are tentative only. The airline, departure, arrival time and routing may change.</strong></p>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary Ex Ahmedabad\xa0 \xa0\nAccommodations at the hotels specified above or similar.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1st December 2025\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\nReturn Airport transfers from all airports.\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative.\xa0\nIf groups size is less than 15 customers then the tour will operate without Tour Manager on Seat in Coach and FIT Basis.\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nGST and TCS as applicable\nIndonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nTourist Tax entering Bali (Approx USD 10) to be paid by guest before arrival to Bali.\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nMeals other than that are mentioned in your itinerary.\nDrinks during meals / sightseeing tours are not included\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 15 January 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nTips / Porterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\nHotels\n\nThis Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts.\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nHotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches\n\nCoaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nDue to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only\nDue to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nCoaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers.\n\n\xa0\nMeals\n\nAll Meals are pre–set.\n\nSightseeing\n\nDue to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports\nsometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\nEvery Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same.\nAll our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc.\n\nGeneral\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour.\nSecurity alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. TCIL will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\nDisabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements.\nTCIL shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour.\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends.\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on\xa0 tour\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/Tegenungan_Waterfall_SRP.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/840623_Bali753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/Kintamani.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/Bali_Swing.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/WaterSports_Bali.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/TegenunganWaterfall753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/NusaPenida_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG012571/itinerary/Bali_Freeday.jpg']}, 'score': 10.722984, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015130', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015130', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Bali  - Winter', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Guaranteed Departure – Minimum 2 Pax Required. 2N Free upgrade to Villa (One Bedroom Pool Villa) Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Dinners What’s More Like – One Souvenir per room Bali: Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset Enjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet ski (subject to weather conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance Visit Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour Visit Bali Coffee Plantation Visit Nusa Penida Island'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 66322, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Bali - Winter' package is a 7-day tour covering the beautiful island of Bali, offering four-star hotel accommodations with a free two-night upgrade to a one-bedroom pool villa, daily breakfast, and specially curated Indian dinners. This guaranteed departure itinerary for a minimum of two guests includes a complimentary souvenir and a host of exciting activities. Participants will experience the famous Bali Swing, visit the iconic Tanah Lot Floating Temple at sunset, enjoy thrilling water sports like banana boat rides, parasailing, and jet skiing at Tanjung Benoa, and explore the Uluwatu Temple while watching a traditional Kecak dance. Additionally, travelers will embark on a Kintamani and Ubud Village tour, visit a local Bali coffee plantation, and take an excursion to the stunning Nusa Penida Island.", 'images': ['Bali75390.jpg', 'Bali_Swing.jpg', 'NusaPenida753.jpg', 'Kecak_Dance_Bali_753.jpg', 'Kintamani.jpg', 'Bali_Freeday.jpg', '840623_Bali753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 66322, 'thumbnailImage': 'Bali26712.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG015130 is named \'Magical Bali  - Winter\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Bali, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Bali - Check In Welcome To Bali, Indonesia, One Of The Most Famous Destinations In The World For Holidays And Packages. Upon Arrival At Denpasar Airport, You Will Be Met By Our Representative/ Tour Manager Who Will Assist You For Your Transfer To The Hotel. On Arrival In Bali, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. NOTE: All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Experience Bali Swing - Tanah Lot Sunset Tour This morning after breakfast, proceed for an exciting adventure at Bali Swing and to experience incredible views while swinging. Later proceed to Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset – an ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves, the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Nusa Penida Island This morning after breakfast, Visit Nusa Penida Tour where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach - stunning cove features a dramatic archway in the rocky cliffs, creating a picturesque "broken" effect that opens up to the sparkling turquoise ocean below, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point - with its iconic T-rex shaped cliff, the beach offers stunning panoramic views of turquoise waters crashing against dramatic limestone formations., the natural pool of Angel\'s Billabong - is a stunning natural pool located on the western coast of Nusa Penida. This picturesque spot features crystal-clear turquoise waters that are surrounded by dramatic rocky cliffs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Enjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance This morning after breakfast, proceed to the Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski. (**Sports Activities subjected to weather conditions) Later proceed for Uluwatu Temple Tour explores Bali\'s iconic 11th-century sea temple perched 70 meters on a sheer cliff. Later this evening enjoy the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’ a stunning Balinese cultural performance set against the backdrop of a dramatic sunset by the Indian Ocean., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour – Visit Bali Coffee Plantation This morning after breakfast, proceed with a visit to Celuk Village famous for its silver & gold handicrafts then proceed to Mas Village famous for high quality wooden carving and wooden statues. Later we will proceed to see beautiful panorama from Kintamani Village to overview the active volcano of Batur Mount and wide Lake of Batur in a valley. Then proceed to visit Bali Coffee Plantation. After lunch proceed to the Ubud Village Tour including Ubud Royal Palace is the official residence of Ubud’s royal family and The Ubud Art Market - great place to find beautiful balinese handicrafts, textiles and souvenirs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This Morning After Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Bali On Your Own Or You Can Enjoy Atv Ride. ATV Ride - 60 Minutes of duration - at USD 35 per person (Minimum 2 Pax Required) (OPTIONAL ACTIVITY), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. Note: The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Final Itinerary will be handed over on the day of arrival CHILD POLICY Infant: 0-1.99 yrs Child No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs Child With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 66322.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta / Bliss Surfer Kuta or similar in Kuta – Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali **Free Upgrade to Aldeoz Grand Kencana Villa or similar in Seminyak - Bali\n, \n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n06 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1 July 2026 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary Return Airport transfers from all airports. All transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If group size is less than 15 customers, the tour will operate on Seat in Coach and FIT basis. For Group Size more than 15 customers there will be English Speaking Guide Assistance and for less than 15 customers there will be Driver cum Guide.. Exclusions: Main Airfare Airport taxes Indonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) The cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost. City Tax or Tourism Tax Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1 July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions. VISAS: Indonesia Visa is not included (To be paid by Guest on arrival). Product Terms and Conditions: General Information: All travelers while returning to India should submit a self-declaration form (mandatory) on the online Air Suvidha portal (www.newdelhiairport.in) before the scheduled travel, including the last 14 days of travel details. Each passenger shall also submit a declaration with respect to the authenticity of the report and will be liable for criminal prosecution if found otherwise.. Highlights of the package: Guaranteed Departure – Minimum 2 Pax Required. 2N Free upgrade to Villa (One Bedroom Pool Villa) Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Dinners What’s More Like – One Souvenir per room Bali: Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset Enjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet ski (subject to weather conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance Visit Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour Visit Bali Coffee Plantation Visit Nusa Penida Island.', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMB560', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Bali - Winter' package is a 7-day tour covering the beautiful island of Bali, offering four-star hotel accommodations with a free two-night upgrade to a one-bedroom pool villa, daily breakfast, and specially curated Indian dinners. This guaranteed departure itinerary for a minimum of two guests includes a complimentary souvenir and a host of exciting activities. Participants will experience the famous Bali Swing, visit the iconic Tanah Lot Floating Temple at sunset, enjoy thrilling water sports like banana boat rides, parasailing, and jet skiing at Tanjung Benoa, and explore the Uluwatu Temple while watching a traditional Kecak dance. Additionally, travelers will embark on a Kintamani and Ubud Village tour, visit a local Bali coffee plantation, and take an excursion to the stunning Nusa Penida Island.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrival In Bali - Check In\nWelcome To Bali, Indonesia, One Of The Most Famous Destinations In The World For Holidays And Packages. Upon Arrival At Denpasar Airport, You Will Be Met By Our Representative/ Tour Manager Who Will Assist You For Your Transfer To The Hotel.\nOn Arrival In Bali, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure.\n\xa0\nNOTE:\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nExperience Bali Swing - Tanah Lot Sunset Tour\nThis morning after breakfast, proceed for an exciting adventure at Bali Swing and to experience incredible views while swinging. Later proceed to Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset – an ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves, the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Nusa Penida Island\nThis morning after breakfast, Visit Nusa Penida Tour where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach - stunning cove features a dramatic archway in the rocky cliffs, creating a picturesque "broken" effect that opens up to the sparkling turquoise ocean below, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point - with its iconic T-rex shaped cliff, the beach offers stunning panoramic views of turquoise waters crashing against dramatic limestone formations., the natural pool of Angel\'s Billabong - is a stunning natural pool located on the western coast of Nusa Penida. This picturesque spot features crystal-clear turquoise waters that are surrounded by dramatic rocky cliffs.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nEnjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\nThis morning after breakfast, proceed to the Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski. (**Sports Activities subjected to weather conditions)\nLater proceed for Uluwatu Temple Tour explores Bali's iconic 11th-century sea temple perched 70 meters on a sheer cliff. Later this evening enjoy the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’ a stunning Balinese cultural performance set against the backdrop of a dramatic sunset by the Indian Ocean.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour\xa0– Visit Bali Coffee Plantation\nThis morning after breakfast, proceed with a visit to Celuk Village famous for its silver & gold handicrafts then proceed to Mas Village famous for high quality wooden carving and wooden statues. Later we will proceed to see beautiful panorama from Kintamani Village to overview the active volcano of Batur Mount and wide Lake of Batur in a valley. Then proceed to visit Bali Coffee Plantation.\nAfter lunch proceed to the Ubud Village Tour including Ubud Royal Palace is the official residence of Ubud’s royal family and The Ubud Art Market - great place to find beautiful balinese handicrafts, textiles and souvenirs.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0**Free Upgrade to Aldeoz Grand Kencana Villa or similar in Seminyak - Bali\n'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis Morning After Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure.\nSpend Rest Of The Day Exploring Bali On Your Own Or You Can Enjoy Atv Ride.\nATV Ride - 60 Minutes of duration - at USD 35 per person (Minimum 2 Pax Required) (OPTIONAL ACTIVITY)', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali **Free Upgrade to Aldeoz Grand Kencana Villa or similar in Seminyak - Bali'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning After Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\nNote: The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Final Itinerary will be handed over on the day of arrival\n\xa0\nCHILD POLICY\nInfant: 0-1.99 yrs\nChild No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs\nChild With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs\n\xa0\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta / Bliss Surfer Kuta or similar in Kuta – Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali **Free Upgrade to Aldeoz Grand Kencana Villa or similar in Seminyak - Bali\n', '\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta / Bliss Surfer Kuta or similar in Kuta – Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali **Free Upgrade to Aldeoz Grand Kencana Villa or similar in Seminyak - Bali\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 66300.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta / Bliss Surfer Kuta or similar in Kuta – Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali **Free Upgrade to Aldeoz Grand Kencana Villa or similar in Seminyak - Bali\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n06 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', '\nExperience Bali Swing\nVisit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset\nEnjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet ski (parasailing subject to weather conditions)\xa0\nVisit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\nVisit Kintamani and Ubud Village Tour\nVisit Bali Coffee Plantation\nVisit Nusa Penida Island\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n<li>Internal airfare included for joining direct passengers</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 1 July 2026\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\nReturn Airport transfers from all airports.\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative.\xa0\nIf group size is less than 15 customers, the tour will operate on Seat in Coach and FIT basis.\xa0\nFor Group Size more than 15 customers there will be English Speaking Guide Assistance and for less than 15 customers there will be Driver cum Guide.\n', 'exclusions': '\nMain Airfare\xa0\nAirport taxes\xa0\nIndonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 1 July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nPorterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\nVISAS: Indonesia Visa is not included (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'General Information:\nAll travelers while returning to India should submit a self-declaration form (mandatory) on the online Air Suvidha portal\xa0(www.newdelhiairport.in)\xa0before the scheduled travel, including the last 14 days of travel details. Each passenger shall also submit a declaration with respect to the authenticity of the report and will be liable for criminal prosecution if found otherwise.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/Bali26712.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/Bali75390.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/Bali_Swing.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/NusaPenida753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/Kecak_Dance_Bali_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/Kintamani.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/Bali_Freeday.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015130/itinerary/840623_Bali753.jpg']}, 'score': 10.209203, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014873', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014873', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Vietnam With Bali (Winter)', 'days': 10, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Hanoi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ha Long Bay', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Hanoi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Da Nang', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Da Nang', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Da Nang', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ["An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners (Lunches are not included in Bali Portion) Enjoy Water Sports activities like Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski in Bali Experience Bali Swing in Bali Enjoy Cyclo ride around the Old Quarter of Hanoi Enjoy Basket Boat Ride at Cam Thanh Village in Da Nang Enjoy Boat Ride with Lantern Releasing in Da Nang What’s More Like Vietnamese Ice Cream at Hoi An in Da Nang Vietnamese Coffee Tasting Experience One souvenir per room Bali Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple For Sunset Enjoy Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject To Weather Conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance Hanoi Guided City Tour Of Hanoi Photo Stop At Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum Photo Stop At One Pillar Pagoda Experience Cyclo Tour Ride Visit Hoan Kiem Lake Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay Overnight Stay On Ha Long Bay / Lan Ha Bay On Cruise Activities Tai Chi Training, Cooking Classes, Kayaking (Subject To Availability, Cruise Type & Weather Conditions) Da Nang Visit Cam Thanh Coconut Village Enjoy Basket Boat Ride At Cam Thanh Village Visit Hoi An Ancient Town Enjoy Boat Ride With Lantern Releasing Day Excursion To Bana Hills By Cable Car Visit Golden Bridge Visit French Gardens Visit French Quarters Visit St. Denis Church Visit Indoor Fantasy Park (Wax Museum Not Included) Photo Stop At Dragon Bridge"], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 193950, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Vietnam With Bali (Winter)' package is a 10-day tour covering Bali, Da Nang, Hanoi, and Ha Long Bay. This air-inclusive tour features four-star accommodations, dedicated tour manager assistance, and specially curated Indian meals. Throughout the journey, participants will enjoy thrilling water sports, the famous Bali Swing, and visits to the Tanah Lot and Uluwatu Temples in Bali. In Hanoi, guests will experience a traditional cyclo ride, a guided city tour, and an overnight cruise on Ha Long Bay with activities like Tai Chi and kayaking. The adventure concludes in Da Nang with a basket boat ride at Cam Thanh Village, a lantern-releasing boat ride in Hoi An, and a scenic cable car ride to Ba Na Hills to visit the iconic Golden Bridge and French Quarters.", 'images': ['BaliSwing.jpg', 'Tanah_Lot_Temple_New_Bali_&53.jpg', 'Nusa_Penida_New_753.jpg', 'KeckDanace.jpg', 'HoChiMinh753.jpg', 'HalongBayCruise753.jpg', 'AdobeStock_296902787_One_Pillar_pagoda_in_Hanoi.jpg', 'HoiAn753.jpg', 'GoldenbridgeDanang753.jpg', 'Danang7538.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 193950, 'thumbnailImage': 'Bali26789.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014873 is named 'Magical Vietnam With Bali (Winter)' and spans 10 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Bali, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival in Bali - Check In Welcome to Bali, Indonesia, one of the most famous destinations in the world for holidays and packages. Upon arrival at the Denpasar airport, you will be met by our representative/ Tour Manager who will assist you for your transfer to the hotel. On arrival in Bali, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. Note: All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Experience Bali Swing - Tanah Lot Sunset Tour Post breakfast, proceed for an exciting swing, the most famous Bali Swing. Later arrive at Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset – An ancient Hindu shrine., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day at Leisure Or Optional Tour of Nusa Penida This morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure. Spend rest of the day exploring Bali on your own OR you can explore Nusa Penida Island OPTIONAL EXCURSION: Full Day Nusa Penida Tour inclusive of Angel Billabong, Broken Beach, Kelingking Beach with Lunch (Set Menu) at USD 45 per person (Minimum 2 Pax Required) Join Day Tour of Nusa Penida, where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point, the natural pool of Angel's Billabong., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance After breakfast, proceed to the Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski. (**Parasailing subjected to weather conditions) Later proceed for Uluwatu Temple Tour; located at 70-meter-high cliff. Later this evening enjoy the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Hanoi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Fly to Hanoi – Day at Leisure This morning after breakfast proceed to Denpasar airport for the flight to Hanoi. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in. (Standard check in time 1500 hrs). Rest of the day at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ha Long Bay, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner, Description: Hanoi – Ha Long Bay – Overnight on Cruise - Visit Pearl Farm Enroute Ha Long Bay This morning after breakfast, we check out and proceed to Ha Long. Enroute visit Pearl Farm. Upon arrival in Ha Long, check in at the overnight cruise. As we sail on the Ha Long bay we visit Surprise Caves & Ti Top Island - enjoy free time at the beach or walk up the hill to enjoy a view of Ha Long Bay. Later enjoy sunset view from sundeck. OR Hanoi – Lan Ha Bay – Overnight on Cruise This morning after breakfast, we check out and proceed to Lan Ha Bay. Upon Arrival in Lan Ha Bay, check in at the Overnight Cruise. As we sail on the Lan Ha Bay, we visit Dark & Bright Cave (Hang Sang & Toi) - Enjoy free time at the beach or enjoy a view of Lan Ha Bay., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Hanoi, Meals: Breakfast, Brunch and Dinner, Description: Sail on Ha Long Bay – Drive to Hanoi - Guided City Tour of Hanoi - Enjoy Cyclo Tour This morning after breakfast, we visit Luon Cave by boat - enjoy kayaking or wooden boat ride through the cave. Enjoy brunch on board the Cruise Return to Halong Wharf and transfer back to Hanoi. (Note: The cruise itinerary can be changed according to weather conditions.) Upon arrival, we proceed on the city tour - See Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum from outside. Visit One Pillar Pagoda followed by a cyclo ride around the Old Quarter of Hanoi. Later enjoy photostop at Hoan Kiem Lake. OR Sail On Lan Ha Bay – Drive to Hanoi - Guided City Tour of Hanoi - Enjoy Cyclo Tour This Morning After Breakfast, Enjoy sunrise photograph and brunch on board the cruise Return to Tuan Chau Harbor and transfer back to Hanoi. (Note: The cruise itinerary can be changed according to the cruise / weather conditions.) Upon arrival, we proceed on the city tour - See Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum from outside. Visit One Pillar Pagoda followed by a cyclo ride around the Old Quarter of Hanoi. Later enjoy photostop at Hoan Kiem Lake., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Da Nang, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Fly to Da Nang - Visit Cam Thanh Village – Enjoy Basket Boat Ride at Cam Thanh Village - Visit Hoi An Ancient Town - Experience Boat Ride with Lantern Releasing This morning after breakfast, we check out and proceed to the airport for our flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival, transfer from the airport to the hotel for check in. (Standard check in time 1500 hrs). Later visit Cam Thanh Village. Enjoy a basket boat ride through the coconut jungle forest. Visit Hoi An ancient town - see the tile-roofed Japanese Bridge, Chinese Assembly halls and ancient houses followed by a boat ride with lantern releasing on the river., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Da Nang, Meals: Breakfast, International Lunch and Dinner, Description: Day Excursion to Ba Na Hills - Visit Golden Bridge - Photo Stop at Dragon Bridge This morning after breakfast, we proceed to Ba Na hills. On arrival take a Cable Car to Ba Na hills station. Visit Golden Bridge followed by visit the Old Villas, French Stable, and Tinh Tam Garden. See the Linh Ung Pagoda. Visit Loc Uyen Garden and Quan Am Pavilion. Our next stop will be the Fantasy Park, an amusement park. Later this evening proceed for a photo stop at Dragon Bridge., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 10 - Da Nang, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End of Tour - Fly Back This morning after breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour. * The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Final Itinerary will be handed over on the day of arrival., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 193950.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n04 Night accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n01 Night accommodation at Golden Cruise / La Regina Royal Cruise /Aqua Legend/ Aqua Elegance or similar in Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Yarra Ocean / Mandila Beach Hotel / Bluesun Hotel\xa0 or similar in Da Nang\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily buffet / packed breakfast (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 International buffet Lunch\n08 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n1 Lunch, 1 Dinner and 1 Brunch onboard Cruise\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n\xa0\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch/ IL/D - International Lunch/Dinner / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n**Depending on Flight timings Packed Meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) will be provided instead of Sitting Meals at Indian / Local Restaurant.\n**Lunches are not included in Bali Portion. Inclusions: Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary. Internal airfare for Bali – Hanoi, Hanoi- Da Nang is included for Joining Direct & NRI passengers Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Vietnam Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest). Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 30 April 2026 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary Airport transfers from all airports. All transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If groups size is less than 15 customers than the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Visa Requirements: Vietnam E-visa included in the package. Indonesia Visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival) Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 30 April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers. All foreign nationals and overseas Vietnamese entering with a visa must complete the digital arrival card prior to immigration clearance. Travelers can fill out the form by scanning a QR code upon arrival at international airports or, preferably, by completing it in advance online at https://prearrival.immigration.gov.vn/ to save time.. Exclusions: Compulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 5 per person per day Indonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival) The cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost. City Tax or Tourism Tax Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 30 April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: General Information: All travelers while returning to India should submit a self-declaration form (mandatory) on the online Air Suvidha portal (www.newdelhiairport.in) before the scheduled travel, including the last 14 days of travel details. Each passenger shall also submit a declaration with respect to the authenticity of the report and will be liable for criminal prosecution if found otherwise.. Highlights of the package: An Air Inclusive Value Tour with Tour Manager's assistance throughout the tour. Visa Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Lunches & Dinners (Lunches are not included in Bali Portion) Enjoy Water Sports activities like Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski in Bali Experience Bali Swing in Bali Enjoy Cyclo ride around the Old Quarter of Hanoi Enjoy Basket Boat Ride at Cam Thanh Village in Da Nang Enjoy Boat Ride with Lantern Releasing in Da Nang What’s More Like Vietnamese Ice Cream at Hoi An in Da Nang Vietnamese Coffee Tasting Experience One souvenir per room Bali Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple For Sunset Enjoy Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject To Weather Conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance Hanoi Guided City Tour Of Hanoi Photo Stop At Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum Photo Stop At One Pillar Pagoda Experience Cyclo Tour Ride Visit Hoan Kiem Lake Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay Overnight Stay On Ha Long Bay / Lan Ha Bay On Cruise Activities Tai Chi Training, Cooking Classes, Kayaking (Subject To Availability, Cruise Type & Weather Conditions) Da Nang Visit Cam Thanh Coconut Village Enjoy Basket Boat Ride At Cam Thanh Village Visit Hoi An Ancient Town Enjoy Boat Ride With Lantern Releasing Day Excursion To Bana Hills By Cable Car Visit Golden Bridge Visit French Gardens Visit French Quarters Visit St. Denis Church Visit Indoor Fantasy Park (Wax Museum Not Included) Photo Stop At Dragon Bridge.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZBV660', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Vietnam With Bali (Winter)' package is a 10-day tour covering Bali, Da Nang, Hanoi, and Ha Long Bay. This air-inclusive tour features four-star accommodations, dedicated tour manager assistance, and specially curated Indian meals. Throughout the journey, participants will enjoy thrilling water sports, the famous Bali Swing, and visits to the Tanah Lot and Uluwatu Temples in Bali. In Hanoi, guests will experience a traditional cyclo ride, a guided city tour, and an overnight cruise on Ha Long Bay with activities like Tai Chi and kayaking. The adventure concludes in Da Nang with a basket boat ride at Cam Thanh Village, a lantern-releasing boat ride in Hoi An, and a scenic cable car ride to Ba Na Hills to visit the iconic Golden Bridge and French Quarters.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival in Bali - Check In\nWelcome to Bali, Indonesia, one of the most famous destinations in the world for holidays and packages. Upon arrival at the Denpasar airport, you will be met by our representative/ Tour Manager who will assist you for your transfer to the hotel.\nOn arrival in Bali, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure.\n\xa0\nNote:\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nExperience Bali Swing - Tanah Lot Sunset Tour\nPost breakfast, proceed for an exciting swing, the most famous Bali Swing.\nLater arrive at Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset – An ancient Hindu shrine.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nDay at Leisure Or Optional Tour of Nusa Penida\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, day is at leisure.\xa0\nSpend rest of the day exploring Bali on your own OR you can explore Nusa Penida Island\nOPTIONAL EXCURSION: Full Day Nusa Penida Tour inclusive of Angel Billabong, Broken Beach, Kelingking Beach with Lunch (Set Menu) at USD 45 per person (Minimum 2 Pax Required)\nJoin Day Tour of Nusa Penida, where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point, the natural pool of Angel's Billabong.\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nWater Sports At Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\nAfter breakfast, proceed to the Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski.\n(**Parasailing subjected to weather conditions)\nLater proceed for Uluwatu Temple Tour; located at 70-meter-high cliff. Later this evening enjoy the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Hanoi – Day at Leisure\nThis morning after breakfast proceed to Denpasar airport for the flight to Hanoi. Later we proceed to the hotel and check in. (Standard check in time 1500 hrs).\nRest of the day at leisure.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': '\nHotel Sen Grand / Army / Grand View or similar in Hanoi'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0Hanoi – Ha Long Bay – Overnight on Cruise - Visit Pearl Farm Enroute Ha Long Bay\nThis morning after breakfast, we check out and proceed to Ha Long. Enroute visit Pearl Farm. Upon arrival in Ha Long, check in at the overnight cruise.\xa0 As we sail on the Ha Long bay we visit Surprise Caves & Ti Top Island - enjoy free time at the beach or walk up the hill to enjoy a view of Ha Long Bay.\nLater enjoy sunset view from sundeck.\nOR\nHanoi – Lan Ha Bay – Overnight on Cruise\nThis morning after breakfast, we check out and proceed to Lan Ha Bay. Upon Arrival in Lan Ha Bay, check in at the Overnight Cruise.\xa0 As we sail on the Lan Ha Bay, we visit Dark & Bright Cave (Hang Sang & Toi) - Enjoy free time at the beach or enjoy a view of Lan Ha Bay.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Local Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Golden Cruise / La Regina Royal Cruise /Aqua Legend/ Aqua Elegance or similar in Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nSail on Ha Long Bay – Drive to Hanoi - Guided City Tour of Hanoi - Enjoy Cyclo Tour\nThis morning after breakfast, we visit Luon Cave by boat - enjoy kayaking or wooden boat ride through the cave. Enjoy brunch on board the Cruise\nReturn to Halong Wharf and transfer back to Hanoi.\n(Note: The cruise itinerary can be changed according to weather conditions.)\nUpon arrival, we proceed on the city tour - See Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum from outside. Visit One Pillar Pagoda followed by a cyclo ride around the Old Quarter of Hanoi. Later enjoy photostop at Hoan Kiem Lake.\nOR\nSail On Lan Ha Bay – Drive to Hanoi - Guided City Tour of Hanoi - Enjoy Cyclo Tour\nThis Morning After Breakfast, Enjoy sunrise photograph and brunch on board the cruise\nReturn to Tuan Chau Harbor and transfer back to Hanoi.\n(Note: The cruise itinerary can be changed according to the cruise / weather conditions.)\nUpon arrival, we proceed on the city tour - See Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum from outside. Visit One Pillar Pagoda followed by a cyclo ride around the Old Quarter of Hanoi. Later enjoy photostop at Hoan Kiem Lake.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Brunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Sen Grand / Army / Grand View or similar in Hanoi'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Da Nang - Visit Cam Thanh Village – Enjoy Basket Boat Ride at Cam Thanh Village - Visit Hoi An Ancient Town - Experience Boat Ride with Lantern Releasing\nThis morning after breakfast, we check out and proceed to the airport for our flight to Da Nang.\nUpon arrival, transfer from the airport to the hotel for check in. (Standard check in time 1500 hrs).\nLater visit Cam Thanh Village. Enjoy a basket boat ride through the coconut jungle forest. Visit Hoi An ancient town - see the tile-roofed Japanese Bridge, Chinese Assembly halls and ancient houses followed by a boat ride with lantern releasing on the river.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Yarra Ocean / Mandila Beach Hotel / Bluesun Hotel\xa0 or similar in Da Nang'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Excursion to Ba Na Hills - Visit Golden Bridge - Photo Stop at Dragon Bridge\nThis morning after breakfast, we proceed to Ba Na hills. On arrival take a Cable Car to Ba Na hills station. Visit Golden Bridge followed by visit the Old Villas, French Stable, and Tinh Tam Garden. See the Linh Ung Pagoda. Visit Loc Uyen Garden and Quan Am Pavilion. Our next stop will be the Fantasy Park, an amusement park.\nLater this evening proceed for a photo stop at Dragon Bridge.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, International Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Yarra Ocean / Mandila Beach Hotel / Bluesun Hotel\xa0 or similar in Da Nang'}, {'day': 10, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd of Tour - Fly Back\nThis morning after breakfast, check out and proceed to the Airport. Return home with wonderful memories of your tour.\n\xa0\n* The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice. Final Itinerary will be handed over on the day of arrival.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n04 Night accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n01 Night accommodation at Golden Cruise / La Regina Royal Cruise /Aqua Legend/ Aqua Elegance or similar in Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Yarra Ocean / Mandila Beach Hotel / Bluesun Hotel\xa0 or similar in Da Nang\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n04 Night accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n01 Night accommodation at Golden Cruise / La Regina Royal Cruise /Aqua Legend/ Aqua Elegance or similar in Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Yarra Ocean / Mandila Beach Hotel / Bluesun Hotel\xa0 or similar in Da Nang\n', '2': '\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'VN', 'countryName': 'Vietnam', 'continentName': 'Asia'}, {'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 193900.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 Night accommodation at Hotel Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island or similar in Kuta, Bali\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n01 Night accommodation at Golden Cruise / La Regina Royal Cruise /Aqua Legend/ Aqua Elegance or similar in Halong Bay / Lan Ha Bay\n01 Night accommodation at Sen Grand Hotel / Army Hotel / Grand View or similar in Hanoi\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Yarra Ocean / Mandila Beach Hotel / Bluesun Hotel\xa0 or similar in Da Nang\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily buffet / packed breakfast (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 International buffet Lunch\n08 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n1 Lunch, 1 Dinner and 1 Brunch onboard Cruise\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n\xa0\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch/ IL/D - International Lunch/Dinner / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n**Depending on Flight timings Packed Meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) will be provided instead of Sitting Meals at Indian / Local Restaurant.\n**Lunches are not included in Bali Portion'], 'visa': ['\nVietnam E-visa included in the package.\nIndonesia Visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 30 April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\nAll foreign nationals and overseas Vietnamese entering with a visa must complete the digital arrival card prior to immigration clearance.\nTravelers can fill out the form by scanning a QR code upon arrival at international airports or, preferably, by completing it in advance online at https://prearrival.immigration.gov.vn/ to save time.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Bali\n\nExperience Bali Swing\nVisit Tanah Lot Floating Temple For Sunset\nEnjoy Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject To Weather Conditions)\xa0\nVisit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\n\nHanoi\n\nGuided City Tour Of Hanoi\xa0\nPhoto Stop At Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum\nPhoto Stop At One Pillar Pagoda\nExperience Cyclo Tour Ride\nVisit Hoan Kiem Lake\n\nHalong Bay / Lan Ha Bay\n\nOvernight Stay On Ha Long Bay / Lan Ha Bay\nOn Cruise Activities Tai Chi Training, Cooking Classes, Kayaking (Subject To Availability, Cruise Type & Weather Conditions)\n\nDa Nang\n\nVisit Cam Thanh Coconut Village\nEnjoy Basket Boat Ride At Cam Thanh Village\nVisit Hoi An Ancient Town\nEnjoy Boat Ride With Lantern Releasing\nDay Excursion To Bana Hills By Cable Car\nVisit Golden Bridge\nVisit French Gardens\nVisit French Quarters\nVisit St. Denis Church\nVisit Indoor Fantasy Park (Wax Museum Not Included)\nPhoto Stop At Dragon Bridge\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n<li>Internal airfare for Bali &ndash; Hanoi, Hanoi-Da Nang is included for Joining Direct &amp; NRI passengers</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class airfare as per the itinerary.\nInternal airfare for Bali – Hanoi, Hanoi- Da Nang is included for Joining Direct & NRI passengers\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nVietnam Visa & Airport taxes (Any further increase in the same must be borne by the guest).\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 30 April 2026\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\nAirport transfers from all airports.\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative.\xa0\nIf groups size is less than 15 customers than the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\n\n\xa0\nVisa Requirements:\n\nVietnam E-visa included in the package.\nIndonesia Visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 30 April 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\nAll foreign nationals and overseas Vietnamese entering with a visa must complete the digital arrival card prior to immigration clearance.\nTravelers can fill out the form by scanning a QR code upon arrival at international airports or, preferably, by completing it in advance online at https://prearrival.immigration.gov.vn/ to save time.\n', 'exclusions': '\nCompulsory tips for tour guide and driver: USD 5 per person per day\nIndonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 30 April 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nPorterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'General Information:\nAll travelers while returning to India should submit a self-declaration form (mandatory) on the online Air Suvidha portal\xa0(www.newdelhiairport.in)\xa0before the scheduled travel, including the last 14 days of travel details. Each passenger shall also submit a declaration with respect to the authenticity of the report and will be liable for criminal prosecution if found otherwise.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/Bali26789.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/BaliSwing.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/Tanah_Lot_Temple_New_Bali_&53.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/Nusa_Penida_New_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/KeckDanace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/HoChiMinh753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/HalongBayCruise753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/AdobeStock_296902787_One_Pillar_pagoda_in_Hanoi.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/HoiAn753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/GoldenbridgeDanang753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014873/itinerary/Danang7538.jpg']}, 'score': 9.441795, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012813', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012813', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Simply Bali 6N Fully Loaded', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Kokat Swing with local Lunch 02 Hour Spa Bounty cruise Complimentary 1xParasailing Or 1X Flying Fish during the water sports activities Complimentary welcome gift on arrival Complimentary 01 bottle of Mineral Water on arrival'], 'pdfName': 'PKG012813_0_20261009171624', 'price': 65715, 'packageSummary': "The 'Simply Bali 6N Fully Loaded' package is a 7-day tour covering the beautiful destinations of Bali and Kuta. The itinerary features a variety of exciting activities, including a thrilling Kokat Swing experience paired with a local lunch, a relaxing two-hour spa treatment, and a scenic Bounty cruise. Participants will also enjoy water sports with a complimentary choice of either parasailing or a flying fish ride, alongside welcoming touches such as a complimentary gift and a bottle of mineral water upon arrival.", 'images': ['Bali_Scenic_7531.jpg', 'Ubud.jpg', 'BaliSwing.jpg', 'Tanah_Lot_Temple_New_Bali_&53.jpg', 'Bali_Sunset_753.jpg', 'KeckDanace.jpg', 'Bali1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 65715, 'thumbnailImage': 'BaliFully267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family', 'Couple Special'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG012813 is named 'Simply Bali 6N Fully Loaded' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuta, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive at Bali (PVT basis) Welcome to Bali – Arrival at the Ngurah Rai, Bali International Airport, meet & greet by our local guide who led you to the parking area to board on vehicle for your transfer to your hotel. It takes about 20 minutes’ drive from airport to your hotel or more depending on the traffic. Upon arrival at the hotel, directly check in and freshen up., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full Day Kintamani Hot Spring & Ubud village Tour (PVT Basis) Pick up for Celuk Silver Art Village Celuk Village is a traditional village which famous for the incredible gold and silver handicrafts are available around this area for very low prices. As you enter the neighborhood, you're going to feel as if you were in a jewelry exhibition. On either side of the road are established many art shops showcasing their finest works inside a glass display case. We will visit one of the best gold and silver art works in celuk village. You can take a closer look at them to appreciate it and buy some if you really like it or you can made custom jewelry based on your design. Visit Mas Wooden Carved Art Village Mas Village is one of traditional villages in Bali fundamentally as an artistic countryside by focusing the art of wood carving. This village is famous in the island as Bali Wood Carving Center located in Ubud sub district and Gianyar Regency. It owns the typical style of wood carving art by placing forward the distinguish synergy of the humanism and naturalism Visit Kintamani Hot Spring Kintamani Hot Spring features eight natural hot spring pools and one warm olympic sized pool. Heated deep within the earth, minerals from the colorless and odorless hot spring brings healing and curative powers. Enjoy a relaxing dip with the majestic panorama! *Inclusions: Natural Hot Spring Pools, Toya Water Slide with Tubes, Towel & Locker, Change & Shower Room, Facility, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner, Description: Full Day Kokat Bali Swing with Local Lunch & 02 Hrs Spa Treatment (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. When in UBUD, Bali, one of the best points of interest not to miss is Bali Swing. Take your loved ones for a thrilling yet exciting ride on the tandem swing, or if you want to feel the sensation of flying by yourself, try the single swing that goes up to 60 meters above ground. Make your trip even more unforgettable by taking pictures in various unique photo spots available, such as adorable birds nest you can sit in ! Later enjoy the local Lunch at Bali Swing Pioneer. Proceed to spoil yourself and soothe your body and mind with our selected Balinese Massage Treatment. Using local herbs and spices along with aromatic oil, we offer a wide range of spa package including specialist treatments, facials body and foot scrub so that you can relax and escape from the stress and pressure of daily life., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Royal Taman Ayun & Tanah Lot Tour (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Taman Ayun Temple or Pura Taman Ayun is a magnificent family temple of Mengwi empire. This one of the most visited temple in Bali, both local & Foreign tourist. Taman Ayun Temple is also one of six royal temples in Bali making it very important both spiritually and historically. This temple’s name Taman Ayun translates to the “ Garden Temple in the Water”. Tanah Lot Temple is one of the most popular Bali Places of Interest and its an ancient Hindu Shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves, the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons. The onshore site is dotted with smaller shrines alongside visitors leisure facilities that compromise restaurants, Shops and cultural park presenting regular dance performances. The temple is located in the Beraban village of the Tabanan regency, an approximate 20 km northwest of Kuta and is included on most tours to Bali western and central regions. Return to hotel post the tour and spend the overnight in Bali., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half Day Water Sports with Uluwatu Temple Tour Followed by Kecak Dance (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Enjoy the Salty Air! Sandy Hair! Feel the tropical breeze and get closer to Indian Ocean with selected water sport activity. 1 x Jet Ski & Banana Boat Ride and Complimentary 1 x Parasailing Later proceed Uluwatu Temple sits on 70 meter high cliff protruding above Indonesian Ocean. The main site of Uluwatu Tours is visiting this temple. There are hundreds of monkeys roaming along the path outside temple. A small forest lies at the front and hundreds of monkey’s dwells here. They are believed to guard the temple from bad influence. The Serpentine pathway to the temple is fortified by concrete walls on the cliff sides. When sun goes down, we will witness the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’. Kecak dance is that the accompanying music is provided by the human voice, the gamelan suara, a choir of a hundred men or more sitting in concentric circle, swaying, standing up, lying prone as the story develops. Amongst the swaying masses the voices of the storytellers can be heard telling the unfolding tale. The music generated from a combination sounds of members cak which were about 50 – 70 people all of them will make music in acapella. Return to hotel post the tour and spend the overnight in Bali., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Bounty Cruise on Private Basis Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel Spend an unforgettable evening cruise on Bounty Dinner Cruise, Bali. Take in a breathtaking view of the sunset over Tanjung Benoa. Enjoy a delicious international buffet dinner with your loved ones. Watch various interactive performances, such as a traditional Balinese dance, comedy number and DJ performance. Return to hotel post the tour and spend the overnight in Bali., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart from Kuta Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. * The itinerary is tentative and subject to change without prior notice. Extension Nights: Travel Validity: 01 Oct 2026 – 24 Mar 2027 CATEGORY HOTELS PACKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN USD SINGLE TWIN /DOUBLE TRIPLE CHILDWITH BED CHILDNO BED STANDARD The Legian Paradiso or similar USD 35 USD 20 USD 20 USD 10 USD 10 VALUE Swiss Belcourt Seminyak /Fairfield Seminyak Or Similar USD 60 USD 30 USD 30 USD 20 USD 20 PREMIUM Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso or Similar USD 105 USD 52 USD 50 USD 30 USD 30, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 65715.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n6 Night's Hotel\xa0Swiss Belcourt\xa0 Seminyak /\xa0Fairfield Seminyak\xa0Or Similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n, \nHotel\xa0Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso or Similar in Kuta, Bali\n, \nHotel The Legian Paradiso or similar in Kuta, Bali\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 06 night’s accommodation with breakfast Return Airport Transfers on Private basis Meet & Greet assistance at the airport Full Day Kintamani Tour with Hot Spring, Ubud Village On Private Basis. Full Day Tour – Kokat Swing with local Lunch followed 02 Hour Spa followed by Bounty cruise on Pvt Basis. Full Day Taman Ayu Temple Tour followed by Tanah Lot Temple tour Half Day Water Sports (1xJet Ski & 1xBanana Boat) Followed by Uluwatu Temple Tour with Kecak Dance Complimentary 1xParasailing Or 1X Flying Fish during the water sports activities Return airport transfers on private basis Complimentary welcome gift on arrival Complimentary 01 bottle of Mineral Water on arrival Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) the charges are approximately USD 35-40 per person. Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights service Meals not mentioned in the itinerary. Any tips for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions. Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge Blackout Dates: Christmas & New year - 15th Dec'2026 to 10th Jan'2027 & 01st Mar 2027 – 11 Mar 2027 Nyepi Day The rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling. Visa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) the charges are approximately USD 35-40 per person.. Product Terms and Conditions: Package Terms and Conditions: The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling. During Peak Season: Minimum 2 Nights Stay is required No Check Out period on New Year Period Nyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 19 March 2026. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 19 March 2026 to 06.00 am 20 March 2026 Compulsory New Year Dinner will be Applicable according to the Resort The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: Kokat Swing with local Lunch 02 Hour Spa Bounty cruise Complimentary 1xParasailing Or 1X Flying Fish during the water sports activities Complimentary welcome gift on arrival Complimentary 01 bottle of Mineral Water on arrival.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '',