ry the single swing that goes up to 60 meters above ground. Make your trip even more unforgettable by taking pictures in various unique photo spots available, such as adorable birds nest you can sit in !\nLater enjoy the local Lunch at Bali Swing Pioneer.\nProceed to spoil yourself and soothe your body and mind with our selected Balinese Massage Treatment. Using local herbs and spices along with aromatic oil, we offer a wide range of spa package including specialist treatments, facials body and foot scrub so that you can relax and escape from the stress and pressure of daily life.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Local Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotels -\xa0The Legian Paradiso\xa0(Standard) /\xa0Swiss Belcourt Seminyak or\xa0Fairfield Seminyak (Value) /\xa0Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso (Premium)\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nRoyal Taman Ayun & Tanah Lot Tour (PVT Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast in Hotel.\nTaman Ayun Temple or Pura Taman Ayun is a magnificent family temple of Mengwi empire. This one of the most visited temple in Bali, both local & Foreign tourist. Taman Ayun Temple is also one of six royal temples in Bali making it very important both spiritually and historically. This temple’s name Taman Ayun translates to the “ Garden\xa0 Temple in the Water”.\n\xa0\nTanah Lot Temple\xa0 is one of the most popular Bali Places of Interest and its an ancient Hindu Shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves, the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons. The onshore site is dotted with smaller shrines alongside visitors leisure facilities that compromise restaurants, Shops and cultural park presenting regular dance performances. The temple is located in the Beraban village of the Tabanan regency, an approximate 20 km northwest of Kuta and is included on most tours to Bali western and central regions.\n\xa0\nReturn to hotel post the tour and spend the overnight in Bali.', 'mealDesc