rary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Zagreb\nTransfers: Upon your arrival at Zagreb airport, you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis.\n\xa0\nWalking Tour of Zagreb: Explore Zagreb’s highlights on a guided walking tour with a scenic funicular ride. Discover the charm of both Lower and Upper Town, uncover hidden gems, and hear the stories that shaped Croatia’s vibrant capital.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Laguna (Standard)//\xa0Hotel AS (Value)//\xa0Hotel Sheraton (Premium) or similar in Zagreb'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nDay Free At Leisure\nOptional Day Trip To Slovenia on SIC Basis: Enjoy a free day or take an optional trip to Slovenia. Visit the charming capital Ljubljana, then escape into nature at Lake Bled, famous for its scenic lake and hilltop castle—an unforgettable getaway from Zagreb.\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nYou need to be in possession of a multiple entry Schengen visa to visit Slovenia.\nSightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Laguna (Standard)//\xa0Hotel AS (Value)//\xa0Hotel Sheraton (Premium) or similar in Zagreb'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nZagreb - Zadar | Enroute Plitvice National Park |\n\xa0\nTransfers:\xa0\n\nThis morning travel to Zadar, enroute visit Plitvice National Park.\nLater continue your journey to Zadar\n\n\xa0\nPlitvice National Park: Plitvice National Park dazzles with waterfalls, lakes, and forested cliffs. Your ticket includes full access to trails and boardwalks, a panoramic train ride, shuttle buses between lakes, and an electric boat cruise on Kozjak Lake.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': "Hotel A'mare (Standard)//Falkensteiner Club Funimation Borik (Value)//Miramare Hotel (Premium) or similar in Zadar\n\xa0\n\xa0"}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nWalking Tour of Zadar |\xa0Zadar - Split\xa0\n\xa0\nTransfers: Today you will travel from Zadar to Split by bus on shared basis.\n\xa0\nWalking Tour of Zadar:\xa0 Enjoy a guided walking tour of Zadar’s Old City, including St. Donat, St. Anastasia, city gates, walls, and the Square of Five Wells. Sample Maraschino liqueur and Pag cheese, then relax by the Sea Organ and admire the sunset.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note: Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Jadrran (Standard)//Hotel Fanat (Value)//Cornaro\xa0(Premium) or similar in Split'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour | Walking Tour of Split\n\xa0\nBlue Lagoon – 3 Island Tour:\xa0 Enjoy a relaxing Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour, visiting UNESCO listed Trogir, the Blue Lagoon, and Šolta’s Stomorska village for swimming and exploring. You can also take a Blue Cave 5 Island Tour to Biševo, Vis, Pakleni, Hvar and Brac\xa0for stunning views and swims.\n\xa0\nWalking Tour of Split:\xa0 Enjoy an evening walking tour of Split and explore the 1700 year old Diocletian’s Palace. See St. Domnius Cathedral, the Peristil, Golden Gate, and Gregory of Nin. End with the 24 hour sun clock at City Square and the Riva promenade.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nYou have an opportunity to upgrade your Blue Lagoon and Guided walking tour of Split to a full-day Blue Cave Tour at an additional cost.\nSightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Jadrran (Standard)//Hotel Fanat (Value)//Cornaro\xa0(Premium) or similar in Split'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nSplit – Dubrovnik | Walking Tour of Dubrovnik |\n\xa0\nTransfers: Today you will travel from Split to Dubrovnik by bus on shared basis.\n\xa0\nWalking Tour of Dubrovnik: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Dubrovnik and a Cable Car ride. Explore the Old Town’s history, architecture, and culture, then ride to the top of Srd Hill for stunning views of the Adriatic Sea and the city below.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nSightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\nYou can opt for a Sunset Dinner Cruise (Dalmatian Cuisine) at a supplement cost\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Vis (Standard)//Hotel Lero (Value)//Hotel President (Premium) in Dubrovnik'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nTrip To Bosnia & Herzegovina\nTrip to Bosnia & Herzegovina: Explore Bosnia and Herzegovina on a day trip and visit UNESCO listed Mostar. Wander cobbled streets, see Ottoman era mosques and bathhouses, and admire the iconic Stari Most—one of the modern world’s most remarkable bridges.\n\xa0\nSpecial Note:\xa0\n\nGuest should be carrying their passport with valid Schengen Visa.\nSightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Vis (Standard)//Hotel Lero (Value)//Hotel President (Premium) in Dubrovnik'}, {'day': 8, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\nTransfers: You will have a private transfer from Dubrovnik hotel to Dubrovnik Airport\nDo spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\n\nCity\n\nHotels\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel Sheraton, Hotel Esplanade Zagreb, Hotel Westin or Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nMiramare Hotel, Teatro Verdi Boutique Hotel, Hotel Bastion or Similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nCornaro Hotel, Radisson Blu Resort & Spa, Hotel Ambasador or Si