r higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nWe are not holding any Hotel blocks for this package.\nInternational Check in time is 1500 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and check-out is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges and from specific airports only.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies and may be from designated points. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on weather conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients travelling during weekends.\nOffer can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. The said organisation would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\nThe organisation will not be responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organisation.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/Split_SRP.png', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Zagerb.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/ZAGRAB-CROATIA_(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Plitvice-Lakes-National-Park-1_(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/split.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/croatia-Split_2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/dubrovnik_2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Elaphiti_Islands.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014763/itinerary/Dubrovnik.jpg']}, 'score': 7.7708406, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014796', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014796', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Impressive Croatia', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Zagreb', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zagreb', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Plitvice Lakes', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Zadar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Split', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Split', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubrovnik', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG014796_0_20260515160359.pdf', 'price': 156802, 'packageSummary': "The 'Impressive Croatia' package is a 9-day tour covering Zagreb, Dubrovnik, Plitvice Lakes, Zadar, and Split. The itinerary includes visits to the historic Old Towns, the breathtaking Plitvice Lakes National Park, the ancient Roman Diocletian's Palace, and the famous city walls of Dubrovnik. Participants will enjoy guided walking tours, scenic coastal drives, and opportunities to explore beautiful Adriatic beaches and local cultural landmarks.", 'images': ['Zagerb.jpg', 'ZAGRAB-CROATIA.jpg', 'Plitvice-Lakes-National-Park-1.jpg', 'ZADAR-c.jpg', 'croatia-Split.jpg', 'Diocletians.jpg', 'Dubrovnik (1).jpg', 'DUBROVNIK-para.jpg', 'Croatia-Dubrovnik.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 156802, 'thumbnailImage': 'Zagreb_SRP.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014796 is named 'Impressive Croatia' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Zagreb, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive Zagreb Transfers: Upon your arrival at Zagreb airport, you will be transferred to the hotel on private basis. Walking Tour of Zagreb: Explore Zagreb's highlights on a guided walking tour with a scenic funicular ride. Discover the charm of both Lower and Upper Town, uncover hidden gems, and hear the stories that shaped Croatia's vibrant capital. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Zagreb, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day Free At Leisure Optional Day Trip to Slovenia on SIC Basis: Enjoy a free day or take an optional trip to Slovenia. Visit the charming capital Ljubljana, then escape into nature at Lake Bled, famous for its scenic lake and hilltop castle - an unforgettable getaway from Zagreb. Special Note: 1. You need to be in possession of a multiple entry Schengen visa to visit Slovenia. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Plitvice Lakes, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zagreb - Plitvice | Visit Plitvice National Park Transfers: Today you will travel from Zagreb to Plitvice by bus on shared basis. Visit Plitvice National Park: Travel to Plitvice and check into your hotel. Explore Plitvice National Park, famous for its stunning waterfalls, lakes, and forested cliffs. Enjoy access to hiking trails, boardwalks, a panoramic train, shuttle buses, and a boat ride on Lake Kozjak. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Zadar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Plitvice - Zadar | Walking Tour Of Zadar Transfers: Today you will travel from Plitvice to Zadar by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Zadar: Enjoy a guided walking tour of Zadar's Old City, including St. Donat, St. Anastasia, city gates, walls, and the Square of Five Wells. Sample Maraschino liqueur and Pag cheese, then relax by the Sea Organ and admire the sunset. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only. 2. You can opt for a Romantic Sunset Cruise at a supplement cost, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Split, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Zadar - Split | Walking Tour Of Split Transfers: Today you will travel from Zadar to Split by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Split: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Split and explore the 1700 year old Diocletian’s Palace. See St. Domnius Cathedral, the Peristil, Golden Gate, and Gregory of Nin. End with the 24 hour sun clock at City Square and the Riva promenade. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Split, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Blue Lagoon - 3 Island Tour Blue Lagoon - 3 Island Tour: Enjoy a relaxing Blue Lagoon 3 Island Tour, visiting UNESCO listed Trogir, the Blue Lagoon, and Solta's Stomorska village for swimming and exploring. You can also take a Blue Cave 5 Island Tour to Biševo, Vis, Pakleni, Hvar and Brac for stunning views and swims. Special Note: 1. You have an opportunity to upgrade your Blue Lagoon tour to a full day Blue Cave Tour at an additional cost. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Split - Dubrovnik| Walking Tour Of Dubrovnik Transfers: Today you will travel from Split to Dubrovnik by bus on shared basis. Walking Tour of Dubrovnik: Enjoy an evening walking tour of Dubrovnik and a Cable Car ride. Explore the Old Town’s history, architecture, and culture, then ride to the top of Srd Hill for stunning views of the Adriatic Sea and the city below. Special Note: 1. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Trip To Bosnia & Herzegovina Trip to Bosnia & Herzegovina: Explore Bosnia and Herzegovina on a day trip and visit UNESCO listed Mostar. Wander cobbled streets, see Ottoman era mosques and bathhouses, and admire the iconic Stari Most - one of the modern world's most remarkable bridges. Special Note: 1. Guest should be carrying their passport with valid Schengen Visa. 2. Sightseeing will be conducted on a shared basis, with pickups arranged from designated central meeting points only., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Dubrovnik, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Transfers: You will have a private transfer from Dubrovnik hotel to Dubrovnik Airport. Do spare a few minutes to share your feedback with our representative or via email - as your valued suggestions will be most appreciated. Arrive home with pleasant memories of your overseas tour, which we are sure you will treasure for a lifetime., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 156802.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\n\nCity\xa0\n\n\nHotels\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0Sheraton,\xa0Hotel\xa0Esplanade\xa0Zagreb,\xa0Hotel\xa0Westin\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nFenomen\xa0Plitvice\xa0Resort\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nMiramare\xa0Hotel,\xa0Teatro\xa0Verdi\xa0Boutique\xa0Hotel\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nRadisson\xa0Blu\xa0Resort\xa0&\xa0Spa,\xa0Hotel\xa0Ambasador\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0President,\xa0hotel\xa0Sun\xa0Gardens,\xa0Hotel\xa0Hilton\xa0Imperial\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nCity\n\n\nVALUE\xa0\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0AS,\xa0Hotel\xa0Dubrovnik,\xa0Canopy\xa0by\xa0Hilton\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nEthno\xa0Houses\xa0Plitvice\xa0Lakes\xa0Hotel,\xa0Lyra\xa0Hotel\xa0Plitvice\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nFalkensteiner\xa0Club\xa0Funimation\xa0Borik,\xa0Hotel\xa0Kolovare\xa0or\xa0Similar\xa0\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nHotel\xa0Fanat,\xa0Hotel\xa0Globo,\xa0Hotel\xa0Cora\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0Lero,\xa0Hotel\xa0Valamar\xa0Lacroma,\xa0Hotel\xa0Lapad\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n, \n\n\n\nCity\xa0Name\n\n\nSTANDARD\xa0CATEGORY\n\n\n\n\nZagreb\n\n\nHotel\xa0Laguna,\xa0Hotel\xa0Central\xa0or\xa0Similar\n\n\n\n\nPlitvice\n\n\nHotel\xa0Plitvice,\xa0Hotel\xa0Jezero\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nZadar\n\n\nA'mare\xa0Hotel\xa0Zadar,\xa0Hotel\xa0Mediteran,\xa0Hotel\xa0Sky\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nSplit\n\n\nHotel\xa0Jadrran,\xa0hotel\xa0AS\xa0Hotel\xa0Batuda\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n\nDubrovnik\n\n\nHotel\xa0Vis,\xa0Hotel\xa0Komodor,\xa0Hotel\xa0Dubrovnik\xa0or\xa0similar\n\n\n\n. Meals include: \nDaily Breakfast *(Except Day 1)\n. Inclusions: Accommodation: 2 Nights accommodation in Zagreb based on the hotel category selected or similar 1 Night accommodation in Plitvice based on the hotel category sel