l be applicable for all bookings and to be borne by the customer.\n", 'termsAndConditions': '\nThe prices will not be valid for any block out date/ period which is informed during confirmation of the booking; if any change in the price, the same will be applicable for all bookings and to be borne by the customer.\n\n\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same.\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTC is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TC would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/ExploreBali267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/Bali1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/BannanaBoat.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/NusaPenida753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/Nusa_Penida_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/Bali12.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/Bali7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013788/itinerary/bali_shutterstock_521467954.jpg']}, 'score': 5.060468, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012546', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012546', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Pristine Bali', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG009597_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 30304, 'packageSummary': "The 'Pristine Bali' package is a 7-day tour covering the vibrant coastal town of Kuta and the cultural heart of Ubud. The itinerary includes visits to the sacred Ubud Monkey Forest, the breathtaking Tegallalang Rice Terraces, and iconic sea temples like Tanah Lot. Participants will enjoy relaxing on pristine beaches, watching traditional Balinese dance performances, exploring local art markets, and experiencing guided cultural tours throughout these beautiful destinations.", 'images': ['Bali1.jpg', 'BannanaBoat.jpg', 'MountBatur753.jpg', 'TanahLotTemple75345.jpg', 'Bali12.jpg', 'Bali7531.jpg', 'Bali75390.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 30304, 'thumbnailImage': 'Bali26709.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Durga Puja Special', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG012546 is named 'Pristine Bali' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuta, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrival at the Ngurah Rai, Bali International Airport, meet & greet by our local guide who lead you to the parking area to board on vehicle for your transfer to your hotel. It takes about 20 minutes’ drive from airport to your hotel or more depending on the traffic. Upon arrival at the hotel, directly check in and freshen up., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half Day Benoa Beach Tour including Banana Boat followed by Half Day Sunset Uluwatu Temple on private basis Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel An ideal Bali holiday is incomplete without water sports & what better than the famous Tanjung Benoa beach. This beach, best known for its aquatic adventure, is located in the Benoa peninsula far away from the hustle & bustle. Please check with our representatives for all the water sports information. Many shacks & restaurants lined up along the beach make sure that your tummy is full & you enjoy yourself the most. Later in the afternoon they proceed to the southern tip of Bali for the Uluwatu Sunset tour. Uluwatu Temple, or Pura Luhur Uluwatu, is renowned for its magnificent location, perched on top of a steep cliff approximately 70 meters above the waves. As one of the 6 key temples considered to be Bali's spiritual pillars, Uluwatu also offers a splendid sunset backdrop. It is one of the top places in Bali for witnessing a delightful sunset, with direct views overlooking the beautiful waves of the Indian Ocean. Note:- Children below 10 years of age are not permitted to participate in water sports, rafting, swing, spa, or ATV activities. For this age group, only entrance tickets are included; participation in activities is not applicable., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Kuta Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Day free for leisure and to explore the city on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Ubud, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Transfer from Kuta to Ubud. Full Day Kintamani Tour with Ubud Village followed by Sunset Tanah Lot Temple on Private Basis Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Inter Hotel Transfer Kuta Hotel to Ubud Hotel. Enroute visit to Kintamani Volcano is a rare opportunity to experience one of Bali’s last remaining active volcanos up close. This is one of the most popular and best day trip in Bali. The tour begins with the sights of a vibrant art village. Here you can meet with the people who keep the techniques of the regions handicrafts alive with a stop at Tohpati village, widely known as the centre of handmade Balinese Batik weaving. Next stop is Celuk village famous for producing high-grade gold and silver handicrafts. Continue trip to Mas Village, one of the many artists villages surrounding Ubud, is the best place on the island to find high-quality Balinese woodcarvings, considered some of the best woodcarvings in the world Evening enjoy Tanah Lot Temple, locally known as Pura Tanah Lot is probably the most popular and photographed temple on the island, located on the coastal side of Beraban countryside, Kediri sub district and Tabanan Regency. Tanah Lot Temple stands for Earth (Tanah) and Sea (Lot), quite appropriate considering its spectacular setting on top of an impressive rock overlooking the Indian Ocean. This cultural icon is among the seven sea temples located in the coast of Bali and has been contained in Balinese mythology for centuries., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Ubud, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ubud Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Day free for leisure and to explore the city on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ubud, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ubud Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Day free for leisure and to explore the city on your own., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Ubud, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Pick up from the hotel to transfer to the Airport according to the scheduled Flight. * The itinerary is tentative and subjected to change withou