Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny Air or Rail fare.\nAny other meal not mentioned in price includes.\nAny other destination not mentioned in itinerary.\nAny monument entrance fees, camera fees, guide charges.\nAny expenses of personal nature.\nGST @ Current Rate\n\n\xa0\n\xa0\n\n\n\n\xa0SUPPLEMENT\nSTANDARD\nVALUE\nPREMIUM\n\n\nUpgrade from Sedan to MUV [Per Vehicle]\n7875\n7875\n7875\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n\nBASICS\n\n\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines\nSeats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAll domestic Hotels/Transport rates are based on current tariff & subject to change without prior notification; the revised rates will be charged extra.\n\nHOTELS\n\nMany regions do not have star category hotels. Generally there isn’t any star categorization in this sector, however the same is demarcated as per prices and put into slabs of 2*/ 3*/ 4*or STD/ DLX/ PRM or equivalent.\nPackages are based on base category rooms, irrespective of the Hotel category opted.\nQuote based on Non-Ac Rooms on Hills. AC Rooms on Extra Charges\nPlease be reminded that all special requests like early check-in, smoking, non-smoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll over Extra mattress on floor provided where proper extra bed isn’t available.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out.\nIn hills, hotels may be located in a way where the view might be of a building in the front, beside or behind it. There will not be any refund in cased any of the sightseeing is missed/uncovered during the trip.\nThe Hotels may/may not have some of following amenities as per its policy. Tea/coffee maker/ mini fridge/ enhanced toiletry kit (with moisturizer, tooth paste, brush, shaving kit, lufa, bathroom sleepers, bath-robe) etc.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis and not on A-la-Carte basis. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la- Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\n\nTRANSPORTATION\n\nUsual vehicle used are Air Conditioned Sedan (Indigo/Etios/Dzire etc) for 2-3 pax; SUV (Innova/Xylo/Ertiga etc) for 4-6 Pax or Tempo\nTraveller for 7-09 pax\nTransfers as per itinerary only for the mentioned Sightseeing only.\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / Transfers timings.\nDue to unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ Bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) the program may get delayed/shuffled. We will request you to bear with us and as soon as vehicle arrives you will have to get in ASAP.\nMonument will remain closed on Public holidays & Sundays.\nNational Park is Closed Around Mid Jun -Mid Nov\n\nINCIDENTAL CHARGES DUE TO UNFORESEEN SITUATIONS\nAll arrangements made by TCIL are in the capacity of an agent only. TCIL will not be liable for claims or expenses arising from circumstances beyond our control such as accidents, injuries, delayed or cancelled flights & acts of Force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc. – We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued itinerary due to these reasons no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the place where you have to stay back. While it is our endeavor to manage the alternate arrangements during such scenarios, please note the difference may be charged for the same.\nOTHER ON TOUR AND PRE TOUR EXPECTATIONS\n\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes; Pullovers or Light Jackets for Hills\nGuests Photo ID to Shared while booking and Carried on tour: Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar are valid photo ids ((except Pan Card)\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nFood in Kashmir: Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy.\n\nBeing Responsible & a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited.\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Pls. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nDo Not Be loud during any part of the journey. If anything not up to the mark, please inform the helpline number and check with local representative\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate ‘rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining\xa0\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo not Drink or Smoke in Public Places;\nDo check with crew/representatives before taking away things from Flight, Hotels and Cabs. Usually, Toiletries (soap/shampoo/moisturises/comb/dental kit/ loofah/slipper) are free takeaways in Hotels if they are placed in small pouches for one person consumption.\nDo not enter restricted areas or off-road where you please. Pls. consult.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place; habitats & vegetation\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that we have paid to experience. Let us all be The “Great Guests” that we expect from others visiting our homes.\nJai Hind!', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/7162146702_b896312393_h.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/Dal_Lake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/25344846040_64ef8bac76_o(1).jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/7162484002_4696c449e0_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013454/itinerary/Sunset_3.jpg']}, 'score': 4.480349, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014959', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014959', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Chardham Heli Yatra - Kedarnath Stay Special', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yamunotri', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gangotri', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kedarnath', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Badrinath', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Palki (Sedan Chair) at Yamunotri. Priority Darshan at Kedarnath & Badrinath. Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath Priority Darshan Assistance at Yamunotri, Gangotri. Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014959_0_20260930193028', 'price': 229000, 'packageSummary': "The 'Chardham Heli Yatra - Kedarnath Stay Special' package is a 6-day tour covering Dehradun, Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. The itinerary features key highlights such as a Palki (Sedan Chair) ride at Yamunotri, priority Darshan at both Kedarnath and Badrinath, and a sacred Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Additionally, participants will receive priority Darshan assistance at Yamunotri and Gangotri, with the entire journey supported by a professional tour manager stationed in Dehradun.", 'images': ['deharadun.webp', '41508974401_6ab3074e15_b.jpg', 'AdobeStock_524205270.jpeg', '49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'AdobeStock_393142467.jpeg', 'badrinath-1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 229000, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_72508860.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Spiritual', 'Family', 'Domestic Winter GIT', 'Heli Yatra', 'Summer GIT'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014959 is named 'Chardham Heli Yatra - Kedarnath Stay Special' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dehradun, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive Dehradun: Upon arrival at Dehradun airport you will transfer to hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Yamunotri, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner., Description: Dehradun to Yamunotri : Transfer from Sahastradhara Helipad (Dehradun) to Kharsali (Yamunotri) by helicopter. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel for breakfast. A Palki will be arranged for your Darshan at Yamunotri (trip duration: approximately 5 hours). After returning, enjoy lunch at Kharsali and relax in your rooms., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Gangotri, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner., Description: Yamunotri to Gangotri : After breakfast, you will fly to Harsil. On arrival, check in at your hotel before leaving by shared vehicle for Darshan at the Gangotri Temple. After returning to the hotel, enjoy lunch and spend the remainder of the day at leisure, relaxing and soaking in the beautiful surroundings., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kedarnath, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner., Description: Gangotri - Sersi/Phata – Kedarnath: Today fly to Kedarnath. (There will be a stopover at Sersi/Phata for a helicopter changeover.) Upon arrival at Sersi/Phata, proceed to Shri Kedarnath Ji Dham. Later, you will be taken to the Kedarnath Temple for darshan and then return to the hotel. The rest of the day is at leisure, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Badrinath, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner., Description: Kedarnath – Sersi/ Phata-Badrinath: Return to Sersi/Phata and enjoy breakfast at the nearest hotel. Later, fly to Badrinath. On arrival, check in to your hotel. After lunch, proceed for a day trip to Mana Village. In the early evening, visit the Badrinath Temple for darshan, then return to the hotel for dinner, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dehradun, Meals: Breakfast., Description: Badrinath - Dehradun : After breakfast at the hotel, you will return to the Sahastradhara Helipad in Dehradun. Upon arrival, collect your luggage, and a vehicle will drop you at Dehradun Airport for your onward journey. Note: Guests planning their return journey from Dehradun are advised to book flights or trains scheduled after 1700 hrs on the final day of the tour Registration: Mandatory Registration: Please ensure you have your registration slip from https://registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in/ for your travel date. Permits will be issued accordingly. Flights Booking: Guests should always book refundable air tickets to avoid situations where they have to stretch the day due to unavoidable situations. Body Weight: Weight Requirements: Each passenger's actual body weight is needed at booking. The average limit is under 75 kg per person. Passengers exceeding 75 kg should check with Operations for available dates. Additional charges of Rs. 2500/- per kg plus GST apply for weights over 75 kg. Please note, if actual weight exceeds the informed weight, the operator may need to de-board passengers. Charges are non-refundable. Weight Exceeds: If declared weight exceeds more than 2KG at the time of travel, than operator reserves the right to de-board such guest and the amount paid is totally nonrefundable Helipads: There are multiple helipads available for helicopter flights to Kedarnath, including Sersi, Phata, Guptkashi, and Sitapur. Customers may board their flight to Kedarnath from any of these locations. Operation of Helicopter: We operate this yatra in collaboration with third party helicopter operators. Please note that all flight operations are subject to weather conditions, government regulations, and other external factors beyond our control. Seating and Capacity: Seating Capacity: Each helicopter can accommodate up to 6 passengers with a maximum total weight of 450 kg. Departure Timings: Timing Confirmation: Departure times will be confirmed one day prior and may change due to weather conditions, VVIP movements, or maintenance work. Kedarnath Darshan: Visit to Kedarnath: Passengers will land at Phata/Sirsi Helipad and receive a slot to fly to Kedarnath. Timings for these non-scheduled flights will be provided upon arrival at Phata/Sirsi. Please expect a waiting period of 2-4 hours depending on ground situations. Facilities: Heater or Blower: Please note that heaters and blowers are not available in the hotels during the Yatra. Assisted Darshan: Assisted Darshan is totally depends by the Mandir Samiti and Uttarakhand Government, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 229000.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\nCity\nNo of Night\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\n1N\nHyatt Regency\xa0\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\n1N\nHotel Yamunakriti\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\n1N\nHimalayan Nature Resort / Similar\n\n\nKedarnath\n1N\nRajasthan Bhawan\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nBadrinath\n1N\nHotel Sarovar Portico / Similar\n\n\n, \n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\nHyatt Centric or similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\nHotel Holy Yamuna Parmarth\xa0or similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\nHotel Harsil Retreat Resort or\xa0similar\n\n\nSersi\nHotel Sersi Heights or\xa0similar\n\n\nBadrinath\nHotel Lords Palace\xa0or similar\n\n\n. Meals include: \nMeal Information: All meals provided are vegetarian.\nPacked Breakfast: Options include a sandwich, paratha, poori with dry bhaji, or poha.\nBreakfast: Served with tea/coffee, paratha with curd, poori bhaji, or upma/poha (0730-1000 Hrs).\nLunch & Dinner: Includes salad, 1 seasonal vegetable, 1 Dal, 1 Paneer dish, Roti & Rice\n, \nMeals as mentioned in the itinerary. Note: Veg meals on fixed menu.\nAll Meals ( Except Lunch At Dehradun)\n. Inclusions: Helicopter trip commencing from Dehradun Accommodation in listed hotels or similar category properties Meals as per the itinerary (vegetarian, fixed menu) Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun All meals included (except lunch at Dehradun) Palki (sedan chair) service at Yamunotri Priority Darshan at Kedarnath and Badrinath Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath Priority Darshan assistance at Yamunotri and Gangotri Duffel bag provided to each passenger Applicable Government royalty fee All local transport by Toyota Innova or best available vehicle Baggage Allowance: Chardham Baggage allowance (5Kg Per person) Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Note: Client’s Required Details at the time of Booking: Name of The Passenger Date of Birth/Age/Gender Identity Proof (Electoral Card/ Aadhar Card) Mandatory as Per Govt. Norms Actual Body Weight of Every Individual (Average body weight is under 75 Kg per person). Exclusions: Rates are subject to change in case of any major hike in fuel prices Train fare and airfare Travel insurance covering medical evacuation, hospitalization, air evacuation, baggage insurance, and trip cancellation Any optional trips not specified in the program En route or personal expenses such as alcoholic and non alcoholic beverages, telephone calls, tips and gratuities, laundry, etc. Personal equipment including clothes, shoes, daypacks, and personal medical kits Any exigency expenses due to reasons beyond normal control Personal expenses, room service, special orders, mineral water, alcoholic and non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry, etc. Extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the specified itinerary Camera fees and guide charges Any incidental or other expenses not mentioned in the inclusions Government Service Tax (GST). Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: Palki (Sedan Chair) at Yamunotri. Priority Darshan at Kedarnath & Badrinath. Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath Priority Darshan Assistance at Yamunotri, Gangotri. Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'CHHEKS', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Chardham Heli Yatra - Kedarnath Stay Special' package is a 6-day tour covering Dehradun, Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. The itinerary features key highlights such as a Palki (Sedan Chair) ride at Yamunotri, priority Darshan at both Kedarnath and Badrinath, and a sacred Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Additionally, participants will receive priority Darshan assistance at Yamunotri and Gangotri, with the entire journey supported by a professional tour manager stationed in Dehradun.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Dehradun:\n\xa0\nUpon arrival at Dehradun airport you will transfer to hotel.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nDinner', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel -\xa0Hyatt Centric or similar in\xa0Dehradun'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nDehradun to Yamunotri :\nTransfer from Sahastradhara Helipad (Dehradun) to Kharsali (Yamunotri) by helicopter. Upon arrival, proceed to the hotel for breakfast. A Palki will be arranged for your Darshan at Yamunotri (trip duration: approximately 5 hours). \xa0After returning, enjoy lunch at Kharsali and relax in your rooms.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch and Dinner.', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - Holy Yamuna Parmarth or similar in\xa0Kharsali (Yamnotri)'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nYamunotri to Gangotri :\nAfter breakfast, you will fly to Harsil. On arrival, check in at your hotel before leaving by shared vehicle for Darshan at the Gangotri Temple. After returning to the hotel, enjoy lunch and spend the remainder of the day at leisure, relaxing and soaking in the beautiful surroundings.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lunch and Dinner.', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - Harsil Retreat Resort or similar in\xa0Gangotri\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nGangotri - Sersi/Phata – Kedarnath:\nT