ase note, if actual weight exceeds the informed weight, the operator may need to de-board passengers. Charges are non-refundable.\n\xa0\nWeight Exceeds: If declared weight exceeds more than 2KG at the time of travel, than operator reserves the right to de-board such guest and the amount paid is totally nonrefundable\n\xa0\nHelipads:\nThere are multiple helipads available for helicopter flights to Kedarnath, including Sersi, Phata, Guptkashi, and Sitapur. Customers may board their flight to Kedarnath from any of these locations.\n\xa0\nOperation of Helicopter:\nWe operate this yatra in collaboration with third party helicopter operators. Please note that all flight operations are subject to weather conditions, government regulations, and other external factors beyond our control.\n\xa0\nSeating and Capacity:\nSeating Capacity: Each helicopter can accommodate up to 6 passengers with a maximum total weight of 450 kg.\n\xa0\nDeparture Timings:\nTiming Confirmation: Departure times will be confirmed one day prior and may change due to weather conditions, VVIP movements, or maintenance work.\n\xa0\nKedarnath Darshan:\nVisit to Kedarnath: Passengers will land at Phata/Sirsi Helipad and receive a slot to fly to Kedarnath. Timings for these non-scheduled flights will be provided upon arrival at Phata/Sirsi. Please expect a waiting period of 2-4 hours depending on ground situations.\n\xa0\nFacilities:\nHeater or Blower: Please note that heaters and blowers are not available in the hotels during the Yatra.\n\xa0\n\nAssisted Darshan:\xa0\nAssisted Darshan\xa0is totally depends by the Mandir Samiti and Uttarakhand Government\xa0", 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast.', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nN/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n\n\nCity\nNo of Night\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\n1N\nHyatt Regency\xa0\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\n1N\nHotel Yamunakriti\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\n1N\nHimalayan Nature Resort / Similar\n\n\nKedarnath\n1N\nRajasthan Bhawan\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nBadrinath\n1N\nHotel Sarovar Portico / Similar\n\n\n', '\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\nHyatt Centric or similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\nHotel Holy Yamuna Parmarth\xa0or similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\nHotel Harsil Retreat Resort or\xa0similar\n\n\nSersi\nHotel Sersi Heights or\xa0similar\n\n\nBadrinath\nHotel Lords Palace\xa0or similar\n\n\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\nHyatt Centric or similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\nHotel Holy Yamuna Parmarth\xa0or similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\nHotel Harsil Retreat Resort or\xa0similar\n\n\nSersi\nHotel Sersi Heights or\xa0similar\n\n\nBadrinath\nHotel Lords Palace\xa0or similar\n\n\n', '1': '\n\n\nCity\nNo of Night\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\n1N\nHyatt Regency\xa0\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\n1N\nHotel Yamunakriti\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\n1N\nHimalayan Nature Resort / Similar\n\n\nKedarnath\n1N\nRajasthan Bhawan\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nBadrinath\n1N\nHotel Sarovar Portico / Similar\n\n\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 229000.0, 'hotels': ['\n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\nHyatt Centric or similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\nHotel Holy Yamuna Parmarth\xa0or similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\nHotel Harsil Retreat Resort or\xa0similar\n\n\nSersi\nHotel Sersi Heights or\xa0similar\n\n\nBadrinath\nHotel Lords Palace\xa0or similar\n\n\n']}], 'meals': ['\nMeal Information: All meals provided are vegetarian.\nPacked Breakfast: Options include a sandwich, paratha, poori with dry bhaji, or poha.\nBreakfast: Served with tea/coffee, paratha with curd, poori bhaji, or upma/poha (0730-1000 Hrs).\nLunch & Dinner: Includes salad, 1 seasonal vegetable, 1 Dal, 1 Paneer dish, Roti & Rice\n', '\nMeals as mentioned in the itinerary. Note: Veg meals on fixed menu.\nAll Meals ( Except Lunch At Dehradun)\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll local transport as per Toyota Innova/ Best available vehicle\n'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': '<p>Included as per itinerary</p>', 'inclusions': '\nHelicopter trip commencing from Dehradun\nAccommodation in listed hotels or similar category properties\nMeals as per the itinerary (vegetarian, fixed menu)\nProfessional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun\nAll meals included (except lunch at Dehradun)\nPalki (sedan chair) service at Yamunotri\nPriority Darshan\xa0at Kedarnath and Badrinath\nRudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath\nPriority Darshan assistance at Yamunotri and Gangotri\nDuffel bag provided to each passenger\nApplicable Government royalty fee\nAll local transport by Toyota Innova or best available vehicle\n\nBaggage Allowance:\xa0\n\nChardham Baggage allowance (5Kg Per person)\xa0\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n\nNote:\xa0\nClient’s Required Details at the time of Booking:\n\nName of The Passenger\nDate of Birth/Age/Gender\nIdentity Proof (Electoral Card/ Aadhar Card) Mandatory as Per Govt. Norms\nActual Body Weight of Every Individual (Average body weight is under 75 Kg per person)\n\n\xa0\n\xa0', 'exclusions': '\nRates are subject to change in case of any major hike in fuel prices\nTrain fare and airfare\nTravel insurance covering medical evacuation, hospitalization, air evacuation, baggage insurance, and trip cancellation\nAny optional trips not specified in the program\nEn route or personal expenses such as alcoholic and non alcoholic beverages, telephone calls, tips and gratuities, laundry, etc.\nPersonal equipment including clothes, shoes, daypacks, and personal medical kits\nAny exigency expenses due to reasons beyond normal control\nPersonal expenses, room service, special orders, mineral water, alcoholic and non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry, etc.\nExtra excursions or sightseeing apart from the specified itinerary\nCamera fees and guide charges\nAny incidental or other expenses not mentioned in the inclusions\nGovernment Service Tax (GST)\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/AdobeStock_72508860.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/itinerary/deharadun.webp', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/itinerary/41508974401_6ab3074e15_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/itinerary/AdobeStock_524205270.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/itinerary/49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/itinerary/AdobeStock_393142467.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014959/itinerary/badrinath-1.jpg']}, 'score': 4.131669, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG011472', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG011472', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': ' Andaman Fully Loaded With Neil Stay', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Port Blair', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Havelock Island', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Havelock Island', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Neil Island', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Port Blair', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Port Blair', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Knowledgeable and Friendly Tour Experience Manager Port Blair, Havelock & Neil Island included Activity Guided Tour of Cellular Jail with Sound & Light show Sunset at Radhanagar Beach with Family Photo Session Meals Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch – 5 each Daily Tea/Coffee/Coconut Water on Tour. Inclusive of all must see sightseeing Corbyns Cove Beach; Sound & Light show at Cellular Jail Museums – Anthropological; Samudrika Radhanagar Beach Elephant Beach Bharatpur Beach, Laxmanpur Beach Howrah Bridge* depending on tide conditions. Complimentary – A Family Photo session Complimentary – Dinner Cruise in Port Blair'], 'pdfName': 'PKG011472_0_20260921120720', 'price': 38500, 'packageSummary': "The 'Andaman Fully Loaded With Neil Stay' package is a 6-day tour covering Port Blair, Havelock Island, and Neil Island. Led by a knowledgeable and friendly Tour Experience Manager, this comprehensive itinerary includes visits to Corbyns Cove Beach, the Anthropological and Samudrika Museums, Elephant Beach, Bharatpur Beach, Laxmanpur Beach, and the natural Howrah Bridge depending on tide conditions. Key activities feature a guided tour of the historic Cellular Jail with its famous Sound and Light show, a sunset visit to Radhanagar Beach accompanied by a complimentary family photo session, and a complimentary dinner cruise in Port Blair. Participants will also enjoy five breakfasts, lunches, and dinners, along with daily tea, coffee, or coconut water throughout the tour.", 'images': ['CellularJailshutterstock_61791799.jpg', 'RadhanagarBeacinHavelockIsland.jpeg', 'ElephantBeachHavelockIsland.jpeg', 'NeilIslandshutterstock_372091714.jpg', 'andaman.jpg', 'HavelockIslandshutterstock_379128109.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 38500, 'thumbnailImage': 'shutterstock_271082837.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Domestic Diwali Special', 'Adventure', 'Winter GIT', 'Domestic Winter GIT'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG011472 is named ' Andaman Fully Loaded With Neil Stay' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Port Blair, Meals: Lunch, Dinner, Evening Tea & Snacks at Cellular Jail, Description: Arrival at Port Blair Arrive at Port Blair where our representative will help assist you board the vehicle. You will be taken to the hotel. Check in, freshen up and relax at the hotel (Depending on your flight timing). At 1500 Hrs we proceed for sightseeing of national memorial monument of Cellular Jail (closed on Mondays). We do the Guided Tour of Cellular Jail Museum and later enjoy beautiful Light and Sound show. Overnight at the hotel in Port Blair. Note: The cellular jail is closed on Monday’s and National Holidays. Entry to Cellular jail and Museum closes by 1600hrs and Light & Sound tickets are on 1st come 1st serve basis and subject to operation. Cellular jail Light and Sound, if closed, we visit the Flag Point, which is the exact spot where the Indian flag was hoisted by Netaji Subash Chandra Bose for the first time on Indian soil on December 30, 1943. The honorable Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi unfurled the Indian flag on the flag point on its inaugural day, the 30th day of December 2018 to mark the 75th anniversary of Azad Hind Government and the first flag hoisting in Indian soil., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Havelock Island, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch (Packed), Dinner, Evening Tea/Cofffee & Snacks, Description: Port Blair to Havelock (Corbyns Cove Beach) Morning we go to Corbyn’s Cove Beach – the most active beach side of Port Blair. Here we have multiple activities to do on direct payment basis. The Top Activity of Sea Kart is Complimentary for all our guests. [Permitted - only for age between 6-60 years. Under 18 can sit but not allowed to drive. For those above 60 years, will be given a complimentary family boat ride] Sea kart is a unique water craft shaped like a go kart; with a steering wheel and a paddle accelerator attached to the right of the steering; It is officially permitted for self-driving by customers; Seakart experience includes photography by an in house DSLR camera which is handed out to customers. We start our journey towards Havelock Island via ferry from Port Blair Harbor. On arrival at Havelock Island, our representative will receive and escort you to check-in to the resort. After relax, day free for own leisure at Havelock Island. Overnight stay at Havelock Island., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Havelock Island, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Tea/Coffee at the Radha Nagar Beach, Description: Havelock – Elephant Beach and Radhanagar Beach After breakfast, today early morning, will proceed to Elephant Beach by motorized boat which is famous for Water Sports Activities at Havelock. The Trip of Elephants Beach. Afternoon we proceed to Radhanagar Beach (Beach No. 7), the Times Magazine rated the finest beach among the best beaches in Asia. It is an ideal place for swimming, sea bathing and basking on the sun kissed beaches. One Session of Candid Family Photo Session is provided here on this No.1 Beach of Asia. Overnight in the Hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Neil Island, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Tea/Coffee at the Beach or hotel, Description: Havelock - Neil Island After buffet breakfast, check out from the hotel. Transfer to the Havelock jetty to board the ferry for Neil Island. Disembark at Neil and transfer to the hotel. Post lunch; proceed to visit Bharatpur beach, Laxmanpur beach and Howrah Bridge (depending on tide conditions). You can do adventure Actitvies like glass bottom boat ride in Neil on direct payment basis Return to the hotel in the evening. Enjoy your dinner and a comfortable overnight stay at the hotel. Overnight at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Port Blair, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Coconut Water, Description: Neil Island - Port Blair [Port Blair City Tour] Morning after breakfast you will transfer to jetty for the ferry to Port Blair. We Check-in in to our Hotels and have lunch. Port Blair City tour includes museums. Anthropological Museum that displays tribal essential and artefacts and Naval Marine Museum (Samudrika) that gives a good retrospect of the history, shells, Corals marine life, geography and archaeology of these islands. Return check in at the hotel & overnight at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Port Blair, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure This morning after breakfast you will transfer to Port Blair airport in time to board your flight. Depart Port Blair with fond memories of these mesmerizing Islands., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 38500.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nBreakfast, Dinner, Lunch – 5 each\nDaily Tea/Coffee/Coconut Water on Tour.\xa0\n. Inclusions: Accommodation on twin sharing basis in hotels mentioned or similar Daily Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner. Entrance Fees to All Monuments Inclusive of all ‘must see’ sightseeing. Corbyns Cove Beach; Sound & Light show at Cellular Jail 2 Museums – Anthropological; Samudrika Radhanagar Beach Elephant Beach Bharatpur Beach, Laxmanpur Beach Howrah Bridge Complimentary –Evening Dinner Cruise in Port Blair Complimentary – A Family Photo session Port Blair – Havelock (Swaraj Dweep) – Port Blair will be by Makruzz/Coastal Cruise/Green Ocean/Sea link. AC Vehicles as per group size on sharing basis (SUV/Tempo); Vehicle cannot be confirmed at the time of booking); Vehicle is not at disposal – means it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary; Minimum Operating Strength for the Group is 10 Pax Tour Manager : Local Tour Escort from 15 Pax Onwards. Professional Tour Manager From 25 Pax Onwards. All presently applicable Hotel taxes but not GST Note: Flight timings are subject to change at any point of time Insurance: Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs. Exclusions: Anything not mentioned in inclusion like Cost of Lunches; Additional / personal use of vehicle; Any personal expenses, room service and special orders, alcoholic and non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc; Camera fees, guide charges ; Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions. GST will be applicable as per prevailing rates Supplement: Supplements Per Person Stanadard Private Vehicle (For Entire Tour) 3000 Per Person Candle Lit Dinner With Wine 3900 Per Person Honeymoon [CLD + Cake + Flower Decoration] in Havelock 6500 Per Person SCUBA ( Havelock) with transfers 4000 Per Person Elephant Beach with Snorkeling with Transfers 1800 Per Person Glass Bottom Boat Ride in Neil Island 600 Per Person. Product Terms and Conditions: Complimentary Once a Tour (non-refundable if activity gets cancelled) Price is subject to change Price is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats/Ferry Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost. Accommodation in Andaman: We have classified hotels into Different categories of tours. This is basis Amenities, Reviews, Value and Destination. Since tastes and expectations may vary, we encourage our guests to do their research online on the hotels and advise us if any change is required. Classification & Standard: Hotels in Andaman are less on amenities if compared to a similar category in Indian Metros. That’s the reason our Economy (Budget) package of Andaman has hotels similar to a 1-2*Basic hotels in mainland India while Destination like Kerala for the same Economy (Budget) Category has “2-3* basic hotels. Accommodation is provided in Mentioned or Similar Hotels. An early morning check-out time at around 8:00 hrs for most hotels. For early check in / late checkout / extending of stay, subjected to the availability. Only 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll Over All special requests like early check-in, smoking, nonsmoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer. In case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out Consumption and serving of alcohol in hotels / rooms is subject to hotel’s rules and regulations. For meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis depending on occupancy level. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la-Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items. Vehicles are used as per the itinerary and cover the mentioned sightseeing only. Extra Sightseeing on extra charges Vehicles are Limited and the SUVs (Xylo, Ertiga, Scorpio, Innova) are mostly provided. Other Vehicle types are available like Sedan, Tempo, Coaches but much less in numbers. We Use AC Vehicles but sometimes due to heavy tourist rush, Non-AC vehicles may be used. Vehicle Transfers are primarily point-to-point. Same vehicle and Driver Does not stay with the guest for the entire tour. This doesn’t matter much as the driving distances in Andaman are very short between any 02 sightseeing points esp. in the most common itineraries. Just Keep in mind, as the vehicles & drivers change always, we will request you to be very careful with personal belongings Ferries: On priority we use Inter-Island Ferries between 03 island (Port Blair, Havelock, Neil) operated by Private Companies (Makruzz, Green Ocean, Coastal Cruise, Sea Link) The sailing of Private Ferries is subject to weather condition. In case it does not sail due to bad weather or a technical snag, the guests will give alternate sailing on Government Ferry. Government ferries are heavier but slower vessels (takes 2.5 hrs between Port Blair – Havelock against 1.5 hrs of private ferries). However, the old Govt, Ferries, too, are an experience for their open deck and many guests request for that! Incidental Charges Due to Unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) - We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued inter-island ferry due to technical snag or bad weather, no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the island where you have to stay back. Guests to carry their ID Proofs with Address (except Pan Card) – Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar is valid photo ids in Andaman. Carry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes Water Sports & Doctor’s advice: Seek Doctor’s advice for water activities like SCUBA & Sea Walk. Please Consult Doctor if you have High BP, Sugar, Asthma, Ear Pain, past Surgery, or Pregnancy. Diving and Sea Walk require good fitness and an age between 10 – 60 years. You Can Do these even if You have never tried diving before or You do not know how to swim or You have no underwater experience or You are between the ages of 10-60 years Glasses or contact lenses may be worn during this Underwater Sea Walk (you will not get your head wet). Food in Andaman: Being an Island, Sea Food (Prawns, Shrimp, Lobster, Fishes and Crabs) is available in good quantity and quality but not inexpensive. Besides, Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings. Itinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate. No refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical) Tour Manager Services in Fixed Tours: Tour Manager Services are provided in Fixed Tours Only. Tour Managers and representatives are fixed to particular islands. They do not travel with the group. They Ensure that the entire Group movement is smooth including the Arrivals & Departure; Hotel Checkin; Ferry Tickets; Entrances; etc Closed on Monday and National Holidays: Anthropological Museum, Fisheries Museum, Cellular Jail, Samudrika, Mahatma Gandhi National Park; Closed every Wednesday: Ross Island; Closed on Sunday and National Holidays: Chatham Saw Mill, Forest Museum, and Sagarika Cottage Industries Emporium. We Shuffle Itinerary to manage this. Weather, Rains & Cyclones in Andaman: Andaman is a Tropical island, with temperature averaging between 23 – 32 degrees year round. This feels pleasant under the shade of coconut groves with cool breeze from the lagoons and sea. Being Tropical, rains is difficult to predict. So light showers in November is no surprise. Cyclones may disrupt ferry movements any time of the year and not necessarily monsoon. In case of discontinued ferries, no refund of on the booked arrangement but we do manage the alternate sightseeing and accommodation basis availability. Being Responsible and a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land: While some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited: Take a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials; Respect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Do not misbehave or manhandle. A little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling; Bother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate rude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining J Maintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin. Do Not Touch Shells & Corals Do not enter waters when inebriated or where or where not allowed Do not Drink in Public Places; Do not enter in restricted or tribal areas around the Islands. Tribal Tours are banned. Do not take pictures of the airport, government dockyard, naval wharf, dhanikari dam, defence establishments and Chatham Saw Mill. Take Proper permits are required to take video or film; Drone Photography is not permitted Do not set up tents and hammocks during nights by the beaches or forest is not allowed. Do not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place. Do not carry Alcohol on board the ferry Leave Places Better than you found it! Most leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that is the prime highlight of that place. Highlights of the package: Knowledgeable and Friendly Tour Experience Manager Port Blair, Havelock & Neil Island included Activity Guided Tour of Cellular Jail with Sound & Light show Sunset at Radhanagar Beach with Family Photo Session Meals Breakfast, Dinner, Lunch – 5 each Daily Tea/Coffee/Coconut Water on Tour. Inclusive of all must see sightseeing Corbyns Cove Beach; Sound & Light show at Cellular Jail Museums – Anthropological; Samudrika Radhanagar Beach Elephant Beach Bharatpur Beach, Laxmanpur Beach Howrah Bridge* depending on tide conditions. Complimentary – A Family Photo session Complimentary – Dinner Cruise in Port Blair.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'AFLNBL', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'AFLNJD', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'AFLNPQ', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'AFLNDL', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ADFLBM', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'AFLNMM', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'AFLNCC', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Andaman Fully Loaded With Neil Stay' package is a 6-day tour covering Port Blair, Havelock Island, and Neil Island. Led by a knowledgeable and friendly Tour Experience Manager, this comprehensive itinerary includes visits to Corbyns Cove Beach, the Anthropological and Samudrika Museums, Elephant Beach, Bharatpur Beach, Laxmanpur Beach, and the natural Howrah Bridge depending on tide conditions. Key activities feature a guided tour of the historic Cellular Jail with its famous Sound and Light show, a sunset visit to Radhanagar Beach accompanied by a complimentary family photo session, and a complimentary dinner cruise in Port Blair. Participants will also enjoy five breakfasts, lunches, and dinners, along with daily tea, coffee, or coconut water throughout the tour.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': 'Arrival at Port Blair\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive at Port Blair where our representative will help assist you board the vehicle.\n\xa0\nYou will be taken to the hotel. Check in, freshen up and relax at the hotel (Depending on your flight timing).\xa0 At 1500 Hrs we proceed for sightseeing of national memorial monument of Cellular Jail (closed on Mondays). We do the Guided Tour of Cellular Jail Museum and later enjoy beautiful Light and Sound show.\xa0\n\xa0\nOvernight at the hotel in Port Blair.\n\xa0\nNote: The cellular jail is closed on Monday’s and National Holidays. Entry to Cellular jail and Museum closes by 1600hrs and Light & Sound tickets are on 1st come 1st serve basis and subject to operation. Cellular jail Light and Sound, if closed, we visit the Flag Point, which is the exact spot where the Indian flag was hoisted by Netaji Subash Chandra Bose for the first time on Indian soil on December 30, 1943. The honorable Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi unfurled the Indian flag on the flag point on its inaugural day, the 30th day of December 2018 to mark the 75th anniversary of Azad Hind Government and the first flag hoisting in Indian soil.', 'mealDescription': 'Lunch, Dinner, Evening Tea & Snacks at Cellular Jail', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel:\xa0TSG Grand or similar in\xa0Port Blair\xa0'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nPort Blair to Havelock (Corbyns Cove Beach)\n\xa0\nMorning we go to Corbyn’s Cove Beach – the most active beach side of Port Blair.\xa0 Here we have multiple activities to do on direct payment basis.\xa0 The Top Activity of Sea Kart is Complimentary for all our guests. [Permitted - only for age between 6-60 years. Under 18 can sit but not allowed to drive. For those above 60 years, will be given a complimentary family boat ride] Sea kart is a unique water craft shaped like a go kart; with a steering wheel and a paddle accelerator attached to the right of the steering; It is officially permitted for self-driving by customers; Seakart experience includes photography by an in house DSLR camera which is handed out to customers.\xa0\n\xa0\nWe start our journey towards Havelock Island via ferry from Port Blair Harbor. On arrival at Havelock Island, our representative will receive and escort you to check-in to the resort.\xa0 After relax, day free for own leisure at Havelock Island. Overnight stay at Havelock Island.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch (Packed), Dinner, Evening Tea/Cofffee & Snacks\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel: TSG Blue or similar in\xa0Havelock\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nHavelock – Elephant Beach and Radhanagar Beach\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, today early morning, will proceed to Elephant Beach by motorized boat which is famous for Water Sports Activities at Havelock. The Trip of Elephants Beach.\n\xa0\nAfternoon we proceed to Radhanagar Beach (Beach No. 7), the Times Magazine rated the finest beach among the best beaches in Asia. It is an ideal place for swimming, sea bathing and basking on the sun kissed beaches. One Session of Candid Family Photo Session is provided here on this No.1 Beach of Asia.\xa0\xa0\n\xa0\nOvernight in the Hotel.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Tea/Coffee at the Radha Nagar Beach', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel: TSG Blue or similar in\xa0Havelock\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nHavelock - Neil Island\n\xa0\nAfter buffet breakfast, check out from the hotel. Transfer to the Havelock jetty to board the ferry for Neil Island. Disembark at Neil and transfer to the hotel. Post lunch; proceed to visit Bharatpur beach, Laxmanpur beach and Howrah Bridge (depending on tide conditions).\xa0 You can do adventure Actitvies like glass bottom boat ride in Neil on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nReturn to the hotel in the evening. Enjoy your dinner and a comfortable overnight stay at the hotel. Overnight at the hotel.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Tea/Coffee at the Beach or hotel', 'overnightStay': 'TSG Aura or similar in\xa0Neil Island'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nNeil Island - Port Blair [Port Blair City Tour]\n\xa0\nMorning after breakfast you will transfer to jetty for the ferry to Port Blair. We Check-in in to our Hotels and have lunch.\n\xa0\nPort Blair City tour includes museums. Anthropological Museum that displays tribal essential and artefacts and Naval Marine Museum (Samudrika) that gives a good retrospect of the history, shells, Corals marine life, geography and archaeology of these islands.\n\xa0\nReturn check in at the hotel & overnight at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, Coconut Water\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel:\xa0TSG Grand or similar in\xa0Port Blair\xa0'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nDeparture\n\xa0\nThis morning after breakfast you will transfer to Port Blair airport in time to board your flight. Depart Port Blair with fond memories of these mesmerizing Islands.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 38500.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nBreakfast, Dinner, Lunch – 5 each\nDaily Tea/Coffee/Coconut Water on Tour.\xa0\n'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<div class="visible-lg visible-md visible-sm web_arrow_box tourArrow-0" style="left: 680px;" data-bind="attr:{class:\'visible-lg visible-md visible-sm web_arrow_box tourArrow-\'+ko.toJS($index)}">Rest assured, Thomas Cook\'s experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it\'s a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</div>', 'flightDescription': '', 'inclusions': 'Accommodation on twin sharing basis in hotels mentioned or similar\nDaily Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner.\xa0\nEntrance Fees to All Monuments\nInclusive of all ‘must see’ sightseeing.\xa0\n\nCorbyns Cove Beach;\xa0\xa0\nSound & Light show at Cellular Jail\n2 Museums – Anthropological; Samudrika\nRadhanagar Beach\nElephant Beach\xa0\nBharatpur Beach,\xa0\nLaxmanpur Beach\xa0\nHowrah Bridge\xa0\nComplimentary –Evening Dinner Cruise in Port Blair\nComplimentary – A Family Photo session\nPort Blair – Havelock (Swaraj Dweep) – Port Blair will be by Makruzz/Coastal Cruise/Green Ocean/Sea link.\xa0\nAC Vehicles as per group size on sharing basis (SUV/Tempo); Vehicle cannot be confirmed at the time of booking); Vehicle is not at disposal – means it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary;\xa0\nMinimum Operating Strength for the Group is 10 Pax\nTour Manager : Local Tour Escort from 15 Pax Onwards. Professional Tour Manager From 25 Pax Onwards.\xa0\nAll presently applicable Hotel taxes but not GST\n\nNote: Flight timings are subject to change at any point of time\nInsurance:\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nAnything not mentioned in inclusion like Cost of Lunches; Additional / personal use of vehicle; Any personal expenses, room service and special orders, alcoholic and non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc; Camera fees, guide charges ; Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions.\nGST will be applicable as per prevailing rates\n\nSupplement:\n\n\n\nSupplements Per Person\nStanadard\n\n\nPrivate Vehicle (For Entire Tour)\n3000\xa0\xa0Per Person\n\n\nCandle Lit Dinner With Wine\xa0\n3900\xa0\xa0Per Person\n\n\nHoneymoon [CLD + Cake + Flower Decoration] in Havelock\n6500\xa0\xa0Per Person\n\n\nSCUBA\xa0 ( Havelock) with transfers\xa0\n4000\xa0\xa0Per Person\n\n\nElephant Beach with Snorkeling with Transfers\n1800\xa0\xa0Per Person\n\n\nGlass Bottom Boat Ride in Neil Island\n600\xa0Per Person\n\n\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\nComplimentary Once a Tour (non-refundable if activity gets cancelled)\nPrice is subject to change\nPrice is based on the “Base” Category of Hotel Room/Airlines Seats/Ferry Seats. This is Irrespective of the Package Category Chosen. Upgrade to Higher Category is available at an extra cost.\nAccommodation in Andaman: We have classified hotels into Different categories of tours. This is basis Amenities, Reviews, Value and Destination. Since tastes and expectations may vary, we encourage our guests to do their research online on the hotels and advise us if any change is required.\nClassification & Standard: Hotels in Andaman are less on amenities if compared to a similar category in Indian Metros. That’s the reason our Economy (Budget) package of Andaman has hotels similar to a 1-2*Basic hotels in mainland India while Destination like Kerala for the same Economy (Budget) Category has “2-3* basic hotels.\nAccommodation is provided in Mentioned or Similar Hotels.\nAn early morning check-out time at around 8:00 hrs for most hotels. For early check in / late checkout / extending of stay, subjected to the availability.\nOnly 01 extra bed/mattress is allowed per room. This extra bed means a Mattress / Roll Over\nAll special requests like early check-in, smoking, nonsmoking, views, floors, king, twin, adjoining and/or interconnecting rooms are strictly subject to availability upon arrival and cannot be guaranteed prior. Any expenses arising out of this is to be borne by the customer.\nIn case of guests cannot climb the higher floors, we request you to update this at the time of booking so that we may take appropriate action and try for rooms in the Ground floor. This is again subject to availability and difference if any will have to be settled directly before check out\nConsumption and serving of alcohol in hotels / rooms is subject to hotel’s rules and regulations.\nFor meal plans, menu will be on fixed plan/ buffet basis depending on occupancy level. MAP & AP Meal plans do not include Evening snacks & cold drinks / liquor, Soups or Deserts. For order on A-la-Carte basis, guests are requested to make direct payment for additional items.\nVehicles are used as per the itinerary and cover the mentioned sightseeing only. Extra Sightseeing on extra charges\nVehicles are Limited and the SUVs (Xylo, Ertiga, Scorpio, Innova) are mostly provided. Other Vehicle types are available like Sedan, Tempo, Coaches but much less in numbers. We Use AC Vehicles but sometimes due to heavy tourist rush, Non-AC vehicles may be used.\nVehicle Transfers are primarily point-to-point. Same vehicle and Driver Does not stay with the guest for the entire tour. This doesn’t matter much as the driving distances in Andaman are very short between any 02 sightseeing points esp. in the most common itineraries. Just Keep in mind, as the vehicles & drivers change always, we will request you to be very careful with personal belongings\nFerries: On priority we use Inter-Island Ferries between 03 island (Port Blair, Havelock, Neil) operated by Private Companies (Makruzz, Green Ocean, Coastal Cruise, Sea Link)\nThe sailing of Private Ferries is subject to weather condition. In case it does not sail due to bad weather or a technical snag, the guests will give alternate sailing on Government Ferry. Government ferries are heavier but slower vessels (takes 2.5 hrs between Port Blair – Havelock against 1.5 hrs of private ferries). However, the old Govt, Ferries, too, are an experience for their open deck and many guests request for that!\nIncidental Charges Due to Unforeseen situations (force majeure/ traffic jams / traffic halts/ diversions/ bandh/ curfew, Union strike, VVIP movement, etc.) - We will request you to bear with us the situations beyond our control. We will arrange for alternate sightseeing. In case of discontinued inter-island ferry due to technical snag or bad weather, no refund on the hotel booking will be provided and alternate accommodations (as per availability) are managed in the island where you have to stay back.\nGuests to carry their ID Proofs with Address (except Pan Card) – Passport/Voter ID/DL/Aadhar is valid photo ids in Andaman.\nCarry comfort clothing – Shorts, T Shirts, Open Footwear, Cap or Hat, Sunglasses, Sun screen lotion, Rubber soled shoes\nWater Sports & Doctor’s advice: Seek Doctor’s advice for water activities like SCUBA & Sea Walk. Please Consult Doctor if you have High BP, Sugar, Asthma, Ear Pain, past Surgery, or Pregnancy. Diving and Sea Walk require good fitness and an age between 10 – 60 years. You Can Do these even if You have never tried diving before or You do not know how to swim or You have no underwater experience or You are between the ages of 10-60 years Glasses or contact lenses may be worn during this Underwater Sea Walk (you will not get your head wet).\nFood in Andaman: Being an Island, Sea Food (Prawns, Shrimp, Lobster, Fishes and Crabs) is available in good quantity and quality but not inexpensive. Besides, Vegetarian, North Indian, South Indian, Continental and Chinese dishes are available at all restaurants and hotels. In hotels, buffet is provided based on occupancy\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips / activities as informed by our representative. It helps manage the tour in a destination low on vehicles and dependent on ferry timings.\nItinerary can be shuffled but in all cases we manage to provide all the inclusions as mentioned or similar or alternate.\nNo refund for Complimentary Activities cancelled or unutilized due to reasons beyond our control (natural/technical)\nTour Manager Services in Fixed Tours: Tour Manager Services are provided in Fixed Tours Only. Tour Managers and representatives are fixed to particular islands. They do not travel with the group. They Ensure that the\xa0entire Group movement is smooth including the Arrivals & Departure; Hotel Checkin; Ferry Tickets; Entrances; etc\nClosed on Monday and National Holidays: Anthropological Museum, Fisheries Museum, Cellular Jail, Samudrika, Mahatma Gandhi National Park; Closed every Wednesday: Ross Island; Closed on Sunday and National Holidays: Chatham Saw Mill, Forest Museum, and Sagarika Cottage Industries Emporium. We Shuffle Itinerary to manage this.\nWeather, Rains & Cyclones in Andaman: Andaman is a Tropical island, with temperature averaging between 23 – 32 degrees year round. This feels pleasant under the shade of coconut groves with cool breeze from the lagoons and sea. Being Tropical, rains is difficult to predict. So light showers in November is no surprise. Cyclones may disrupt ferry movements any time of the year and not necessarily monsoon. In case of discontinued ferries, no refund of on the booked arrangement but we do manage the alternate sightseeing and accommodation basis availability.\n\n\xa0\nBeing Responsible and a Better Guest in Someone else’s Land:\nWhile some of the pointers require Self-awareness, some actually are strictly prohibited:\n\nTake a Little Consent before taking pictures of people & their materials;\nRespect things local including Drivers, Guides, and Staff. Do not misbehave or manhandle.\nA little bargaining is expected but not too much haggling;\nBother to learn/understand the local language – it helps a lot. This helps differentiate\nrude’ from ‘local tone’ and also helps your bargaining J\nMaintain Cleanliness. Pls. use dustbins or take back the days litter to your hotel’s bin.\nDo Not Touch Shells & Corals\nDo not enter waters when inebriated or where or where not allowed\nDo not Drink in Public Places;\nDo not enter in restricted or tribal areas around the Islands. Tribal Tours are banned.\nDo not take pictures of the airport, government dockyard, naval wharf, dhanikari dam, defence establishments and Chatham Saw Mill.\nTake Proper permits are required to take video or film;\nDrone Photography is not permitted\nDo not set up tents and hammocks during nights by the beaches or forest is not allowed.\nDo not dirty & damage vehicles, hotels; property; place.\nDo not carry Alcohol on board the ferry\nLeave Places Better than you found it!\n\n\xa0\nMost leisure holiday destinations are relaxed, remote places. They may look less on professionalism but are high on humility. Let us be respectful of locals and the ‘culture’ that is the prime highlight of that place', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/shutterstock_271082837.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/itinerary/CellularJailshutterstock_61791799.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/itinerary/RadhanagarBeacinHavelockIsland.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/itinerary/ElephantBeachHavelockIsland.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/itinerary/NeilIslandshutterstock_372091714.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/itinerary/andaman.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG011472/itinerary/HavelockIslandshutterstock_379128109.jpg']}, 'score': 4.131669, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015547', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015547', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Bali New Year Special', 'days': 8, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015530_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 69290, 'packageSummary': "The 'Bali New Year Special' package is an 8-day tour covering the vibrant coastal town of Kuta and the cultural heart of Ubud. The itinerary features exciting activities such as a spectacular New Year's Eve beach celebration, visits to the iconic Uluwatu Temple, and exploration of the scenic Tegallalang Rice Terraces. Participants will also enjoy guided tours of the Ubud Monkey Forest, traditional Balinese dance performances, thrilling water sports, and relaxing beachside leisure time.", 'images': ['Kuta.jpeg', 'Bananaboat.jpg', 'Baliswing_new_753.jpeg', 'Bali75309.jpg', 'Gatetheaven7531.jpg', 'Seminyak753.jpg', 'NusaPenida753.jpg', 'Bali_Scenic_7531.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 69290, 'thumbnailImage': 'Bali_New_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015547 is named 'Bali New Year Special' and spans 8 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Kuta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Transfer from Ubud to Seminyak Enjoy Breakfast at the Hotel Inter Hotel Transfer Ubud Hotel to Seminyak Hotel on Private Basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 69290.0. Hotels envisaged include: \xa0\n\n\n\nDestinations\n\xa0Hotel\n\n\nKuta\nRisata Hotel Kuta or similar\n\n\nUbud\nAlam Puisi Villa Ubud or similar\n\n\nSeminyak\nJambuluwuk Oceano Seminyak or similar\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\nDestinations\nHotel\n\n\nKuta\xa0\xa0\nKuta Paradisoor similar\n\n\nUbud\xa0\nFurama Villa Ubud or similar\n\n\nSeminyak\xa0\nCross Paasha Seminyak or similar\n\n\n, \xa0\n\n\n\n\nDestinations\nHotels\n\n\n\xa0Kuta\nGrand Mega Resort in Kuta or Similar\n\n\n\xa0Ubud\nChampulang Sari\xa0Ubud or Similar\n\n\n\xa0Seminyak\nSwiss Belcourt\xa0Seminyak or Similar\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Ubud 04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Kuta. Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Return Airport Transfer (Airport – Hotel – Airport) – on PVT Basis Benoa Water Sports Water Sports (including one round of Couple Parasailing (3 minutes) - Banana Boat (5 minutes) - Jet Ski (4-5 minutes) Phinisi Dinner Cruise West Nusa Penida Tour with Snorkelling Lempuyang “Gate of Heaven” 2 hrs. Balinese Massage ATV Tandem Jungle Swing New Year Dinner on 31st December 2026. Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa Charges Visa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) are approximately USD 35-40 per person. Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights services Entrance fees Meals which are not mentioned in the itinerary. Any tips - for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions. Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of personal nature (Such as Usage of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc.) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge The rates are valid for minimum 01 adults travelling together at all times.. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions: The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for a minimum of 02 adults travelling together at all times. During Peak Season: Minimum 2 Nights Stay is required No Check Out period on 31 December 2025 and 01 January 2026 Nyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 19 March 2026. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 19 March 2026 to 06.00 am 20 March 2026 Compulsory New Year Dinner will be Applicable according to the Resort The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same. Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': '