nning Balinese cultural performance set against the backdrop of a dramatic sunset by the Indian Ocean.\nOvernight in Bali", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nProceed to Jakarta - Check In – Evening visit Autograph Tower\nThis morning after breakfast reach Denpasar Airport for Flight to Jakarta, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the Jakarta airport.\xa0\nOn arrival in Jakarta, Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs).\xa0\nLater in the evening visit Autograph Tower Jakarta- to enjoy unforgettable 360-degree views of Jakarta from Indonesia’s Tallest Observatory Deck. More than just a view, visit the Sky Garden a multi-level, semi-outdoor experience where visitors can explore immersive spaces and enjoy thrilling sky-high attractions (Glass Floors, UPswing, UPside, UP High)\nOvernight in Jakarta', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nCity Tour of Jakarta - Merdeka Square, National Museum, Presidential Palace – Visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari – Free time at Kuta Tua - Jakarta’s Old Town\xa0\nThis morning after breakfast we will explore the Merdeka Square (Independence Square), Photostop at National Monument, Visit National Museum, Visit Presidential Palace (Subject to operation). Later we visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari Indonesia's largest indoor living planet - where the mysteries of the ocean meet the excitement of a safari adventure. Later in the evening enjoy your free time at Kuta Tua - Jakarta’s Old Town the area is filled with historic buildings, museums, and open spaces that still preserve the atmosphere of old Jakarta.\xa0\nOvernight in Jakarta", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning After Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\nNote : The Given Itinerary is a tentative itinerary. Itinerary and activities can be rescheduled or substituted based on weather, operational requirements, or unforeseen circumstances', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n', '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Bali\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n\n\xa0\nNote : Under unavoidable circumstances, Hotels are subject to change, in such condition substitute hotel of similar category is provided.'], 'hotels_list': {'2': '\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Bali\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n\n\xa0\nNote : Under unavoidable circumstances, Hotels are subject to change, in such condition substitute hotel of similar category is provided.'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 92200.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Bali\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n\n\xa0\nNote : Under unavoidable circumstances, Hotels are subject to change, in such condition substitute hotel of similar category is provided.']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n06 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary', '\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Bali:\n\nExperience Bali Swing\nVisit Tanah Lot Floating Temple For Sunset\nEnjoy Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject To Weather Conditions)\xa0\nVisit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\n\n\xa0\nJakarta:\n\nCity Tour\xa0\nVisit Merdeka Square\nPhotostop At National Monument\nVisit National Museum\nVisit Presidential Palace (Subject To Operation).\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 15 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 15 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 15 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li><strong>Main Airfare is not included&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li>Internal Airfare for Bali &ndash; Jakarta is included for all passengers including Joining Direct / NRI Passengers</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nInternal Airfare for Bali – Jakarta is included for all passengers including Joining Direct / NRI Passengers\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 31 July 2026\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\nReturn Airport transfers from all airports.\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative.\xa0\nIf group size is less than 15 customers, the tour will operate on Seat in Coach and FIT basis.\xa0\nFor Group Size more than 15 customers there will be English Speaking Guide Assistance and for less than 15 customers there will be Driver cum Guide.\n', 'exclusions': '\nMain Airfare\xa0\nAirport taxes\xa0\nIndonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 31 July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nPorterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/SRP BALI.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/Bali7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/BaliSwing.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/NusaPenida753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/KeckDanace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/Jakarta.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/Jakarta753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015271/itinerary/Bali891.jpg']}, 'score': 3.7792792, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014983', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014983', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Pahalgam', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gulmarg', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Srinagar', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Stay in Houseboat on Dal Lake Enjoy Shikara ride on Dal Lake till Char Chinar The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014983_0_20260826144349', 'price': 45700, 'packageSummary': "The 'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special' package is a 7-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features unique experiences such as staying in a traditional houseboat on Dal Lake and enjoying a relaxing Shikara ride to Char Chinar. Additionally, participants will have the opportunity to experience the famous Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg, with tickets subject to availability, making for an unforgettable holiday in the valley.", 'images': ['Dallake.jpg', 'AdobeStock_296897404.jpeg', 'AdobeStock_1062426595.jpeg', '7162146702_b896312393_h.jpg', 'gondola.jpg', '49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'kashmir8.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 45700, 'thumbnailImage': 'AdobeStock_362192710.jpeg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Winter GIT', 'Domestic Winter GIT', 'Durga Puja Domestic'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Durga Puja Special', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG014983 is named \'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special\' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Srinagar, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival in Srinagar Welcome to Srinagar and transfer to the houseboat. Check in to the houseboat and freshen up. Enjoy a romantic Shikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake (Kashmir\'s iconic jewel, a serene houseboat haven) Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the houseboat Note: Room heating facilities in houseboats are available depending on weather conditions., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Srinagar to Pahalgam (90 Km / ~03 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the houseboat and check out. Srinagar sightseeing Shankaracharya Temple (Dedicated to Lord Shiva) Nishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens) Pari Mahal (Palace of Fairies) Drive to Pahalgam (A picturesque valley surrounded by snow-capped mountains, offering stunning natural beauty and adventure opportunities) En route visit Pampore for saffron demonstration and shopping Avantipur Ruins (ancient temple complex) Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Check in at the hotel and relax. Dinner and overnight stay in Pahalgam at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Pahalgam, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Pahalgam Morning breakfast at the hotel. Full Day city tour, visiting the below attractions Betaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab") Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Enjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam Note: Day excursion to Betaab is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Gulmarg, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Pahalgam to Gulmarg (140Km / ~ 04 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the hotel and check out. Drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of flowers) En route visit, Martand Sun Temple (ancient ruins) Kashmiri Cricket Bat Factory (Witness the craftsmanship of world-renowned cricket bats made from Kashmir willow) Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Check in at the hotel and relax. Dinner and overnight stay in Gulmarg at the hotel. Note : In case of heavy rainfall/ Gulmarg is not operational due to any sort of Weather conditions, we will take clients to Doodhpathri. Gulmarg Gondola Ticket up to Phase 1 is part of the package and subject to availability as per the booking dates. Please be noted, that Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling. In Gulmarg - The Tour Vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg hotel. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Gulmarg to Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 02 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the hotel and check out. Experience the Gulmarg Gondola (Asia\'s highest cable car project) Enjoy panoramic views of the Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley. Experience sledge riding on snow – on direct payment basis Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Enroute visit Handloom Emporium on the way back to Srinagar. Drive to Srinagar Check in to the hotel and relax Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel. Important Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking Gulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest. Gondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging. Guests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com] Though we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner, Description: Srinagar – Sonmarg – Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 2 hours drive) Morning breakfast at the hotel. Drive to Sonmarg (Golden meadow) Enjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier- on direct payment basis Enjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute. Optional: Sledge or snowmobile ride – on direct payment basis Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Srinagar, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Morning breakfast at the hotel and check out. Proceed to the airport for your onward journey, taking with you cherished memories of your Kashmir experience. Note: As this is a group tour, the airport transfer departs from the Srinagar hotel at 10:00 AM., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 45700.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 06; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\n\xa0. Inclusions: Hotels: Twin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar Meals: Breakfasts: 06; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 06 Breakfast & Dinners will be Buffet Lunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed Extra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day Additional Inclusions: Round-trip economy class airfare Water: 500 ml water per person per day Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Airfare not included for joining direct passengers Additional / personal use of vehicle. Any personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral water, alcoholic & non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc. Any extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary. Camera fees Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions. GST will be applicable as per prevailing rates. Product Terms and Conditions: The tour price printed is dynamic & is purely on first come first serve basis. The person booking tour early is likely to get the lowest price as communicated / offered by the Company, subject to availability of seats It is mandatory to carry photo ID card (except Pan Card) while you are on tour. Valid ID for Kashmir: Driving License/ Voter ID/Passport/Aadhar Card The vehicle used for transfers is not at disposal. This is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon circumstances. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfers timings. At Sonmarg, Gulmarg & Pahalgam the vehicles are allowed only up to the common parking lot. Thereafter one has to walk or hire ponies/ local vehicles for local conveyance on direct payment basis. Tour-program is subject to change depending upon circumstances Please note that only post paid mobile number works in Kashmir. Highlights of the package: Stay in Houseboat on Dal Lake Enjoy Shikara ride on Dal Lake till Char Chinar The Gondola Ride (Phase -1) At Gulmarg (Tickets are subject to availability).', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'JKDPEK', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Exotic Kashmir With Gulmarg Stay Durga Puja Special' package is a 7-day tour covering the scenic destinations of Srinagar, Pahalgam, and Gulmarg. The itinerary features unique experiences such as staying in a traditional houseboat on Dal Lake and enjoying a relaxing Shikara ride to Char Chinar. Additionally, participants will have the opportunity to experience the famous Phase-1 Gondola ride in Gulmarg, with tickets subject to availability, making for an unforgettable holiday in the valley.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': "\xa0\nArrival in Srinagar\n\xa0\nWelcome to Srinagar and transfer to the houseboat.\n\xa0\nCheck in to the houseboat and freshen up.\n\xa0\nEnjoy a romantic Shikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake (Kashmir's iconic jewel, a serene houseboat haven)\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the houseboat\xa0\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0Room heating facilities in houseboats are available depending on weather conditions.", 'mealDescription': 'Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - Khyber Houseboats or similar in Srinagar'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar to Pahalgam (90 Km / ~03 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the houseboat and check out.\n\xa0\nSrinagar sightseeing\n\nShankaracharya Temple (Dedicated to Lord Shiva)\nNishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens)\nPari Mahal (Palace of Fairies)\n\n\xa0\nDrive to Pahalgam (A picturesque valley surrounded by snow-capped mountains, offering stunning natural beauty and adventure opportunities)\n\xa0\nEn route visit\n\nPampore for saffron demonstration and shopping\nAvantipur Ruins (ancient temple complex)\n\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nCheck in at the hotel and relax.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Pahalgam at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - White Water Resorts or similar in Pahalgam\xa0'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel.\n\xa0\nFull Day city tour, visiting the below attractions\n\nBetaab Valley (Known for its picturesque beauty, made famous by the Bollywood movie "Betaab")\n\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nEnjoy leisure time, shopping at the local Pahalgam market – on your own.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay at the hotel in Pahalgam\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0Day excursion to Betaab is conducted by local taxis (Tavera/Sumo/Eeco) operating on a fixed schedule set by the Pahalgam Taxi Union.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': '\xa0\nHotel - White Water Resorts or similar in Pahalgam\xa0'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nPahalgam to Gulmarg (140Km / ~ 04 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel and check out.\n\xa0\nDrive to Gulmarg (Meadow of flowers)\n\xa0\nEn route visit,\n\nMartand Sun Temple (ancient ruins)\nKashmiri Cricket Bat Factory (Witness the craftsmanship of world-renowned cricket bats made from Kashmir willow)\n\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nCheck in at the hotel and relax.\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Gulmarg at the hotel.\n\xa0\nNote :\n\nIn case of heavy rainfall/ Gulmarg is not operational due to any sort of Weather conditions, we\xa0 will take clients to Doodhpathri.\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket up to Phase 1 is part of the package and subject to availability as per the booking dates. Please be noted, that Gulmarg date can change since itinerary is subject to shuffling.\nIn Gulmarg - The Tour Vehicle only provides drop to the Gulmarg hotel. For local movement guest has to either hire the pony or local vehicle on direct payment basis.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel -\xa0Royal Park or Similar in\xa0Gulmarg\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\nGulmarg to Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 02 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel and check out.\n\xa0\nExperience the Gulmarg Gondola (Asia's highest cable car project)\n\xa0\nEnjoy panoramic views of the Pir Panjal Mountains and Valley.\n\xa0\nExperience sledge riding on snow – on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nEnroute visit\n\xa0\n\nHandloom Emporium on the way back to Srinagar.\n\n\xa0\nDrive to Srinagar\n\xa0\nCheck in to the hotel and relax\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel.\n\xa0\nImportant Notice: Gulmarg Gondola Ride Ticket Booking\n\xa0\n\nGulmarg Gondola Ticket is complimentary but not guaranteed as it is booked basis availability exclusively on the Jammu & Kashmir Cable Car Corporation’s portal [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing options Plus the refund of Gondola Ticket Price as per actual to the guest.\nGondola Ticket availability is very limited and demand is very high and more so in summer peak times. Moreover, the opening time of these slots is neither pre-decided nor fixed, making the booking process even more challenging.\nGuests can also try and book Tatkal tickets directly at the Gondola ticket windows [https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com]\nThough we endeavor to provide Gondola ride to all our guests, in the event the tickets are not available, we will arrange alternative sightseeing Buta Pathri.\n", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner\n\xa0', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Paisley Palace or similar'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nSrinagar – Sonmarg – Srinagar (83 Km / ~ 2 hours drive)\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel.\n\xa0\nDrive to Sonmarg (Golden meadow)\n\xa0\nEnjoy riding on a pony up to Thajiwas Glacier- on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nEnjoy lunch, tea/coffee & snacks enroute.\n\xa0\nOptional: Sledge or snowmobile ride – on direct payment basis\n\xa0\nDinner and overnight stay in Srinagar at the hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast , Lunch & Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Paisley Palace or similar'}, {'day': 7, 'description': '\xa0\nDepart\n\xa0\nMorning breakfast at the hotel and check out.\n\xa0\nProceed to the airport for your onward journey, taking with you cherished memories of your Kashmir experience.\n\xa0\nNote:\xa0As this is a group tour, the airport transfer departs from the Srinagar hotel at 10:00 AM.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 45700.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 06; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\n\xa0'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['\nVehicles as per group size on Sharing basis (6 Pax in Innova; 10 in Tempo Traveller; Vehicle Type Cannot be confirmed at the time of Booking)\nVehicle is not at disposal – means it is for transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\nSeats Allotment in the Vehicle is on first come first serve basis at the venue, irrespective of the booking dates.\n'], 'sightseeing': ['Srinagar\n\nShikara ride on the enchanting Char Chinar Dal lake\n\nNishat Bagh (Mughal Gardens)\nPari Mahal (Palace of Fairies)\n\nPahalgam\n\nPampore\nAvantipur Ruins\nBetaab Valley\nChandanwari\nMartand Sun Temple\nKashmiri Cricket Bat Factory\xa0\n\nGulmarg\n\nGondola\nHandloom Emporium\xa0\n\n\xa0', 'As per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 25 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '', 'inclusions': 'Hotels:\n\nTwin sharing basis in the listed hotels or similar\n\nMeals:\n\nBreakfasts: 06; Lunches: 05; Dinners: 06\nBreakfast & Dinners will be Buffet\nLunches will be enroute in a restaurant/hotel or packed\nExtra Toppings: Snacks with coffee, tea, or a cold drink once during the day\n\nAdditional Inclusions:\n\nRound-trip economy class airfare\nWater: 500 ml water per person per day\n\nInsurance\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAirfare not included for joining direct passengers\nAdditional / personal use of vehicle.\nAny personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral water, alcoholic & non alcoholic beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc.\nAny extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary.\nCamera fees\nAny incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions.\nGST will be applicable as per prevailing rates\n\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': '\nThe tour price printed is dynamic & is purely on first come first serve basis. The person booking tour early is likely to get the lowest price as communicated / offered by the Company, subject to availability of seats\nIt is mandatory to carry photo ID card (except Pan Card) while you are on tour. Valid ID for Kashmir: Driving License/ Voter ID/Passport/Aadhar Card\nThe vehicle used for transfers is not at disposal.\nThis is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon circumstances. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfers timings.\nAt Sonmarg, Gulmarg & Pahalgam the vehicles are allowed only up to the common parking lot. Thereafter one has to walk or hire ponies/ local vehicles for local conveyance on direct payment basis.\nTour-program is subject to change depending upon circumstances\nPlease note that only post paid mobile number works in Kashmir\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/AdobeStock_362192710.jpeg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/Dallake.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/AdobeStock_296897404.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/AdobeStock_1062426595.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/7162146702_b896312393_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/gondola.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/49943812578_6f76e97314_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014983/itinerary/kashmir8.jpg']}, 'score': 3.5751948, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG014974', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG014974', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Char Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yamunotri', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Gangotri', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kedarnath', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Badrinath', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Evening Arti Dardhan at Badrinath. Palki (Sedan Chair) at Yamunotri. Priority Darshan at Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath and Badrinath Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun'], 'pdfName': 'PKG014974_0_20261005150447', 'price': 242500, 'packageSummary': "The 'Char Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay' package is a 6-day tour covering Dehradun, Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. The itinerary features priority darshan at all four sacred sites, including Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. Participants will experience a special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath, attend the evening Arti Darshan at Badrinath, and utilize a palki (sedan chair) at Yamunotri, all while being assisted by a professional tour manager stationed in Dehradun.", 'images': ['deharadun2.jpg', '41508974401_6ab3074e15_b.jpg', 'gangotri_Dham.jpg', '49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'Badrinath.jpg', 'badrinath-1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 242500, 'thumbnailImage': '49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Summer GIT', 'Heli Yatra', 'Domestic Winter GIT', 'Family', 'Spiritual'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG014974 is named 'Char Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dehradun, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive Dehradun: Upon arrival at Dehradun Airport, you will be transferred to your hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Yamunotri, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Dehradun to Yamunotri : After breakfast, fly from Sahastradhara (Dehradun) to Kharsali (Yamunotri) by helicopter (Tentative flight time is scheduled after 11:30 AM). On arrival, check in to your hotel. Later, proceed for a guided darshan at Yamunotri by Palki (trip duration: approximately 5 hours). Upon your return, enjoy lunch at Kharsali and relax in your rooms., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Gangotri, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner., Description: Yamunotri to Gangotri : After breakfast, fly to Harsil. On arrival, check in to your hotel. Later, leave for Gangotri Temple by Innova car. Return to the hotel and, after lunch, enjoy the rest of the day at leisure amidst the beautiful surroundings., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Kedarnath, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner., Description: Gangotri - Sersi - Kedarnath : After breakfast, fly to Kedarnath. (There will be a stopover at Sersi/Phata/Sitapur for a helicopter changeover.) Upon arrival at Sersi/Phata/Sitapur, proceed to Shri Kedarnath Ji Dham. Later, you will be taken to the Kedarnath Temple for darshan and then return to the hotel. The rest of the day is at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Badrinath, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Kedarnath - Sersi - Badrinath : In the morning, return to Sersi/Phata/Sitapur and enjoy breakfast at the nearest hotel. Later, fly to Badrinath. On arrival, check in to your hotel. After lunch, proceed for a day trip to Mana Village. In the evening, visit the Badrinath Temple for darshan, then return to the hotel for dinner, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dehradun, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Badrinath - Dehradun : Breakfast at Hotel and proceed to Helipad for your return flight to Dehradun Note: Guests, who would like to book their return journeys from Dehradun, can book their flights/trains after 1800 hrs on the last day of tour. Registration: Please ensure that you have obtained your registration slip from https://registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in/ for your travel date. Permits will be issued accordingly and must be carried during the tour. Flights Booking: Guests should always book refundable air tickets to avoid situations where travel days need to be extended due to unavoidable circumstances. Baggage Capacity: Do Dham Yatra by helicopter, baggage capacity is strictly limited to 5 kg per person in duffel bag only Operation of Helicopter The yatra is operated in collaboration with third party helicopter operators. All flight operations are subject to weather conditions, government regulations,VVIP movements and other external factors beyond our control. Departure Timings Departure times are confirmed one day prior as per slots given by UCADA. Timings may change due to weather conditions, VVIP movements, or maintenance work. Tour Manager & Branding We have our own Tour Manager in Dehradun who conducts the Pre Yatra briefing with the partner’s team and sets expectations. Additionally, one Tour Manager is based at Kedarnath. Guests also usually see partner branding on the vehicles. Assisted Darshan All assisted darshan arrangements are subject to the Mandir Samiti and Uttarakhand Government. Due to heavy rush, even VIP darshan and special puja may involve a waiting time of 2–3 hours, especially at Kedarnath. Kedarnath Shuttle Passengers will land at Sitapur/Phata/Sersi helipad and receive a slot to fly to Kedarnath. Timings for these non scheduled flights are provided upon arrival. Guests should expect a waiting period of 3–4 hours depending on ground situations. Slot Information As per our contracting, Guest fly in the second slot (after 1100 Hours) for Kedarnath stay/ Do Dham packages, Depending on the weather conditions. This sometimes gives impression that operator is giving preference to the other guest. Bad Weather Situation at Kedarnath: Due to bad weather, is unable to return and gets stranded at Kedarnath, the customer will be required to make direct payment for their stay at Kedarnath. Seating and Capacity Each helicopter can accommodate 6 passengers with a maximum total weight of 450 kg. Booking 6 seats does not mean all passengers will travel together or that it will be a private charter. Body Weight Each passenger’s actual body weight must be provided at the time of booking. The average limit is under 75 kg per person. Passengers exceeding 75 kg should check with Operations Team for available dates and supplement cost. Weight Exceeds If the declared weight exceeds by more than 2 kg at the time of travel, the operator reserves the right to de board such guests, and the amount paid will be non refundable. Helipads Multiple helipads are available for flights to Kedarnath, including Sersi, Phata, Guptkashi, and Sitapur. Guests may board from any of these locations. Facilities: Please note that heaters and blowers are not available in the hotels during Yatra. Guests are advised to carry adequate warm clothing to stay comfortable during their stay. VIP Darshan: All VIP Darshan arrangements are entirely at the discretion of the Mandir Samiti and the Uttarakhand Government., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 242500.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\nCity\nNo of Night\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\n1N\nHyatt Regency\xa0\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\n1N\nHotel Yamunakriti\xa0/ Similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\n1N\nKhili Resort/Similar\n\n\nKedarnath\n1N\nGayatri Sadan/Similar\n\n\nBadrinath\n1N\nDikesh Inn/Similar\n\n\n, \n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\nHyatt Regency or similar\n\n\nKharsali (Yamnotri)\nHotel Yamunakriti or similar\n\n\nDharali/Harsil (Gangotri)\nHimalayan Nature Resort /Similar\n\n\nSersi (Kedarnath)\nGayatri Sadan/Similar\n\n\nBadrinath\nSarovar Portico/Similar\n\n\n. Meals include: \nMeals as mentioned in the itinerary. Note: Veg meals on fixed menu.\nAll Meal (Expect Lunch At Dehradun)\n, \nMeals as mentioned in the itinerary. Note: Veg meals on fixed menu.\nAll Meals ( Except Lunch At Dehradun)\n. Inclusions: Helicopter trip starts from Dehradun. Accommodation in the hotels listed or similar. Meals as mentioned in the itinerary. Note: Veg meals on fixed menu. Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun All Meal (Expect Lunch at Dehradun) Government Royalty Fee Duffel Bag to each passenger Palki (Sedan Chair) at Yamunotri. Priority Darshan Assistance at Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath & Badrinath. Special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Evening Arti Darshan at Badrinath. All local transport as per Toyota Innova/ Best available vehicle Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Rates are subject to change in case of any major hike in fuel prices. Train fare/ Airfare Travel insurance covering medical evacuation, hospitalization, air evacuation, baggage insurance and trip cancellation. Any optional trips other than specified in the program. Any en-route or personal expenses such as alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages, telephone calls, tips & gratuities, laundry etc. Personal equipment like clothes, shoes, daypacks, personal medical kit etc. Any exigency expenses due to reasons beyond our normal control Any personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral waters alcoholic & non-alcoholic, beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc. Any extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary. Camera fees, guide charges Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions. Government Service Tax (GST). Product Terms and Conditions: N/A. Highlights of the package: Special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Evening Arti Dardhan at Badrinath. Palki (Sedan Chair) at Yamunotri. Priority Darshan at Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath and Badrinath Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'CHBHKS', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Char Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay' package is a 6-day tour covering Dehradun, Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. The itinerary features priority darshan at all four sacred sites, including Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath. Participants will experience a special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath, attend the evening Arti Darshan at Badrinath, and utilize a palki (sedan chair) at Yamunotri, all while being assisted by a professional tour manager stationed in Dehradun.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrive Dehradun:\n\xa0\nUpon arrival at Dehradun Airport, you will be transferred to your hotel.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Hyatt Regency or similar\xa0'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nDehradun to Yamunotri :\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, fly from Sahastradhara (Dehradun) to Kharsali (Yamunotri) by helicopter (Tentative flight time is scheduled after 11:30 AM). On arrival, check in to your hotel. Later, proceed for a guided darshan at Yamunotri by Palki (trip duration: approximately 5 hours). Upon your return, enjoy lunch at Kharsali and relax in your rooms.\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Yamunakriti\xa0or similar'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nYamunotri to Gangotri :\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, fly to Harsil. On arrival, check in to your hotel. Later, leave for Gangotri Temple by Innova car. Return to the hotel and, after lunch, enjoy the rest of the day at leisure amidst the beautiful surroundings.', 'mealDescription': '\xa0\nBreakfast, Lun