 baggage insurance and trip cancellation.\nAny optional trips other than specified in the program.\nAny en-route or personal expenses such as alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages, telephone calls, tips & gratuities, laundry etc.\nPersonal equipment like clothes, shoes, daypacks, personal medical kit etc.\nAny exigency expenses due to reasons beyond our normal control\nAny personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral waters alcoholic & non-alcoholic, beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc.\nAny extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary.\nCamera fees, guide charges\nAny incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions.\nGovernment Service Tax (GST)\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '', 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/itinerary/deharadun2.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/itinerary/41508974401_6ab3074e15_b.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/itinerary/gangotri_Dham.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/itinerary/49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/itinerary/Badrinath.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014974/itinerary/badrinath-1.jpg']}, 'score': 3.5751948, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013799', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013799', 'availableMonths': ['october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Do Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay 3N - Value', 'days': 4, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kedarnath', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Badrinath', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Sandhya Arti at Badrinath. Priority Darshan at Kedarnath & Badrinath. Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun & Kedarnath'], 'pdfName': 'PKG013438_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 158500, 'packageSummary': "The 'Do Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay 3N - Value' package is a 4-day tour covering Dehradun, Kedarnath, Badrinath, and returning to Dehradun. This spiritual journey offers participants priority Darshan at both Kedarnath and Badrinath, along with a special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath and the opportunity to attend the serene Sandhya Arti at Badrinath. Throughout the pilgrimage, travelers will be assisted by a professional tour manager stationed in Dehradun and Kedarnath to ensure a seamless and comfortable experience.", 'images': ['AdobeStock_72508860.jpeg', '49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'AdobeStock_64774614_BadrinathTemple.jpg', 'AdobeStock_43933130_Rudraprayag.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 158500, 'thumbnailImage': '6268475484_f559126411_k.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Heli Yatra', 'Spiritual', 'Domestic Winter GIT', 'Family', 'Summer GIT'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG013799 is named 'Do Dham Yatra By Helicopter With Kedarnath Stay 3N - Value' and spans 4 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dehradun, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrived Dehradun: Upon arrival at Dehradun airport, you will transfer to hotel. Dinner and Overnight stay at the hotel., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kedarnath, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner, Description: Dehradun - Sersi – Kedarnath : Today fly to Kedarnath Via Sersi. (Tentative flight time is scheduled after 12:00 PM, There will be a Stopover at Sersi/Phata and Changeover of Helicopter) Arrive at Kedarnath Helipad and proceed for Shri Kedarnath Ji Dham Darshan. Rest of the day at leisure., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Badrinath, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Kedarnath - Sersi -Badrinath: After Breakfast relax at hotel. Later fly to Badrinath. After check-in, Lunch & proceed for a Day Trip to Mana Village. Evening visit to Badrinath Temple for the Darshan & Evening back to Hotel Dinner., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Dehradun, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Badrinath - Dehradun - Departure: Today back to Dehradun. On arrival at Dehradun, we will collect the luggage from the hotel at Dehradun and drop pilgrims to the airport/ railway station. Note – Guests who would like to book their return journeys from Dehradun can book their flights/trains after 1800 hrs. on the last day of the tour. Registration: Please ensure that you have obtained your registration slip from https://registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in/ for your travel date. Permits will be issued accordingly and must be carried during the tour. Flights Booking Guests should always book refundable air tickets to avoid situations where travel days need to be extended due to unavoidable circumstances. Baggage Capacity: Do Dham Yatra by helicopter, baggage capacity is strictly limited to 3 kg per person in duffel bag only Operation of Helicopter The yatra is operated in collaboration with third party helicopter operators. All flight operations are subject to weather conditions, government regulations,VIP movements and other external factors beyond our control. Departure Timings Departure times are confirmed one day prior as per slots given by UCADA. Timings may change due to weather conditions, VVIP movements, or maintenance work. Tour Manager & Branding We have our own Tour Manager in Dehradun who conducts the Pre Yatra briefing with the partner’s team and sets expectations. Additionally, one Tour Manager is based at Kedarnath. Guests also usually see partner branding on the vehicles. Assisted Darshan All assisted darshan arrangements are subject to the Mandir Samiti and Uttarakhand Government. Due to heavy rush, even VIP darshan and special puja may involve a waiting time of 2–3 hours, especially at Kedarnath. Kedarnath Shuttle Passengers will land at Sitapur/Phata/Sersi helipad and receive a slot to fly to Kedarnath. Timings for these non scheduled flights are provided upon arrival. Guests should expect a waiting period of 3–4 hours depending on ground situations. Slot Information As per our contracting, Guest fly in the second slot (after 1100 Hours) for Kedarnath stay/ Do Dham packages, Depending on the weather conditions. This sometimes gives impression that operator is giving preference to the other guest. Seating and Capacity Each helicopter can accommodate 6 passengers with a maximum total weight of 450 kg. Booking 6 seats does not mean all passengers will travel together or that it will be a private charter. Body Weight Each passenger’s actual body weight must be provided at the time of booking. The average limit is under 75 kg per person. Passengers exceeding 75 kg should check with Operations Team for available dates and supplement cost. Weight Exceeds If the declared weight exceeds by more than 2 kg at the time of travel, the operator reserves the right to de board such guests, and the amount paid will be non refundable. Helipads Multiple helipads are available for flights to Kedarnath, including Sersi, Phata, Guptkashi, and Sitapur. Guests may board from any of these locations. Facilities: Please note that heaters and blowers are not available in the hotels during Yatra. Guests are advised to carry adequate warm clothing to stay comfortable during their stay. VIP Darshan: All VIP Darshan arrangements are entirely at the discretion of the Mandir Samiti and the Uttarakhand Government., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 158500.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun\nFairfield by Marriot or Similar\n\n\nKedarnath\nPunjab Sindh/Gayatri Bhawan or Similar\n\n\nBadrinath\nSarovar Portico /Similar\n\n\n, \n\n\nCity\nHotel Name\n\n\nDehradun 1N\nHyatt Regency or Similar\n\n\nKedarnath 1N\nGayatri Bhawan\xa0or Similar\n\n\nBadrinath 1N\nHotel Dikesh Inn or Similar\n\n\n. Meals include: \nMeal Information: All meals provided are vegetarian.\nPacked Breakfast: Options include a sandwich, paratha, poori with dry bhaji, or poha.\nBreakfast: Served with tea/coffee, paratha with curd, poori bhaji, or upma/poha (0730-1000 Hrs).\nLunch & Dinner: Includes salad, one seasonal vegetable, One Dal, One Paneer Dish, Roti, and Rice.\n. Inclusions: Helicopter trip starts from Dehradun. Accommodation in the hotels listed or similar. Meals as mentioned in the itinerary. Note: Veg meals on fixed menu. All Meal (Except Lunch at Dehradun) Special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Priority Darshan Kedarnath and Badrinath. (Subject to government/Mandir Samiti approval) Government Royalty Fee All local transport as per Toyota Innova/ Best available vehicle in Badrinath Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Rates are subject to change in case of any major hike in fuel prices. Train fare/ Airfare Travel insurance covering medical evacuation, hospitalization, air evacuation, baggage insurance and trip cancellation. Any optional trips other than specified in the program. Any en-route or personal expenses such as alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages, telephone calls, tips & gratuities, laundry etc. Personal equipment like clothes, shoes, daypacks, personal medical kit etc. Any exigency expenses due to reasons beyond our normal control Any personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral waters alcoholic & non-alcoholic, beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc. Any extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary. Camera fees, guide charges Any incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions. Product Terms and Conditions: Registration: Mandatory Registration: Please ensure you have your registration slip from https://registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in/ for your travel date. Permits will be issued accordingly. Body Weight: Weight Requirements: Each passenger's actual body weight is needed at booking. The average limit is under 75 kg per person. Passengers exceeding 75 kg should check with Operations for available dates. Additional charges of Rs. 2500/- per kg plus GST apply for weights over 75 kg. Please note, if actual weight exceeds the informed weight, the operator may need to de-board passengers. Charges are non-refundable. Seating and Capacity: Seating Capacity: Each helicopter can accommodate up to 6 passengers with a maximum total weight of 450 kg. Departure Timings: Timing Confirmation: Departure times will be confirmed one day prior and may change due to weather conditions, VVIP movements, or maintenance work. Kedarnath Darshan: Visit to Kedarnath: Passengers will land at Phata/Sirsi Helipad and receive a slot to fly to Kedarnath. Timings for these non-scheduled flights will be provided upon arrival at Phata/Sirsi. Please expect a waiting period of 2-4 hours depending on ground situations. Luggage Allowance: Luggage: Each passenger is allowed a maximum of 5 kg for Chardham and 3 kg for Do Dham Yatra. Facilities: Heater or Blower: Please note that heaters and blowers are not available in the hotels during the Yatra. Meals: Meal Information: All meals provided are vegetarian. Packed Breakfast: Options include a sandwich, paratha, poori with dry bhaji, or poha. Breakfast: Served with tea/coffee, paratha with curd, poori bhaji, or upma/poha (0730-1000 Hrs). Lunch & Dinner: Includes salad, one seasonal vegetable, one dal, one paneer dish, roti, and rice. Things To Note Govt. Service Tax (GST) extra on total billing. Maximum 06 Passengers/Guest will be allowed in 01 Helicopter. Only 5 kg luggage per passenger will be permitted due to limited space in the helicopter. Passengers bringing excess baggage would not be allowed to take the same in the chopper. At any cost we won’t allow passenger to take more luggage. This is the standard rule for Aviation. All temples are located at high altitude areas. Passengers are advice to carry regular medical kit. Passengers should carry only handbags (Soft Bags/duffle bags) as suitcases cannot be kept in the helicopter. Trolleys are not allowed. Every any person beyond 75 Kg extra charges will be applicable. Total passengers weight should not be more than 420 Kgs. Please share your actual body weight at the time of Booking. Your body weight will be measured before your departure. Photo ID card mandatory while you are on tour (Pan Card not valid) A/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive. Person With Asthma Or Any Health Problems Need To Get A Medical Check Up And To Travel On advise Of The Doctor. Bottle of Oxygen available at medical shops. Can be arranged at extra cost if required. Children above the age of 2 years will be considered full ticket. There is no provision of concession to children or senior citizens for helicopter yatra. The booking has to be done in advance with a deposit of 50% of the charter amount. Remaining 50% amount to be paid 15 Days before the journey starts. In case the journey is not finished within the given time and passengers would not be able to Dham due to bad weather conditions/technical reasons. In this scenario company will still try to visit the all dham by extending the timeframe. Company will do all the dhams on the next day if weather condition remains poor whole day. Prices will remain same even in case the royalty fees changes or remains same. Any Extra Night due to bad weather will be borne by client itself. Payment and Cancellation Terms: To book and confirm your tour, we request you to deposit 25% advance. Balance amount to be paid before 30 days prior to the commencement of the tour Full payment has to be paid at least 30 days prior to departure. For bookings less than 30 days prior to date of departure, full money is to be paid at the time of booking. Tickets & Tour Documents would be issued 4 days prior to date of departure. Cancellation: Please note Cancellation request needs to reach us in writing. Any amendment received after booking will be treated as cancellation. The Cancellation policy is as follows: Cancellation / Amendment notice received Cancellation Charges per person Up to 30 days prior to date of departure Rs. 30000 In between 0 to 30 Days - No Refund 100% of the total package cost Other terms & conditions would be applicable as mentioned on our ‘Booking Form’. Do’s: Document: Carry one Id proof for yatra About Food: Drink Mineral water en route yatra. Avoid oily food; eat as you comfortable for walk Fitness: Yamunotri trek (12km) & Kedarnath ji(42kms round trek) ; therefore fitness is required. Anybody can join this Yatra if they think themselves fit and have strong willpower. People suffering from cardiac or respiratory problems should consult to their doctor. Morning and evening walks, jogging, stretching, meditation and regular exercise make the journey comfortable for all. Clothing’s: As the temperature varies greatly between day and night (from max. 20 degrees Celsius to min. -16 degrees Celsius) one should prepare accordingly. Clothing’s for both extremes of climate and temperature. While driving to Chardham Yatra, it will be warm inside the vehicle and light clothing will be required, but as soon as you step out of the vehicle, warm clothing will be required to keep off the cold winds of the Himalayas. Evening will be generally cold and warm clothing will be required. Bring the following items with you: Woolen gloves, Balaclava, Sun hat, Thermal wear, Water bottle, Woolen socks, Towel, Light Jacket, Sunglasses, Sun cream, Torch with extra batteries/bulbs, Muffler, Mask, Raincoat, Sweater, Shirt/T-shirt & Trekking shoes Attitude Sickness :- This is an environment related condition that can effect anyone who ascends too rapidly to high elevations without acclimatizing properly and also consult your doctor Health Consideration: - All Tourist We do ask you to bring along your own small first aid kit (available at Pharmacies). Some of the items we ask you to bring in the kit are: Antiseptic cream or Wound disinfectant: Iodine and tube-squeeze cream. Foot care and Blister Treatment, band-aids, adhesive roll & strips, gauze pads, moleskin. (Please bring ankle high boots to avoid muscle sprain.) Responsibility:- All arrangements within Chardham Yatra, reserves by us the right to change itineraries without prior notice, depending on the weather and road condition. Insurance: - We recommend that you insure yourself against sickness, EMERGENCY RESCUE, accident Hospitalization, etc. We are not liable and responsible for any damages or extra expenses that may arise from mishaps and the loss of their belongings during the pilgrimage. Bad Weather Situation: If you are stuck in a bad weather situation on any particular day out of the 5 days we will still try to finish the darshan on next day . In case we are completely unable to visit any dham due to bad weather situation we will refund proportionate money. This means that if due to any reason we are unable to do 2 dhams then we will refund 50% payment. If unable to do 3 Dhams then we will refund 75% and so on. Highlights of the package: Special Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath. Sandhya Arti at Badrinath. Priority Darshan at Kedarnath & Badrinath. Professional Tour Manager stationed in Dehradun & Kedarnath.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'DYHKVL', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {