onal trips other than specified in the program.\nAny en-route or personal expenses such as alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages, telephone calls, tips & gratuities, laundry etc.\nPersonal equipment like clothes, shoes, daypacks, personal medical kit etc.\nAny exigency expenses due to reasons beyond our normal control\nAny personal expenses, room service & special orders, mineral waters alcoholic & non-alcoholic, beverages, porterage, tips, phone calls, laundry etc.\nAny extra excursions or sightseeing apart from the above specified itinerary.\nCamera fees, guide charges\nAny incidental and other expenses which are not specified in the inclusions\n', 'termsAndConditions': "Registration:\nMandatory Registration: Please ensure you have your registration slip from https://registrationandtouristcare.uk.gov.in/ for your travel date. Permits will be issued accordingly.\n\xa0\nBody Weight:\nWeight Requirements: Each passenger's actual body weight is needed at booking. The average limit is under 75 kg per person. Passengers exceeding 75 kg should check with Operations for available dates. Additional charges of Rs. 2500/- per kg plus GST apply for weights over 75 kg. Please note, if actual weight exceeds the informed weight, the operator may need to de-board passengers. Charges are non-refundable.\n\xa0\nSeating and Capacity:\nSeating Capacity: Each helicopter can accommodate up to 6 passengers with a maximum total weight of 450 kg.\n\xa0\nDeparture Timings:\nTiming Confirmation: Departure times will be confirmed one day prior and may change due to weather conditions, VVIP movements, or maintenance work.\n\xa0\nKedarnath Darshan:\nVisit to Kedarnath: Passengers will land at Phata/Sirsi Helipad and receive a slot to fly to Kedarnath. Timings for these non-scheduled flights will be provided upon arrival at Phata/Sirsi. Please expect a waiting period of 2-4 hours depending on ground situations.\n\xa0\nLuggage Allowance:\nLuggage: Each passenger is allowed a maximum of 5 kg for Chardham and 3 kg for Do Dham Yatra.\n\xa0\nFacilities:\nHeater or Blower: Please note that heaters and blowers are not available in the hotels during the Yatra.\n\xa0\nMeals:\nMeal Information: All meals provided are vegetarian.\nPacked Breakfast: Options include a sandwich, paratha, poori with dry bhaji, or poha.\nBreakfast: Served with tea/coffee, paratha with curd, poori bhaji, or upma/poha (0730-1000 Hrs).\nLunch & Dinner: Includes salad, one seasonal vegetable, one dal, one paneer dish, roti, and rice.\xa0\n\xa0\nThings\xa0To Note\n\nGovt. Service Tax (GST) extra on total billing.\nMaximum 06 Passengers/Guest will be allowed in 01 Helicopter.\nOnly 5 kg luggage per passenger will be permitted due to limited space in the helicopter. Passengers bringing excess baggage would not be allowed to take the same in the chopper. At any cost we won’t allow passenger to take more luggage. This is the standard rule for Aviation.\nAll temples are located at high altitude areas. Passengers are advice to carry regular medical kit.\nPassengers should carry only handbags (Soft Bags/duffle bags) as suitcases cannot be kept in the helicopter. Trolleys are not allowed.\nEvery any person beyond 75 Kg extra charges will be applicable.\nTotal passengers weight should not be more than 420 Kgs.\nPlease share your actual body weight at the time of Booking. Your body weight will be measured before your departure.\nPhoto ID card mandatory while you are on tour (Pan Card not valid)\nA/c in Vehicle will be switched off during hilly drive.\nPerson With Asthma Or Any Health Problems Need To Get A Medical Check Up And To Travel On advise Of The Doctor. Bottle of Oxygen available at medical shops. Can be arranged at extra cost if required.\nChildren above the age of 2 years will be considered full ticket.\nThere is no provision of concession to children or senior citizens for helicopter yatra.\nThe booking has to be done in advance with a deposit of 50% of the charter amount.\nRemaining 50% amount to be paid 15 Days before the journey starts.\nIn case the journey is not finished within the given time and passengers would not be able to Dham due to bad weather conditions/technical reasons. In this scenario company will still try to visit the all dham by extending the timeframe. Company will do all the dhams on the next day if weather condition remains poor whole day.\nPrices will remain same even in case the royalty fees changes or remains same.\nAny Extra Night due to bad weather will be borne by client itself.\n\n\xa0\nPayment and Cancellation Terms:\n\nTo book and confirm your tour, we request you to deposit 25% advance. Balance amount to be paid before 30 days prior to the commencement of the tour Full payment has to be paid at least 30 days prior to departure.\nFor bookings less than 30 days prior to date of departure, full money is to be paid at the time of booking.\nTickets & Tour Documents would be issued 4 days prior to date of departure.\n\n\xa0\nCancellation:\n\nPlease note Cancellation request needs to reach us in writing.\xa0\nAny amendment received after booking will be treated as cancellation.\xa0\nThe Cancellation policy is as follows:\n\n\n\n\nCancellation / Amendment notice received\nCancellation Charges per person\n\n\nUp to 30 days prior to date of departure\nRs. 30000\xa0\n\n\nIn between 0 to 30 Days - No Refund\n100% of the total package cost\xa0\n\n\n\nOther terms & conditions would be applicable as mentioned on our ‘Booking Form’.\n\xa0\nDo’s:\nDocument: Carry one Id proof for yatra\n\xa0\nAbout Food: Drink Mineral water en route yatra. Avoid oily food; eat as you comfortable for walk\n\xa0\nFitness: Yamunotri trek (12km) & Kedarnath ji(42kms round trek) ; therefore fitness is required. Anybody can join this Yatra if they think themselves fit and\nhave strong willpower. People suffering from cardiac or respiratory problems should consult to their doctor. Morning and evening walks, jogging,\nstretching, meditation and regular exercise make the journey comfortable for all.\n\xa0\nClothing’s: As the temperature varies greatly between day and night (from max. 20 degrees Celsius to min. -16 degrees Celsius) one should prepare accordingly. Clothing’s for both extremes of climate and temperature. While driving to Chardham Yatra, it will be warm inside the vehicle and light clothing will be required, but as soon as you step out of the vehicle, warm clothing will be required to keep off the cold winds of the Himalayas. Evening will be generally cold and warm clothing will be required.\n\xa0\nBring the following items with you: Woolen gloves, Balaclava, Sun hat, Thermal wear, Water bottle, Woolen socks, Towel, Light Jacket, Sunglasses, Sun cream, Torch with extra batteries/bulbs, Muffler, Mask, Raincoat, Sweater, Shirt/T-shirt & Trekking shoes\n\xa0\nAttitude Sickness :- This is an environment related condition that can effect anyone who ascends too rapidly to high elevations without acclimatizing properly and also consult your doctor\n\xa0\nHealth Consideration: - All Tourist We do ask you to bring along your own small first aid kit (available at Pharmacies). Some of the items we ask you to bring in the kit are: Antiseptic cream or Wound disinfectant: Iodine and tube-squeeze cream. Foot care and Blister Treatment, band-aids, adhesive roll & strips, gauze pads, moleskin. (Please bring ankle high boots to avoid muscle sprain.)\n\xa0\nResponsibility:- All arrangements within Chardham Yatra, reserves by us the right to change itineraries without prior notice, depending on the weather and road condition.\n\xa0\nInsurance: - We recommend that you insure yourself against sickness, EMERGENCY RESCUE, accident\nHospitalization, etc. We are not liable and responsible for any damages or extra expenses that may arise from mishaps and the loss of their belongings during the pilgrimage.\n\xa0\nBad Weather Situation: If you are stuck in a bad weather situation on any particular day out of the 5 days we will still try to finish the darshan on next day . In case we are completely unable to visit any dham due to bad weather situation we will refund proportionate money. This means that if due to any reason we are unable to do 2 dhams then we will refund 50% payment. If unable to do 3 Dhams then we will refund 75% and so on", 'pkgSubtypeId': 1, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013799/6268475484_f559126411_k.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013799/itinerary/AdobeStock_72508860.jpeg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013799/itinerary/49976081921_bf1a474f20_k.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013799/itinerary/AdobeStock_64774614_BadrinathTemple.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013799/itinerary/AdobeStock_43933130_Rudraprayag.jpg']}, 'score': 3.150826, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015557', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015557', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'october_2026'], 'packageName': 'Super Deal Bali on Singapore Airlines – Multiple Hubs', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Kuta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ubud', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['SIGHTSEEINGS: Water Sports (Jet Ski, Banana Boat, Parasailing) Uluwatu temple Tour Ubud Tour ( Coffee Plantation, Celuk Mass Village) Swing by My Swing Bedugul Tour (Ulun Danu Temple) Tanah Lot Sunset'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 87700, 'packageSummary': "The 'Super Deal Bali on Singapore Airlines – Multiple Hubs' package is a 7-day tour covering the popular Balinese destinations of Ubud and Kuta. The itinerary features thrilling water sports like jet skiing, banana boat rides, and parasailing, as well as cultural highlights including the Uluwatu Temple tour and the Bedugul tour to see the Ulun Danu Temple. Travelers will also enjoy an Ubud tour with visits to a local coffee plantation and Celuk Mass Village, experience the famous Swing by My Swing, and witness a spectacular sunset at the iconic Tanah Lot temple.", 'images': ['Balicity.jpg', 'BaliAdventure.jpg', 'Uluwatu_Temple_753.jpg', 'Bali_1.jpg', 'Bali22.jpg', '47777_Ubud_Green_Rice_Bali753.jpg', 'Bali_Sunset_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 87700, 'thumbnailImage': 'BaliSRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015557 is named 'Super Deal Bali on Singapore Airlines – Multiple Hubs' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Kuta, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Ubud, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 87700.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \nKuta – 4 Nights at Grand Zuri / Kuta Central Park / Famous Hotel Kuta or similar\nUbud –2 Nights at Alam Puisi (One Room Pool Villa) or similar\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\n. Inclusions: Return Airfare (Singapore Airlines) 04 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Kuta 02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Ubud as per the selected city option Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Return airport transfers on private basis Inter Hotel Transfers Full Day Water sports (Jet Ski, Banana Boat, Parasailing) followed by Uluwatu temple Tour Transfer on PVT basis. Ubud tour with Swing by My Swing, Coffee Plantation, Celuk Mas Village on PVT Basis. Bedugul tour (Ulun Danu Temple) + Tanah Lot sunset. Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST. The rates are valid for a minimum of 2 adults travelling together at all times. Pre and post tour services & costs. Hotel rates not valid during blackout period / surcharge dates / stop sales. Blackout date surcharges – Midnight surcharge. Meals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary. Tips for guide & driver. City tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable). Expenditure of a personal nature (minibar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.) Camera fee. Porterage facility Departure PCR test, if applicable. Visa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable). Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of optional excursions. Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list. Note: In the Premium category for this Bali Product, Kuta stay will be at a 4-star hotel while Ubud stay will be at a 5-star hotel. Visa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) the charges are approximately USD 35-40 per person.. Product Terms and Conditions: The package price is valid. The rates are valid for a minimum of 2 adults travelling together at all times. Note: In the Premium category for this Bali Product, Kuta stay will be at a 4-star hotel while Ubud stay will be at a 5-star hotel. Hotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. Hotel upgrade pricing does not guarantee rooms at the preferred / envisaged hotels. Hotel upgrade rooms remain subject to availability at the time of booking. If the selected upgrade hotel is unavailable, we will provide multiple alternate options of a similar category. The rates are not valid on blackout dates & Trade fair periods. Any applicable surcharges will be communicated, and passengers will be required to pay them accordingly. Surcharges, if applicable, are additional to the total package price quoted at the time of booking. Guests are requested to confirm their onward/connecting flights with the sales team before booking. All rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400/1500 hours & Check out time is 1100/1200 hours respectively, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Wherever transfers are included, they are provided without night surcharges. No refunds (partial or full) will be provided for any unutilized services. All sightseeing tours and excursions are operated by local service providers; timings and operating days are subject to change. Changes or Updates, if any, will be shared at the time of booking. Sightseeing tours are strictly subject to weather conditions, and local service providers reserve the right to cancel tours without prior notice. Rates are subject to change without prior notice, including for clients travelling during weekends. Any promotional offer, if applicable, may be withdrawn at any time without prior notice. Once bookings are confirmed, cancellation charges will apply as per policy and will be informed at that time. Organization is not responsible for any price changes arising from factors beyond our control. A refundable security deposit is required at check-in as per international hotel policy, payable by credit card or cash; the amount varies by hotel and is returned at checkout. Guests should avoid using debit cards since the amount is charged instantly and may take 2–3 weeks to refund. Any additional hotel services (such as minibar, room service, etc.) may be deducted from this deposit, and Company is not responsible for such transactions, as these are directly between the hotel and the guest.. Highlights of the package: SIGHTSEEINGS: Water Sports (Jet Ski, Banana Boat, Parasailing) Uluwatu temple Tour Ubud Tour ( Coffee Plantation, Celuk Mass Village) Swing by My Swing Bedugul Tour (Ulun Danu Temple) Tanah Lot Sunset.", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Super Deal Bali on Singapore Airlines – Multiple Hubs' package is a 7-day tour covering the popular Balinese destinations of Ubud and Kuta. The itinerary features thrilling water sports like jet skiing, banana boat rides, and parasailing, as well as cultural highlights including the Uluwatu Temple tour and the Bedugul tour to see the Ulun Danu Temple. Travelers will also enjoy an Ubud tour with visits to a local coffee plantation and Celuk Mass Village, experience the famous Swing by My Swing, and witness a spectacular sunset at the iconic Tanah Lot temple.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n.', 'mealDescription': '.', 'overnightStay': '.'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n.', 'mealDescription': '.', 'overnightStay': '.'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n.', 'mealDescription': '.', 'overnightStay': '.'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n.', 'mealDescription': '.', 'overnightStay': '.'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n.', 'mealDe