Id': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Bali - Buy 1 Get 1 Free' package is a 6-day getaway covering the beautiful destinations of Bali and Kuta. This special promotion features an exclusive Buy One Get One Free (BOGO) offer valid for two adults, where you pay for one person and your adult companion travels for free. Additionally, travelers can extend their tropical vacation with one complimentary night when booking a four-night stay, providing the perfect opportunity to enjoy the stunning beaches, vibrant local culture, and relaxing atmosphere of the region.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival in Bali\nArrival at the Ngurah Rai, Bali International Airport, meet & greet by our local guide who lead you to the parking area to board a vehicle for your transfer to your hotel. It takes about 20 minutes’ drive from airport to your hotel or more depending on the traffic.\n\xa0\nUpon arrival at the hotel, directly check in and freshen up.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Kuta', 'mealDescription': 'N/A', 'overnightStay': 'Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nBenoa Watersports Experience on Seat in Coach basis\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nExperience an action-packed day at Benoa Beach with exciting watersport activities on a shared (SIC) basis. The package includes 01x Jet Ski ride - (1 - 2 min), 01x Banana Boat ride (5 min), and 01x Couple Parasailing experience (1 - 2Min), offering the perfect mix of adventure, fun, and stunning coastal views.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Kuta\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFull Day Ubud & Kintamani Tour on Private Basis\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nProceed for a scenic full-day tour covering the cultural and natural highlights of Bali including:\n\xa0\n\nVisit to Celuk Village, famous for traditional silver and gold craftsmanship\nExperience authentic Balinese Coffee Plantation with local coffee tasting\nEnjoy panoramic views of Mount Batur and Kintamani Highlands\nExplore the artistic and cultural charm of Ubud region\n\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Kuta\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nLeisure & Shopping\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nFree day for shopping and exploring local markets, cafes, and beach areas.\n\xa0\nOvernight stay at Kuta\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nDay Free for Leisure\xa0\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\n\xa0\nFree day for leisure or opt from any optional activities.\nOvernight stay at Kuta\n\xa0', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nDeparture\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the Hotel\nPick up from the hotel to transfer to the Airport according to the scheduled Flight.\n\xa0\n\xa0\n* The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.\n\xa0\nEXTENSION NIGHTS\nTravel Validity: 01 - 24 JUN 2026 & 01 SEP - 15 DEC 2026 & 10 JAN - 24 MAR 2027\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n\n\nHOTELS\n\n\nPACKAGE COST:PER PERSON IN USD\n\n\n\n\nTWIN / DOUBLE\n\n\n\n\nValue\n\n\nGrand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar\n\n\n14\n\n\n\n\n\xa0\nTravel Validity: 01 July 2026 - 24 August 2026\n\n\n\n\nCATEGORY\n\n\nHOTELS\n\n\nPACKAGE COST:PER PERSON IN USD\n\n\n\n\nTWIN / DOUBLE\n\n\n\n\nValue\n\n\nGrand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar\n\n\n25\n\n\n\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ["Travel Validity: 10 JAN – 25 MAR 2026\n\n3 Night's Hotel\xa0Swissbell Inn\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Seminyak, Bali\n2 Night's Hotel\xa0Bali Spirit\xa0Ubud\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Ubud, Bali\n\n\xa0\nTravel Validity: 01 APR – 25 JUN 2026,\xa001 JULY – 25 AUG\xa0& 01 SEP – 25 SEP 2026\n\n3 Night's Hotel\xa0Primera Seminyak/Swissbell Inn Seminyak\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Seminyak, Bali\n2 Night's Hotel\xa0Champulang Ubud\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Ubud, Bali\n", '\n5N in\xa0Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta\n', "\n3 Night's Hotel\xa0Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Seminyak,\xa0Bali\n2 Night's Hotel\xa0Royal Casa Ganesha\xa0Or Similar in Ubud,\xa0Bali\n"], 'hotels_list': {'2': "\n3 Night's Hotel\xa0Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Seminyak,\xa0Bali\n2 Night's Hotel\xa0Royal Casa Ganesha\xa0Or Similar in Ubud,\xa0Bali\n", '1': '\n5N in\xa0Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta\n', '0': "Travel Validity: 10 JAN – 25 MAR 2026\n\n3 Night's Hotel\xa0Swissbell Inn\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Seminyak, Bali\n2 Night's Hotel\xa0Bali Spirit\xa0Ubud\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Ubud, Bali\n\n\xa0\nTravel Validity: 01 APR – 25 JUN 2026,\xa001 JULY – 25 AUG\xa0& 01 SEP – 25 SEP 2026\n\n3 Night's Hotel\xa0Primera Seminyak/Swissbell Inn Seminyak\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Seminyak, Bali\n2 Night's Hotel\xa0Champulang Ubud\xa0Or Similar in\xa0Ubud, Bali\n"}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 23700.0, 'hotels': ['\n5N in\xa0Grand Mega Resort / Harris Riverview Kuta or similar in Kuta\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['\nFull Day Kintamani Hot Spring Followed by Ubud Market On Pvt Basis.\xa0\nFull Day Benoa Water sports (01 Banana Boat + Jet Ski + Couple Parasailing) Followed By Sunset Tanah Lot Temple Tour On Pvt Basis.\n', '\nHalf Day Water Sports (1xJet Ski & 1xBanana Boat) at Tanjung Benoa on SIC Basis\xa0\xa0\nFull Day Ubud & Kintamani Tour Basis.\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\n05 night’s accommodation with breakfast\nReturn Airport Transfers on Private basis\nMeet & Greet assistance at the airport\xa0\nHalf Day Water Sports (1xJet Ski & 1xBanana Boat) at Tanjung Benoa on SIC Basis\xa0\xa0\nFull Day Ubud & Kintamani Tour Basis.\xa0\xa0\nMeals as mentioned in the itinerary.\nTravel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.)\n', 'exclusions': '\nTCS & GST\nVisa Charges\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable\xa0\nAll flights services\xa0\nEntrance fees\nBlack Out Date 15 Dec – 06 Jan Christmas & New Year, 12 Mar – 20 Mar Nyepi Day\xa0\nMeals not mentioned in the itinerary.\nAny tips - for guide & Driver\xa0\nAnything not mentioned in the inclusions.\nPre & Post tour services & cost\xa0\nExpenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc.)\nAll drink and beverages\xa0\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\xa0\nTourism Tax (if applicable)\nMidnight surcharge\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nVisa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) the charges are approximately USD 35-40 per person.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Package Terms and Conditions:\n\nThe package price is valid until as mentioned above.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nDuring Peak Season: Minimum 2 Nights Stay is required\nNo Check Out period on 31 December 2025 and 01 January 2026\nNyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 19 March 2026. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 19 March 2026 to 06.00 am 20 March 2026\nCompulsory New Year Dinner will be Applicable according to the Resort\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/Bali26713.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/itinerary/Balicity.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/itinerary/BaliAdventure.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/itinerary/Bali_Batur_Volcano_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/itinerary/bali5.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/itinerary/Bali7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014981/itinerary/Kintamani.jpg']}, 'score': 9.147675, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015272', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015272', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Bali with Yogyakarta and Jakarta - Winter', 'days': 9, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yogyakarta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Yogyakarta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Jakarta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Jakarta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Jakarta', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Guaranteed Departure – Minimum 2 Pax Required Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Dinners What’s More Like – One Souvenir per room Bali: Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset Visit Nusa Penida Island Enjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject to Weather Conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance Yogyakarta: Visit Borobdur Temple Visit Prambanan Temple Free time at Malioboro Market Jakarta: Visit Autograph Tower City Tour Visit Merdeka Square Photostop At National Monument Visit National Museum Visit Presidential Palace (Subject to Operation) Visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari Free time at Kuta Dua - Jakarta’s Old Town'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 125848, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Bali with Yogyakarta and Jakarta - Winter' package is a 9-day tour covering the vibrant Indonesian destinations of Bali, Yogyakarta, and Jakarta. This guaranteed-departure tour includes 4-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, travel insurance, specially curated Indian dinners, and a complimentary souvenir per room. In Bali, participants will experience the famous Bali Swing, visit the Tanah Lot Floating Temple at sunset, explore Nusa Penida Island, enjoy water sports at Tanjung Benoa, and witness the Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance. The itinerary also features visits to the historic Borobudur and Prambanan Temples in Yogyakarta, free time at Malioboro Market, and a comprehensive city tour of Jakarta that includes the Autograph Tower, Merdeka Square, the National Monument, the National Museum, the Jakarta Aquarium Safari, and Jakarta's Old Town.", 'images': ['Bali75309.jpg', 'TanahLotTemple75345.jpg', 'NusaPenida753.jpg', 'KeckDanace.jpg', 'Yogyakarta753.jpg', 'Yogyakarta7531.jpg', 'jakarta-D1.jpg', 'Museum753.jpg', 'Bali1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 125848, 'thumbnailImage': 'PrambananTempleYogyakarta2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG015272 is named \'Magical Bali with Yogyakarta and Jakarta - Winter\' and spans 9 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Bali, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Bali - Check In Welcome To Bali, Indonesia, One Of The Most Famous Destinations In The World For Holidays And Packages. Upon Arrival At Denpasar Airport, You Will Be Met By Our Representative/ Tour Manager Who Will Assist You For Your Transfer To The Hotel. On Arrival In Bali, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. Overnight in Bali. NOTE All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Experience Bali Swing - Tanah Lot Sunset Tour This morning after breakfast, proceed for an exciting adventure at Bali Swing and to experience incredible views while swinging. Later proceed to Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset – an ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves, the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons. Overnight in Bali, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Nusa Penida Island This morning after breakfast, Visit Nusa Penida Tour where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach - stunning cove features a dramatic archway in the rocky cliffs, creating a picturesque "broken" effect that opens up to the sparkling turquoise ocean below, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point - with its iconic T-rex shaped cliff, the beach offers stunning panoramic views of turquoise waters crashing against dramatic limestone formations., the natural pool of Angel\'s Billabong - is a stunning natural pool located on the western coast of Nusa Penida. This picturesque spot features crystal-clear turquoise waters that are surrounded by dramatic rocky cliffs. Overnight in Bali, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Enjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance This morning after breakfast, proceed to the Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski. (**Sports Activities subjected to weather conditions) Later proceed for Uluwatu Temple Tour explores Bali\'s iconic 11th-century sea temple perched 70 meters on a sheer cliff. Later this evening enjoy the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’ a stunning Balinese cultural performance set against the backdrop of a dramatic sunset by the Indian Ocean. Overnight in Bali., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Yogyakarta, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Fly to Yogyakarta This morning after breakfast reach Denpasar Airport for Flight to Yogyakarta, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the Yogyakarta airport. On arrival in Yogyakarta, Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. Overnight in Yogyakarta, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Yogyakarta, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Borobudur Temple – Visit Prambanan Temple – Free time at Malioboro Market This morning after breakfast proceed to Visit Borobudur Temple - the largest Buddhist temple in the world Constructed completely without glue or mortar, using an interlocking system. Later Visit Prambanan Temple is a 9th-century Hindu temple Built for the Trimurti deities (Shiva, Vishnu, and Brahma). In the evening enjoy your free time at Malioboro Market - the most famous shopping street and cultural heart of Yogyakarta. Overnight in Yogyakarta, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Jakarta, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Proceed to Jakarta by High-Speed Train - Check In – Evening visit Autograph Tower This morning after breakfast we will proceed to Jakarta by High-Speed Train. On arrival in Jakarta, Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Later in the evening visit Autograph Tower Jakarta- to enjoy unforgettable 360-degree views of Jakarta from Indonesia’s Tallest Observatory Deck. More than just a view, visit the Sky Garden a multi-level, semi-outdoor experience where visitors can explore immersive spaces and enjoy thrilling sky-high attractions (Glass Floors, UPswing, UPside, UP High). Overnight in Jakarta, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 8 - Jakarta, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: City Tour of Jakarta - Merdeka Square, National Museum, Presidential Palace – Visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari – Free time at Kuta Tua - Jakarta’s Old TownThis morning after breakfast we will explore the Merdeka Square (Independence Square), Photostop at National Monument, Visit National Museum, Visit Presidential Palace (Subject to operation). Later we visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari Indonesia\'s largest indoor living planet - where the mysteries of the ocean meet the excitement of a safari adventure. Later in the evening enjoy your free time at Kuta Tua - Jakarta’s Old Town the area is filled with historic buildings, museums, and open spaces that still preserve the atmosphere of old Jakarta. Overnight in Jakarta, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 9 - Jakarta, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 125848.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Kimaya Sudirman Yogyakarta by Harris / The Rich Hotel or similar in Yogyakarta\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n08 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Internal Airfare for Bali – Yogyakarta is included for all passengers including Joining Direct / NRI Passengers Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. Cost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 31 July 2026 Medical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. Meals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary Return Airport transfers from all airports. All transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If group size is less than 15 customers, the tour will operate on Seat in Coach and FIT basis. For Group Size more than 15 customers there will be English Speaking Guide Assistance and for less than 15 customers there will be Driver cum Guide.. Exclusions: Main Airfare is not Included Airport taxes Indonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival) Visa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable) The cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost. City Tax or Tourism Tax Cruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays) Cost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 31 July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure. The tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. General Info Currency used: Indonesia : Indonesian Rupiah Time difference: Indonesia: 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st June 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Cost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package. Hotels This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels.Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant. Coaches: Coaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. Meals: All Meals are pre–set. Packed lunches will be provided on certain days. Sightseeing: Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations.We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays,at the same time there may be delays caused due to over crowding ,local regulations ,security check etc. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the your initial part of you tour. Security alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching.THOMAS COOK will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. THOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour.All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Guaranteed Departure – Minimum 2 Pax Required Insurance 4 Star Hotels on Bed & Breakfast Basis Specially Curated Indian Jain / Veg / Non-Veg Dinners What’s More Like – One Souvenir per room Bali: Experience Bali Swing Visit Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset Visit Nusa Penida Island Enjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject to Weather Conditions) Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance Yogyakarta: Visit Borobdur Temple Visit Prambanan Temple Free time at Malioboro Market Jakarta: Visit Autograph Tower City Tour Visit Merdeka Square Photostop At National Monument Visit National Museum Visit Presidential Palace (Subject to Operation) Visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari Free time at Kuta Dua - Jakarta’s Old Town.', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZYJ560', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Bali with Yogyakarta and Jakarta - Winter' package is a 9-day tour covering the vibrant Indonesian destinations of Bali, Yogyakarta, and Jakarta. This guaranteed-departure tour includes 4-star hotel accommodations with breakfast, travel insurance, specially curated Indian dinners, and a complimentary souvenir per room. In Bali, participants will experience the famous Bali Swing, visit the Tanah Lot Floating Temple at sunset, explore Nusa Penida Island, enjoy water sports at Tanjung Benoa, and witness the Uluwatu Temple and Kecak Dance. The itinerary also features visits to the historic Borobudur and Prambanan Temples in Yogyakarta, free time at Malioboro Market, and a comprehensive city tour of Jakarta that includes the Autograph Tower, Merdeka Square, the National Monument, the National Museum, the Jakarta Aquarium Safari, and Jakarta's Old Town.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival In Bali - Check In\nWelcome To Bali, Indonesia, One Of The Most Famous Destinations In The World For Holidays And Packages. Upon Arrival At Denpasar Airport, You Will Be Met By Our Representative/ Tour Manager Who Will Assist You For Your Transfer To The Hotel.\nOn Arrival In Bali, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure.\n\xa0\nOvernight in Bali.\n\xa0\nNOTE\n\nAll our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card\nJoining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs.\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nExperience Bali Swing - Tanah Lot Sunset Tour\nThis morning after breakfast, proceed for an exciting adventure at Bali Swing and to experience incredible views while swinging.\nLater proceed to Tanah Lot Floating Temple for Sunset – an ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves, the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons.\nOvernight in Bali', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit Nusa Penida Island\nThis morning after breakfast, Visit Nusa Penida Tour where you’ll visit iconic spots like the stunning Broken Beach - stunning cove features a dramatic archway in the rocky cliffs, creating a picturesque "broken" effect that opens up to the sparkling turquoise ocean below, the awe-inspiring Kelingking Secret Point - with its iconic T-rex shaped cliff, the beach offers stunning panoramic views of turquoise waters crashing against dramatic limestone formations., the natural pool of Angel\'s Billabong - is a stunning natural pool located on the western coast of Nusa Penida.\n This picturesque spot features crystal-clear turquoise waters that are surrounded by dramatic rocky cliffs.\nOvernight in Bali', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nEnjoy Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa – Visit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\nThis morning after breakfast, proceed to the Tanjung Benoa near Nusa Dua Bali. Here you will enjoy the water sport activities included in your tour like - Banana boat, Parasailing and Jet Ski.\n(**Sports Activities subjected to weather conditions)\nLater proceed for Uluwatu Temple Tour explores Bali's iconic 11th-century sea temple perched 70 meters on a sheer cliff. Later this evening enjoy the Theatrical Fire Dance Show ‘Kecak Fire Dance’ a stunning Balinese cultural performance set against the backdrop of a dramatic sunset by the Indian Ocean.\nOvernight in Bali.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel or similar in Kuta, Bali'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nFly to Yogyakarta \nThis morning after breakfast reach Denpasar Airport for Flight to Yogyakarta, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the Yogyakarta airport. \xa0\nOn arrival in Yogyakarta, Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). \nRest of the day is at leisure.\nOvernight in Yogyakarta', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Kimaya Sudirman Yogyakarta by Harris / The Rich Hotel or similar in Yogyakarta'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Borobudur Temple – Visit Prambanan Temple – Free time at Malioboro Market\nThis morning after breakfast proceed to Visit Borobudur Temple - the largest Buddhist temple in the world Constructed completely without glue or mortar, using an interlocking system. Later Visit Prambanan Temple is a 9th-century Hindu temple Built for the Trimurti deities (Shiva, Vishnu, and Brahma).\nIn the evening enjoy your free time at Malioboro Market - the most famous shopping street and cultural heart of Yogyakarta.\nOvernight in Yogyakarta', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Kimaya Sudirman Yogyakarta by Harris / The Rich Hotel or similar in Yogyakarta'}, {'day': 7, 'description': 'Proceed to Jakarta by High-Speed Train - Check In – Evening visit Autograph Tower\nThis morning after breakfast we will proceed to Jakarta by High-Speed Train.\nOn arrival in Jakarta, Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs).\nLater in the evening visit Autograph Tower Jakarta- to enjoy unforgettable 360-degree views of Jakarta from Indonesia’s Tallest Observatory Deck. More than just a view, visit the Sky Garden a multi-level, semi-outdoor experience where visitors can explore immersive spaces and enjoy thrilling sky-high attractions (Glass Floors, UPswing, UPside, UP High).\nOvernight in Jakarta', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta'}, {'day': 8, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\n\xa0\nCity Tour of Jakarta - Merdeka Square, National Museum, Presidential Palace – Visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari – Free time at Kuta Tua - Jakarta’s Old TownThis morning after breakfast we will explore the Merdeka Square (Independence Square), Photostop at National Monument, Visit National Museum, Visit Presidential Palace (Subject to operation).\nLater we visit Jakarta Aquarium Safari Indonesia's largest indoor living planet - where the mysteries of the ocean meet the excitement of a safari adventure. Later in the evening enjoy your free time at Kuta Tua - Jakarta’s Old Town the area is filled with historic buildings, museums, and open spaces that still preserve the atmosphere of old Jakarta.\xa0\nOvernight in Jakarta", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta'}, {'day': 9, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning After Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Kimaya Sudirman Yogyakarta by Harris / The Rich Hotel or similar in Yogyakarta\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Kimaya Sudirman Yogyakarta by Harris / The Rich Hotel or similar in Yogyakarta\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n', '2': '\n2 nights accommodation in Hanoi with breakfast @ La Casa / Flower Garden\n1 night stay at Halong Bay on board the cruise Glory / Garden / Orchid Trendy Cruise\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Harmony / Bay / Eden\n3 nights accommodation with breakfast @ Memoir / Tara Angkor / Soma Devi\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'ID', 'countryName': 'Indonesia', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 125800.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel\xa0Harper Kuta Bali / Bliss Surfer Hotel / Sun Island\xa0or similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Kimaya Sudirman Yogyakarta by Harris / The Rich Hotel or similar in Yogyakarta\n02 Nights’ accommodation at Hotel Santika Premiere Hayam Wuruk / Aston Pluit & Residence or similar in Jakarta\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n08 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Bali\n\nExperience Bali Swing\nVisit Tanah Lot Floating Temple For Sunset\nEnjoy Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa - Banana Boat, Parasailing And Jet Ski (Parasailing Subject To Weather Conditions)\xa0\nVisit Uluwatu Temple & Kecak Dance\n\nYogyakarta\n\nVisit Borobdur Temple\xa0\nVisit Prambanan Temple\n\nOr\n\nTaman Sari Water Castle\nMount Merapi Jeep Lava Tour\nMalioboro Market\n\n\xa0\nJakarta\n\nCity Tour\xa0\nVisit Merdeka Square\nPhotostop At National Monument\nVisit National Museum\nVisit Presidential Palace (Subject To Operation).\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li><strong>Main Airfare is not included&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li>Internal Airfare for Bali &ndash; Yogyakarta is included for all passengers including Joining Direct / NRI Passengers</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nInternal Airfare for Bali – Yogyakarta is included for all passengers including Joining Direct / NRI Passengers\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nCost of the ticket taxes for the above itinerary as of 31 July 2026\nMedical insurance for the duration of the tour is included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nMeals, transfers, entrances, sightseeing, and surface transport as mentioned in the itinerary\nReturn Airport transfers from all airports.\nAll transfers and excursions inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative.\xa0\nIf group size is less than 15 customers, the tour will operate on Seat in Coach and FIT basis.\xa0\nFor Group Size more than 15 customers there will be English Speaking Guide Assistance and for less than 15 customers there will be Driver cum Guide.\n', 'exclusions': '\nMain Airfare is not Included\nAirport taxes\xa0\nIndonesia visa (To be paid by Guest on arrival)\nVisa charges for NRI passengers. (If applicable)\nThe cost of deviation, if you want to deviate from the group departure dates will be at an additional cost.\nCity Tax or Tourism Tax\nCruise Gratuity (applicable for cruise holidays)\nCost of deviation will be advised on confirmation of the deviation date, in case you want to deviate from the group departure dates mentioned in the brochure.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nThe cost of airfare included in the above tour cost is based on the fare structure existing as on 31 July 2026. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers and the company will not be held responsible for the same\nAny increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in surface transportation and land arrangements which may come into effect prior to departure.\nThe tour price is subject to increase without notice if this rate of exchange changes substantially prior to departure.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nPorterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which are not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\n\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\xa0\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\nGeneral Info\nCurrency used:\xa0\n\nIndonesia : Indonesian Rupiah\n\nTime difference:\xa0\n\nIndonesia: 2 hours and 30 minutes ahead of IST\n\n\xa0\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st June 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nCost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package.\n\n\xa0\nHotels\n\nThis Package doesn’t offer city center hotels.Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nHotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant.\n\nCoaches:\n\nCoaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nDue to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only\xa0\nDue to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nCoaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and\xa0 getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers.\n\nMeals:\n\nAll Meals are pre–set.\nPacked lunches will be provided on certain days.\n\nSightseeing:\n\nDue to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\nEvery Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations.We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same.\nAll our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays,at the same time there may be delays caused due to over crowding ,local regulations ,security check etc.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number\xa0 of\xa0 members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during\xa0 the your initial part of you tour.\nSecurity alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching.THOMAS COOK\xa0 will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\nDisabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements.\nTHOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried\xa0 along all throughout while on tour.\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour.All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends.\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/PrambananTempleYogyakarta2671.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/Bali75309.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/TanahLotTemple75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/NusaPenida753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/KeckDanace.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/Yogyakarta753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/Yogyakarta7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/jakarta-D1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/Museum753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015272/itinerary/Bali1.jpg']}, 'score': 8.8960285, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012817', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012817', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Simply Bali Split Stay - 4N Hotel and 2N Villa', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Bali', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['01 Complimentary Floating Breakfast in Villa'], 'pdfName': 'PKG012817_0_20260915111857', 'price': 64840, 'packageSummary': "The 'Simply Bali Split Stay - 4N Hotel and 2N Villa' package is a 7-day tour covering the tropical paradise of Bali. This relaxing itinerary features a split stay consisting of four nights in a hotel and two nights in a villa, allowing travelers to experience different styles of island accommodation. As a key highlight of the trip, participants will enjoy a complimentary floating breakfast in their villa, along with ample time to experience the island's vibrant culture, stunning beaches, and scenic landscapes.", 'images': ['Bali_Scenic_7531.jpg', 'Tanah_Lot_Temple_New_Bali_&53.jpg', 'BALI_BananaBoat.jpg', 'Bali_753.jpg', 'Bali1.jpg', 'Batur.jpg', 'Bali9.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 64840, 'thumbnailImage': 'bali5.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Couple Special', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Split Stay', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG012817 is named 'Simply Bali Split Stay - 4N Hotel and 2N Villa' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Bali, Meals: N/A, Description: Arrive at Bali (PVT basis) Welcome to Bali – Arrival at the Ngurah Rai, Bali International Airport, meet & greet by our local guide who led you to the parking area to board on vehicle for your transfer to your hotel. It takes about 20 minutes’ drive from airport to your hotel or more depending on the traffic. Upon arrival at the hotel, directly check in and freshen up., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Full Day Kintamani Hot Spring & Ubud village Tour –With Tanah Lot Sunset Tour (PVT Basis) Pick up for Celuk Silver Art Village Celuk Village is a traditional village which famous for the incredible gold and silver handicrafts are available around this area for very low prices. As you enter the neighborhood, you're going to feel as if you were in a jewelry exhibition. On either side of the road are established many art shops showcasing their finest works inside a glass display case. We will visit one of the best gold and silver art works in celuk village. You can take a closer look at them to appreciate it and buy some if you really like it or you can made custom jewelry based on your design. Visit Mas Wooden Carved Art Village Mas Village is one of traditional villages in Bali fundamentally as an artistic countryside by focusing the art of wood carving. This village is famous in the island as Bali Wood Carving Center located in Ubud sub district and Gianyar Regency. It owns the typical style of wood carving art by placing forward the distinguish synergy of the humanism and naturalism Visit Kintamani Hot Spring Kintamani Hot Spring features eight natural hot spring pools and one warm olympic sized pool. Heated deep within the earth, minerals from the colorless and odorless hot spring brings healing and curative powers. Enjoy a relaxing dip with the majestic panorama! *Inclusions: Natural Hot Spring Pools, Toya Water Slide with Tubes, Towel & Locker, Change & Shower Room, Facility Continue to visit Tanah Lot for Sunset Tour Tanah Lot Temple is one of the most popular Bali Places of Interest and its an ancient Hindu shrine perched on top of an outcrop amidst constantly crashing waves the temple is simply among Bali not to be missed icons. The onshore site is dotted with smaller shrines alongside visitor’s leisure facilities that comprise restaurants, shops and cultural park presenting regular dance performances. The temple is located in the Beraban village of the Tabanan regency, an approximate 20 Km northwest of Kuta and is included on most of the Bali western and central regions., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa Beach (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Salty Air! Sandy Hair! Feel the tropical breeze and get closer to Indian Ocean with our selected Water Sports Activity. Pick up for Water Sports at Tanjung Benoa Beach (Incl. 1 x Jet Ski – Banana Boat Ride) and Complimentary 1 x Parasailing or Flying Fish Note:- Children below 10 years of age are not permitted to participate in water sports, rafting, swing, spa, or ATV activities. For this age group, only entrance tickets are included; participation in activities is not applicable., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day at Leisure Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Today Day is at leisure to explore Bali or shopping at the local market., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Kuta – Villa (PVT Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Pick up for Inter Hotel Transfers to Villa, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day at Leisure Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Today Day is at leisure to explore Bali or shopping at the local market., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Bali, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart from Kuta Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. * The itinerary is tentative and subject to change without prior notice. Extension Nights : Travel Validity: 01 Oct 2026 – 24 Mar 2027 CATEGORY HOTELS PACKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN USD SINGLE TWIN / DOUBLE TRIPLE CHILD WITH BED CHILD NO BED STANDARD The Legian Paradiso or similar USD 50 USD 45 USD 45 USD 20 USD 20 VALUE Swiss Belcourt Seminyak / Fairfield Seminyak Or Similar USD 86 USD 75 USD 75 USD 30 USD 30 PREMIUM Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso or Similar USD 135 USD 120 USD 120 USD 50 USD 50 CATEGORY HOTELS PACKAGE COST: PER PERSON IN USD SINGLE TWIN /DOUBLE TRIPLE CHILDWITH BED CHILDNO BED Villa Grand Kesambi Villas Seminyak or similar USD 135 USD 70 USD 70 USD 60 USD 60, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 64840.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n4 Nights Hotel\xa0The Legian Paradiso or similar in Kuta, Bali\n2 Nights\xa0Grand Kesambi Villas Seminyak\xa0or Similar in Villa\n, \n4 Nights Hotel\xa0Sense Swiss Belcourt Seminyak / Fairfield Seminyak\xa0or Similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n2 Nights\xa0Grand Kesambi Villas Seminyak\xa0or Similar in Villa\n, \n4 Nights Hotel\xa0Bintang Bali Resort / Kuta Paradiso or Similar in Kuta, Bali\xa0\n2 Nights\xa0Grand Kesambi Villas Seminyak\xa0or Similar in Villa\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 06 night’s accommodation with breakfast Return Airport Transfers on Private basis Meet & Greet assistance at the airport Full Day Kintamani Hot Spring with Ubud Village Tour Tanah Lot Sunset Tour Half Day Water Sports (1 x Jet Ski & 1xBanana Boat) at Tanjung Benoa Complimentary 01 Floating Breakfast on the 2nd day of stay at the villa Complimentary 1xParasailing during the water sports activities. Complimentary welcome gift on arrival Complimentary 01 bottle of Mineral Water on arrival Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) the charges are approximately USD 35-40 per person. Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights service Meals not mentioned in the itinerary. Any tips for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions. Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge Blackout Dates: Christmas & New year - 15th Dec'2026 to 10th Jan'2027 & 01st Mar 2027 – 11 Mar 2027 Nyepi Day The rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling. Visa on arrival charges as applicable (as of 01st October 2023) the charges are approximately USD 35-40 per person.. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions: The upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel. The rates are valid for minimum 01 adult travelling. During Peak Season: Minimum 2 Nights Stay is required No Check Out period on 31 December 2024 and 01 January 2025 No Check Out period on 31 December 2025 and 01 January 2026 Nyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 19 March 2026. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 19 March 2026 to 06.00 am 20 March 2026 Compulsory New Year Dinner will be Applicable according to the Resort The rates are not valid on block out dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TC is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is u