sales.\nBlackout date surcharges\nChristmas & New Year 15 Dec 2026 to 06 Jan 2027\nNyepi day 03 Mar to 08 Mar 2027\nNyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 08 Mar 2027. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 08 Mar to 06.00 am 09 Mar 2027.\nMidnight surcharge.\nMeals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary.\nTips for guide & driver.\nCity tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable).\nExpenditure of a personal nature (mini bar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.)\nCamera fee.\nPorterage facility\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable.\nVisa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable).\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary.\xa0\nCost of optional excursions.\nAnything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Package Terms and Conditions:\n\nThe package price is valid until as mentioned above.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, In case the hotel chosen is unavailable we will provide with multiple options of similar category hotel.\nThe rates are valid for minimum 02 adults travelling together at all times.\xa0\nDuring Peak Season: Minimum 2 Nights Stay is required\nNo Check Out period on 31 December 2025 and 01 January 2026\nNyepi Day (Silent Day) is on 19 March 2026. No outdoor activity is allowed, and Airport will be closed from 05.59 am 19 March 2026 to 06.00 am 20 March 2026\nCompulsory New Year Dinner will be Applicable according to the Resort\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on block out dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their on-wards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing’s tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have rights to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check- in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as it will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/BaliWaterSport267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Seminyak753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/TanahLotTemple75345.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Bali_Scenic_7531.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Ubud.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/Bali_Sunset_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG014042/itinerary/bali_shutterstock_224711452.jpg']}, 'score': 3.0157604, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG013995', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG013995', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027'], 'packageName': 'Ramayan Yatra Chapter Bal Kand Ayodhya Kand', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Prayagraj', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Prayagraj', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ayodhya', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG013995_0_20260910125200', 'price': 32500, 'packageSummary': "The 'Ramayan Yatra Chapter Bal Kand Ayodhya Kand' package is a 6-day spiritual tour covering Varanasi, Ayodhya, and Prayagraj. The itinerary includes visits to the Ram Janmabhoomi Temple, Hanuman Garhi, Kanak Bhawan, the holy Triveni Sangam, and the ancient Kashi Vishwanath Temple. Participants will enjoy witnessing the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti, taking holy dips in the sacred rivers, and embarking on guided temple tours that bring the epic stories of the Bal Kand and Ayodhya Kand to life.", 'images': ['47519436781_5d96ebe956_h.jpg', 'Prayagraj.jpg', 'Ayodya.jpg', 'GangaAarti.jpg', 'Varanasi1.jpg', 'Varanasi.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 32500, 'thumbnailImage': 'Ayodhya.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Spiritual', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': 'Package ID: PKG013995 is named \'Ramayan Yatra Chapter Bal Kand Ayodhya Kand\' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Prayagraj, Meals: NA, Description: Prayagraj Arrival Morning arrival at Prayagraj airport, transfer to prebooked hotel (The city\'s original name – Prayag, or "place of offerings" – comes from its position at the Sangam (confluence) of the Ganga, Yamuna and Sarasvati riveIt is the second-oldest city in India, and plays a central role in Hindu scriptures. Allahabad was originally called Kaushambi (now a separate district) by the Kuru rulers of Hastinapur, who developed it as their capital. Since then, Allahabad has been a political, cultural and administrative centre of the Doab region. Mughal emperor Akbar renamed it Ilahabad, which the British changed to Allahabad. In 1833 it became the seat of the Ceded and Conquered Provinces region before its capital was moved to Agra in 1835. Allahabad became the capital of the North-Western Provinces in 1858, and was the capital of India for a day. The city was the capital of the United Provinces from 1902 to 1920 and remained at the forefront of national importance during the struggle for Indian independence.) Overnight in Prayagraj. Places of interest HOLY DIP IN SANGAM, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree (Akshayavat ("the indestructible banyan tree") is a sacred fig tree mentioned in the Hindu mythology. According to a legend, once the sage Markandeya asked Lord Narayana to show him a specimen of the divine power. Narayana flooded the entire world for a moment, during which only the Akshayavat could be seen above the water level.) & Anand Bhawan (Birthplace of first Prime Minister of Independent India Pt. Jawaharlal Nehru) Experience the exclusivity of Magh Mela as you explore the sacred Sangam, witness vibrant rituals, and immerse yourself in the spiritual essence of this grand gathering., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Prayagraj, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prayagraj - Chitrakoot – Prayagraj (120 Km, 3 Happrox. One Way) After breakfast day trip to Chitrakoot (Chitrakoot, "the hills of many wonders" is indeed a gift of nature and the gods. Located in the Banda district of modern Uttar Pradesh(U.P), on the banks of river Paisuni(Mandikini), Chitrakoot is a tranquil retreat on the northern spur of the Vindhyas. Just 6 km south of Karvi and 72 km south east of Banda district on the road to Allahabad, Chitrakoot Dham is one of the most ancient holy pilgrim places of India. Legends have it that it was the abode of Lord Rama, his wife Sita and brother Lakshman for eleven years of their fourteen years of exile. This is also the place,where they came in contact with sage Atri and sati Anasuya.This abode of the gods is credited to have seen the incarnations of Brahma,Vishnu and Mahesh. Chitrakoot ,sacred with the touch of Lord\'s feet,was where Goswami Tulsidas, the creator of the epic "Shri Ramcharitmanas" spent many years of his life. Dotted with innumerable temples and shrines, nature\'s splendor here is wrapped in peace and tranquility, permeated only by singing birds and gushing streams.). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Prayagraj. Places of Interest:- Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Ayodhya, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Prayagraj - Ayodhya (180 Km, 4 Happrox. One Way) After breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Ayodhaya (Ayodhya, also known as Saketa, is an ancient city of India, believed to be the birthplace of Rama and setting of the epic Ramayana. It is adjacent to Faizabad city in the central region of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh. Ayodhya used to be the capital of the ancient Kosala Kingdom. Owing to the belief as the birthplace of Rama, Ayodhya (Awadh) has been regarded as one of the seven most important pilgrimage sites (Saptapuri) for Hindus. It is believed that the birth spot of Rama). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Faizabad. Places of Interest:- Ram Janam Bhoomi; Kanak Bhawan; Hanuman Garhi; Raj Darbar; Karsevak Sthal., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Varanasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Ayodhaya – Varanasi (230 Km, 6 Happrox. One Way) After breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Varanasi. On arrival at Varanasi, check into prebooked hotel. later in evening transfer to Ganges for Boating and Evening Ganga Aarti on famous Dashashwamedh Ghat (Dashashwamedh Ghat is the main ghat in Varanasi on the Ganga River. It is located close to Vishwanath Temple and is probably the most spectacular ghat. Two Hindu legends are associated with it: According to one, Lord Brahma created it to welcome Lord Shiva. According to another legend, Lord Brahma sacrificed ten horses during Dasa-Ashwamedha yajna performed here.) Overnight in Varanasi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Varanasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Varanasi Early morning Temple darshan (Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir, Kala Bhairov Mandir) followed with Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir & Benaras Hindu University (BHU). After breakfast move for Sarnath (Sarnath is the place where Gautam Buddha after attain enlightenment delivers his first sermon to 5 followers). Sightseeing of Sarnath including Sarnath Museum (Our National Emblem excavated from Sarnath is on Display built by Samrat Ashoka), Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple. Evening is free. Overnight in Varanasi., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Varanasi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Varanasi – Depart After breakfast, checkout from hotel and drop at Varanasi airport for onward/return journey. (VEHICLE IS AVAILABLE ONLY FOR AIRPORT DROP), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 32500.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation on DBL/TWIN sharing basis In mentioned or similar hotels Breakfast Airport arrival and Departure All transfer and sightseeing by 01 Private vehicles as per the tour itinerary. Insurance Standard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour. For guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.. Exclusions: Any airfare/rail fare Guide service/charge Remittance charge/Bank charge for transfer of money. Tips and gratuities Any entrance/monuments fees/mobile/ camera/video tickets. Meals other than mentioned. Any VIP darshan/Dakshina/Prashad/Garland fees Any personal nature expenses. GST Extra Personal expenditure like soft drinks, mineral water, phone calls, tips, porter age etc. Anything not specifically mentioned in the “Package tour price includes” box. Any expenses of personal nature. High season surcharge, applicable during Chinese New Year period High Season / Special events supplements will be applicable at the time of booking only. Any optional tour.. Product Terms and Conditions: At all location they have to walk a lot and at no condition the vehicle will drop and pickup from the tourist site. Vehicle like BUS/TEMPO are not allowed to enter into the city. Tourists have to Take RICKSHAW to go. After drop the vehicle will stand in the parking only, and client have to go to the parking only for boarding. Wheelchair facility will be available upon direct payable basis. As per the order of DM MAX. 2 Person is allowed to share the room (FAMILY MEMBER ONLY). As of now Ram Mandir in Ayodhaya is not open for public visit, tourist/bhakt can visit upto Hanuman Garhi only. Please do discuss the status of relief/restrictions before confirming the booking The tour price printed is dynamic prices & is purely on first come first serve basis. It is mandatory to carry photo ID card (Pan Card is not accepted) while you are on tour. The vehicle used for transfers & sightseeing purpose only and is not at disposal. This is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon multiple circumstances during the actual course of travel. Please consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfer timings. Please follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips /activities as informed by our representative.. Highlights of the package: .', 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Allahabad', 'cityCode': 'IXD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Ramayan Yatra Chapter Bal Kand Ayodhya Kand' package is a 6-day spiritual tour covering Varanasi, Ayodhya, and Prayagraj. The itinerary includes visits to the Ram Janmabhoomi Temple, Hanuman Garhi, Kanak Bhawan, the holy Triveni Sangam, and the ancient Kashi Vishwanath Temple. Participants will enjoy witnessing the mesmerizing Ganga Aarti, taking holy dips in the sacred rivers, and embarking on guided temple tours that bring the epic stories of the Bal Kand and Ayodhya Kand to life.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nPrayagraj Arrival\n\xa0\nMorning arrival at Prayagraj airport, transfer to prebooked hotel (The city\'s original name – Prayag, or "place of offerings" – comes from its position at the Sangam (confluence) of the Ganga, Yamuna and Sarasvati riveIt is the second-oldest city in India, and plays a central role in Hindu scriptures. Allahabad was originally called Kaushambi (now a separate district) by the Kuru rulers of Hastinapur, who developed it as their capital. Since then, Allahabad has been a political, cultural and administrative centre of the Doab region. Mughal emperor Akbar renamed it Ilahabad, which the British changed to Allahabad. In 1833 it became the seat of the Ceded and Conquered Provinces region before its capital was moved to Agra in 1835. Allahabad became the capital of the North-Western Provinces in 1858, and was the capital of India for a day. The city was the capital of the United Provinces from 1902 to 1920 and remained at the forefront of national importance during the struggle for Indian independence.) Overnight in Prayagraj.\nPlaces of interest HOLY DIP IN SANGAM, Bada Hanuman Mandir, Akshayvat Tree (Akshayavat ("the indestructible banyan tree") is a sacred fig tree mentioned in the Hindu mythology. According to a legend, once the sage Markandeya asked Lord Narayana to show him a specimen of the divine power. Narayana flooded the entire world for a moment, during which only the Akshayavat could be seen above the water level.) & Anand Bhawan (Birthplace of first Prime Minister of Independent India Pt. Jawaharlal Nehru)\n\xa0\nExperience the exclusivity of Magh Mela as you explore the sacred Sangam, witness vibrant rituals, and immerse yourself in the spiritual essence of this grand gathering.', 'mealDescription': 'NA', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel -\xa0Golden Tree (Standard) / Rama Continental (Value) / Placid (Premium) or similar in Prayagraj'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nPrayagraj - Chitrakoot – Prayagraj (120 Km, 3 Happrox. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast day trip to Chitrakoot (Chitrakoot, "the hills of many wonders" is indeed a gift of nature and the gods. Located in the Banda district of modern Uttar Pradesh(U.P), on the banks of river Paisuni(Mandikini), Chitrakoot is a tranquil retreat on the northern spur of the Vindhyas. Just 6 km south of Karvi and 72 km south east of Banda district on the road to Allahabad, Chitrakoot Dham is one of the most ancient holy pilgrim places of India. Legends have it that it was the abode of Lord Rama, his wife Sita and brother Lakshman for eleven years of their fourteen years of exile. This is also the place,where they came in contact with sage Atri and sati Anasuya.This abode of the gods is credited to have seen the incarnations of Brahma,Vishnu and Mahesh. Chitrakoot ,sacred with the touch of Lord\'s feet,was where Goswami Tulsidas, the creator of the epic "Shri Ramcharitmanas" spent many years of his life. Dotted with innumerable temples and shrines, nature\'s splendor here is wrapped in peace and tranquility, permeated only by singing birds and gushing streams.). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Prayagraj.\nPlaces of Interest:- Kamad Giri, Sphatik Shila, Hanuman Dhara, Ram Ghat, Janki Kund.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel -\xa0Golden Tree (Standard) / Rama Continental (Value) / Placid (Premium) or similar in Prayagraj'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nPrayagraj - Ayodhya (180 Km, 4 Happrox. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Ayodhaya (Ayodhya, also known as Saketa, is an ancient city of India, believed to be the birthplace of Rama and setting of the epic Ramayana. It is adjacent to Faizabad city in the central region of the Indian state of Uttar Pradesh. Ayodhya used to be the capital of the ancient Kosala Kingdom. Owing to the belief as the birthplace of Rama, Ayodhya (Awadh) has been regarded as one of the seven most important pilgrimage sites (Saptapuri) for Hindus. It is believed that the birth spot of Rama). Return hotel check in and overnight stay in Faizabad.\n\xa0\nPlaces of Interest:- Ram Janam Bhoomi; Kanak Bhawan; Hanuman Garhi; Raj Darbar; Karsevak Sthal.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Bedis dreamland (Standard) / Padmashree Palace (Value) / Cygnett (Premium) or similar in Ayodhya'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nAyodhaya – Varanasi (230 Km, 6 Happrox. One Way)\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and transfer to Varanasi. On arrival at Varanasi, check into prebooked hotel. later in evening transfer to Ganges for Boating and Evening Ganga Aarti on famous Dashashwamedh Ghat (Dashashwamedh Ghat is the main ghat in Varanasi on the Ganga River. It is located close to Vishwanath Temple and is probably the most spectacular ghat. Two Hindu legends are associated with it: According to one, Lord Brahma created it to welcome Lord Shiva. According to another legend, Lord Brahma sacrificed ten horses during Dasa-Ashwamedha yajna performed here.) Overnight in Varanasi.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Vikram palace (Standard) / Buddha Lineage (Value) / Mudra (Premium) or similar in Varanasi\xa0'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi\n\xa0\nEarly morning Temple darshan (Kashi Vishwanath, Annapurna Mandir, Kala Bhairov Mandir) followed with Sankat Mochan Mandir, Durga Mandir, Tulsi Manas Mandir & Benaras Hindu University (BHU). After breakfast move for Sarnath (Sarnath is the place where Gautam Buddha after attain enlightenment delivers his first sermon to 5 followers). Sightseeing of Sarnath including Sarnath Museum (Our National Emblem excavated from Sarnath is on Display built by Samrat Ashoka), Ancient ruins, Mahabodhi society Temple. Evening is free. Overnight in Varanasi.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel - Vikram palace (Standard) / Buddha Lineage (Value) / Mudra (Premium) or similar in Varanasi\xa0'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\nVaranasi – Depart\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, checkout from hotel and drop at Varanasi airport for onward/return journey. (VEHICLE IS AVAILABLE ONLY FOR AIRPORT DROP)', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Na'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '2': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'IN', 'countryName': 'India', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 32500.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 37500.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 42600.0, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['All transfers and sightseeing as per itinerary using A/c Vehicle as per the group size', 'As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\nAccommodation on DBL/TWIN sharing basis In mentioned or similar hotels\xa0\nBreakfast\xa0\nAirport arrival and Departure\xa0\nAll transfer and sightseeing by 01 Private vehicles as per the tour itinerary.\xa0\xa0\n\nInsurance\xa0\n\nStandard travel insurance coverage for the entire duration of the tour.\nFor guests aged 70 and above, or those choosing to extend their stay, additional insurance fees may apply to accommodate these specific needs.\n', 'exclusions': '\nAny airfare/rail fare\xa0\nGuide service/charge\xa0\nRemittance charge/Bank charge for transfer of money.\xa0\nTips and gratuities\xa0\nAny entrance/monuments fees/mobile/ camera/video tickets.\xa0\nMeals other than mentioned.\xa0\nAny VIP darshan/Dakshina/Prashad/Garland fees\xa0\nAny personal nature expenses.\xa0\nGST Extra\xa0\nPersonal expenditure like soft drinks, mineral water, phone calls, tips, porter age etc.\xa0\nAnything not specifically mentioned in the “Package tour price includes” box.\xa0\nAny expenses of personal nature.\xa0\nHigh season surcharge, applicable during Chinese New Year period\xa0\nHigh Season / Special events supplements will be applicable at the time of booking only.\xa0\nAny optional tour.\xa0\n\n\xa0', 'termsAndConditions': '\nAt all location they have to walk a lot and at no condition the vehicle will drop and pickup from the tourist site. Vehicle like BUS/TEMPO are not allowed to enter into the city. Tourists have to Take RICKSHAW to go. After drop the vehicle will stand in the parking only, and client have to go to the parking only for boarding. Wheelchair facility will be available upon direct payable basis.\nAs per the order of DM MAX. 2 Person is allowed to share the room (FAMILY MEMBER ONLY).\nAs of now Ram Mandir in Ayodhaya is not open for public visit, tourist/bhakt can visit upto Hanuman Garhi only. Please do discuss the status of relief/restrictions before confirming the booking\nThe tour price printed is dynamic prices & is purely on first come first serve basis.\nIt is mandatory to carry photo ID card (Pan Card is not accepted) while you are on tour.\nThe vehicle used for transfers & sightseeing purpose only and is not at disposal.\nThis is an indicative itinerary and subject to change depending upon multiple circumstances during the actual course of travel.\nPlease consult driver / local representative for next day’s sightseeing schedule / transfer timings.\nPlease follow the stipulated timings for the sightseeing trips /activities as informed by our representative.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 2, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 0, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/Ayodhya.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/itinerary/47519436781_5d96ebe956_h.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/itinerary/Prayagraj.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/itinerary/Ayodya.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/itinerary/GangaAarti.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/itinerary/Varanasi1.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG013995/itinerary/Varanasi.jpg']}, 'score': 2.1556754, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}]
