Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc)\xa0\nAll drink and beverages\xa0\xa0\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\xa0\xa0\nTourism Tax (if applicable)\xa0\nMidnight surcharge\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nTerms And Conditions:\n\nThe upgrade of hotel prices is subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the hotels envisaged.\xa0\xa0\nThe upgraded hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\xa0\nFor the upgraded hotel, in case the hotel chosen is unavailable, we will provide multiple options of similar category hotels.\xa0\nThe rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adults travelling.\xa0\nThe rates are not valid on blackout dates.\xa0\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers will be requested to pay the same\xa0\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their onwards/connecting flights.\xa0\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\xa0\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\xa0\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\xa0\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\xa0\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\xa0\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\xa0\nSightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\xa0\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\xa0\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\xa0\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\xa0\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\xa0\nAs a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/DubaiTrending267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/itinerary/Dhow_Cruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/itinerary/Burj_Khalifa_1_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/itinerary/Desert_Safari_Dubai_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/itinerary/Dubai_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/itinerary/753_new_Abu_Dhabi.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015635/itinerary/Dubai_Cityview_753.jpg']}, 'score': 10.220714, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015286', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015286', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Magical Dubai (Winter)', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Experience a Limousine Ride 360 Degrees Panoramic View of the Palm Island - The View Palm Jumeirah Ride on a Monorail to the Palm Island Visit Gold & Spice Souk Experience the Yacht Ride on Dubai Marina Guided City tour of Dubai Visit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (non-prime slot) Visit Global Village Visit Dolphin Aquarium Experience the Desert Safari with Dune bashing & BBQ Dinner WHATS MORE Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Free flow of soft drinks and beer on Yacht Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box (1 box per family)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG010555_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 116184, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Dubai (Winter)' package is a 6-day tour covering the spectacular city of Dubai. The itinerary is packed with exciting activities, including a luxurious limousine ride, a scenic yacht ride on Dubai Marina with free-flowing soft drinks and beer, a monorail ride to Palm Island, and a breathtaking 360-degree panoramic view from The View Palm Jumeirah. Participants will enjoy a guided city tour of Dubai with complimentary ice cream, visits to the traditional Gold and Spice Souk, the 124th floor of the iconic Burj Khalifa, the Global Village, and the Dolphin Aquarium. The adventure also features a thrilling desert safari with dune bashing and a barbecue dinner, and each family will receive an exclusive Dubai Memories souvenir box to commemorate their trip.", 'images': ['Dubai56.jpg', 'PALM JUMEIRAH - 753X430.jpg', 'BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'dubai_gold.jpg', '50573_Dubai_Marina_City_Night_View_Dubai_753.jpg', 'Dubai6.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 116184, 'thumbnailImage': 'Dubai26789.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015286 is named 'Magical Dubai (Winter)' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Dubai - Check In - Enjoy Limo Ride Welcome to United Arab Emirates. On arrival in Dubai, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. Later enjoy Limousine ride, sit back in the most comfortable and luxurious stretch limousine and explore the night city view. Note: All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs. Early morning arrivals will be provided Breakfast (Not applicable for Joining Direct Passengers), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit The View At Palm Jumeirah - Ride On Monorail – Visit Gold Souk - Experience The Yacht Cruise This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to Palm Jumeirah to experience a breathtaking view of the Palm Island from the top. Ride on the monorail ride to the Palm. Free time for shopping at Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Later this evening proceed to the marina for a Yacht Cruise with free flow of soft drinks & beer. Overnight in Dubai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Burj Khalifa - Guided City Tour Of Dubai – Global Village This morning after buffet breakfast, Visit 124th Floor of Burj Khalifa (non-prime hours). Later proceed for a guided city tour of Dubai along with Photo stop at the Dubai Frame, Museum of the Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace. Proceed for Global Village a shopping, dining, and entertainment attraction located on Sheikh Mohammed Bin Zayed Road. There are four main sections in the Village. These sections consist of events and concerts, carnivals, food, and shopping. Overnight in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Dubai Dolphinarium – Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & Bbq Dinner This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Dubai Dolphinarium. The Dolphin & Seal Show, the #1 in the UAE. These interactive extravaganzas showcase the amazing animals' astounding skills. Visitors watch in wonder as the dolphins and seals dance, sing, juggle, play ball, jump through hoops and even paint. Later proceed for Desert Safari to enjoy the thrilling dune bashing on a desert safari adventure exploring the massive sand dunes of the Arabian deserts. Enjoy BBQ Dinner and the belly dancing performance at the Desert Camp. Overnight in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Dubai On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. Late Evening Departures Will Be Provided Lunch (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers) Note: On few days there will be a coach merger with other Dubai product's (if required) Note : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 116184.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n05 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai (Free upgrade to 5* Hotel Crown Plaza)\n. Meals include: \nDaily American buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 Local BBQ Buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n, Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. All local taxes including services taxes as of 1st August 2026. Cost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 15 customers then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Tourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT Visa Requirements: UAE Visa included (E-visa) Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 1st August 2026) Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Important Notes: Airline and Airfare The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st November, 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Cost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package. Hotels This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant. Coaches Coaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. Meals All Meals are pre–set. Packed lunches will be provided on certain days. Sightseeing Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc. General On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour. Security alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. THOMAS COOK will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. THOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Experience a Limousine Ride 360 Degrees Panoramic View of the Palm Island - The View Palm Jumeirah Ride on a Monorail to the Palm Island Visit Gold & Spice Souk Experience the Yacht Ride on Dubai Marina Guided City tour of Dubai Visit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (non-prime slot) Visit Global Village Visit Dolphin Aquarium Experience the Desert Safari with Dune bashing & BBQ Dinner WHATS MORE Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Free flow of soft drinks and beer on Yacht Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box (1 box per family).", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZMD753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Magical Dubai (Winter)' package is a 6-day tour covering the spectacular city of Dubai. The itinerary is packed with exciting activities, including a luxurious limousine ride, a scenic yacht ride on Dubai Marina with free-flowing soft drinks and beer, a monorail ride to Palm Island, and a breathtaking 360-degree panoramic view from The View Palm Jumeirah. Participants will enjoy a guided city tour of Dubai with complimentary ice cream, visits to the traditional Gold and Spice Souk, the 124th floor of the iconic Burj Khalifa, the Global Village, and the Dolphin Aquarium. The adventure also features a thrilling desert safari with dune bashing and a barbecue dinner, and each family will receive an exclusive Dubai Memories souvenir box to commemorate their trip.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival In Dubai\xa0- Check In -\xa0Enjoy Limo Ride\xa0\nWelcome to United Arab Emirates. On arrival in Dubai, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure.\n\xa0\nLater enjoy Limousine ride, sit back in the most comfortable and luxurious stretch limousine and explore the night city view.\nNote:\n\nAll Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card\nJoining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs.\xa0\nEarly morning arrivals will be provided Breakfast (Not applicable for Joining Direct Passengers)\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nVisit The View At Palm Jumeirah - Ride On Monorail – Visit Gold Souk - Experience The Yacht Cruise\nThis morning\xa0 after buffet breakfast, proceed to Palm Jumeirah to experience a breathtaking view of the Palm Island from the top. Ride on the\xa0 monorail ride to the Palm.\xa0\nFree time for shopping at Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Later this evening proceed to the marina for a Yacht Cruise with free flow of soft drinks & beer.\xa0\nOvernight in Dubai.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Burj Khalifa - Guided City Tour Of Dubai – Global Village\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, Visit 124th Floor of Burj Khalifa (non-prime hours).\nLater proceed for a guided city tour of Dubai along with Photo stop at the Dubai Frame, Museum of the Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace.\nProceed for Global Village a shopping, dining, and entertainment attraction located on Sheikh Mohammed Bin Zayed Road. There are four main sections in the Village. These sections consist of events and concerts, carnivals, food, and shopping.\nOvernight in Dubai', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\nVisit Dubai Dolphinarium – Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & Bbq Dinner\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Dubai Dolphinarium. The Dolphin & Seal Show, the #1 in the UAE. These interactive extravaganzas showcase the amazing animals' astounding skills.\xa0 Visitors watch in wonder as the dolphins and seals dance, sing, juggle, play ball, jump through hoops and even paint.\xa0\nLater proceed for Desert Safari to enjoy the thrilling dune bashing on a desert safari adventure exploring the massive sand dunes of the Arabian deserts. Enjoy BBQ Dinner and the belly dancing performance at the Desert Camp.\nOvernight in Dubai", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Dubai On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 6, 'description': "\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\nLate Evening Departures Will Be Provided Lunch (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers)\nNote: On few days there will be a coach merger with other Dubai product's (if required)\nNote : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n05 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai (Free upgrade to 5* Hotel Crown Plaza)\n'], 'hotels_list': {'1': '\n05 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai (Free upgrade to 5* Hotel Crown Plaza)\n', '0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AE', 'countryName': 'United Arab Emirates', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 116200.0, 'hotels': ['\n05 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai (Free upgrade to 5* Hotel Crown Plaza)\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily American buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 Local BBQ Buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['\nUAE Visa included ( E-visa)\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st November 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\n', 'As per itinerary'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', '\nExperience a Limousine Ride ( 60 minutes)\n360 Degrees Panoramic View of the Palm Island\xa0 - The View Palm Jumeirah\xa0\xa0\nRide on a Monorail to the Palm Island – remove from Astra\nExperience the Desert Safari with Dune bashing & BBQ dinner mention\nGuided City tour of Dubai\xa0\nVisit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (non-prime slot)\nFree time at Dubai Mall\nVisit Dolphin Aquarium\xa0\nVisit Gold & Spice Souk\nExperience the Yacht Ride on Dubai Marina ( 120 minutes)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Provision of a Tour Manager is subject to the final operating group size. An accompanying Tour Manager will be provided for groups of 20 or more confirmed passengers. For groups with fewer than 20 passengers, the tour will operate on a Seat in Coach (SIC) / Free independent Tour (FIT) basis, and a Virtual Tour Manager or local representative/assistance will be provided to assist remotely with coordination, guidance, daily briefings, reconfirmations, and on tour support. The Virtual Tour Manager does not accompany the group in person. The company reserves the right to operate the tour without a physical Tour Manager should the final group size be less than 20 passengers. Confirmation of Tour Manager arrangement will be communicated 10-15 days prior to the departure.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nAll local taxes including services taxes as of 1st August 2026.\nCost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour.\nSightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAll transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 15 customers then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nTourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT\n\nVisa Requirements:\n\nUAE Visa included (E-visa)\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 1st August 2026)\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nPorterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions.\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Important Notes:\nAirline and Airfare\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st November, 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nCost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package.\n\nHotels\n\nThis Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts.\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room.\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nHotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant.\n\n\xa0\nCoaches\n\nCoaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nDue to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only\nDue to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nCoaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers.\n\nMeals\n\nAll Meals are pre–set.\nPacked lunches will be provided on certain days.\n\nSightseeing\n\nDue to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\nEvery Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same.\nAll our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc.\n\nGeneral\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour.\nSecurity alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. THOMAS COOK will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\nDisabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements.\nTHOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour.\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends.\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/Dubai26789.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/itinerary/Dubai56.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/itinerary/PALM_JUMEIRAH_-_753X430.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/itinerary/BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/itinerary/dubai_gold.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/itinerary/50573_Dubai_Marina_City_Night_View_Dubai_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015286/itinerary/Dubai6.jpg']}, 'score': 9.679558, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015588', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015588', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Simply Dubai 5N 6D', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015588_0_20260915173700.pdf', 'price': 81497, 'packageSummary': "The 'Simply Dubai 5N 6D' package is a 6-day tour dedicated entirely to exploring the spectacular city of Dubai. The itinerary includes iconic experiences such as a guided half-day city tour of Dubai's modern and historical landmarks, a thrilling desert safari featuring dune bashing and a traditional barbecue dinner under the stars, and a relaxing dhow cruise with dinner along the marina. Participants will also enjoy stunning panoramic views from the observation deck of the Burj Khalifa, visit the massive Dubai Mall for shopping and entertainment, and have ample leisure time to explore the city's vibrant souks and pristine beaches.", 'images': ['Dhow_Cruise.jpg', 'Stock_4426_Dubai_Burj_Khalifa753.jpg', 'DubaiDesertSafari753.jpg', '50573_Dubai_Marina_City_Night_View_Dubai_753.jpg', 'BurjKhalifaDubaiiStock183371461.jpg', 'DubaiCity753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 81497, 'thumbnailImage': 'Dubai267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015588 is named 'Simply Dubai 5N 6D' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Dubai, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Dubai, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dubai, Meals: ., Description: ., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 81497.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n05 Nights Hotels\xa0Khalidia Palace Deira / Avani Deira / Crowne Plaza Deira /\xa0Movenpick Bur Dubai Deira or Similar in\xa0Dubai (Validity: 05 Jan – 30 Apr 2026 & 01 Sep – 25 Sep 2026)\n05 Nights Hotels\xa0Khalidia Palace Deira / Avani Deira / Crowne Plaza Deira Or Similar in\xa0Dubai\xa0(Validity: 01 May’26 – 26 Aug’26)\n, \n05 Nights Hotels\xa0Omega Bur / Sea View Bur / Ascot Bur /\xa0Fortune Grand Hotel Deira\xa0/\xa0Arabian Courtyard & Spa Bur / Royal Ascot Bur or Similar in Dubai (Validity: 05 Jan – 30 Apr 2026 & 01 Sep – 25 Sep 2026)\n05 Nights\xa0Versallies Hotel by Veiras / Omega Hotel Bur Dubai / Sea View Hotel Bur Dubai / Ascot Hotel Bur Dubai / Arabian Courtyard Hotel & Spa Bur Dubai / Ascot hotel Bur Dubai / Royal Ascot Hotel Bur Dubai\xa0or Similar in Dubai (Validity: 01 May’26 – 26 Aug’26)\n, \n05 Nights Hotel\xa0Citymax Bur / Admiral Plaza Bur / Gateway Bur / Arabian Park Edge by Rotana /\xa0Fortune Pearl Deira / Fortune Plaza Al Quasis /\xa0Smana Al Raffa /\xa0City Avenue Hotel Deria\xa0\xa0Or Similar in Dubai\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 05 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Dubai. Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Dubai Airport – Dubai Hotel – Dubai Airport Transfers (Private Basis) Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner (SIC basis) Half Day City Tour followed by Burj Khalifa 124th Floor Non-Prime (SIC Basis) Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner (SIC Basis) 03 Dinner Cuopon without transfers 5% VAT Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST UAE VISA Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights service Meals that are not mentioned in the itinerary. Any tips for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions. Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge Black Out Dates Surcharge: Diwali (05 Nov-13 Nov) | National Day (02 Dec-05 Dec) | Dubai Air Show (06 Dec -11 Dec) |Christmas & New Year (23 Dec -03 Jan) |Arab Health (23 Jan-29 Jan) Eid Al Fitr (06 Mar -12 Mar) | Gulf Food (13 Mar -20 Mar). Product Terms and Conditions: The upgrade of hotel prices is subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the hotels envisaged. The upgraded hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgraded hotel, in case the hotel chosen is unavailable, we will provide multiple options of similar category hotels. The rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adults travelling. The rates are not valid on blackout dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers will be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their onwards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cit