ates are not valid on blackout dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers will be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their onwards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard.\nIf we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 1, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/Dubai267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/itinerary/Dhow_Cruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/itinerary/Stock_4426_Dubai_Burj_Khalifa753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/itinerary/DubaiDesertSafari753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/itinerary/50573_Dubai_Marina_City_Night_View_Dubai_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/itinerary/BurjKhalifaDubaiiStock183371461.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015588/itinerary/DubaiCity753.jpg']}, 'score': 9.238157, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015268', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015268', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Dubai For All - Winter', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015268_0_20260915201401', 'price': 58458, 'packageSummary': "The 'Dubai For All - Winter' package is a 6-day tour dedicated entirely to exploring the vibrant city of Dubai. The itinerary is packed with exciting activities suitable for all travelers, including a thrilling desert safari with a traditional barbecue dinner, a visit to the observation deck of the iconic Burj Khalifa, and a relaxing dhow cruise. Participants will also experience guided city tours showcasing both historical and modern landmarks, shopping at world-famous souks and malls, and visits to popular seasonal attractions like the Dubai Miracle Garden.", 'images': ['dubaiyatch.jpg', 'BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'DubaiDesertSafari.jpg', 'Dhow_Cruise.jpg', '753_DUBAI.jpg', 'Dubai_City.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 58458, 'thumbnailImage': 'Dubai2678.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Budget Friendly', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015268 is named 'Dubai For All - Winter' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Dubai - Check In Welcome To United Arab Emirates. On Arrival In Dubai, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs).Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. Note All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Burj Khalifa - Guided City Tour Of Dubai - Free Time To Explore Dubai Mall - See The Fountain Show. This morning after buffet breakfast, Visit 124th Floor of Burj Khalifa (non-prime hours). Free time at the Dubai Mall later enjoy Fountain Show. Later proceed for a guided city tour of Dubai along with Photo stop at the Dubai Frame, Museum of the Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace,, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Morning Free Time - Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & BBQ Dinner This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, The Morning Free To Explore On Your Own. Later This Afternoon Proceed For Desert Safari To Enjoy The Thrilling Dune Bashing On A Desert Safari Adventure Exploring The Massive Sand Dunes Of The Arabian Deserts. Enjoy Bbq Dinner And The Belly Dancing Performance At The Desert Camp., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure - Experience The Dhow Cruise With Dinner. This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Dubai On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers. Later In The Evening Proceed For Dinner On The Dhow Cruise., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Day At Leisure This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Dubai On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning after Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. Note : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 58458.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n5 Nights accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or Similar in Dubai\n, Overnight stay at the Hotels. Meals include: \nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n01 Local buffet dinner on Dhow Cruise\n01\xa0 Local BBQ buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n03\xa0 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n, Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. All local taxes including services taxes as of 01st August 2026. Cost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary. Airport transfers from Dubai airport. All transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Tourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT VISA REQUIREMENTS: UAE Visa included ( E-visa) Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.. Exclusions: The cost of Air Travel is not a part of the package. Cost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions. Product Terms and Conditions: Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st August 2020. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Cost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package. Hotels: This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels.Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant. Coaches: Coaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. Meals: All Meals are pre–set. Packed meals will be provided on certain days. Sightseeing: Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations.We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays,at the same time there may be delays caused due to over crowding ,local regulations ,security check etc. General Points: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the your initial part of you tour. Security alerts and unforseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. Thomas Cook I Limited will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. Thomas Cook I Limited shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour.All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends . There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZDA752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Dubai For All - Winter' package is a 6-day tour dedicated entirely to exploring the vibrant city of Dubai. The itinerary is packed with exciting activities suitable for all travelers, including a thrilling desert safari with a traditional barbecue dinner, a visit to the observation deck of the iconic Burj Khalifa, and a relaxing dhow cruise. Participants will also experience guided city tours showcasing both historical and modern landmarks, shopping at world-famous souks and malls, and visits to popular seasonal attractions like the Dubai Miracle Garden.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\nArrival In Dubai\xa0- Check In\nWelcome To United Arab Emirates. On Arrival In Dubai, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs).Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure.\n\xa0\nNote\n\nAll Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card\nJoining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\nVisit Burj Khalifa - Guided City Tour Of Dubai - Free Time To Explore Dubai Mall - See The Fountain Show.\nThis morning after buffet breakfast, Visit 124th Floor of Burj Khalifa (non-prime hours). Free time at the Dubai Mall later enjoy Fountain Show.\xa0Later proceed for a guided city tour of Dubai along with Photo stop at the Dubai Frame, Museum of the Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace,', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 3, 'description': '\xa0\nMorning Free Time - Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & BBQ Dinner\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, The Morning Free To Explore On Your Own. Later This Afternoon Proceed For Desert Safari To Enjoy The Thrilling Dune Bashing On A Desert Safari Adventure Exploring The Massive Sand Dunes Of The Arabian Deserts. Enjoy Bbq Dinner And The Belly Dancing Performance At The Desert Camp.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\nDay At Leisure - Experience The Dhow Cruise With Dinner.\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Dubai On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.\nLater In The Evening Proceed For Dinner On The Dhow Cruise.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDay At Leisure\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Day Is At Leisure. Spend Rest Of The Day Exploring Dubai On Your Own Or “ Plan Your Day” From The Various Optional Tours Available On Attractive Offers.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning after Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\nNote : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n5 Nights accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or Similar in Dubai\n', 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n5 Nights accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or Similar in Dubai\n', '1': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AE', 'countryName': 'United Arab Emirates', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 58500.0, 'hotels': ['\n5 Nights accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or Similar in Dubai\n']}], 'meals': ['\nDaily buffet breakfast (Except Day 1)\n01 Local buffet dinner on Dhow Cruise\n01\xa0 Local BBQ buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n03\xa0 Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners at Indian restaurant\nNote: Packed meals, if applicable, will be Jain/vegetarian\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n', 'Breakfast Included'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August, 2026. Any further i increase in the same has to be borne by the passengers.\nFor JD clients visa is NOT included.\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Sightseeing as per itinerary', '\nGuided City Tour of Dubai\nVisit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (Non-prime slot)\nFree time at Dubai Mall\nFountain Show at Dubai Mall\nExperience Dhow Cruise with Dinner\nDesert Safari – dune bashing followed by the BBQ dinner\xa0\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': "<p>Rest assured, Thomas Cook's experienced &amp; knowledgeable tour manager will be with the group at every step of the journey. Be it transportation, accommodation &amp; everything in between, ensuring a seamless &amp; stress-free travel experience from start to finish. Whether it's a question or a challenge, our tour manager is always readily available to offer support, assistance &amp; ensure that your trip becomes a most cherished memory. (Presence of the Tour Manager is subject to a minimum of 15 - 20 customers, depending on package/destination booked)</p>", 'flightDescription': '<ul>\n<li>Return Airport Transfers Included ( Ex Dubai, Ex Sharjah)</li>\n</ul>', 'inclusions': '\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\nAll local taxes including services taxes as of 01st August 2026.\nCost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour.\nSightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\nAirport transfers from Dubai airport.\nAll transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\nTourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT\n\n\xa0\nVISA REQUIREMENTS:\n\nUAE Visa included ( E-visa)\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\n', 'exclusions': '\nThe cost of Air Travel is not a part of the package.\nCost of Basic Travel Quota equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\nPorterage Facility\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\nAdditional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary.\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\nCost of Optional Excursions\n', 'termsAndConditions': 'Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices.\nAirline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st August 2020. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\nPassengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nCost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package.\n\nHotels:\n\nThis Package doesn’t offer city center hotels.Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts.\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and room size will be the same as double room\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers.\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nHotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant.\n\nCoaches:\n\nCoaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nDue to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only\nDue to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nCoaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers.\n\nMeals:\n\nAll Meals are pre–set.\nPacked meals will be provided on certain days.\n\nSightseeing:\n\nDue to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\nEvery Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations.We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same.\nAll our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays,at the same time there may be delays caused due to over crowding ,local regulations ,security check etc.\n\nGeneral Points:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the your initial part of you tour.\nSecurity alerts and unforseen closures may affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. Thomas Cook I Limited will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage\nDisabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements.\nThomas Cook I Limited shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour.All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends .\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'N', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package does not include flights. You can book flights separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/Dubai2678.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/itinerary/dubaiyatch.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/itinerary/BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/itinerary/DubaiDesertSafari.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/itinerary/Dhow_Cruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/itinerary/753_DUBAI.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015268/itinerary/Dubai_City.jpg']}, 'score': 9.238157, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015174', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015174', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Exciting Dubai With Abu Dhabi', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015174_0_20260825204024', 'price': 91574, 'packageSummary': "The 'Exciting Dubai With Abu Dhabi' package is a 6-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Dubai and Abu Dhabi. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the towering Burj Khalifa, the magnificent Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, and the thrilling Ferrari World theme park. Participants will enjoy a memorable desert safari with a traditional barbecue dinner, a scenic dhow cruise, and comprehensive guided city tours that showcase the region's futuristic architecture and rich cultural heritage.", 'images': ['Beauty_of_Marina_Dubai_shutterstock_151616084.avif', 'Dubai_Skyline_Adobe_753.jpg', 'DesertCamp_753_new.jpg', '28674_Abu_Dhabi_sheikh_zayed_grand_mosque_UAE_753.jpg', 'AbuDhabiwithFerrariWorld753.jpg', 'Abu_Dhabi_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 91574, 'thumbnailImage': 'Dubai_new_267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015174 is named 'Exciting Dubai With Abu Dhabi' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive in Dubai - Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner (SIC Basis) Transfers: Upon arriving at the airport, you will be met by our representative and transferred to your hotel in Dubai. (Standard Check in time after 14:00 Hrs.) Marina Dhow Cruise - Cruise through the sparkling waters of Dubai Marina aboard a traditional dhow, enjoying panoramic skyline views, an international buffet dinner, and captivating onboard entertainment, including a vibrant Tanoura dance show. Overnight in Dubai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half Day City Tour of Dubai (SIC basis), Visit to Burj Khalifa (124th Floor – Non-prime time) (Slot subject to availability) with Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo Enjoy Breakfast at the hotel. Dubai City Tour - Explore Dubai by going on a half-day tour around the famous cosmopolitan city. See city's most popular attractions such as the Burj Al Arab Hotel, the Palm Islands, and the Dubai Creek. Marvel at what Dubai has to offer, especially the wonderful interiors and massive library collection of the Blue Mosque. Drop off at Dubai Mall. Burj Khalifa - Visit the iconic Burj Khalifa and ascend to the 124th and 125th-floor observation decks for breathtaking panoramic views of Dubai's skyline, desert, and Arabian Gulf. Step onto the open-air terrace for an unforgettable experience. Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo - Explore the spectacular Dubai Aquarium & Underwater Zoo, home to thousands of marine animals, including sharks and rays. Walk through the stunning 48-meter underwater tunnel for breathtaking views and discover fascinating aquatic life from around the world. Overnight in Dubai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner with Tanoora show and many more activities (SIC Basis) Enjoy Breakfast at the hotel. Morning day free for leisure. Desert Discover the magic of Dubai's desert with an adrenaline-filled dune bashing adventure. End the evening at a Bedouin-style camp, where Arabic coffee, dates, a BBQ dinner, and vibrant cultural performances create a memorable experience. Overnight in Dubai., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart Dubai - Proceed Abu Dhabi enroute Abu Dhabi City tour with BAPS Mandir followed by teamLab, Louvre Abu Dhabi, Natural History Museum & Zayed National Museum. – SIC Transfers Enjoy Breakfast at the hotel. Abu Dhabi City Tour - Explore Abu Dhabi's rich heritage and modern landmarks on a city tour featuring the Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, Emirates Palace, Corniche Drive, Qasr Al Watan photo stop, Presidential Palace, Bateen Area, and the vibrant Dates Market. Baps Mandir - Experience the magnificent BAPS Hindu Mandir, Abu Dhabi's first traditional Hindu stone temple. Admire its intricate carvings, stunning architecture, peaceful surroundings, and cultural significance, symbolizing harmony, faith, and unity in the UAE. teamLab – Immerse yourself in teamLab Phenomena Abu Dhabi, an extraordinary digital art experience where interactive light, sound, and motion create ever-changing immersive installations, blending technology, creativity, and nature in a truly captivating journey. Louvre Abu Dhabi Museum – Explore the Louvre Abu Dhabi, a world-renowned museum showcasing masterpieces from diverse civilizations. Admire its iconic floating dome, inspiring galleries, and exceptional collection of art, history, and culture spanning thousands of years. Natural History Museum - Discover the Natural History Museum Abu Dhabi, where immersive exhibits showcase Earth's history, rare fossils, dinosaurs, ancient life, and the wonders of nature, offering an engaging journey through billions of years of evolution and discovery. Zayed National Museum - Discover the Zayed National Museum, dedicated to the legacy of Sheikh Zayed and the rich heritage of the UAE. Explore engaging exhibits showcasing the nation's history, culture, traditions, and remarkable journey from past to present., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: 1 Day 2 Parks (Shuttle Transfers) Enjoy Breakfast at the hotel. Experience any one park out of the mentioned. Ferrari World Experience the thrill of Ferrari World Abu Dhabi, home to Formula Rossa, the world's fastest roller coaster. Enjoy over 20 exhilarating rides, family attractions, immersive experiences, and Ferrari-themed adventures on Yas Island. OR Warner Bros. Step into Warner Bros. World™ Abu Dhabi, an indoor theme park featuring 29 exciting rides, live entertainment, beloved characters, interactive attractions, themed dining, and family fun across immersive worlds. OR SeaWorld® Discover SeaWorld® Yas Island Abu Dhabi, an immersive marine life park with eight themed realms, thrilling attractions, interactive exhibits, and up-close encounters with fascinating marine animals, celebrating ocean conservation., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Abu Dhabi Airport After breakfast, you will be transferred to the airport for your return flight. CHILD POLICY Infant: 0-1.99 yrs Child No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs Child With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs A person aged 12 years and below is considered a child, while anyone above 12 years is classified as an adult., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 91574.0. Hotels envisaged include: \n3 Nights Standard Hotels - Park Inn by Radisson Abu Dhabi Yas Island / Centro Yas Island or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n, \n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Grand Millennium Al Wadha / Dusit Thani\xa0or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n, \n3 Nights Hotel Ramada corniche /\xa0City Season Hamra\xa0/ Hawthrone or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Dubai 02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Abu Dhabi Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Return airport transfers from Dubai Airport (SIC basis) Inter Hotel Transfers with Abu Dhabi City Tour with Baps Temple (Closed on Monday) +Louvre Abu Dhabi, Natural History Museum and Zayed National Museum Half Day City Tour with Burj Khalifa 124 Floor Non-Prime Time (Non-Refundable) + Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo Standard Desert Safari with Dinner Standard Marina Dhow Cruise with Dinner Access To Any 02 Parks (Guest to Manage Transfers Through Shuttle)- One Day 02 Parks, Guest Will Have to Use Shuttle Between the Parks Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: VISAS : UAE VISA REQUIRED AT AN ADDITIONAL COST TCS & GST. UAE VISA USD 100 per person The rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling. All flight services. Pre and post-tour services & costs. Hotel rates are not valid during blackout period / surcharge dates / stop sales. Midnight surcharge. Meals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary. Tips for guide & driver. City tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable). Expenditure of a personal nature (minibar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.) Camera fee. Porterage facility Departure PCR test, if applicable. Visa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable). Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary. Cost of optional excursions. Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list. Blackout date surcharges: DUBAI Diwali 05 – 13 NOV 2026 National Day 02 – 05 DEC 2026 Dubai Air Show 06 – 11 DEC 2026 Christmas & New Year 23 DEC – 03 JAN 2027 Arab Health 23 – 29 JAN 2027 EID AL FITR 06 – 12 MAR 2027 Gulf Food 13 – 20 MAR 2027 ABU DHABI ADIPEC 01 – 05 Nov 2026 Formula 1 - 03 – 06 Dec 2026 IDEX 24 – 29 Jan 2027 | EID AL FITR 07 -10 Mar 2027. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions: The package price is valid until 25 Mar 2027. Rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling. Hotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking. Hotel upgrade pricing does not guarantee rooms at the preferred / envisaged hotels. Hotel upgrade rooms remain subject to availability at the time of booking. If the selected upgrade hotel is unavailable, we will provide alternate options for a similar category. The rates are not valid on blackout dates & Trade Fair periods. Any applicable surcharges will be communicated, and passengers will be required to pay them accordingly. Surcharges, if applicable, are additional to the total package price quoted at the time of booking. Guests are requested to confirm their onward/connecting flights with the sales team before booking. All rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400/1500 hours & Check out time is 1100/1200 hours respectively, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Wherever transfers are included, they are provided without night surcharges. No refunds (partial or full) will be provided for any unutilized services. All sightseeing tours and excursions are operated by local service providers; timings and operating days are subject to change. Changes or Updates, if any, will be shared at the time of booking. Sightseeing tours are strictly subject to weather conditions, and local service providers reserve the right to cancel tours without prior notice. Rates are subject to change without prior notice, including for clients travelling during weekends. Any promotional offer, if applicable, may be withdrawn at any time without prior notice. Once bookings are confirmed, cancellation charges will apply as per policy and will be informed at that time. Organization is not responsible for any price changes arising from factors beyond our control. A refundable security deposit is required at check in as per international hotel policy, payable by credit card or cash; the amount varies by hotel and is returned at check out. Guests should avoid using debit cards since the amount is charged instantly and may take 2–3 weeks to refund. Any additional hotel services (such as mini bar, room service, etc.) may be deducted from this deposit, and Company is not responsible for such transactions, as these are directly between the hotel and the guest.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chandigarh', 'cityCode': 'IXC', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jammu', 'cityCode': 'IXJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'cityCode': 'KNU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kozhikode', 'cityCode': 'CCJ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mangalore', 'cityCode': 'IXE', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Patna', 'cityCode': 'PAT', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Raipur', 'cityCode': 'RPR', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Vadodara', 'cityCode': 'BDQ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Varanasi', 'cityCode': 'VNS', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Visakhapatnam', 'cityCode': 'VTZ', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Exciting Dubai With Abu Dhabi' package is a 6-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Dubai and Abu Dhabi. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the towering Burj Khalifa, the magnificent Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, and the thrilling Ferrari World theme park. Participants will enjoy a memorable desert safari with a traditional barbecue dinner, a scenic dhow cruise, and comprehensive guided city tours that showcase the region's futuristic architecture and rich cultural heritage.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrive in Dubai - Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner (SIC Basis)\n\xa0\nTransfers: Upon arriving at the airport, you will be met by our representative and transferred to your hotel in Dubai.\xa0\n(Standard Check in time after 14:00 Hrs.)\n\xa0\nMarina Dhow Cruise - Cruise through the sparkling waters of Dubai Marina aboard a traditional dhow, enjoying panoramic skyline views, an international buffet dinner, and captivating onboard entertainment, including a vibrant Tanoura dance show.\n\xa0\nOvernight in Dubai.', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Citymax Hotel Bur Dubai (Standard) | Versailles Hotel by Veiras (Value) | Khalidia Palace Dubai Deira (Premium) or Similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 2, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nHalf Day City Tour of Dubai (SIC basis), Visit to Burj Khalifa (124th Floor – Non-prime time) (Slot subject to availability) with Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the hotel.\xa0\n\xa0\nDubai City Tour - Explore Dubai by going on a half-day tour around the famous cosmopolitan city. See city's most popular attractions such as the Burj Al Arab Hotel, the Palm Islands, and the Dubai Creek. Marvel at what Dubai has to offer, especially the wonderful interiors and massive library collection of the Blue Mosque. Drop off at Dubai Mall.\n\xa0\nBurj Khalifa - Visit the iconic Burj Khalifa and ascend to the 124th and 125th-floor observation decks for breathtaking panoramic views of Dubai's skyline, desert, and Arabian Gulf. Step onto the open-air terrace for an unforgettable experience.\n\xa0\nDubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo - Explore the spectacular Dubai Aquarium & Underwater Zoo, home to thousands of marine animals, including sharks and rays. Walk through the stunning 48-meter underwater tunnel for breathtaking views and discover fascinating aquatic life from around the world.\n\xa0\nOvernight in Dubai.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Citymax Hotel Bur Dubai (Standard) | Versailles Hotel by Veiras (Value) | Khalidia Palace Dubai Deira (Premium) or Similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nDesert Safari with BBQ Dinner with Tanoora show and many more activities (SIC Basis)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the hotel.\xa0\n\xa0\nMorning day free for leisure.\nDesert Discover the magic of Dubai's desert with an adrenaline-filled dune bashing adventure. End the evening at a Bedouin-style camp, where Arabic coffee, dates, a BBQ dinner, and vibrant cultural performances create a memorable experience.\n\xa0\nOvernight in Dubai.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Citymax Hotel Bur Dubai (Standard) | Versailles Hotel by Veiras (Value) | Khalidia Palace Dubai Deira (Premium) or Similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 4, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\nDepart Dubai - Proceed Abu Dhabi enroute Abu Dhabi City tour with BAPS Mandir followed by teamLab, Louvre Abu Dhabi, Natural History Museum & Zayed National Museum. – SIC Transfers\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the hotel.\xa0\n\xa0\nAbu Dhabi City Tour - Explore Abu Dhabi's rich heritage and modern landmarks on a city tour featuring the Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, Emirates Palace, Corniche Drive, Qasr Al Watan photo stop, Presidential Palace, Bateen Area, and the vibrant Dates Market.\n\xa0\nBaps Mandir - Experience the magnificent BAPS Hindu Mandir, Abu Dhabi's first traditional Hindu stone temple. Admire its intricate carvings, stunning architecture, peaceful surroundings, and cultural significance, symbolizing harmony, faith, and unity in the UAE.\n\xa0\nteamLab – Immerse yourself in teamLab Phenomena Abu Dhabi, an extraordinary digital art experience where interactive light, sound, and motion create ever-changing immersive installations, blending technology, creativity, and nature in a truly captivating journey.\n\xa0\nLouvre Abu Dhabi Museum – Explore the Louvre Abu Dhabi, a world-renowned museum showcasing masterpieces from diverse civilizations. Admire its iconic floating dome, inspiring galleries, and exceptional collection of art, history, and culture spanning thousands of years.\n\xa0\nNatural History Museum - Discover the Natural History Museum Abu Dhabi, where immersive exhibits showcase Earth's history, rare fossils, dinosaurs, ancient life, and the wonders of nature, offering an engaging journey through billions of years of evolution and discovery.\n\xa0\nZayed National Museum - Discover the Zayed National Museum, dedicated to the legacy of Sheikh Zayed and the rich heritage of the UAE. Explore engaging exhibits showcasing the nation's history, culture, traditions, and remarkable journey from past to present.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel City Season Al Hamra | Ramada Wyndham Abu Dhabi | Ramada Downtown | Tryp By Wyndham (Standard, Value, Premium) or Similar in Abu Dhabi'}, {'day': 5, 'description': "\xa0\n\xa0\n1 Day 2 Parks (Shuttle Transfers)\n\xa0\nEnjoy Breakfast at the hotel.\xa0 Experience any one park out of the mentioned.\n\xa0\nFerrari World\nExperience the thrill of Ferrari World Abu Dhabi, home to Formula Rossa, the world's fastest roller coaster. Enjoy over 20 exhilarating rides, family attractions, immersive experiences, and Ferrari-themed adventures on Yas Island.\n\xa0\nOR\n\xa0\nWarner Bros.\nStep into Warner Bros. World™ Abu Dhabi, an indoor theme park featuring 29 exciting rides, live entertainment, beloved characters, interactive attractions, themed dining, and family fun across immersive worlds.\n\xa0\nOR\n\xa0\nSeaWorld®\nDiscover SeaWorld® Yas Island Abu Dhabi, an immersive marine life park with eight themed realms, thrilling attractions, interactive exhibits, and up-close encounters with fascinating marine animals, celebrating ocean conservation.\n\xa0", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel City Season Al Hamra | Ramada Wyndham Abu Dhabi | Ramada Downtown | Tryp By Wyndham (Standard, Value, Premium) or Similar in Abu Dhabi'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nDeparture Abu Dhabi Airport\xa0\n\xa0\nAfter breakfast, you will be transferred to the airport for your return flight.\n\xa0\n\xa0\nCHILD POLICY\n\xa0\n\nInfant: 0-1.99 yrs\nChild No Bed: 2-5.99 yrs\nChild With Bed: 6-11.99 yrs\nA person aged 12 years and below is considered a child, while anyone above 12 years is classified as an adult.\xa0\n', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['\n3 Nights Standard Hotels - Park Inn by Radisson Abu Dhabi Yas Island / Centro Yas Island or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n', '\n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Grand Millennium Al Wadha / Dusit Thani\xa0or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n', '\n3 Nights Hotel Ramada corniche /\xa0City Season Hamra\xa0/ Hawthrone or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': '\n3 Nights Standard Hotels - Park Inn by Radisson Abu Dhabi Yas Island / Centro Yas Island or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n', '2': '\n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Grand Millennium Al Wadha / Dusit Thani\xa0or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n', '1': '\n3 Nights Hotel Ramada corniche /\xa0City Season Hamra\xa0/ Hawthrone or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AE', 'countryName': 'United Arab Emirates', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Standard', 'Value', 'Premium'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Standard', 'price': 91600.0, 'hotels': ['\n3 Nights Standard Hotels - Park Inn by Radisson Abu Dhabi Yas Island / Centro Yas Island or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n']}, {'category': 'Value', 'price': 98000.0, 'hotels': ['\n3 Nights Hotel Ramada corniche /\xa0City Season Hamra\xa0/ Hawthrone or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n']}, {'category': 'Premium', 'price': 104900.0, 'hotels': ['\n3 Nights Hotel\xa0Grand Millennium Al Wadha / Dusit Thani\xa0or Similar in Abu Dhabi\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included'], 'visa': [], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['\nHalf Day Abu Dhabi City tour (SIC basis)\nTeam Labs\n2 Day 2 Parks with Shuttle transfers\n', '\nHalf Day Abu Dhabi City tour (SIC basis)\n2 Day 2 Parks with Shuttle transfers\n', '\nHalf day Abu Dubai city tour (SIC basis)\n2 Day Access to any 2 Parks (Ferrari world or Warner bros or Sea world)\n'], 'tourManagerDescription': '', 'flightDescription': 'Return Economy Class Airfare', 'inclusions': '\n03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Dubai\n02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Abu Dhabi\nDaily breakfast, except on Day 1\nReturn airport transfers from Dubai Airport (SIC basis)\xa0\nInter Hotel Transfers with Abu Dhabi City Tour with Baps Temple (Closed on Monday) +Louvre Abu Dhabi, Natural History Museum and Zayed National Museum\nHalf Day City Tour with Burj Khalifa 124 Floor Non-Prime Time (Non-Refundable) + Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo\nStandard Desert Safari with Dinner\nStandard Marina Dhow Cruise with Dinner\nAccess To Any 02 Parks (Guest to Manage Transfers Through Shuttle)- One Day 02 Parks, Guest Will Have to Use Shuttle Between the Parks\nTravel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.)\xa0\n', 'exclusions': '\nVISAS : UAE VISA REQUIRED AT AN ADDITIONAL COST\xa0\nTCS & GST.\nUAE VISA USD 100 per person\xa0\nThe rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling.\nAll flight services.\nPre and post-tour services & costs.\nHotel rates are not valid during blackout period / surcharge dates / stop sales.\nMidnight surcharge.\nMeals and beverages that are not mentioned in the itinerary.\nTips for guide & driver.\nCity tax & Tourism Tax (if applicable).\nExpenditure of a personal nature (minibar, refrigerator use, laundry, telephone calls, etc.)\nCamera fee.\nPorterage facility\nDeparture PCR test, if applicable.\nVisa charges for NRI passengers (if applicable).\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees, and local guides not mentioned in the itinerary.\xa0\nCost of optional excursions.\nAnything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions list.\n\nBlackout date surcharges:\nDUBAI\xa0\n\nDiwali 05 – 13 NOV 2026\xa0\nNational Day 02 – 05 DEC 2026\xa0\nDubai Air Show 06 – 11 DEC 2026\xa0\nChristmas & New Year 23 DEC – 03 JAN 2027\nArab Health 23 – 29 JAN 2027\xa0\nEID AL FITR 06 – 12 MAR 2027\xa0\nGulf Food 13 – 20 MAR 2027\xa0\n\nABU DHABI\xa0\n\nADIPEC 01 – 05 Nov 2026\xa0\nFormula 1 - 03 – 06 Dec 2026\xa0\nIDEX 24 – 29 Jan 2027 |\nEID AL FITR 07 -10 Mar 2027\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nTerms and Conditions:\n\nThe package price is valid until 25 Mar 2027.\nRates are valid for a minimum of 01 adult travelling.\nHotel upgrade prices are subject to availability at the time of booking.\nHotel upgrade pricing does not guarantee rooms at the preferred / envisaged hotels.\nHotel upgrade rooms remain subject to availability at the time of booking.\nIf the selected upgrade hotel is unavailable, we will provide alternate options for a similar category.\nThe rates are not valid on blackout dates & Trade Fair periods.\xa0\nAny applicable surcharges will be communicated, and passengers will be required to pay them accordingly.\nSurcharges, if applicable, are additional to the total package price quoted at the time of booking.\nGuests are requested to confirm their onward/connecting flights with the sales team before booking.\nAll rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing at the time of booking.\nWe reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\xa0\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\xa0\nInternational Check in time is 1400/1500 hours & Check out time is 1100/1200 hours respectively, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\xa0\nWherever transfers are included, they are provided without night surcharges.\nNo refunds (partial or full) will be provided for any unutilized services.\nAll sightseeing tours and excursions are operated by local service providers; timings and operating days are subject to change. Changes or Updates, if any, will be shared at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly subject to weather conditions, and local service providers reserve the right to cancel tours without prior notice.\nRates are subject to change without prior notice, including for clients travelling during weekends.\nAny promotional offer, if applicable, may be withdrawn at any time without prior notice.\nOnce bookings are confirmed, cancellation charges will apply as per policy and will be informed at that time.\nOrganization is not responsible for any price changes arising from factors beyond our control.\nA refundable security deposit is required at check in as per international hotel policy, payable by credit card or cash; the amount varies by hotel and is returned at check out. Guests should avoid using debit cards since the amount is charged instantly and may take 2–3 weeks to refund. Any additional hotel services (such as mini bar, room service, etc.) may be deducted from this deposit, and Company is not responsible for such transactions, as these are directly between the hotel and the guest.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/Dubai_new_267.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/itinerary/Beauty_of_Marina_Dubai_shutterstock_151616084.avif', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/itinerary/Dubai_Skyline_Adobe_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/itinerary/DesertCamp_753_new.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/itinerary/28674_Abu_Dhabi_sheikh_zayed_grand_mosque_UAE_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/itinerary/AbuDhabiwithFerrariWorld753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015174/itinerary/Abu_Dhabi_753.jpg']}, 'score': 8.87126, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG012838', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG012838', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Astonishing Dubai With Abu Dhabi', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG012838_0_20260916133011.pdf', 'price': 74679, 'packageSummary': "The 'Astonishing Dubai With Abu Dhabi' package is a 6-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Dubai and Abu Dhabi. The itinerary includes a variety of exciting activities such as a thrilling desert safari with a barbecue dinner, a traditional dhow cruise, and a visit to the observation deck of the iconic Burj Khalifa. Participants will also enjoy comprehensive guided city tours, exploring major landmarks like the magnificent Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque and the high-speed attractions of Ferrari World.", 'images': ['Dubai7534.jpg', 'BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'DesertCamp_753_new.jpg', '753_Sheikh_Zayed_Grand_Mosque_Abu_Dhabi_UAE.jpg', 'FerrariWorld_753.jpg', '1114_Abu_Dhabi753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 74679, 'thumbnailImage': 'Dubai267.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG012838 is named 'Astonishing Dubai With Abu Dhabi' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrive at Dubai - Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner (SIC basis) Welcome to Dubai – famous for the record-breaking Burj Khalifa, Dubai Mall, and the Palm, its vibrant culture, turbulent history, modern infrastructure, huge aquariums, and indoor ski slopes. Upon arrival at the airport, pick up from the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.) Later we visit the Marina Dhow Cruise. Marina Dhow Cruise offers dazzling amazing views of the Dubai cityscape. Take in the lavish architecture of residences, resorts, and shopping facilities, as you feast on a scrumptious fare of international cuisines served in a sophisticated, traditional ambiance. As you dine, you'll enjoy mind-blowing entertainment on-board by dazzling lights that reflect off the water as well as Egyptian Tanura Dance performances., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half Day City Tour of Dubai (SIC basis), Visit to Burj Khalifa (124th Floor – Non prime time) (Slot subject to availability) with Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo (SIC Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Explore Dubai by going on a half-day tour around the famous cosmopolitan city. See city's most popular attractions such as the Burj Al Arab Hotel, the Palm Islands, and the Dubai Creek. Marvel at what Dubai has to offer, especially the wonderful interiors and massive library collection of the Blue Mosque. Drop off at Dubai Mall. Walk to Burj Khalifa. A visit to Burj Khalifa's observation deck on the 124th and 125th floors is a must-do for every visitor in Dubai. Once at the top, enjoy breathtaking views of Dubai's skyline, desert and ocean through the floor-to-ceiling glass walls. Make sure to use the telescopes provided for close-up real time views of the areas below. Venture outside into the open-air terrace and enjoy a more clear perspective of the sweeping views of Dubai. Later we visit Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo. See the true marvels of Dubai with a visit to the city's aquarium and underwater zoo. Dubai Mall is home to one of the world's largest suspended aquariums. The 10-million-liter tank is home to over 300 sharks and rays and boasts the largest collection of tiger sharks in the world., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Premium Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner, Belly dance, Tanoora show and many more activities (SIC Basis) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Later, in the evening desert safari in Dubai is one of the most memorable experiences that you can have in this vibrant city. After getting picked up at your hotel, head to the sand dunes to experience the dune bashing. Enjoy this exhilarating adventure as you speed up and down the golden sands. As it gets dark, proceed to the Bedouin campsite where you can sip some Arabic coffee and munch on sweet dates. Watch spectacular belly dancing and tanoura dancing performances as well as an awesome fire show. Refuel with a huge BBQ dinner., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Dubai – Abu Dhabi City Tour & BAPS Visit After breakfast proceed to Abu Dhabi Discover the UAE’s capital on an Abu Dhabi city tour starting from Dubai. Begin at the beautiful BAPS Hindu Mandir, then enjoy a scenic drive along the Corniche with views of modern skyscrapers and pristine beaches. Marvel at the majestic Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque. Stop for photos at the iconic Emirates Palace and visit Qasr Al Watan for a unique insight into Arab heritage and governance Check in at the hotel (standard time approx. 1400 hrs.) Note: BAPS temple is closed on Mondays, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Abu Dhabi – Any 2 Park Access Ticket (Shuttle) Breakfast at hotel You have an option to choose between Ferrari World OR Warner Bros OR SEA WORLD Ferrari World Nothing gets the adrenaline pumping like riding the world's fastest rollercoaster, Formula Rossa, here at Ferrari World Abu Dhabi. Feel the exhilaration as you go from 0 to 240km/h in 4.9 seconds while soaring 52 meters in the air. The whole family will find an adrenaline-fueled ride just for them; everyone can join in the high-octane fun. The Ferrari-branded theme park on Yas Island is home to more than 20 record-breaking attractions, including the highest loop ride, and it all happens underneath the tallest space-frame structure on the planet. OR Warner Bros. Enter a vibrant world of unlimited fun tucked away indoors at the Warner Bros. World™ Abu Dhabi. Spending a day at the whopping 1.65 million square foot park is easy as you fill in the hours by hopping between the 29 amazing rides! Interactive family-friendly attractions and live entertainment are guaranteed giggles for the younger ones, while shopping and dining venues keep you happy and energized. OR SeaWorld® Welcome to SeaWorld® Yas Island, Abu Dhabi - the next generation of marine life theme parks that will take your breath away! Prepare for an unforgettable adventure that uncovers the interconnectivity between life on Earth and our oceans, inspiring a deep commitment to conserving our planet. Be captivated by the park’s 'One Ocean' story, uncovering how we are all connected to the ocean and how the ocean connects us all. Through ‘One Ocean’, you can explore eight themed realms where you can witness over 100 animal experiences and get the opportunity to get up close to some of the marine world’s marvelous creatures. (Note: 2-day 2 park access can be utilized on Day 4 & 5), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Depart from Abu Dhabi Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India. Note: The above itinerary is tentative and subject to change without prior notice, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 74679.0. Hotels envisaged include: Standard Hotels:\xa0\n\n3 Nights stay in Howard Jonhson / City Max Bur Dubai / Admiral / Fortune Pearl or Similar\xa0in Dubai\n2 Nights stay in Ramada Corniche / Hawthrone by Whyndham or similar\xa0in Abu Dhabi\n, Premium Hotels:\xa0\n\n3 Nights stay in Avani Deira or similar\xa0in Dubai\n2 Nights stay in Crowne Plaza Abu Dhabi or similar\xa0in Abu Dhabi\n, Value Hotels:\xa0\n\n3 Nights stay in LaQuinta / Ramada Plaza Deira Or Similar\xa0in Dubai\n2 Nights stay in Ramada Corniche / Downtown Ramada / City Seasons Hamra/ Hawthrone Suites by Whyndham Abu Dhabi or similar\xa0in Abu Dhabi\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Dubai. 02 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Abu Dhabi Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Dubai Airport – Dubai Hotel (Private Basis) Abu Dhabi – Abu Dhabi Airport (Private Basis) Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner (SIC basis) Half Day City Tour followed by Burj Khalifa 124th Floor Non-Prime (SIC Basis) Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner (SIC Basis) Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo Abu Dhabi City Tour with BAPS visit and drop to hotel (SIC Basis) 2 Park pass with free shuttle bus only from hotel. 5% VAT Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST UAE VISA Departure PCR test, if applicable All flights service Meals that are not mentioned in the itinerary. Any tips for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions. Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms and Conditions: The upgrade of hotel prices is subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the hotels envisaged. The upgraded hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgraded hotel, in case the hotel chosen is unavailable, we will provide multiple options of similar category hotels. The rates are valid for a minimum of 02 adults travelling. The rates are not valid on blackout dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers will be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their onwards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Kannur', 'cityCode': 'CNN', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Goa', 'cityCode': 'GOI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhopal', 'cityCode': 'BHO', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Madurai', 'cityCode': 'IXM', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Aurangabad', 'cityCode': 'IXU', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Nagpur', 'cityCode': 'NAG', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Mumbai'