ityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['DUBAI Experience a Limousine Ride 360 Degrees Panoramic View of the Palm Island - The View Palm Jumeirah Ride on a Monorail to the Palm Island Visit Gold & Spice Souk Experience the Yacht Ride on Dubai Marina Guided City tour of Dubai Visit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (non-prime slot) Visit Global Village Visit Dolphin Aquarium Experience the Desert Safari with Dune bashing & BBQ Dinner ABU DHABI Visit Team Lab Guided City tour of Abu Dhabi Photo stop at the Sheikh Zayed Mosque, Grand Mosque Visit Ferrari World or Warner Bros or Sea World (Guests will be offered a 1 Day 1 Park Ticket with access to any of the 1 theme parks) WHATS MORE Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Free flow of soft drinks and beer on Yacht Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box ( 1 box per family)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG003806_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 136932, 'packageSummary': "The 'Magical Dubai With Abu Dhabi (Winter)' package is an exciting 6-day tour covering the spectacular cities of Dubai and Abu Dhabi. Throughout this journey, participants will experience a luxurious limousine ride, a scenic yacht cruise along Dubai Marina with free-flow drinks, a monorail ride to Palm Island, and breathtaking 360-degree views from The View Palm Jumeirah. The itinerary also includes guided city tours of both Dubai and Abu Dhabi, visits to the traditional Gold and Spice Souk, the iconic 124th floor of the Burj Khalifa, the Global Village, the Dolphin Aquarium, and a thrilling desert safari complete with dune bashing and a barbecue dinner. Additionally, travelers will explore Team Lab, make a photo stop at the majestic Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque, enjoy a full-day ticket to their choice of Ferrari World, Warner Bros, or Sea World, and receive special perks like ice cream during tours and an exclusive souvenir box.", 'images': ['dubaiyatch.jpg', 'PALM JUMEIRAH - 753X430.jpg', 'BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'DesertCamp_753_new-ezgif.com-resize.jpg', 'AbuDhabiwithFerrariWorld753.jpg', 'AbudhabiCity.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 136932, 'thumbnailImage': 'DubaiWithAbuDhabi2671.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Most Booked', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015292 is named 'Magical Dubai With Abu Dhabi (Winter)' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Dubai - Check In – Enjoy Limo Ride Welcome to United Arab Emirates. On arrival in Dubai, you will be greeted by your friendly Tour Manager / local representative outside the baggage hall area at the airport. Transfer to the hotel & check-in. (Standard Check in time after 1500Hrs). Rest of the day is at leisure. Later enjoy two-hour Limousine ride, sit back in the most comfortable and luxurious stretch limousine and explore the night city view. NOTE: All our guests are advised to activate international calling/data & international credit card Joining direct passengers / NRI passengers can check-in on your own at the hotel. The standard check-in time is 1500 hrs. Early morning arrivals will be provided Breakfast (Not applicable for Joining Direct Passengers), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit The View At Palm Jumeirah - Ride On Monorail – Visit Gold Souk - Experience The Yacht Cruise This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to Palm Jumeirah to experience a breathtaking view of the Palm Island from the top. Ride on the monorail ride to the Palm. Free time for shopping at Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Later this evening proceed to the marina for a Yacht Cruise with free flow of soft drinks & beer. Overnight in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Burj Khalifa - Guided City Tour Of Dubai – Global Village This morning after buffet breakfast, Visit 124th Floor of Burj Khalifa (non-prime hours). Later proceed for a guided city tour of Dubai along with Photo stop at the Dubai Frame, Museum of the Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace. Proceed for Global Village a shopping, dining, and entertainment attraction located on Sheikh Mohammed Bin Zayed Road. There are four main sections in the Village. These sections consist of events and concerts, carnivals, food, and shopping. Overnight in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Dubai Dolphinarium – Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & Bbq Dinner This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to visit Dubai Dolphinarium. The Dolphin & Seal Show, the #1 in the UAE. These interactive extravaganzas showcase the amazing animals' astounding skills. Visitors watch in wonder as the dolphins and seals dance, sing, juggle, play ball, jump through hoops and even paint. Free time for shopping at Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Later this evening proceed to the marina for a Yacht Cruise with free flow of soft drinks & beer. Overnight in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Proceed To Abu Dhabi - Visit Team Lab - Guided City Tour Of Abu Dhabi - Photostop At Grand Mosque - Entrance To Ferrari World / Warner Bros / Sea World (Any 1 Park) This morning after buffet breakfast, proceed to Abu Dhabi. Visit Team Lab - an digital museum that collaborates the confluence of art, science, technology, and the natural world. Later we proceed on a guided city tour of Abu Dhabi city tour along-with a photostop at the Grand Mosque . Later this afternoon we proceed to Yas Island - Our guest have a choice to visit Ferrari World or Warner Bros or Sea World (1 Park entry included). Overnight in Abu Dhabi, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. Late Evening Departures Will Be Provided Lunch (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers) Note: On few days there will be a coach merger with other UAE product's (if required) Note : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 136932.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n04 nights accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai (Free upgrade to 5* Hotel Crown Plaza)\n01 night accommodation at Hotel Ramada Corniche or similar in Abu Dhabi (Free upgrade to 5* Hotel Dusit Thani)\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily American buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n03 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 Lunch Coupon ( At Park visit in Abu Dhabi)\n01 Local BBQ Buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n04\xa0 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)\n. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. All local taxes including services taxes as of 1st August 2026. Cost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Tourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT Visa Requirements: UAE Visa included ( E-visa) Cost Of Visas Including Documentation And Processing Fees As Of 1st June 2026. Any Further Increase In The Same Must Be Borne By The Passengers.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 1st August 2026) Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: General Info Currency Used: UAE : UAE Dirham Time Difference: UAE : 1 hours and 30 minutes behind IST Important Notes: AIRLINE AND AIRFARE The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st November 2025. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Cost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package. HOTELS This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and the room size will be the same as double room. 04 guest in one room are not allowed For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs, you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant. COACHES Coaches are an important part of your journeys, and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors, it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop-off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. MEALS All Meals are pre–set. Packed lunches will be provided on certain days. SIGHTSEEING Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc. GENERAL On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour. Security alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. THOMAS COOK will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. THOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”. Highlights of the package: DUBAI Experience a Limousine Ride 360 Degrees Panoramic View of the Palm Island - The View Palm Jumeirah Ride on a Monorail to the Palm Island Visit Gold & Spice Souk Experience the Yacht Ride on Dubai Marina Guided City tour of Dubai Visit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (non-prime slot) Visit Global Village Visit Dolphin Aquarium Experience the Desert Safari with Dune bashing & BBQ Dinner ABU DHABI Visit Team Lab Guided City tour of Abu Dhabi Photo stop at the Sheikh Zayed Mosque, Grand Mosque Visit Ferrari World or Warner Bros or Sea World (Guests will be offered a 1 Day 1 Park Ticket with access to any of the 1 theme parks) WHATS MORE Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Free flow of soft drinks and beer on Yacht Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box ( 1 box per family).", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAH753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityN