rice due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. TCIL would not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 1, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/Dubai865.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/itinerary/Dhow_Cruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/itinerary/Stock_4426_Dubai_Burj_Khalifa753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/itinerary/DubaiDesertSafari753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/itinerary/Abudhabi7532.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/itinerary/AbuDhabiwithFerrariWorld753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015594/itinerary/AbudhabiCity.jpg']}, 'score': 8.296414, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015581', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015581', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Highlights of Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah (Winter)', 'days': 6, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ras Al Khaimah', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ras Al Khaimah', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box (1 box per family)'], 'pdfName': 'PKG009156_0_undefined.pdf', 'price': 121076, 'packageSummary': "The 'Highlights of Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah (Winter)' package is a 6-day tour covering the beautiful destinations of Ras Al Khaimah and Dubai. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will enjoy key activities such as a refreshing ice cream treat during a city tour or a visit to the Dolphin Aquarium. To make the trip even more memorable, each family will receive an exclusive 'Dubai Memories' souvenir box as a special keepsake of their travels.", 'images': ['dubaiyatch.jpg', 'Burj_Khalifa_1_753.jpg', 'DubaiDesertSafari753.jpg', 'jumeriahbeachDubai_753.jpg', 'RasAlKhaimah753.jpg', 'RasAlKhaimah7534.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 121076, 'thumbnailImage': 'Atlantispalmbeach.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Recommended', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015581 is named 'Highlights of Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah (Winter)' and spans 6 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Dubai - Check In Welcome To United Arab Emirates. On Arrival In Dubai, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs).Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure. Note All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs. Early Morning Arrivals Will Be Provided Breakfast (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers), GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Guided City Tour Of Dubai - Visit Burj Khalifa - Visit Global Village This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Dubai Alongwith Photo Stop At The Dubai Frame , Museum Of The Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace. Free Time For Shopping At Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Visit 124th Floor Of Burj Khalifa (Non-Prime Hours).Later This Evening Visit Global Village., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Dubai Dolphinarium - Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & BBQ Dinner This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Dubai Dolphinarium. The Dolphin & Seal Show, the #1 in the UAE. These interactive extravaganzas showcase the amazing animals' astounding skills. Visitors watch in wonder as the dolphins and seals dance, sing, juggle, play ball, jump through hoops and even paint. Later This Afternoon Proceed For Desert Safari To Enjoy The Thrilling Dune Bashing On A Desert Safari Adventure Exploring The Massive Sand Dunes Of The Arabian Deserts. Enjoy Bbq Dinner And The Belly Dancing Performance At The Desert Camp., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Enjoy Limousine Ride - Visit The View At Palm Jumeirah - Experience The Yacht Cruise This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed On A Limousine Ride(60 Minutes) And Explore The City. Later Proceed To Palm Jumeirah To Experience A Breathtaking View Of The Palm Island From The Top. Later This Evening Proceed To The Marina For A Yacht Cruise With Free Flow Of Soft Drinks & Beer., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Ras Al Khaimah, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Proceed To Ras Al Khaimah - City Tour Of Ras Al Khaimah This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Ras Al Khaimah. Later We Proceed On A City Tour Of Ras Al Khaimah., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ras Al Khaimah, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. Late Evening Departures Will Be Provided Lunch (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers) Note : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 121076.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, \n04 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai\n01 night accommodation at Hotel Pullman Resort Al Marjan Island or similar in Ras\xa0Al Khaimah\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included, \nDaily American buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 Local BBQ Buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n04\xa0 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner). Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. All local taxes including services taxes as of 1st August 2026. Cost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 8 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 5 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Tourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT Visa Requirements Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 202. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 1st August 2026) Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: Hotel Security Deposit Policy: International hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay. The amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out. Thomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel. General Info Currency Used : UAE : UAE Dirham Time Difference: UAE : 1 hours and 30 minutes behind IST Important Notes:Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st October 2024. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. Cost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package. Hotels: This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and the room size will be the same as double room. 04 guest in one room are not allowed For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room. A person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult. Due to international events and trade fairs, you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary. Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant. Coaches: Coaches are an important part of your journeys, and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors, it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives. Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop-off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. Meals: All Meals are pre–set. Packed lunches will be provided on certain days. Sightseeing: Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour. Security alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. THOMAS COOK will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. THOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box (1 box per family).", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Guwahati', 'cityCode': 'GAU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Lucknow', 'cityCode': 'LKO', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Indore', 'cityCode': 'IDR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Surat', 'cityCode': 'STV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Amritsar', 'cityCode': 'ATQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Pune', 'cityCode': 'PNQ', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Coimbatore', 'cityCode': 'CJB', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Joining Direct', 'cityCode': 'JD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAR753', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}], 'packageItinerary': {'summary': "The 'Highlights of Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah (Winter)' package is a 6-day tour covering the beautiful destinations of Ras Al Khaimah and Dubai. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will enjoy key activities such as a refreshing ice cream treat during a city tour or a visit to the Dolphin Aquarium. To make the trip even more memorable, each family will receive an exclusive 'Dubai Memories' souvenir box as a special keepsake of their travels.", 'itinerary': [{'day': 1, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nArrival In Dubai - Check In\nWelcome To United Arab Emirates. On Arrival In Dubai, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs).Rest Of The Day Is At Leisure.\n\xa0\nNote\n\nAll Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card\nJoining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs.\nEarly Morning Arrivals Will Be Provided Breakfast (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers)\n', 'mealDescription': 'Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 2, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nGuided City Tour Of Dubai - Visit Burj Khalifa - Visit Global Village\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed For A Guided City Tour Of Dubai Alongwith Photo Stop At The Dubai Frame , Museum Of The Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace. Free Time For Shopping At Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Visit 124th Floor Of Burj Khalifa (Non-Prime Hours).Later This Evening Visit Global Village.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 3, 'description': "\xa0\nVisit Dubai Dolphinarium\xa0- Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & BBQ Dinner\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Dubai Dolphinarium. The Dolphin & Seal Show, the #1 in the UAE.\xa0These interactive extravaganzas showcase the amazing animals' astounding skills.\xa0 Visitors watch in wonder as the dolphins and seals dance, sing, juggle, play ball, jump through hoops and even paint.\nLater This Afternoon Proceed For Desert Safari To Enjoy The Thrilling Dune Bashing On A Desert Safari Adventure Exploring The Massive Sand Dunes Of The Arabian Deserts. Enjoy Bbq Dinner And The Belly Dancing Performance At The Desert Camp.", 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 4, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnjoy Limousine Ride - Visit The View At Palm Jumeirah - Experience The Yacht Cruise\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed On A Limousine Ride(60 Minutes) And Explore The City. Later Proceed To Palm Jumeirah To Experience A Breathtaking View Of The Palm Island From The Top. Later This Evening Proceed To The Marina For A Yacht Cruise With Free Flow Of Soft Drinks & Beer.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai'}, {'day': 5, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nProceed To Ras Al Khaimah - City Tour Of Ras Al Khaimah\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Ras Al Khaimah. Later We Proceed On A City Tour Of Ras Al Khaimah.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner', 'overnightStay': 'Hotel\xa0Pullman Resort Al Marjan Island or similar in Ras Al Khaimah'}, {'day': 6, 'description': '\xa0\n\xa0\nEnd Of Tour - Fly Back\nThis Morning\xa0 After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour.\n\xa0\nLate Evening Departures Will Be Provided Lunch (Not Applicable For Joining Direct Passengers)\n\xa0\nNote : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice.', 'mealDescription': 'Breakfast', 'overnightStay': 'N/A'}]}, 'hotels': ['Overnight stay at the Hotels', '\n04 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai\n01 night accommodation at Hotel Pullman Resort Al Marjan Island or similar in Ras\xa0Al Khaimah\n'], 'hotels_list': {'0': 'Overnight stay at the Hotels', '1': '\n04 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai\n01 night accommodation at Hotel Pullman Resort Al Marjan Island or similar in Ras\xa0Al Khaimah\n'}, 'continents': [{'continentId': 1, 'countryCode': 'AE', 'countryName': 'United Arab Emirates', 'continentName': 'Asia'}], 'packageTourType': ['Value'], 'packageTourType_details': [{'category': 'Value', 'price': 121100.0, 'hotels': ['\n04 nights’ accommodation at Howard Johnson by Wyndham or similar in Dubai\n01 night accommodation at Hotel Pullman Resort Al Marjan Island or similar in Ras\xa0Al Khaimah\n']}], 'meals': ['Breakfast Included', '\nDaily American buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n04 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n01 Local BBQ Buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n04\xa0 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner)'], 'visa': ['As per itinerary', '\nUAE Visa included ( E-visa)\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st June 2025. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\n'], 'transfer': ['As per itinerary'], 'sightseeing': ['Dubai\n\nGuided City tour of Dubai\xa0\nVisit Gold & Spice Souk\nVisit Burj Khalifa 124th floor (non-prime slot)\nVisit Global Village\nVisit Dubai Dolphinarium\nExperience the Desert Safari with Dune bashing & BBQ\xa0\nExperience a Limousine Ride ( 60 minutes)\n360 Degrees Panoramic View of the Palm Island\xa0 - The View Palm Jumeirah\xa0\xa0\nExperience the Yacht Ride on Dubai Marina ( 120 minutes)\n\nRas Al Khaimah\n\nCity tour of Ras Al Khaimah\n', 'Sightseeing as per itinerary'], 'tourManagerDescription': '<p>Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 8 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 5 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.</p>', 'flightDescription': '<p>Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.</p>', 'inclusions': '\nReturn economy class group airfare as per the itinerary.\xa0\nAccommodation at the hotels specified above or similar.\xa0\nAll local taxes including services taxes as of 1st August 2026.\xa0\nCost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour.\xa0\nSightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary.\xa0\nAll transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach.\xa0\nProfessional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 8 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 5 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis.\nTourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT\xa0\n\nVisa Requirements\n\nCost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 202. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.\n', 'exclusions': '\nIf you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date.\xa0\nCost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 2,50,000.\xa0\nAny increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 1st August 2026)\xa0\nApplicable Government Taxes and other service charges.\xa0\nThe tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges.\xa0\nPorterage Facility\xa0\nAny other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package.\xa0\nAdditional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary.\xa0\nCost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary.\xa0\nCost of Optional Excursions.\xa0\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nHotel Security Deposit Policy:\n\nInternational hotels may require a refundable security deposit per room at check-in, payable by credit card or cash. The amount varies and covers incidentals that might occur during the stay.\nThe amount charged to a client’s card is on hold till the length of stay and gets auto-released. We advise the guests to confirm the same at check out.\nThomas Cook is not responsible for these transactions, which are solely between the guest and the hotel.\n\n\xa0\nGeneral Info\n\nCurrency Used :\xa0 UAE : UAE Dirham\nTime Difference: UAE : 1 hours and 30 minutes behind IST\n\nImportant Notes:Airline and Airfare:\n\nThe airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st October 2024. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers.\xa0\nPassengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers.\nFor prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents.\nCost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package.\n\nHotels:\n\nThis Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be in the airport area or on the outskirts.\xa0\nAs a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer roll-away beds and the room size will be the same as double room.\n04 guest in one room are not allowed\nFor Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room.\nA person 12 years and below is considered a child and above 12 years, an adult.\nDue to international events and trade fairs, you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city.\xa0\nAny damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers.\xa0\nWe also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary.\nHotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurant.\n\nCoaches:\n\nCoaches are an important part of your journeys, and we request our guests to keep the coach clean.\nDue to hygiene factors, it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However, the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives.\nEating & drinking is not permitted in the coach.\nDue to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only\xa0\nDue to parking regulations and designated drop-off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop.\nCoaches do not have wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach.\nCoaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers.\n\nMeals:\n\nAll Meals are pre–set.\nPacked lunches will be provided on certain days.\n\nSightseeing:\n\nDue to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same.\nGenerally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however, the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry a good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible.\nEvery Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same.\nAll our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays, at the same time there may be delays caused due to overcrowding, local regulations, security check etc.\n\nGeneral:\n\nOn some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members.\nA local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the initial part of your tour.\nSecurity alerts and unforeseen closures may affect the itinerary.\nPlease take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. THOMAS COOK will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage.\nDisabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements.\nTHOMAS COOK shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour.\nNormal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges.\nThe management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services.\nThe Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour. All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends.\nThere are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour\nIn case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed.\nThe images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only.\nTours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time.\nPlease refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 3, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'GIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': -1, 'productId': 4, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package includes flights in the package price.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/Atlantispalmbeach.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/itinerary/dubaiyatch.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/itinerary/Burj_Khalifa_1_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/itinerary/DubaiDesertSafari753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/itinerary/jumeriahbeachDubai_753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/itinerary/RasAlKhaimah753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015581/itinerary/RasAlKhaimah7534.jpg']}, 'score': 8.067059, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015260', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015260', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'october_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah 6N/7D Winter', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ras Al Khaimah', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ras Al Khaimah', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ras Al Khaimah', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Ras Al Khaimah', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': [''], 'pdfName': 'PKG015260_0_20260922163140', 'price': 84406, 'packageSummary': "The 'Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah 6N/7D Winter' package is a 7-day tour covering the exciting destinations of Ras Al Khaimah and Dubai. The itinerary includes visits to iconic landmarks such as the towering Burj Khalifa, the Dubai Mall, Jumeirah Mosque, and the majestic mountain peaks of Jebel Jais. Participants will enjoy guided city tours, a thrilling desert safari with a traditional barbecue dinner, a scenic dhow cruise, and ample time to relax on the pristine beaches of Ras Al Khaimah.", 'images': ['Dhow_Cruise_DXB_753.jpg', 'BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'Desert_Safari_753.png', 'Ras_Al_Khaimah_City_753.jpg', 'Wadi_Shehah_Ras_Al_Khaimah_753.jpg', 'Ras-Al-Khaimah-1.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 84406, 'thumbnailImage': 'Ras_Al_Khaimah_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Family', 'Adventure'], 'isTcilRecomended': '', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015260 is named 'Dubai With Ras Al Khaimah 6N/7D Winter' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival - Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner - Shared Basis Welcome to Dubai. Upon arrival at the airport, you will be picked up and transferred to your hotel for check in. standard check in time is approximately 1400 hrs. Later in the evening, enjoy the Marina Dhow Cruise - Shared basis Enjoy Marina Dhow Cruise Sail along Dubai Marina’s glittering skyline aboard a traditional dhow. Admire modern architecture, waterfront resorts, and shopping complexes while enjoying onboard entertainment and cultural performances. Relish Buffet Dinner Relish a sumptuous international buffet dinner served in an elegant setting. The meal is complemented by dazzling reflections on the water and live shows, making it a memorable culinary and cultural experience. See Tanura Dance Witness the mesmerizing Tanura Dance, a traditional performance featuring vibrant costumes and spinning movements. This cultural highlight adds authenticity and charm to your evening on the dhow cruise. Overnight in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Half Day City Tour with Burj Khalifa. Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Proceed on a guided tour of Dubai Photo-stop at Burj Al Arab Hotel Admire the world famous Burj Al Arab, Dubai’s sail shaped luxury hotel. Known for its opulent interiors and striking architecture, it stands as a global symbol of modern design and extravagant hospitality. Drives pass Palm Islands Marvel at the Palm Islands, an engineering wonder shaped like a palm tree. These man made islands host luxury resorts, residences, and entertainment venues, showcasing Dubai’s ambition and creativity. Drive pass Dubai Creek Discover Dubai Creek, the historic waterway that divides the city into Deira and Bur Dubai. Once a hub for pearl diving and trade, it now offers a blend of heritage, bustling souks, and modern attractions. Photo-stop at Jumeirah Mosque renowned for its stunning view. Its intricate design and spiritual ambiance make it a cultural gem and a peaceful retreat in the city. Visit Burj Khalifa Observation Deck Ascend to the 124th floor of the Burj Khalifa for breathtaking views of Dubai’s skyline, desert, and coastline. Floor to ceiling glass panels and telescopes offer close up perspectives of the glittering cityscape. Visit Dubai Aquarium Explore one of the world’s largest indoor aquariums, home to thousands of aquatic creatures. Walk through the immersive tunnel and marvel at sharks, rays, and vibrant tropical fish swimming overhead. Visit Underwater Zoo Encounter fascinating marine species at the Underwater Zoo, from penguins and crocodiles to jellyfish. Interactive exhibits bring you face to face with diverse creatures in a captivating environment. Overnight Stay in Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast and Dinner, Description: Visit Outlet Mall - Expereince Desert Safari (SIC BASIS) Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Later this afternoon expereince the Desert Safari. Shop at Dubai Outlet Mall , a premier destination for discounted luxury and high street brands. With over 200 stores offering fashion, accessories, and lifestyle products, it’s a paradise for bargain hunters and style enthusiasts. Expereince the Desert Safari Embark on an exhilarating desert safari adventure across Dubai’s golden dunes. Experience thrilling dune bashing in 4x4 vehicles, offering an adrenaline packed ride through the vast desert landscape. Enjoy Campsite Relax at a traditional Bedouin campsite where you can sip aromatic Arabic coffee and enjoy sweet dates. The setting offers an authentic glimpse into desert hospitality and Emirati culture. Belly Dancing Be captivated by graceful belly dancing performances under the desert sky. The dancers’ fluid movements and vibrant costumes create a mesmerizing cultural spectacle for guests. Tanoura Dance Watch the hypnotic Tanoura Dance, featuring performers spinning in colorful skirts. This traditional art form symbolizes spiritual devotion and adds cultural depth to the evening’s entertainment. Fire Show Enjoy an awe inspiring fire show where skilled performers manipulate flames with precision. The dazzling display of light and heat adds excitement and drama to the desert safari experience. BBQ Dinner Feast on a hearty BBQ dinner with a wide variety of grilled meats, salads, and desserts. The meal, served under the stars, perfectly complements the evening’s entertainment and desert ambiance. Overnight Stay In Dubai, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Ras Al Khaimah, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Drive to Ras Al Khaimah Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel., check-out and drive to Ras Al Khaimah. You will be picked up and transferred to your hotel for check in. standard check in time is approximately 1400 hrs. Drive to Ras Al Khaimah, a scenic emirate known for its rugged mountains, pristine beaches, and cultural heritage. It offers a blend of adventure, relaxation, and history, making it a refreshing escape from Dubai’s bustle. Evening at Leisure to explore and enjoy the resort. Overnight Stay in Ras Al Khaimah, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Ras Al Khaimah, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day at Leisure Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Enjoy Marjan Island Resort Spend a leisurely day at Marjan Island in Ras Al Khaimah. Surrounded by pristine beaches and turquoise waters, the resort offers relaxation, luxury amenities, and stunning views, making it an ideal retreat for unwinding. Overnight in Ras Al Khaimah, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Ras Al Khaimah, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Day at Leisure Enjoy Breakfast in Hotel. Enjoy Marjan Island Resort Spend a leisurely day at Marjan Island in Ras Al Khaimah. Surrounded by pristine beaches and turquoise waters, the resort offers relaxation, luxury amenities, and stunning views, making it an ideal retreat for unwinding. Overnight in Ras Al Khaimah, GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Ras Al Khaimah, Meals: Breakfast, Description: Departure Morning after breakfast; you will be transferred to the airport for your flight back home to India., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 84406.0. Hotels envisaged include: Travel Validity: 05 Jan – 30 Apr 2026 & 01 Sep – 26 Sep 2026\n\n\n\nCity\nHotels\n\n\nDubai\nCitymax Hotel Bur Dubai | Admiral Plaza Hotel Bur Dubai| Gateway Hotel Bur Dubai | Arabian Park Edge by Rotana or Similar\n\n\n\n\xa0\nTravel Validity: 01 May’26 – 27 May’26\n\n\n\nCity\nHotels\n\n\nDubai\nCitymax Hotel Bur Dubai | Admiral Plaza Hotel Bur Dubai | Gateway Hotel Bur Dubai |Fortune Pearl Hotel Deira | Smana Al Raffa |City Avenue Hotel Deria | Arabian Park Edge by Rotana or Similar\n\n\n\n\xa0\nTravel Validity: 01 Jun’26 – 27 Aug’26\n\n\n\nCity\nHotels\n\n\nDubai\nCitymax Hotel Bur Dubai | Admiral Plaza Hotel Bur Dubai | Gateway Hotel Bur Dubai | Howard Johnson |Arabian Park Edge by Rotana | Fortune Pearl Hotel Deira | Fortune Plaza Al Quasis |Smana Al Raffa | City Avenue Hotel Deira or Similar\n\n\n, Travel Validity: 05 Jan – 30 Apr 2026 & 01 Sep – 26 Sep 2026\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel\n\n\nDubai\nOmega Hotel Bur Dubai | Sea View Hotel Bur Dubai | Ascot Hotel Bur Dubai |Arabian Courtyard Hotel & Spa Bur Dubai | Royal Ascot Hotel Bur Dubai or Similar\n\n\n\n\xa0\nTravel Validity: 01 May’26 – 27 May’26\xa0\n\n\n\nCity\nHotel\n\n\nDubai\nVersallies Hotel by Veiras | Omega Hotel Bur Dubai | Sea View Hotel Bur Dubai | Ascot Hotel Bur Dubai |Arabian Courtyard Hotel & Spa Bur Dubai | Ascot hotel Bur Dubai | Royal Ascot Hotel Bur Dubai or Similar\n\n\n, \n\n\nCity\nHotel\n\n\nDubai\nKhalidia Palace Dubai Deir | Avani Deira Dubai |Crowne Plaza Dubai Deira or Similar\n\n\n. Meals include: Breakfast Included. Inclusions: 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Dubai. 03 nights stay at the selected hotel option or similar in Ras Al Khaimah. Daily breakfast, except on Day 1 Airport / hotel / airport transfers on (PVT Basis) Arrive at Dubai – Marina Dhow Cruise with Buffet Dinner (SIC basis) Half Day City Tour Followed by Burj Khalifa 124 Floor Non-Prime Time (Non-Refundable & Slot are Subject to Availability) + Dubai Aquarium & Underwater Zoo Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner with Tanoora show and many more activities (SIC Basis) Duabi - Ras Al Khaimah - Dubai on (PVT Basis) 5% VAT Travel Insurance (Valid for the age group till 60 Yrs.). Exclusions: TCS & GST Visa charges All flights service Meals that are not mentioned in the itinerary. Any tips for guide & Driver Anything not mentioned in the inclusions. Pre & Post tour services & cost Expenditure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc) All drink and beverages Hotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel Tourism Tax (if applicable) Midnight surcharge. Product Terms and Conditions: Terms & Condition The package price is valid until 25 March 2027. The upgrade of hotel prices is subject to availability at the time of booking. The upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels. The upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking. For the upgrade hotel, in case the hotel chosen is unavailable, we will provide multiple options of similar category hotels. The rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adults travelling. The rates are not valid on blackout dates. Surcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same Surcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking. Guests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their onwards/connecting flights. The rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates. Prices are not valid during Trade Fair periods. Rates are valid for Indian Passport holders only. International Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed. Transfers wherever included are without night surcharges. No refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service. All the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking. Sightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice. Rates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends. Offer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice. Bookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time. TCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization. As a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. We will not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.. Highlights of the package: .", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Dehradun', 'cityCode': 'DED', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': '', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kanpur', 'c