ure of a personal nature (Such as uses of Mini – Bar & Refrigerator, laundry service, telephone call, camera fee, tips & Etc)\nAll drink and beverages\xa0\nHotel promotional rates not valid during Black out Period / Surcharge Dates / Stop Sales on Hotel\xa0\nTourism Tax (if applicable)\nMidnight surcharge\n', 'termsAndConditions': '\xa0\nTerms & Condition\n\nThe package price is valid until 31 March 2027.\nThe upgrade of hotel prices is subject to availability at the time of booking.\nThe upgrade hotel prices DO NOT GUARANTEE rooms at the envisaged hotels.\xa0\nThe upgrade hotel rooms are subject to availability at the time of booking.\xa0\nFor the upgrade hotel, in case the hotel chosen is unavailable, we will provide multiple options of similar category hotels.\nThe rates are valid for a minimum of 01 adults travelling.\nThe rates are not valid on blackout dates.\nSurcharges as and when applicable will be advised and passengers would be requested to pay the same\nSurcharges could be over and above the total package price quoted to the passengers at the time of booking.\xa0\nGuests are requested to check with sales staff before booking their onwards/connecting flights.\nThe rates are subject to availability of hotel accommodation and sightseeing tours at the time of booking. We reserve the right to use an alternate hotel accommodation of an equal or higher standard. If we source a more expensive alternative, we reserve the right to re-quote based on the higher rates.\nPrices are not valid during Trade Fair periods.\nRates are valid for Indian Passport holders only.\nInternational Check in time is 1400 hours / Check out time is 1100 hours, early check in and checkout is subject to availability and cannot be guaranteed.\nTransfers wherever included are without night surcharges.\nNo refunds either in part or in full will be made for any unutilized service.\nAll the sightseeing tours and excursions are organized by local companies. The timings and days of operation are subject to alteration. Changes if any will be intimated at the time of booking.\nSightseeing tours are strictly based on whether conditions and also local service providers have the right to cancel the sightseeing tours without prior notice.\nRates subject to change without prior notice and also for clients traveling during weekends.\nOffer if any can be withdrawn at any point without prior notice.\nBookings once confirmed are subject to cancellation charges which shall be advised at that time.\nTCIL is not responsible for any change in the price due to factors not in the control of the organization.\nAs a practice, all international hotels charge a security deposit via credit card or cash, at the time of check-in for each room. The amount will vary according to the hotel and is refunded back to the clients upon check-out. Debit cards should not be offered as they will be charged immediately and refunded only after 2-3 weeks. If any additional services or mini bar or any other service is utilized at the hotel, the hotel reserves the right to charge the same on this security deposit provided by the client. We will not be responsible for these transactions, and these are solely between the hotels and the clients.\n', 'pkgSubtypeId': 4, 'pkgSubtypeName': 'FIT', 'pkgTypeId': 1, 'isFlightIncluded': 'Y', 'holidayPlusSubType': 2, 'productId': 11, 'flightsAvailability': 'This package offers optional flights. You can choose to add flights or book separately.', 'serviceSlots': None, 'constructed_thumbnailImage': 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/ezgif-898b7307b458683b.jpg', 'constructed_images': ['https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/AUHcityscape_-_753x430.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/Abu_dhabi_-_753x430.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/AbudhabiCityscape_-_753x430.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/Dhow_Cruise.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/Stock_4426_Dubai_Burj_Khalifa753.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/DesertCamp_753_new.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/RAKalqawasimcorniche_753_JPG.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/RAK-AlMarjanIsland-_753x430.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/rak_marjan_-_753x430.jpg', 'https://resources.thomascook.in/images/holidays/PKG015265/itinerary/Jebel_Jais_753.jpg']}, 'score': 7.533186, 'departureCity_details': None, 'fareCalendar': None}, {'id': 'PKG015294', 'itinerary_data': {'packageId': 'PKG015294', 'availableMonths': ['november_2026', 'january_2027', 'december_2026', 'march_2027', 'february_2027'], 'packageName': 'Arabian Extravaganza - Winter', 'days': 7, 'cities': [{'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Dubai', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}, {'cityName': 'Abu Dhabi', 'geoLocation': {'lon': 0.0, 'lat': 0.0}}], 'highlights': ['Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box (1 box per family)'], 'pdfName': None, 'price': 165608, 'packageSummary': "The 'Arabian Extravaganza - Winter' package is a 7-day tour covering the vibrant cities of Abu Dhabi and Dubai. Throughout this exciting journey, participants will enjoy delightful highlights such as having ice cream during a city tour and visiting the Dolphin Aquarium. To make the trip even more memorable, each family will receive an exclusive 'Dubai Memories' souvenir box as a special keepsake of their Arabian adventure.", 'images': ['47954_Dubai_Marina_753.jpg', 'BurjKhalifa_753_New_183371461.jpg', 'DubaiDesertSafari753.jpg', '28674_Abu_Dhabi_sheikh_zayed_grand_mosque_UAE_753.jpg', 'AbuDhabiwithFerrariWorld753.jpg', 'AbuDhabi7534.jpg', 'Abu_Dhabi_753.jpg'], 'minimumPrice': 165608, 'thumbnailImage': '119979_Abu_Dhabi_SRP.jpg', 'packageTheme': ['Adventure', 'Family'], 'isTcilRecomended': 'Luxury Escape', 'packageData': "Package ID: PKG015294 is named 'Arabian Extravaganza - Winter' and spans 7 days. The itinerary includes:\nDay 1 - Dubai, Meals: Dinner, Description: Arrival In Dubai - Check In – Enjoy Limousine Ride Welcome To United Arab Emirates. On Arrival In Dubai, You Will Be Greeted By Your Friendly Tour Manager / Local Representative Outside The Baggage Hall Area At The Airport. Transfer To The Hotel & Check-In. (Standard Check In Time After 1500hrs). Later Enjoy One-Hour Limousine Ride, Sit Back In The Most Comfortable And Luxurious Stretch Limousine And Explore The Night City View. Note All Our Guests Are Advised To Activate International Calling/Data & International Credit Card Joining Direct Passengers / Nri Passengers Can Check-In On Your Own At The Hotel. The Standard Check-In Time Is 1500 Hrs., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 2 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Burj Khalifa - Guided City Tour Of Dubai - Visit Global Village This morning after buffet breakfast, Visit 124th Floor of Burj Khalifa (non-prime hours). Free time at the Dubai Mall later enjoy Fountain Show. Later proceed for a guided city tour of Dubai along with Photo stop at the Dubai Frame, Museum of the Future, Jumeirah Beach, Jumeirah Mosque & Zabeel Palace. Proceed for Global Village a shopping, dining, and entertainment attraction located on Sheikh Mohammed Bin Zayed Road. There are four main sections in the Village. These sections consist of events and concerts, carnivals, food, and shopping., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 3 - Dubai, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch and Dinner, Description: Visit Dubai Dolphinarium - Visit Gold Souk - Desert Safari With Dune Bashing & BBQ Dinner This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Dubai Dolphinarium. The Dolphin & Seal Show, the #1 in the UAE. These interactive extravaganzas showcase the amazing animals' astounding skills. Visitors watch in wonder as the dolphins and seals dance, sing, juggle, play ball, jump through hoops and even paint. Free time for shopping at Gold Souk & Spice Souk. Later This Afternoon Proceed For Desert Safari To Enjoy The Thrilling Dune Bashing On A Desert Safari Adventure Exploring The Massive Sand Dunes Of The Arabian Deserts. Enjoy Bbq Dinner And The Belly Dancing Performance At The Desert Camp., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 4 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Proceed To Abu Dhabi - Visit Team Lab - Guided City Tour Of Abu Dhabi - Photostop At Grand Mosque - Entrance To Ferrari World / Warner Bros / Sea World (Any 1 Park) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Abu Dhabi. Visit Team Lab - An Digital Museum That Collaborates The Confluence Of Art, Science, Technology, And The Natural World. Later We Proceed On A Guided City Tour Of Abu Dhabi City Tour Along-With A Photo Stop At The Grand Mosque. Later This Afternoon We Proceed To Yas Island - Our Guest Have A Choice To Visit Ferrari World Or Warner Bros Or Sea World (1 Park Entry Included). Note: Photo stop means NO Entry inside the attraction., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 5 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Swami Narayan Temple. Entrance to Ferrari World / Warner Bros / Sea World (Any 1 park) This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit The Baps Hindu Mandir - A Traditional Hindu Mandir Built By The Baps Swaminarayan Sanstha. This Is The First Traditional Hindu Mandir In Abu Dhabi. Later This Afternoon We Proceed To Yas Island - Our Guest Have A Choice To Visit Ferrari World Or Warner Bros Or Sea World (1 Park Entry Included)., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 6 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon and Dinner, Description: Visit Snow Abu Dhabai – Visit Qasr Al Watan This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Proceed To Visit Snow Abu Dhabi. Later In Evening We Proceed To Visit Qasr Al Watan - An Imposing Royal Palace In Abu Dhabi, It Is A Unique Testament To The Spirit Of The United Arab Emirates' People And Its Leaders., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nDay 7 - Abu Dhabi, Meals: Breakfast, Description: End Of Tour - Fly Back This Morning After Buffet Breakfast, Check Out And Proceed To The Airport. Return Home With Wonderful Memories Of Your Tour. Note: On few days there will be a coach merger with other Dubai product's (if required) Note : The above itinerary is tentative and subjected to change without prior notice., GeoLocation: (Lat: 0.0, Lon: 0.0).\nThe price is 165608.0. Hotels envisaged include: Overnight stay at the Hotels, Valid Till March 2026\n\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Crown Plaza or similar in Dubai\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Dusit Thani /\xa0Le Royal Meridien\xa0or similar or similar in Abu Dhabi\n\n\xa0\nValid From Apr 2026 To Sept 2026\n\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Crown Plaza or similar in Dubai\n03 nights accommodation at Hotel Dusit Thani or similar or similar in Abu Dhabi\n. Meals include: \nDaily American buffet breakfast. (Except Day 1)\n02 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Lunches\xa0\n02 Lunch Coupon ( At Park visit in Abu Dhabi)\n01 Lunch Coupon ( At Snow Abu Dhabi)\n01 Local BBQ Buffet dinner at Desert Safari\n05 Indian Jain / Vegetarian / Non - Vegetarian Dinners\xa0\n\n(B–Breakfast / PB-Packed Breakfast / BR – Brunch / L-Lunch / LL–Local Lunch / LC-Lunch coupon / PL–Packed Lunch / D-Dinner / LD-Local Dinner / PD – Packed Dinner), Breakfast Included. Inclusions: Return economy class group airfare as per the itinerary. Accommodation at the hotels specified above or similar. All local taxes including services taxes as of 1st August 2026. Cost of Visa & Travel Insurance for the duration of the tour. Sightseeing, accommodation & services as per the above-mentioned itinerary. All transfers and excursions are inclusive of entrance fees (as specified in the itinerary) by a deluxe air-conditioned coach. Professional services of a friendly and multilingual Tour Manager (Subject to minimum 20 customers) or a local Representative. If the group size is less than 15 customers, then the tour will operate on Seat in Coach basis. Tourism Dirham Fees + 5% VAT Visa Requirements UAE Visa included (E-visa) Cost of visas including documentation and processing fees as of 1st August 2026. Any further increase in the same must be borne by the passengers.. Exclusions: If you wish to travel in advance i.e. before the published departure date as mentioned in the brochure or like to come back on a later date after the tour ends, there will be an additional charge that will be applicable (subject to availability of seats for the given dates & ticket validity) which will be advised to you by our sales staff / travel agent. Kindly note, the deviation will be actioned only 30 Days prior to departure date. Cost of Basic Travel Quota is equivalent to USD 2,50,000. Any increase in the airfare charged by the airline on your air ticket (presently calculated as of 1st August 2026) Applicable Government Taxes and other service charges. The tour cost does not include POE charges and passport charges. Porterage Facility Any other expenses of personal nature such as porterage, laundry expenses, mini-bar, mineral water, telephone charges, foods and beverages that are not included as a part of the package. Additional Meals which is not specifically included in the above itinerary. Cost of excursions, city sightseeing, entrance fees and local guides availed of by the passengers, other than that mentioned in the above itinerary. Cost of Optional Excursions.. Product Terms and Conditions: General Information: All travelers while returning to India should submit a self-declaration form (mandatory) on the online Air Suvidha portal (www.newdelhiairport.in) before the scheduled travel, including the last 14 days of travel details. Each passenger shall also submit a declaration with respect to the authenticity of the report and will be liable for criminal prosecution if found otherwise. If tour is operated on FIT basis (Less than 10 passengers); FIT supplement applicable will as follows: Below Slabs are Based on the Number of Adults Traveling Together:(Cost is Per Person In USD) Slab Per Adult Per Child 2-3 PAX 390 315 4 PAX 150 120 5-9 PAX 85 70 Note: Surcharges may be applicable on few of the above departure dates. Please contact your local travel agent for information on Surcharge dates and prices. Important Note: Airline and Airfare: The airfare is based on the fare structure existing as on 1st February 2022. Any further increase in the airfare due to an increase in the fuel price, change in Government regulations, taxes, etc., charged by the airline will have to be borne by the passengers. Passengers missing flights - In such cases the entire ticket/booking gets a no show and stands canceled. A new return ticket needs to be purchased by the passengers. For prices and departure dates from your hub city please contact our local sales offices/travel agents. The cost of Travel to Hub City is not a part of the package Hotels: This Package doesn’t offer city center hotels. Hotels will be located in the airport area or on the outskirts. As a 3rd person in a triple room, most hotels offer rollaway beds and room size will be the same as a double room. For Child with bed: At times hotel don’t have enough roll-away beds, in that case they might give a double and a separate single room A person 12 years and below is considered child and above 12 years, an adult Due to international events and trade fairs you may have to stay in hotels further away from the city. Any damages caused to the hotel rooms / Coach during the stay shall be payable by the passengers. We also reserve the right to substitute a hotel of similar class if it is deemed advisable or necessary Hotels in certain cities are not offering buffet breakfasts due to health regulations. If the same does not change by the time the tours operate, we will organize breakfasts at Indian / local restaurants. Coaches: Coaches are an important part of your journeys and we request our guests to keep the coach clean. Due to hygiene factors it is not permitted to use toilets in the coach. However the tour manager will make comfort stops during long drives Eating & drinking is not permitted in the coach. Due to limited boot space in the coach we suggest you to carry one check-in bag & one hand bag per person only Due to parking regulations and designated drop off & pick up points it is not possible to stop at all the places during the city tour. Tour Manager will try his/her best to stop coach wherever possible for a photo stop. Coaches do not have a wheelchair access. There are steps to board / alight from the coach. Coaches are forbidden inside most of the historic city centers; to preserve them from damage caused by pollution and getting overcrowded. Most of your sightseeing will be done by local buses and by foot in the historic and heritage centers. Meals: All Meals are pre–set. Packed lunches will be provided on certain days. Sightseeings: Due to logistical reasons certain departures may have amendments or reverse the itinerary. However, all the services / inclusions will remain the same. Generally, you will have to walk at sightseeing places, amusement parks and at the airports sometimes for a long distance; however the same will be timely instructed by the Tour Manager. It is advisable to carry good pair of comfortable sports shoes. The tour manager and the driver will do their best to get you as close to the monuments as possible. Every Site / Monuments has its own set of rules and regulations. We need to respect this and ensure that we follow the same. All our visits are booked in advance to avoid delays,at the same time there may be delays caused due to over crowding ,local regulations ,security check etc. General: On some occasions you may have to join another group in case the group does not have adequate number of members. A local representative or a driver may only be there to assist you during the your initial part of you tour. Security alerts and unforseen closures may affect the itinerary. Please take extra care of your personal belongings while on the tour, every country you travel to is prone to thefts and bag snatching. Thomas Cook I Limited will not be liable for any loss of belongings / baggage. Disabled clients shall carry their own wheelchair & be accompanied by a qualified companion who is able to provide assistance to the disabled client per their regular/routine requirements. Thomas Cook I Limited shall not accept any liability or responsibility for any damages, loss, baggage loss, theft, injury, accident, death, breakdown or irregularity, which may occur in carrying out the tour arrangement, weather conditions, strikes, war, quarantine and any other cause whatsoever and all such loss or expense must be borne by the passengers alone. Insurance policies must be carried along all throughout while on tour. Normal insurance charges for the duration of the tour are included in the tour price. However, any passenger above the age of 60 years and those who wish to extend their stay will be required to pay additional charges. The management reserves the right to claim any additional expenses incurred due to delay or changes in schedules of train, airplane, bus, ship or other services. The Tour Manager and the company reserves the right to amend the itinerary, alter, vary or withdraw any particular departure, excursion advertised. For the convenience of our passengers, we may at times amend the itinerary to suit prevalent conditions & at the same time attain optimum utilization of the tour.All the services as per itinerary shall remain the same as it is during such amends. There are no refunds for any services i.e. meals, sightseeing etc. not utilized on your tour In case you decide to change the date of your return reservation once confirmed the exact amount payable to the airline will be advised once the same is confirmed. The images used in this brochure are for representation purpose only. Tours operated are subject to RBI / GOI regulations. Part of the tour cost will be paid in USD EURO / CHF out of your BTQ at prevailing rate of exchange at the relevant time. • Please refer to the Booking Form for detailed “Terms and Conditions”.. Highlights of the package: Ice Cream during City tour or Dolphin Aquarium Dubai Memories - An Exclusive Souvenir Box (1 box per family).", 'departureCities': [{'cityName': 'Mumbai', 'cityCode': 'BOM', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Delhi', 'cityCode': 'DEL', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Chennai', 'cityCode': 'MAA', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bangalore', 'cityCode': 'BLR', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Hyderabad', 'cityCode': 'HYD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kochi', 'cityCode': 'COK', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Kolkata', 'cityCode': 'CCU', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Ahmedabad', 'cityCode': 'AMD', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Jaipur', 'cityCode': 'JAI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Thiruvananthapuram', 'cityCode': 'TRV', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId': ''}, {'cityName': 'Bhubaneswar', 'cityCode': 'BBI', 'ltItineraryCode': 'ZAX752', 'holidayLtPricingId'